window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":401,"title":"Chapter 401: Prayers and Complaints","paragraphs":["Xie Zhiyan nodded in agreement. \"So the Junior Preceptor means to ask Royal Father for more soldiers and generals, just like with that small island last time, and have the imperial court dispatch ships as soon as possible to take over and garrison it.\"","A cold look flashed across Xie Zhiyan's face. \"The Eastern Yi fear power but have no gratitude; they fixate on trivialities but lack a sense of righteousness. I'm just worried that once they get what they want, they'll go back on their word. It's not like their ancestors haven't done this before!\"","Emperor Mingxi said dismissively, \"If the Eastern Yi really dare to do so, our Great Yan is not to be trifled with. Bullying our dynasty's Junior Preceptor is tantamount to declaring war on Great Yan.\"","Thinking of this ready-made excuse to deploy troops, Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but pick up his teacup and take a large gulp. If Huo Ying, Feng Tang, and the others knew about this, who knows how many wicked ideas they could come up with.","As the saying goes, speak of the devil. Just as Emperor Mingxi thought of this, he heard a young eunuch outside announcing that Lord Huo Ying and several other officials were requesting an audience outside the hall.","Yue Fuguang did not ask the system what Emperor Mingxi and his ministers discussed during their late-night, candlelit conversation regarding Chrysanthemum Island and the Eastern Yi.","The next day, when she finally got up, Cuizhu served her as she washed and dressed, while telling Yue Fuguang about Yanji's visit.","\"Miss, after I gave him the note you wrote last night, you should have seen the look on his face when he read the contents.\"","Cuizhu mimicked Yanji's expression at the time, vividly performing it for Yue Fuguang. This mixture of crying and laughing was exactly what Yue Fuguang had expected.","\"I guess Yanji's expression back then definitely wasn't as pretty as Cuizhu's is right now.\"","\"Miss, your guess is spot on. I was there too, and that Eastern Yi prince can't even compare to Sister Cuizhu.\" The ever-praising Qingzhu immediately chimed in.","\"You're such a sweet-talker!\" Cuizhu gently tapped Qingzhu on the forehead. Qingzhu ran outside, covering her forehead, not forgetting to leave a trail of flattery as she went: \"Miss is always right!\"","[Host, Qingzhu is wrong this time. Even you make mistakes!]","\"What's the matter, 07? Tell me, how am I wrong?\"","[Host, I'm not the one saying this; it's the rumors spreading outside.]","The system immediately distanced itself from the statement, lest its host decide to punish it as well. As her abilities grew stronger, her heart was growing darker too.","After dealing with the noble families, it was as if a restrictive switch had been flipped for its host. If it weren't for the karmic restraints of the merit system, she probably would have let loose completely by now.","\"Rumors spreading? Do you mean someone is deliberately guiding public opinion? Can you find out who did it?\"","[It started with complaints from your 'believers,' which were then deliberately steered and spread by people with ulterior motives from various factions. Since many people visit relatives and friends during the New Year holidays, the news naturally spread much faster.]","Yue Fuguang poked the rice in her bowl with her chopsticks. \"So, those faint accusations and complaints I heard in my sleep at night weren't dreams, but the actual words of my believers?\"","With her fragile ego, how could she bear this? The title of 'Immortal' gave her enough confidence to say no, but as a hypocrite, she couldn't stand it when others said no to her.","The more she thought about it, the angrier she got. She pushed her bowl aside, and after everyone else had left the room, she continued speaking to the system, \"Since they don't believe in me, they won't need to believe in me ever again!\"","Although she quite enjoyed being called 'Divine Maiden' by others, she hadn't lost herself in it.","Yue Fuguang always remembered that her primary identity was a tasker, and completing her mission was the top priority.","As for faith and incense offerings, those were just unexpected bonuses. As long as it didn't affect the progress of her mission, what did it matter if she lost some incense?","In short, she couldn't allow herself to be wronged!","She had a fragile ego and was petty; she lacked the magnanimity to simply ignore the ignorant or the common folk.","[Host, what do you want to do?] the system asked cautiously. She wouldn't just kill everyone in a fit of rage, would she?","There weren't too many people across the lands of Great Yan saying these things, but it wasn't a small number either. If she really killed them all, Emperor Mingxi would have a massive headache dealing with the aftermath.","If Yue Fuguang knew that the system thought of her this way, she would definitely roll her eyes hard and ask it, 'Am I that kind of person?'","\"Naturally, I'll revoke their qualifications to worship me. You didn't think I'd kill them all, did you?\" What kind of person did it take her for!","Yue Fuguang sat cross-legged, closed her eyes, and focused her mind on her qi acupoints. She looked inward to guard her dantian, purifying her body, calming her breath, and clearing her mind.","Following the faint connections of incense offerings, she listened intently, seemingly able to hear the various prayers and complaints more clearly.","A cacophony of murmurs rushed into her ears like the buzzing of a swarm, containing both prayers and grievances.","She traced the connections toward the sources of obvious malice.","At the Du family in Big Willow Village, Old Lady Du was respectfully offering incense to the 'Divine Maiden.' She had just lit the incense and hadn't even had time to beg the Divine Maiden for rain, when she saw her husband and several sons walking listlessly into the courtyard carrying hoes and shovels.","As soon as her youngest son, Du Hetao, entered the house, he yelled, \"Mother, is the food ready? I'm starving to death!\"","Old Man Du couldn't help but scold him, \"Little Four, can't you see your mother is offering incense to the Divine Maiden? Yelling and shouting like that will disturb the Divine Maiden, watch your skin!\"","For a family like theirs, if they encountered such weather in previous years, they wouldn't dare eat a full meal. Fearing the whole family wouldn't survive a famine year, they would save as much of their rations as possible.","Now, thanks to the Divine Maiden's grace, poor laborers like them were able to plant crops that yielded thousands of catties per acre. The weather in the first half of last year was still decent, and even in their poorest-quality fields, the potatoes and sweet potatoes they planted yielded over a thousand catties per acre.","Even the acre or so of wasteland that he and his eldest son had cleared at the foot of the mountain, which was entirely planted with sweet potatoes, yielded over eight hundred catties because the father and sons were willing to put in the hard work to tend the fields.","Therefore, the family was not short of food for the time being. It was just water that the whole family had to use sparingly.","Old Man Du took the incense from his old wife, bowed respectfully, and carefully placed it into the small clay incense burner, which was already piled high with ash.","When Old Man Du sat down and slowly drank some water, Old Lady Du looked at the bright sky outside and asked, \"Old man, why are you back so early today?\"","Old Man Du put down his coarse porcelain bowl, stroked his gray beard, and sighed. \"The fields are all dry; there aren't even many weeds left. The land to be planted next year has long been prepared. There's no work to do right now, so we came back early.\"","Although the village had dug wells and stored water in ponds, that water was meant for irrigating the fields when planting started in the spring. No one was allowed to touch it now, so the land just had to remain dry for the time being.","Sitting under the eaves, he looked up at the sun overhead and a sky without a single cloud. Even though it was only the fifth day of the first lunar month and still within the New Year festival period, the festive atmosphere in the village had diminished greatly due to the drought. Even the children didn't dare to be too rowdy with their holiday laughter and play, for fear of angering the elders who were already anxious about the dry weather.","\"Old woman, if it still doesn't rain by the time the fifteenth passes, let the boys go to town to find some work.\" With no work in the fields, their daily routine consisted of just chopping wood and fetching water. If they didn't go out to find some jobs, they couldn't just sit around idle.","Poor families couldn't afford to be idle for even a single day."]},{"number":402,"title":"Chapter 402: Deputy Chief Examiner","paragraphs":["Hearing their father's words, Du Laoda and Du Laosan were both somewhat tempted. However, their village lacked water, and the city was no different. Everyone knew a drought was coming, leaving them uncertain. Who would dare to easily hire workers now? Finding a job wouldn't be easy.","Seeing her husband's distressed face, Old Lady Du could not help but comfort him, \"Old man, we still have enough grain at home, so you don't need to worry too much.\" As for water, they could only take it one step at a time and see if the heavens would leave them a way to survive.","Speaking of grain, this year the imperial court had exchanged eighty percent of the sweet potatoes and potatoes grown in their fields for wheat, sorghum, and silver.","Fortunately, both she and her old man had experienced natural disasters in their youth and were terrified of starvation. They never felt secure without food at home, so at the time, they had chosen half grain and half silver.","They had planned it all out perfectly: after another year of farming, they could exchange their harvest for silver to renovate and expand their house.","The Du family had three sons and two daughters. The youngest daughter was married off at the end of last year, and all three sons had taken wives. With two grandchildren already born, it was obvious that the house was running out of room.","The youngest son, who had been complaining of hunger, first saw his parents acting as if they hadn't heard him, solely focused on burning incense. Now, hearing their conversation, he was quite reluctant to leave his newlywed wife to go find work.","\"Father, Mother, if you ask me, you shouldn't be burning incense every day. We could save the money spent on incense and candles to buy some meat.\"","He patted his belly. He had thought that with a good harvest this year, they could eat meat a few more times. Who would have thought they would encounter a drought? It hadn't rained for months, and his parents were too stingy to spend their newly acquired silver on meat.","At the thought of meat, Du Hetao almost drooled. Since the autumn harvest, he hadn't tasted a drop of grease until New Year's Day, and even then, it was just a tiny bit!","He glanced at the idol enshrined in the main room and said with great dissatisfaction, \"If you ask me, this 'Divine Maiden' isn't as efficacious as you think. Otherwise, every household in our village has been praying for so long, yet not a single drop of rain has fallen. I say we might as well...\"","\"I'll beat you to death, you bastard! How dare you speak disrespectfully of the Divine Maiden! I think you're tired of living!\" Old Man Du didn't wait for his youngest son to continue his nonsense; he picked up a broom nearby and threw it at him.","\"Father!\" Du Laosi tilted his head to dodge it. \"You can't be so unreasonable! Was I wrong? The Divine Maiden just doesn't work!\"","\"You're still talking! Still talking! I'll teach you to keep talking!\" Old Man Du stood up abruptly, looked around, and upon spotting a large broom by the door, grabbed it and swung it at his youngest son.","\"Today, I will beat you to death, you ungrateful wretch!\" Nearly fifty years old, Old Man Du chased after his young and strong son, huffing and puffing.","\"Father, even if you beat me to death today, I'll still say the same thing. The Divine Maiden doesn't work. There's really no need to burn incense. Wouldn't it be better if we saved the incense money and our whole family had a meal of meat?\"","Du Laosi kept dodging his father, running ahead while his mouth never stopped running.","Old Man Du had just stopped to catch his breath when he heard his youngest son's reckless words again. He turned to his eldest son and said, \"Du Laoda, help me hold your brother down. Watch me beat him to death today!\"","Old Lady Du looked at her husband, his old face red with anger and panting heavily from exhaustion, and then at her youngest son, whom the couple had always favored a bit more since childhood. The words of plea she wanted to say remained unspoken after she cast a glance at the Divine Maiden's statue.","Since her youngest son dared to speak recklessly about the Divine Maiden, it was right for his father to teach him a good lesson. A person shouldn't be an ungrateful wretch.","Hearing his father's words, Du Laoda put down the basket he was weaving and went after the jumping Du Laosi. He had wanted to beat his younger brother for a long time, but because their parents doted on him, he had never had the chance.","\"Third Brother, save me!\" Seeing that his mother wasn't intervening, his eldest brother was only listening to their father, and his wife and sisters-in-law had long since hidden in their own rooms, Du Laosi could only seek help from Du Laosan.","Actually, Du Laosan quite agreed with what his younger brother said. In his heart, he felt that the Divine Maiden was nothing special; when faced with a drought, she was just as helpless! Unfortunately, he lacked his brother's courage and didn't dare to say it out loud.","\"Father, please calm down. What Fourth Brother said isn't wrong. Who knows when it will rain? Praying to the Divine Maiden is worse than praying to the Dragon King.\" The Dragon King was the one in charge of rain; his parents were praying to the wrong deity.","Seeing his third brother speak up for him, Du Laosi instantly felt even more justified in his words. He hid behind Du Laosan, and before his eldest brother could pin him down, he darted off toward the altar where the statue of the Divine Maiden Yue Fuguang was enshrined.","Standing by the altar, he spoke to the statue, \"'Divine Maiden,' tell me, was what I just said wrong? Is worshipping you really of no use!\"","Seeing their youngest son's actions, Old Man Du and his wife were stunned for a moment before reacting and rushing into the room. \"Du Hetao, do you want to die!\"","Old Man Du's voice was filled with anger and terror, his voice even cracking a bit.","Old Lady Du was closer to the door, but she was so frightened by her youngest son's actions that her legs went weak, and she couldn't run.","The youngest son she had doted on for eighteen years, she never expected him to be such a scoundrel, daring to speak directly to the Divine Maiden's statue like that. Did he not know that the statue could communicate with the divine!","\"Little Four, hurry... stop right now!\" Seeing her youngest son reaching out toward the statue, Old Lady Du hurriedly yelled to stop him.","Bang!","The echo of the word \"stop\" was still reverberating in the Du family courtyard, and Old Man Du and his wife had just reached the door, when they saw that right as Du Laosi's large hand was about to touch the statue, the statue exploded on its own!","With a bang, sounding like popped rice at the town market, the statue shattered into powder, covering the face and head of the closest person, Du Laosi.","Following this explosion, it was as if the pause button had been pressed on the Du family courtyard. Everyone who saw it stood frozen in place.","\"It's over, it's all over!\" Old Man Du slid down against the doorframe to sit on the ground. His weather-beaten face, lined from years of hard labor, suddenly seemed to age ten years, and his deeply wrinkled visage was filled with ashen despair.","If what happened today spread, not only their youngest son but their entire family would never be able to hold their heads up again in Big Willow Village and the surrounding villages.","What good end could come to someone who offended the Divine Maiden and was forsaken by her!","A single spit from everyone would be enough to drown them!","\"Father... I... I...\" Du Hetao swallowed hard. Only now did he realize the magnitude of the disaster he had caused.","Looking at the faces of his parents and brothers, he felt he was doomed!","Situations like the Du family's were constantly playing out all over the land of Dayan.","Especially after the Lantern Festival, the saying \"No rain on Shangyuan means a spring drought\" spread wider and wider. The believers' doubts about the Divine Maiden's abilities grew day by day, reaching a point where the imperial court had to step in to control public opinion. The news that blaspheming the Divine Maiden would cause the enshrined portraits at home to spontaneously combust and statues to self-destruct could no longer be covered up. Once leaked, it spread rapidly.","By the time Emperor Mingxi and the others heard this news, they were in the middle of the morning court assembly, and Yue Fuguang had just been appointed by Emperor Mingxi as the deputy chief examiner for the upcoming special imperial examination.","Anyone who had taken or hosted the imperial examinations knew that the spring exams generally featured two chief examiners, one primary and one deputy, who oversaw all matters in the examination hall, including setting the questions and establishing the admission standards.","It could be said that they held great power, but the task was equally heavy!","Yue Fuguang looked down at her twelve-year-old self. Her shoulders were too small; it seemed she couldn't bear such a heavy burden."]},{"number":403,"title":"Chapter 403: Who Agrees, Who Opposes","paragraphs":["\"Your Majesty, which lord are you planning to appoint as the chief examiner?\"","Yue Fuguang lowered her eyes and swept her gaze over the lords standing in the grand hall. Emperor Mingxi had bypassed the chief examiner to first announce her as the deputy chief examiner for the metropolitan examination in the royal court. Since she did not want to shoulder the heavy burden, the choice of the chief examiner was crucial.","She hoped the emperor would understand her slacker nature and pick a capable person to take charge above her.","Hearing Yue Fuguang ask this, how could Emperor Mingxi not understand what she meant?","However, he was not in a hurry to announce the candidate for the chief examiner. Instead, he asked Yue Fuguang, \"Fuguang, in your opinion, which lord do you think is the most suitable to be appointed as the chief examiner?\"","As the emperor's words fell, the lords who had been keeping their heads down carefully raised them to steal glances at the emperor and Yue Fuguang.","Some of them had their desire to be the chief examiner written all over their faces, not afraid that Yue Fuguang would see it, but rather afraid that she wouldn't.","Being the chief examiner would not only make them the mentor of the new scholars but also bring them closer to the Junior Preceptor than their colleagues.","It could be said that even after three years, the Great Yan courtiers' desire to cling to Yue Fuguang's coattails had not ceased. On the contrary, because her prophecies of natural disasters had come true, they were even more eager. Even if they couldn't be the chief examiner, being a co-examiner, a supervising official, or an administering official would be fine!","But in a royal court, there could never be only one voice. While some wanted to cling to Yue Fuguang, others wanted to bring her down.","Although three years had passed, a small portion of the officials in the court were still not within the coverage of her inner voice.","She was neither a saint nor magnanimous. Who told these people to have such low affection for her? She didn't want these people who felt indifferent or even harbored hidden malice towards her to get the chance to enter the central power core.","After all, the tacit understanding between the ruler and his ministers in the entire Great Yan court was that the central decision-making positions must be held by those who could hear the Junior Preceptor's inner voice. Otherwise, if they knew nothing, how could they play the game?","Yue Fuguang being appointed as the deputy chief examiner by Emperor Mingxi had already made some people restless. But the experience of the past two or three years told them that those who opposed the Junior Preceptor never ended well.","They were either dragged to the vegetable market to be beheaded or had their entire families exiled!","The luckier ones were demoted to barren lands, never to rise again for the rest of their lives. So they were still very afraid of retaliation.","Yue Fuguang: I just exposed the dirty secrets of those who disliked me and tried to provoke me. How could that be called retaliation?","Embezzlement, allowing their servants to rob civilian women and lands, maliciously injuring and killing people—they did all these things themselves!","She merely told the plain truth, and the court dealt with them according to the law. She certainly didn't use her power for personal revenge.","Although everyone was very cautious when dealing with her, Emperor Mingxi not only chose a little girl like her to be the deputy chief examiner of the imperial examination but also actually consulted Yue Fuguang on the choice of the chief examiner!","Those who originally wanted to endure it finally couldn't help but jump out. This time they had reason on their side, so what was there to be afraid of!","Those who dared to jump out were not overflowing with a sense of justice and acting entirely for the public good. It was because there had been many doubts among the people recently about the Divine Maiden's abilities, which allowed these people who had long wanted to pull Yue Fuguang down to see an opportunity.","If they could step on the Junior Preceptor's name to rise to power, not to mention the present, even in the future history books, they would definitely have a page of their own.","\"Your Majesty, the metropolitan examination is to select outstanding talents for the imperial court. The responsibilities of the chief examiner and the deputy chief examiner are of utmost importance. How can this be treated as child's play?\" An official with a gray beard, wearing an official uniform that was seventy percent new, with deep wrinkles on his face and legs that didn't look very nimble, spoke up with an accusation right away.","\"The Junior Preceptor is young and has never presided over the spring examinations before. It is already inappropriate for her to be the deputy chief examiner. How can you even consult her opinion on the chief examiner?","How can the words of a child be trusted! This... this is inappropriate, highly inappropriate, Your Majesty!\"","Saying so, he knelt down before Emperor Mingxi, tears welling up in his eyes, with a face full of loyalty and devotion to the public, as resolute as if he were taking a solemn oath, making Emperor Mingxi look like a foolish ruler who favored a 'villain'!","[Master, this old fellow not only wants to step on your head, but he also doesn't plan to let the emperor off the hook!]","Emperor Mingxi's face darkened, and the other lords were not much better. Feng Tang was the first to lose his patience and said, \"Lord Song, the child you speak of is the Junior Preceptor of our dynasty, ranking above the Three Excellencies!","Moreover, she is a prince of our dynasty, and her name is recorded in the royal genealogy! How exalted is her status?","Leaving aside other matters, Your Majesty, I impeach Lord Song for disregarding the hierarchy and committing the crime of great disrespect against the Junior Preceptor!\"","\"Your Majesty, I, Ye Lin, object!\" As soon as Feng Tang's words fell, an official with slightly dark skin and an ordinary face, in his thirties, impatiently jumped out to question Feng Tang's words.","Yue Fuguang saw that this person looked a bit unfamiliar. Although she didn't pay much attention to who the officials standing at the back of the court assembly were, she had little impression of this person, so she guessed he must be an official transferred here in the past year or two.","Saying a year or two was because the new year had just passed, so it was basically two years!","\"Although the Junior Preceptor's status is noble, can it be nobler than Your Majesty and His Royal Highness the Crown Prince?\" Saying so, he respectfully bowed to Emperor Mingxi and Xie Zhiyan, establishing the image of a humble and respectful subject.","Emperor Mingxi: That's not necessarily true!","Crown Prince: Don't drag me into this to step on others! Stay away from me JPG","Seeing that his flattery did not achieve the desired effect, Ye Lin assumed the royal father and son were being reserved, and continued along his own line of thought, \"Your Majesty, I personally think that what Lord Song just said is very reasonable.\"","He bowed slightly to Yue Fuguang, \"Although the Junior Preceptor's reputation among the people has a tendency to surpass that of Your Majesty due to her accidental discovery of high-yield crops, she is still young after all and rarely participates in political affairs on regular days.","Being able to serve as the deputy chief examiner for the major examination is already Your Majesty's profound grace. For her to decide the candidate for the chief examiner is truly inappropriate. If word gets out, wouldn't our neighboring countries laugh at our Great Yan for having no capable people in the court?\"","\"Lord Ye, you are overstating things!\" There was no need for Feng Tang to scold him; Wu Yong, an official of the same rank, bowed and stepped forward, \"Your Majesty, I believe...\"","'Little Zhu, who is this guy? Saying my reputation among the people is higher than the emperor's, he's secretly trying to draw the emperor's hatred towards me!'","[Master, if the emperor really becomes wary of you because of this, we'll just move to another place!]","Emperor Mingxi: How innocent am I! Getting shot even while lying down, is there any justice left! Pray for me JPG","[Master, this person was just promoted from the local provinces half a year ago, so he looks unfamiliar to you.]","'Is this person very capable?' If he was a capable official who hadn't broken the law or violated discipline, she would just exact a tiny revenge and let it go. Otherwise, she would send him to keep Old Man Song company. At the end of the day, she was not a magnanimous person.","[Uh... he was recommended mainly because of his 'good reputation'. This person's persona is being uncorrupted and honest, as well as filial to his widowed mother. He was set up as a model example, and with good luck, he was transferred from the local provinces back to the capital.","Then he met a noble patron who promoted him, allowing him to luckily slip into the royal court.]","After the divine artifact lord said this, Emperor Mingxi and the Minister of Personnel, Ji Hongming, also recalled this person's promotion history."]},{"number":404,"title":"Chapter 404: Want to Be a Widower","paragraphs":["Ji Hongming secretly gritted his teeth. He had personally sought the Emperor's approval to transfer this man to the capital, putting in extra effort only because the recommender was a fellow graduate and a good friend of his.","Who knew this guy was so stubborn and reckless? Having been in the court for three or four months, he had seemed honest and well-behaved. How could his very first remonstrance be aimed directly at the untouchable Grand Preceptor!","He had been in the capital for over half a year, after all. He might not have heard much about the Grand Preceptor while in the provinces, but he should have heard plenty of rumors since arriving in the capital. Did he really lack a clear understanding of this living ancestor's status?","Ji Hongming's thoughts were spot on. Ever since Ye Lin entered the capital, his ears had been filled with all kinds of praise and admiration for this Grand Preceptor.","For Ye Lin, who had always looked down on women and considered himself extraordinary, this triggered a rebellious mentality. The more good things he heard, the more annoyed he became, as if he had entered a rebellious phase.","Ye Lin believed he had seen a lot in the provinces. He felt Yue Fuguang's achievements were suspiciously obtained, convinced that the Yu family had orchestrated them. He thought she was merely a person fishing for fame and compliments, and that the folk rumors were largely fabricated.","As for the matter of the improved seeds, it must have been the Yu family's doing to create a god. Otherwise, how could a little girl who never left the house come into contact with such things?","It could be said that, according to common sense, Ye Lin wasn't entirely wrong. If it were a native young girl of this era, she indeed wouldn't have had the chance to access these things. But what he didn't know was that Yue Fuguang defied common sense—she had a cheat system!","\"Is he deliberately targeting me, or is he just straightforward?\"","[Master, this man looks down on all women. He has had a problem with you for a long time, thinking you are just fishing for fame. If this matter hadn't touched upon his interests, he wouldn't have chosen to jump out. So, the reason this selfish man chose to stand up and object at this time is also to back up his future father-in-law, Old Man Song.]","Yue Fuguang heard Wu Yong finish his sarcastic scolding and begin to enumerate her public achievements.","Treating her own great achievements as background noise, Yue Fuguang adopted the attitude of a spectator enjoying a show. Eating pastries and drinking tea, she asked the system, \"These two are father-in-law and son-in-law? Then it makes sense!\"","Little did she know that her dismissive attitude of casually eating and drinking deeply pierced Ye Lin's fragile and sensitive ego.","Yue Fuguang didn't know that when the system said Ye Lin was uncorrupted, it was true. It wasn't just a superficial act. This man was truly the hope of his entire village. Having tested out of a poor, backward village to become the only advanced scholar within a hundred miles, he naturally had his own pride and arrogance.","While serving in the provinces, he couldn't get along with colleagues from prominent families. It wasn't because he was overly upright; it was purely driven by a hatred of the rich.","He envied the privileged class. In his heart, he wanted to become someone who was supported by others, someone who could spend money like water and easily decide the fate of those at the bottom. However, because he wasn't one of them, he resented those who were.","Not only that, but he also couldn't get along with colleagues who, like him, came from humble, grassroots backgrounds. The root cause was that they had no foundation and couldn't provide him with any assistance. In his eyes, interacting with them was ineffective socialization.","After enduring for a dozen years, he eventually, by a twist of fate, made his way to the imperial court due to his reputation for poverty and filial piety. One could only say it was a matter of timing and destiny.","[Master, look, this Old Man Song is almost seventy years old, nearing the age of retirement. Despite his poor health, he clings to power and refuses to retire to his hometown, all for the sake of finding a successor.]","\"What do you mean by finding a successor? If I remember correctly, Song Nian holds the position of Director in the Ministry of Rites, responsible for the Department of Banquets, which is a fairly lucrative office. Is he treating the position as his family's property, even looking for a successor?\"","[Master has a good memory. Song Nian has worked in the position of Director for over a decade, and he actually inherited it from his former father-in-law. So he wants to imitate his father-in-law and pass this Director position to his own son-in-law.]","\"Why pass it to a son-in-law instead of a son? Is a son-in-law closer, or is this just their family tradition?\"","[Song Nian's old father-in-law had no biological sons, and the adopted youths from his clan were not cut out for studying. So, as he was about to retire, he promoted his son-in-law to the position of Director. He also hoped that Song Nian would treat his daughter better out of gratitude for the promotion. That happened back when Emperor Mingxi's father was on the throne.","Unfortunately, less than two years after the old father-in-law retired to his hometown, Song Nian's first wife passed away from illness. Following that, he elevated his current wife from a concubine to the main wife. That was during the time when the favored concubine and her son were fighting most fiercely against the Empress Dowager and her son.","Otherwise, he would never have dared to do such a thing during the Mingxi reign.","As for Song Nian, he doesn't lack sons. He has three sons in total. The eldest was born to his first wife. After she passed away, he sent this son far away to the provinces to serve as a minor official.","His second wife bore him two sons and two daughters. Neither of the sons is cut out for studying. The eldest took the exams for over twenty years before barely passing as a provincial graduate at the very bottom of the list.","He then took the metropolitan examination three consecutive times without passing. If nothing unexpected happens, Master might even run into the second Song son in the examination hall this time.","As for the third Song son, he is still only a junior scholar.","Therefore, Song Nian wanting to imitate his old father-in-law is similarly a move made out of helplessness. Of the two daughters born to his second wife, the eldest was widowed early on and wanted to remarry, but she never met a suitable match.","This was right until she encountered Ye Lin, who had been transferred back to the capital and also served in the Ministry of Rites.]","Ji Hongming and Zhang Zhongping both felt their faces burning. One was an executive of the Ministry of Personnel, in charge of the promotion and assessment of officials at all levels.","What happened during the tenures of his predecessor and the previous emperor had nothing to do with him, but now Song Nian's dangerous idea was inextricably linked to him.","As the Minister of Rites, Zhang Zhongping didn't even know he had such a person among his subordinates. Were Song Nian and Ye Lin trying to play tricks right under his nose, thinking he was a pushover?","\"Worthy of being from the Ministry of Rites, they all want to use rites to suppress me.\"","This remark made Zhang Zhongping instantly shrink three inches, wishing he could bury his head into his official robes.","\"Wait, isn't Ye Lin's wife still alive? Is Ye Lin trying to climb the social ladder by suspending his marriage to take a new wife? His wife has borne him two sons and three daughters, and she hasn't committed any faults. Surely his first move upon coming to the capital wouldn't be to get rid of his faithful wife?\"","There has never been a shortage of Chen Shimei (a heartless husband) throughout history. Let alone in ancient times, even in the modern era, once men became successful, weren't there many who first changed their cars and houses, and finally changed their wives? Even those who didn't change their wives kept their main household intact while maintaining affairs on the side.","Take her father, Yue Qi'an, for example. It was the system that told her he had illegitimate children outside, who would have the same inheritance rights as her in the future.","Yue Fuguang was surprisingly not that shocked when she heard the news back then.","Coming back to Ye Lin, if he wanted to divorce his wife, given the current social climate, people would only say he had character flaws and moral deficiencies, which would incur the displeasure of the Emperor and his colleagues and somewhat hinder his career, but it wouldn't affect his current official position.","[Master, Ye Lin has no intention of divorcing his wife. He wants to become a widower!]","A widower? This bastard really wants to murder his wife to remarry!","Yue Fuguang felt her fists clench, and her voice instantly dropped a few degrees. \"Little Zhu, Ye Lin can't possibly be unaware that the laws of Great Yan have been amended and that murdering one's wife is a major crime.\""]},{"number":405,"title":"Chapter 405: How about you say a few words, master","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang only found out during the Gao Ming case and numerous family disappearance cases that a husband killing his wife actually did not require him to pay with his life; at most, he would be sentenced to exile.","If the wife's family forgave his actions, he could even be acquitted and released just by paying a certain amount of compensation.","When she learned of this news back then, a million curses raced through her mind.","If Gao Ming had not been involved in a court case and the crime of murdering a fellow student, his mere act of killing his wife would have at most cost him his official position. It would not have affected him being a free man. It was simply too outrageous.","Therefore, this was the first Great Yan law that Yue Fuguang urged Emperor Mingxi and his ministers to amend after she arrived in Great Yan.","[Master, Ye Lin naturally took this into consideration, so his plan is to let his own wife die of illness.","Madam Lin came from the south and was unaccustomed to the local environment. Unable to adapt to the climate of the capital city, she fell ill shortly after arriving. Now, because Madam Lin has been taking medicine spiked by Ye Lin for a long time, she is so severely ill that she cannot even get out of bed to manage household affairs.]","\"Did Madam Lin not realize there was a problem with her medicine?\" As long as this Madam Lin was not a fool, her condition worsening the more medicine she took, combined with the fact that it was not a terminal illness, would make anyone with a bit of sense suspect that the medicine was wrong for the disease.","[She naturally suspected it and even changed doctors because of it. Unfortunately, she did not know that while the first doctor was fine, the newly replaced one had close ties with the Song family.","Regarding his wife's doubts, Ye Lin dismissed them all by saying that years of hard work had caused her to accumulate illness from overwork. This sickness had weakened her body, bringing out all the old root causes of her ailments.]","Glancing at Song Nian and Ye Lin, who were still kneeling on the ground, self-righteously advising the emperor to retract his orders, Yue Fuguang's lips curled into a wicked little smile. \"System, open the inner voice channel to Song Nian and Ye Lin.\"","Destroying a person's mind before taking their life was the highest realm of revenge.","\"Little Zhu, Song Nian is in such a hurry to stop the emperor from asking for my opinion. Could there be another reason behind this?","And the doctor who treated Madam Lin, was he instructed by Song Nian?\"","[Master, the way Song Nian's late wife died is exactly how Madam Lin will die in the future.","After Old Man Song set his sights on Ye Lin as his son-in-law, he used the convenience of his position to transfer Ye Lin to work under him. After a few interactions, Ye Lin also grasped Song Nian's intentions.","Even the idea of his wife dying from illness was the safest, side-effect-free path to becoming a widower that Ye Lin came up with after Song Nian's subtle hints.","That doctor is a nephew from Song Nian's clan. Song Nian's deceased wife had once sought medical treatment from his father. This person was his father's medicine boy at the time, so he is very familiar with the whole process.]","Beep beep! Gasp gasp!","Beep!","Hearing this, Song Nian, who had been impassioned and ready to die for his remonstration, began trembling like a leaf. Then, his face turned crimson as if something was strangling his throat, and he could only make gasping sounds.","Ye Lin, with an even paler face, looked at Yue Fuguang in terror. He opened his mouth, but apart from his face flushing red, the words he wanted to say to defend himself all turned into beeping sounds. When he tried to speak further, it felt as if he was being choked, unable to utter a sound, accompanied by a feeling of impending death.","Yue Fuguang coldly swept her gaze over Ye Lin, who was already prostrating on the ground, continuously kowtowing with loud thuds. \"Little Zhu, what is wrong with this Ye Lin? The emperor only asked one question, and I have not even said anything yet. Why is his reaction so extreme?","Is this how remonstrations are popularly done in the Great Yan court nowadays?\"","[How about you say a few words, Master?]","Yue Fuguang readily agreed, \"Since Your Majesty has asked for my recommendation for the chief examiner, I shall speak my mind. However...\" Her gaze fell on Song Nian and Ye Lin, who looked defeated and dared not raise their heads.","\"Lord Song and this Lord Ye seem to have a great deal of objection to this Junior Preceptor. Serving in the same court makes us colleagues. Must one's age and background be debated before expressing an opinion in this imperial court?\"","Yue Fuguang's gaze swept across all the civil and military officials in the grand hall, an innocent smile hanging on her lips. \"In this court, who is allowed to speak and who should shut their mouths? Why don't you two lords teach me?\"","\"This... this humble official wouldn't dare!\" Ye Lin was young after all, his wife was still alive, and his grave mistake had not yet been finalized. He quickly adjusted his mindset and prostrated himself on the ground before Yue Fuguang. \"Just now... this humble official was reckless. Please forgive me, Lord Junior Preceptor!\"","Keeping his head down, ignoring the sweat blurring his eyes, he continued respectfully, \"This humble official has only been in the capital for a short time. Having just heard Lord Wu's account, I now know that with Lord Junior Preceptor's contributions to the nation and esteemed status, you are naturally more than qualified for the position of deputy chief examiner for the metropolitan examination.\"","He then bowed deeply to Emperor Mingxi. \"This humble minister has presumptuously criticized Lord Junior Preceptor, which is a great disrespect. I beg Your Majesty to punish me!\"","He is trying to sever his tail to survive! Yue Fuguang sneered inwardly. This Ye Lin was quick to adapt; he turned back before hitting the south wall. What a spineless coward.","Emperor Mingxi's gaze was cold. When he looked at Song Nian and Ye Lin, it was as if he were looking at filth. His majestic and stern voice echoed in the hall. \"Ye Lin, for presumptuously criticizing a key minister of the court, you are demoted by one rank, your salary is docked for two years, and you are to reflect on your mistakes behind closed doors for three months. You are not to leave your residence without a summons.\"","\"This humble minister Ye Lin accepts the decree!\" Ye Lin prostrated on the ground, his body trembling.","[Master, the reason this Song Nian was in such a hurry to object is that he accepted bribes from others and wanted to tamper with the candidates in this metropolitan examination. He was afraid that the person you chose would be too formidable and difficult to deal with.]","Thump!","Song Nian was old after all. Hearing his beheading-worthy secret exposed, he was directly scared into a faint.","His head hit the golden bricks, making a loud thump.","'Why did this person suddenly faint?'","[Maybe he's too old and lacks physical strength?]","'Tampering with the metropolitan examination... With his body that's practically half in the grave, why would he do something that could lead to his execution and the extermination of his entire clan?'","[Because someone offered too much. To ensure his descendants could enjoy a lifetime of wealth and glory, Song Nian was willing to risk the crime of beheading.","Song Nian knows that the two sons of the Song family in this generation have no hope in the imperial examinations. He wants his second son to become a Jinshi, so he can only take crooked paths.","Although Song Nian has already planned to pass his position to Ye Lin, he is not at ease.","First, the court laws today are much stricter than during the late emperor's reign. Whether he can ultimately succeed depends on the Ministry of Personnel and the Emperor.","It's easy to say, but the actual operation is no longer as simple as it was over a decade ago.","Second, he doesn't fully trust a man who would kill his wife and remarry just to climb the social ladder. He doubts Ye Lin would take good care of his two brothers-in-law in the future.","He himself is a prime example. As a person of the same kind, Song Nian doesn't trust Ye Lin much either.]","Ye Lin, who had just been punished by Emperor Mingxi in court, was now hiding in the back, shivering. Imperial examination fraud was a crime far more severe than murdering one's wife. He had almost been implicated in this matter. If that had happened, it would truly be a capital offense from which he could not escape!","Meanwhile, the unconscious Song Nian remained restless even in his faint. His forehead was slick with cold sweat, likely plagued by nightmares of impending doom.","\"Another imperial examination scandal?\" Yue Fuguang instantly felt the plum blossom pastry in her hand lose its appeal. \"The blood spilled in the sixth year of Yuankang has yet to completely dry. How could anyone still dare to take such a risk?\"","She tossed the pale pink pastry onto the lotus-shaped white jade plate. The faint pink hue of the sweet before her eyes looked just like the last smear of crimson that had stained the spring snow during that year's examinations."]},{"number":406,"title":"Chapter 406: Spring Imperial Examinations","paragraphs":["No, the noble families haven't figured it out yet. It's not suitable for anyone else to die for the time being!","Someone else is courting death again. Do I still have to be this annoying deputy chief examiner? Just thinking about it makes me feel like it's a huge hassle!","And the thing a slacker like her feared most was trouble.","[How about you appoint someone capable and with enough status to suppress the situation as the chief examiner, Master? You came up with the newly added mathematics questions this year. Don't you want to see how the candidates answer them as soon as possible?]","Hearing that someone was pulling little tricks again in this year's spring examination, many officials who originally wanted to compete for a position in the examination hall couldn't help but shrink back.","As much as they previously hoped to be noticed by Yue Fuguang and the Emperor, they now hoped just as much to be treated as invisible by these two.","In cases of imperial examination fraud, if things went south, not only would one lose their own life, but their entire family would suffer along with them.","However, some people were not afraid. Since they knew about this in advance and the Junior Preceptor was involved, there was truly nothing to worry about.","Yue Fuguang scanned the officials below once more. Seeing those who were cowering, she directly skipped over them; she was unwilling to use people who could not shoulder heavy responsibilities.","Finally, her gaze landed on the Crown Prince, who was standing straight. The Crown Prince also felt her gaze and returned a smile.","Having married and become a father, the Crown Prince had indeed matured a lot over the past two years. He was diligent and steady in his work, and his status was sufficient. She hoped that those people, seeing that the two of them were joining forces, would rein in their horses at the edge of the cliff and stop in time.","At this moment in the capital city of Shangjing, they really didn't need a few more heads rolling!","Yue Fuguang made up her mind, smiled, and pointed at the Crown Prince, saying, Your Majesty, how about choosing the Crown Prince as the chief examiner?","[Capable and obedient, the Crown Prince is indeed a good choice. Even if someone really tries to cheat in the examination, with the two of you there, you can crush them on the spot.]","The fairness of the imperial examination cannot be broken by anyone, otherwise, even the most stable dynasty will be finished.","Emperor Mingxi and his son looked at each other, both feeling that the two ancestors were absolutely right. If this court were filled entirely with nobles from aristocratic families and hereditary officials, the Xie family's throne would be neither stable nor long-lasting.","What did an emperor who loved playing the game of balance fear the most?","Factionalism!","Hearing Yue Fuguang's suggestion, Emperor Mingxi nodded without much hesitation and said, The Crown Prince is indeed a good choice.","As for the list he had previously chosen but hadn't yet had Eunuch Qian announce on the spot, Emperor Mingxi chose to ignore it.","Moreover, choosing Yue Fuguang as the deputy chief examiner for this metropolitan examination was something Emperor Mingxi had carefully considered. Not to mention that the mathematics questions in this exam were all created by Yue Fuguang.","There was also the popular support she had accumulated among the common people due to high-yield seeds and agricultural tools, as well as the prestige she had built among scholars and students due to her early children's enlightenment books, the schools she had promoted for nearly two years, and her recent poetry.","Her serving as the deputy chief examiner was inherently indisputable. As for Song Nian and Ye Lin, Emperor Mingxi selectively ignored them.","The metropolitan examination would begin on the ninth day of the second lunar month and last for nine consecutive days. During these days, Yue Fuguang could not leave the examination hall. This amount of time was enough for Emperor Mingxi to completely clean up the remnants of the noble families, without a single drop of blood splashing onto Yue Fuguang.","As for the doubts among the common people regarding the Divine Maiden due to the drought, Emperor Mingxi narrowed his eyes. Once he dealt with the noble families, these voices would naturally fade away.","By the time the grand court assembly ended, the entire leadership team for the metropolitan examination in the early spring of the eighth year of Yuankang had been finalized.","Even Wu Yong was requested by Yue Fuguang to serve as the sealing officer.","On the ninth day of the second month of the eighth year of Yuankang, before the east was bright, Yue Fuguang was woken up in the middle of the night. Since coming to the Great Yan dynasty, this was the earliest she had ever gotten up, aside from the time she fled the Zhou family in the dark of night.","The carriage drove smoothly on the cement streets. Over the past two years, the major streets and minor alleys of Shangjing City had gradually been paved with cement roads.","Just because people no longer had to step into mud on rainy days, Yue Fuguang's reputation among the citizens of Shangjing City could not possibly be bad.","The night breeze blew past the copper bells on the carriage, producing a clear and pleasant ringing sound that echoed far away down the empty streets.","It even attracted a squad from the Night Patrol Division. Once they clearly saw the insignia on the carriage, they silently and orderly bowed in salute and stood respectfully on both sides.","Only after the carriage had gone far away did a young soldier crane his neck, looking at the carriage that was now just a speck of light, and asked his captain, Boss, was the person sitting in the carriage that just passed really our Junior Preceptor?","The middle-aged man addressed as boss smoothed out his lapels, which had been wrinkled from tension just now, his tone full of certainty. How could it be fake? The Junior Preceptor's carriage is built to the specifications of a Prince of the Blood. Who else but that esteemed lord would dare to ride in it?","He glanced at the childish-looking rookie. What, why are you asking so clearly? What are you planning?","The night patrol captain immediately became alert. Having caught many spies and been repeatedly educated by his superiors in various classes, he now pondered over the slightest anomaly, feeling that everyone was suspicious!","Seeing his boss's face suddenly turn a bit fierce, the young soldier waved his hands repeatedly, denying it with a triple negation: No, no, no, I don't, I'm not, Boss, you've misunderstood!","He rubbed his head in embarrassment and said, Before coming to our Night Patrol Division, I went to test for the Yue Army, hehehe, but unfortunately, my physical fitness didn't meet the standards.","A hint of frustration showed on his face. Let me eat well for another year, build up my strength, and then I'll go again!","The captain was a bit speechless. It turned out his division was just someone's fallback option! Their Night Patrol Division was basically raising and training soldiers for someone else! However, if that someone else was the Junior Preceptor, it wasn't unacceptable.","The captain forcefully patted the young soldier's thin shoulder and said, Then you must eat well and train hard. The Yue Army is entirely made up of elites.","The young soldier nodded vigorously, jogging to keep up with the team while saying, Our whole family is especially grateful to the Junior Preceptor. Last year, our family bought land confiscated from the aristocratic families and planted sweet potatoes and potatoes.","My younger brother and sister are eight years old and attend the enlightenment school run by the Junior Preceptor. My older sister and I also went to night school last year to learn how to read. Over the past two years, the Yue Army's recruitment required all applicants to know at least a few words.","Next came the sound of the young soldier reciting, Heaven and earth, dark and yellow, the universe, vast and desolate...","Yue Fuguang had no idea about what was happening behind her. Her carriage had already arrived at the gates of the examination compound.","Unlike other places that were still slumbering, this place had long since awakened. It was brightly lit everywhere, bubbling with a cacophony of voices.","She looked out through the gauze curtains; the parents, relatives, and friends sending off the examinees were even more numerous and nervous than the candidates themselves.","This couldn't help but remind Yue Fuguang of when she took the college entrance exam. Her parents were absent, and only a butler had escorted her to the testing center.","What was her mood at the time... It seemed too long ago, and she couldn't quite recall it for a moment. She only vaguely remembered watching from the car for a long time as other parents fussed over their children's comfort. For her, that was not a pleasant memory.","It was at this moment that Yue Fuguang suddenly realized she hadn't thought about her past life in a very long time, and her memories of the past were growing increasingly blurry.","As Yue Fuguang's carriage drove in, the two heavy, vermilion-lacquered doors of the examination compound slowly opened in the dark like the maw of a mythical beast, revealing the seemingly endless green-grey corridor hidden within the night."]},{"number":407,"title":"Chapter 407: Cheating with Crib Notes Harms Others","paragraphs":["The door hinges creaked with a long, dull sound, as if grinding across the hearts of every provincial candidate approaching the main gate.","They watched as Yue Fuguang's carriage passed smoothly, as if entering an uninhabited land. The sharp-eyed ones even noticed that the imposing soldiers on both sides stopped their work, involuntarily standing tall and solemn as the carriage went by.","\"Brother Wang, do you know which official just passed by?\" A candidate from out of town gazed at the departing exquisite carriage and its disciplined escort, full of admiration. Such grandeur was surely reserved only for the purple-robed officials in the imperial court.","The local candidate addressed as Brother Wang revealed a mysterious smile. \"That one? If I tell you, you've definitely heard of her...\"","Yue Fuguang's carriage had already arrived at the Zhigong Hall.","She stepped down from the carriage and headed straight for the outer curtain of the Zhigong Hall. Above the lintel of the outer curtain were four gilded characters reading \"Seeking Talent for the Nation.\" The calligraphy was vigorous and powerful, harboring a hidden strength, and gleamed with a cold, hard luster in the faint light of the lanterns hanging from the eaves.","Inside the Zhigong Hall at this moment, aside from Yue Fuguang, all the officials—including the Crown Prince, who was the chief examiner—had moved in the previous night.","No sooner had Yue Fuguang set foot inside the Zhigong Hall than the courtyard was locked behind her, a gesture to demonstrate fairness and impartiality.","Seeing the busy chief examiner and co-examiners, Yue Fuguang greeted them and then found a place to drink tea and rest. After all, she was just a mascot brought in to hold the fort; unless something major happened, no one would bother her.","\"Little Zhu, I'm so bored, and I can't sleep. I want to see what's happening outside.\"","Didn't they say someone wanted to cheat? It was the perfect opportunity for her to see if the examination searches of these ancients were as strict as those back home.","She also wanted to see how these predecessors managed to smuggle in cheat sheets.","\"Master, it's very lively outside!\" The system's cheerful voice rang out, showing that its attention had been entirely focused outside all this time.","Hmph! Yue Fuguang snorted softly. This guy was secretly watching the fun all by itself and didn't even think to call her!","Hearing Yue Fuguang's soft snort, the system silently hugged itself, and a live broadcast screen quickly opened.","From the live stream, one could see the thousands of people at the gate displaying a myriad of attitudes.","The few people at the very front were all top scorers from their respective provinces. Dressed in neat green robes, their backs were as straight as pines, and their faces were filled with pride.","Since they were all top scorers, it was inevitable that they would secretly compete and compare themselves with one another, both openly and covertly. Even through the live stream, Yue Fuguang could feel that this was quite a dramatic scene.","One top scorer, about thirty years old with a slightly dark complexion and a short beard, held his examination basket steadily in both hands, though his knuckles were slightly white from the force.","He did not look left or right, only gazing deeply at the dark outer gate. His lips moved silently, as if he were reciting the writings of the sages.","It was a deliberately maintained calmness, like a fully drawn bow, storing immense power within.","Beside him was a young candidate in his twenties, fair-faced and beardless, with bright eyes. Even the slightly worn coarse green robe he wore gave off a handsome and free-spirited vibe.","It had to be said that a successful candidate in his twenties indeed had the foundation to be proud. Among all the top scorers, he and the candidate next to him were the youngest.","However, although that other person also wore a green robe, one could tell from the fabric that he came from a wealthy family. The noble air about him and the unconscious sense of superiority in his every movement made the others instinctively more polite and distant when speaking to him.","\"Does Master see any talents you fancy?\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. She hadn't had time to check their backgrounds yet, so naturally, she wouldn't blindly select talents based solely on first impressions.","She wasn't very confident in her ability to judge people. Once everyone entered the examination hall and she activated her merit detection, it would be a different story.","Yue Fuguang's perspective shifted backward with the live stream. Behind the top scorers were the ordinary candidates from various provinces and prefectures.","Yue Fuguang noticed a middle-aged candidate whose short beard was already showing signs of gray. His brow was furrowed with deep lines carved by years of hard study. He repeatedly touched the inkstone and brushes in his examination basket, his movements almost devout, as if these items were magical artifacts to calm his mind.","A gust of morning wind swept by, fluttering the hem of his washed-out robe. He suddenly trembled, vigilantly guarding his basket, and looked around. Seeing nothing unusual, he let out a long breath of white mist, which lingered in the cold night air for a long time.","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. This was definitely not his first time participating in the spring examination. Judging by his behavior, he had probably been harmed by someone before, or had seen someone else harmed.","Indeed, one could never be too careful. It was entirely possible that there were people with crooked intentions here who wanted to eliminate dissidents and reduce the competition by slipping cheat sheets into other candidates' baskets. Honestly, as long as one was quick and secretive enough, it was a highly effective tactic.","\"Little Zhu, keep an eye out. Don't let people with ulterior motives smuggle in cheat sheets to frame others.\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's words, Xie Zhiyan, who had finally found a moment to drink a cup of tea amidst his busyness, immediately looked up nervously at the live broadcast screen.","It wasn't as if he hadn't heard of such situations. When his imperial father first ascended the throne, during one year's metropolitan examination, a candidate was found with a smuggled cheat sheet and flatly denied that the item belonged to him.","Later, upon investigation, it was proven that he had indeed been intentionally framed, simply because he was quite talented and had a good chance of passing.","In the live stream, there were young candidates whose faces still bore traces of childishness, yet two clusters of fire burned in their eyes. Impatient with waiting, they stood on their tiptoes and craned their necks, wishing they could immediately throw themselves into the battlefield that would decide their fate.","One person accidentally stepped on someone else's black boots and hurriedly bowed, muttering excuses non-stop, while fine sweat beaded on his forehead, whether from anxiety or shame, it was hard to tell.","In a corner, an elderly candidate stood out conspicuously. His hair was already gray, his back slightly hunched, and he was supported by a young servant. His frail, thin hands tightly gripped a polished bamboo cane, his knuckles as rugged as old tree roots.","He didn't look at the gate or the people; his cloudy eyes only stared blankly at the fading stars in the sky. He muttered to himself, and it was unclear whether he was praying or lamenting how many times he had already stepped through this gate.","Years and disappointments weighed heavily on his shoulders. Before Yue Fuguang could even sigh over this man's persistence and dedication to official rank, she heard the system suddenly exclaim in excitement, \"Master, I've found something!\"","\"Little Zhu, where?\"","As soon as Yue Fuguang spoke, the system immediately marked the problematic individuals with red and green colors above their heads.","The red boxes glowing like traffic lights shone onto the faces of those few people, making them look as if they were about to suffer a bloody disaster. Inside the boxes were several large white characters reading, I am a bad person, I use cheat sheets to frame my fellow candidates.","Meanwhile, the few marked in green had bright, striking green glowing above their heads. There were also words inside the green boxes, but this time they read, Someone is framing me, there is a cheat sheet in my examination basket.","Seeing this scene, Yue Fuguang almost laughed out loud but managed to cover her upward-curving lips in time by taking a sip of tea.","She really wanted to remind the system: did you even ask for their permission before making their heads glow bright green?","However, what she actually said was, \"So these three in red stuffed cheat sheets into the baskets of these ones in green?\"","Yue Fuguang looked closely and realized that among these little green men was that extremely cautious middle-aged man who clearly had a story."]},{"number":408,"title":"Chapter 408: Have You Found the Talent You're Interested In","paragraphs":["When she first saw this person just now, what caught her attention was the dark cloud over his glabella. She originally thought it foretold his failure in the examination, but she didn't expect it to be the disaster of being framed for cheating.","If he hadn't met her, this dark omen hinting at a bloody disaster would have come true this morning.","At the juncture of the Yin and Mao hours, thump, thump, thump! Three muffled drumbeats sounded. As the beats faded, a loud voice echoed through the grounds: \"The inspection begins!\"","Like ice water poured into a boiling oil pot, the crowd instantly surged.","The candidates lined up to step forward. The officials, dressed in ink-black robes with faces as calm as still water, carried out the strict and meticulous inspection procedures.","The process was swift and practiced. They rummaged through the examination baskets, shook out the bedding, and even spared no detail like hairbuns, clothing seams, and shoe soles.","Yue Fuguang could tell just by looking at their proficiency that these men were all veterans.","A plump candidate, upon having the tiny cheat sheet hidden in his robes discovered, instantly turned ashen. His legs gave way, and he nearly collapsed to the ground. He was dragged away expressionlessly by two soldiers, his sleeves trailing through the dust, leaving two deep marks.","His desperate whimpers were short and shrill, soon swallowed by an even greater silence. Ever since one person was caught carrying a cheat sheet, the atmosphere in the line suddenly became stagnant.","The surrounding candidates were all awe-struck, lowering their heads to double-check themselves. A thicker tension spread through the air, mixed with the smell of sweat and ink.","As the inspections continued, small white paper wads sporadically appeared on the ground; some belonged to the candidates themselves, while others had been forcibly stuffed onto them by someone else.","Yue Fuguang stared at those little green figures, watching to see if they could successfully save themselves. If they truly couldn't, she would then have the system intervene.","Out of the five people who had cheat sheets planted on them, only one ultimately discovered the sheet in his basket—the middle-aged man who was cautious to the point of being neurotic.","After such a fright, his already nervous state of mind became taut like a bowstring. If things went wrong, this string of his might snap before the exam even ended.","Considering it was not easy for them to study hard for years in poverty, and seeing that this man's family background appeared quite ordinary, Yue Fuguang said, \"Little Zhu, give that He Pingshan a Calming Pill. Then, take the cheat sheets from the baskets of the other four and put them into the baskets of the other three culprits.\"","There was no revenge more satisfying and immediate than instant karmic retribution.","As for those four, they were quite foolish as well. Being completely unaware of the planted cheat sheets was one thing, but during the self-check, perhaps out of overconfidence, they just went through the motions, never once thinking someone might scheme against them.","Seeing Yue Fuguang easily resolve the issue, the Crown Prince raised his hand to dismiss his attendants. If his people were to step forward in such a setting, without evidence, the most they could do was warn the victims; they really had no immediate way to deal with the three perpetrators.","The candidates were like prisoners in their narrow spaces. Some immediately organized their brushes and ink, keeping everything in perfect order. Some slumped down for a moment, closing their eyes to regulate their breathing. Others, as soon as they sat down, couldn't help but crane their necks to peek at their neighbors, their eyes darting around.","Exactly at the Chen hour, a deafening strike of the cloud board echoed through the sky above the examination compound.","The lingering sound collided and reverberated through the solemn alleys, lasting for a long time.","The previously somewhat noisy examination hall suddenly plunged into dead silence. Even the trembling sound of the early spring morning breeze blowing through the treetops and the distant noises of the town seemed to be sucked away by the sound of the cloud board.","All the candidates, regardless of their previous demeanors, froze like clay figures and wooden sculptures at this moment.","The next moment, almost simultaneously, countless hands fiercely tore open the examination paper bags on their small desks.","Clang! A soft rustling sound of paper unfolding could be heard, subtle yet unconsciously provoking people's nerves.","Some looked at the exam questions as if holding a sacred text, staring straight ahead; others had solemn gazes, unable to lower their brush-holding hands, as if the hollow bamboo tubes weighed a thousand pounds.","Yue Fuguang then saw the oldest candidate in the entire hall. He squinted his eyes and pushed the exam paper toward the daylight. Once he saw the questions clearly, his hands trembled so violently that he could barely hold the paper.","A faint light suddenly flashed in his cloudy eyes, only to be extinguished in the deep pools immediately after.","The examination cells in the compound were densely arranged like a honeycomb, so narrow they could barely fit a person.","Yue Fuguang, along with the Crown Prince, the associate examiners, and a group of other officials, stood on the attic looking down. In their eyes were hundreds of wolf-hair brushes dipping simultaneously into inkstones, and in their ears was the rustling sound of ink being dipped, like spring silkworms devouring leaves, or like a dense, urgent rain.","The scent of ink wafting to their noses was mixed with the years-old musty and dusty smells of the examination cells.","The thought of being forced to smell the body odor emanating from the candidates and the stench near the latrine cells in two or three days made her face involuntarily scrunch up.","Her voice suddenly became extremely gloomy, \"Little Zhu, am I regretting becoming this associate examiner?\"","[Master, what's wrong? Why do you say that!]","Its host was just very happy watching those three reap what they sowed, crying out in terror as they were dragged away by the runners. How could she regret it after only a short while?","Xie Zhiyan and the other officials standing next to her couldn't help but feel nervous. What if the Junior Preceptor demanded that they open the compound gates for her to leave? Should they agree, or should they agree!","Although the current dynasty was not as draconian as the previous one—records from the previous dynasty told of a tragedy where the examination compound caught fire, and for the sake of fairness, the gates remained shut even as candidates burned to death.","However, the Great Yan Dynasty still had rules stating that the gates could not be opened unless the lives of the majority were at stake.","If the exception was the Junior Preceptor, they wouldn't really need to worry about anyone taking the opportunity to cheat. After all, playing tricks in front of her was like delivering one's head to the King of Hell.","Yue Fuguang was of course just talking. She wasn't capricious enough to touch upon laws and bottom lines just because of a minor personal preference.","\"Just thinking about the smells that will be here over the next few days makes me uncomfortable.\"","[Master, how about I open a protective shield for you, or you turn off your sense of smell?]","\"That's the only way!\" Turning off her sense of smell was a good idea. As for opening a protective shield, Yue Fuguang was reluctant to consume her points and energy.","[Does Master have any talents in mind? You are, after all, selecting talents for the imperial court now. Why not take this opportunity to pick a few useful people.]","Xie Zhiyan nodded. If the talents chosen by the Junior Preceptor now could grow and develop, they would be enough to serve both him and his imperial father across two generations of monarchs.","Yue Fuguang's gaze swept over the rows of examination cells, landing on candidates who were either writing furiously or frowning in deep thought. Her voice carried obvious disgust, \"This Chen Tang relied entirely on his wife's dowry to fund his exams all the way here, yet he plans to divorce her and marry a noble lady from a high-ranking family once he passes and becomes a Jinshi.","Then there's Li Youshan. His parents, brother, and sister-in-law used the entire family's strength to support his studies. He eats their food and drinks their water, yet despises their low birth, refusing to acknowledge them and complaining that he doesn't have a high-ranking official for a father.","And that Huang Youfeng, his family has quite a bit of wealth, but this guy dabbles in gluttony, drinking, whoring, and gambling.\"","She looked at his answers and shook her head. His body had been hollowed out by wine and women. He indeed had a reputation for talent in his youth, but unfortunately, he was a fallen prodigy. In this spring examination, he was just making up the numbers; he definitely wouldn't pass.","The chief examiner, the Crown Prince, and the associate examiners Ling Yinghua, Ji Hongming, and the others all frowned upon hearing this. They didn't really want to employ people with flawed personal morals either.","Yue Fuguang then went on to critique several renowned scholars one by one. There were those with noble character, those with empty reputations, those who were only suited for academia but not for officialdom, and those with good abilities but slightly lacking in literary talent."]},{"number":409,"title":"Chapter 409: Opium Paste","paragraphs":["[Master, that Gao Zifang is Gao Ziyou's cousin. Although he lacks somewhat in academic knowledge, his practical working abilities are quite excellent. If he fails the exam this time, you could pick up a bargain and send him to your fiefdom to benefit the local area.]","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"It just so happens that Gao Ziyou is the magistrate in Sanchadi. Sending him over to keep him company would be perfect.\"","Hearing the words \"pick up a bargain,\" the Crown Prince's mouth twitched involuntarily. That Gao Ziyou was a classmate and good friend of Bao Zihui. He still remembered hearing the Junior Preceptor mention on Bao Zihui's wedding day that Gao Ziyou was a talent in agriculture.","Since his cousin was also a talent, even if he failed the exam, he couldn't be wasted. He had to be brought in to serve the country. The Hongnong Temple would be very suitable for him.","Thinking of this, the Crown Prince hoped even more that since these two ancestors knew so much, they would say a bit more. All talents must be drawn into the imperial fold.","[Master, look at the one named Wu Chengbin in the Bingzi cell.]","From where Yue Fuguang and the others were standing, they actually couldn't see the Bingzi cell, so the system directly played a live video feed for her.","In the video, the exam candidate the system called Wu Chengbin was about thirty years old. He had a square face with a short beard, and his complexion was pale and emaciated. Although he was sitting, Yue Fuguang felt that he couldn't be very tall.","At this moment, he was holding a steamed bun filled with a dark red paste in one hand while reviewing the exam paper he had just completed.","Was he just eating breakfast?","\"Little Zhu, what's wrong with this person? He looks a bit frail. I just wonder if he can survive the imperial examination.\"","[Master, look at the food in Wu Chengbin's hand. That is not date paste or red bean paste.]","The system's voice suddenly became a bit eerie. [Master, guess what's added inside?]","Hearing the system say this, Yue Fuguang half-tilted her head and looked at Wu Chengbin's hand in the video. Though it was called a filled steamed bun, it had actually been cut into small pieces by the inspectors upon entry. The white bun was sticky with the dark red filling. At first glance, it looked like red bean or date paste, but upon closer inspection, it resembled neither.","\"Little Zhu, is it really not date paste?\" Yue Fuguang thought about it and felt that it looked most like date paste.","[Master, the date paste filling has been spiked. Do you remember opium paste?]","Reminded by the system, Yue Fuguang actually recalled that stuff.","She was born in a peaceful era and had never seen the real thing, but she had watched many movies and TV shows. The props were made so realistically, and it looked exactly like what Wu Chengbin was holding!","Yue Fuguang's face immediately turned ashen. Seeing her sudden change in expression, the Crown Prince and the others didn't quite understand what this opium paste was to make this ancestor so angry.","At this moment, Yue Fuguang and the system, who were dropping these bombshells, forgot to educate the people of the Great Yan Dynasty. Although they had exposed the dangers of poppies as early as the fourth year of Yuankang, and the Great Yan Dynasty had strictly forbidden their cultivation and trade, the Crown Prince and the others did not know about the finished poppy product, also known as opium paste.","Because there had indeed been no trace of poppies in Great Yan over the years, Yue Fuguang had forgotten to bring it up again.","\"Little Zhu, does this Wu Chengbin know that his food is mixed with opium paste?\" One must know that opium is usually smoked. If he ate it directly, wouldn't it kill him? Who knows how long he had been doing this. To still be alive, he sure was tough.","However, when Yue Fuguang saw Wu Chengbin pick out the reddish-brown filling from his hand and throw it into the small burning stove next to his desk, curling blue smoke rose, and his originally sluggish spirit improved significantly. What else was there not to understand?","[Master, Wu Chengbin likely noticed something was wrong with his body, but he didn't know where the problem lay. The person trying to harm him knows his habits very well. Knowing he dislikes sweets, especially dates, they deliberately gave him date paste cakes and date paste buns. Every time, Wu Chengbin couldn't refuse their goodwill and couldn't bear to waste food, so he always ate the outer layer and threw the sweet filling into the fire to burn. That person calculated exactly this, which is why they only started providing him with this food at the beginning of winter.]","\"Didn't the Emperor order a ban on any poppies within the borders of Great Yan? How can there still be opium paste? Could it be Nanzhao playing tricks behind the scenes again!\"","Princess Lan Xuan'er of Nanzhao was still in Great Yan and hadn't returned to her country. She wondered if this matter had anything to do with her.","[Master, after these years of prohibition in Great Yan, it is indeed hard to find traces of poppies. But whether officials or commoners in Great Yan, their understanding of poppies is pitifully little. Go ask the Crown Prince, he probably doesn't even know what opium paste is or what it looks like.]","The Crown Prince: Wasn't that the truth? He had seen poppy flowers and poppy pods, but he had truly never heard of or seen this so-called opium paste made from them.","Yue Fuguang was a bit tired from standing. She turned and sat back in her chair, picked up a piece of date paste cake, took a bite, and asked Xie Zhiyan, who was holding a cup and sipping tea, seemingly casually, \"Crown Prince, have you ever seen opium paste?\"","She broke the pastry in her hand, revealing the filling inside. \"I just realized that the filling in this cake looks quite a bit like that stuff.\"","The Crown Prince seemed interested. Out of curiosity, he also picked up a date paste pastry and broke it open to inspect it.","He looked at it for a long time before shaking his head. \"Little Aunt, what is opium paste? Does it look like this date paste? Is it also something to eat?\"","Xie Zhiyan asked three questions in one breath, his eyes full of curiosity and a thirst for knowledge. He even deliberately and unconsciously swallowed his saliva.","Watching him made Yue Fuguang shake her head, the word drama queen almost slipping from her lips.","The acting desire and skills of the monarch and officials of the Great Yan Dynasty were improving day by day. She didn't know if they were afraid that Yue Fuguang was getting older and harder to fool, or if their skills had grown after years of refinement. Anyway, everyone's attention to detail in front of her was maxed out. If she didn't know the inside story, with her intelligence and experience, she would truly be kept completely in the dark.","Yue Fuguang sighed inwardly that only her own acting skills remained the same after ten years, while everyone else's growth left her behind.","At the same time, she shook her head to enlighten Xie Zhiyan. \"This opium paste is not a good thing, and of course, it cannot be eaten.\"","She tossed the date paste cake back onto the porcelain plate. \"Does the Crown Prince still remember the poppy, also known as the imperial rice? Opium paste is a poison made from that stuff. Smoking it is much more harmful than the meat dishes spiked with poppy shells at the Zuilai Restaurant back then.\"","Xie Zhiyan's face was full of shock, as if he had just learned about this. Seeing the worry on Yue Fuguang's face, he lowered his eyes and said, \"Fortunately, Little Aunt warned us in time back then, preventing poppies from spreading in Great Yan.\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"I didn't detail the dangers of poppies back then, nor did I explain the harm of turning it into opium paste. This stuff also has another name, opium.","The severe harm of smoking opium is not just causing addiction, organ damage, and a weakened body prone to illnesses that are hard to cure, but it also makes one's temper irritable and anxious.\""]},{"number":410,"title":"Chapter 410: True Purpose","paragraphs":["\"Once these people become addicted, no amount of family wealth can withstand their consumption. Some would even sell their land, houses, and even their own sons and daughters just for a single puff, resulting in broken families and separated spouses. They are one of the most unstable factors in society.\"","\"Not only do the bodies of such people weaken day by day, making them unable to do heavy labor, but from then on, their minds are filled with nothing but opium.","Because they are addicted, they turn into evil spirits if they don't smoke it. Therefore, to get this substance, they will even lose their basic moral bottom line as human beings. If this were to spread to the army...\"","Yue Fuguang did not continue, because upon hearing these dangers, Xie Zhiyan's face had already turned somewhat pale. Not only was he imagining what would happen if soldiers and officials smoked this substance, but he also realized that this thing had not been eradicated in Great Yan as he had thought.","Xie Zhiyan gazed in the direction of Room Bingzi, lost in deep thought.","Yue Fuguang, meanwhile, continued chatting with the system about Wu Chengbin. \"Little Zhu, it's still early. Tell me in detail about this Wu Chengbin and the opium paste.\"","[Does Master just want to enjoy the gossip, or do you want to intervene in this matter?]","Yue Fuguang toyed with a bright red apple in her hand. \"We can ignore the rest, but since this involves opium, we must give the Emperor and the lords a warning.","The lingering poison of this substance doesn't just affect the current generation; it will also impact the next generation, and the generation after that. If it spreads, its harm will be no less than that century-long catastrophe.\"","It would actually affect the next generation?","Hearing this, the officials who had been either busy or pretending to be busy could no longer sit still.","If the examination compound hadn't already been locked down, Ling Yinghua, Ji Hongming, and the others would have loved to report this to the Emperor immediately and order a thorough investigation.","Ji Hongming even ordered someone to quietly retrieve Wu Chengbin's file. Since this man had been framed, starting the investigation with him would surely yield some clues.","[Master, this Wu Chengbin is originally from Xinzhou Prefecture. He rushed to Shangjing City from his hometown last October to prepare for the imperial examination. Coming with him was his classmate and good friend, Song Qingsong.","Because Wu Chengbin was quite famous locally for his talents, and so was Song Qingsong, the two became close friends.","However, in terms of academics, Wu Chengbin was always able to steadily suppress Song Qingsong. Because Song Qingsong always ranked below him in every examination, Song Qingsong outwardly acted as if he were a gentle breeze and bright moon, seemingly unbothered.","In reality, caring the most about fame and fortune, he deeply hated Wu Chengbin in his heart for keeping him in this eternal second place.","So, upon arriving in the capital, the moment someone sowed a bit of discord and provided a method to harm him, he willingly became a knife in someone else's hands.","Song Qingsong comes from a good family background. For this trip to the capital, he brought not only a pageboy but also a female cook.","After Wu Chengbin accidentally got an upset stomach, he had no choice but to accept Song Qingsong's kindness and share meals with him.","By then, winter had already arrived, and Wu Chengbin, completely unaware, passively began consuming opium.","At first, he even felt that the smoke from burning the jujube paste cake could refresh his mind and invigorate his spirit, but after a little over a month, he found that he seemingly could no longer live without this substance.]","\"He has become addicted!\" Yue Fuguang sighed. \"Jealousy truly twists a person beyond recognition. Do you know who the person behind this is, and why they want to harm Wu Chengbin?\"","[Master, although Wu Chengbin's family has fallen into decline, his ancestors used to be wealthy. His grandfather, named Wu Kenan, was once a border defense general.","No less than a hundred Nanzhao and Nanyue people died at his hands, so in the hearts of some people from those two countries, they absolutely detest Wu Kenan and the Wu family.","By the generation of Wu Chengbin's father, his two older uncles had both died in battle one after another. His father was in poor health, and to leave a bloodline for the Wu family, his grandfather Wu Kenan had his father study literature instead of martial arts.]","The system shook its head. [Unfortunately, his father achieved nothing in either literature or martial arts. After his grandfather died, the family fell into decline. Later, to treat his father's illness and to support Wu Chengbin's imperial examinations, the family wealth accumulated by the Wu ancestors was mostly depleted.","Wu Chengbin only brought one pageboy with him to the capital for the exam, which gave Song Qingsong and the people behind him an opportunity.","The person behind this was originally a Nanzhao spy. Later, he was bought off by the Nanyue people and became a double agent, physically in Nanzhao but loyal to Nanyue.","His family has a blood feud with the Wu family; his own father died at the hands of Wu Kenan.","Someone in Nanzhao used poppies to produce an opium paste much purer than smoking poppy shells. Once this spy learned the news, he immediately passed it on to Nanyue.","Gan Sheng, whose ambitions toward Great Yan had never died, immediately thought of using this substance against the military and civilians of Great Yan.]","Gan Sheng could be said to be the one among the emperors of the six nations who most enjoyed using venomous schemes. To achieve his goals, his heart was truly black.","\"So this substance was bought by Gan Sheng from Nanzhao and then smuggled into Great Yan?\"","[Exactly. Taking advantage of the opportunity to deliver things to Lan Xuan'er in Shangjing City before the New Year, that Nanzhao spy snuck into Shangjing City with the substance.","He unexpectedly ran into Wu Chengbin, the grandson of his enemy, which led to the subsequent plan. Of course, dealing with Wu Chengbin was only out of personal revenge, done in passing.","Their true target is the New Army of Great Yan.]","\"The New Army?\" Upon hearing that it was aimed at the New Army, not to mention the Crown Prince who nearly crushed his chair's armrest, even Yue Fuguang could no longer remain calm.","What was the New Army? It wasn't just an army; it was the sharpest blade in Great Yan's hands, and it also contained Yue Fuguang's own blood, sweat, and tears.","It was also the first arrow Yue Fuguang intended to shoot at her opponents to expand their territories, and one of the guarantees for whether she could complete the system's tasks.","If it were destroyed, wouldn't she have to start all over again? How much time would that waste!","Anyone who affected the progress of her tasks was an enemy!","A cold glint flashed across Yue Fuguang's eyes. No one noticed that at this moment, Yue Fuguang had already developed a murderous intent toward Gan Sheng, the man who always came out to disrupt things.","[It is the New Army. Gan Sheng also knows they are Great Yan's strongest combat force, so naturally, he wants to destroy them!]","Yue Fuguang stroked an emerald bead in her hand. The cool sensation struck straight to her heart, allowing her to calm down slightly. \"Little Zhu, the New Army has strict discipline. I'm afraid it won't be easy to make them all acquire the bad habit of smoking opium, right?","Could it be that someone in the high command of the New Army has been bought off?\"","The Crown Prince was thinking the exact same thing at this moment. The New Army had currently expanded to nearly three hundred thousand men, including two hundred and seventy thousand land troops and nearly thirty thousand naval troops.","The supreme leader was naturally his royal father. Below him was his young aunt, Yue Fuguang, and he himself commanded nearly fifty thousand men.","It was impossible for the three of them to have any issues, which left only the Minister of War, Huo Ying, Great General Wei Shouyi, and the generals below them.","Huo Ying, who was currently attending the morning court, and Wei Shouyi, who was currently drilling the troops, both felt an inexplicable, sudden chill run down their bodies at this moment. They sneezed several times in a row, and as they looked up at the bright sun shining outside, they couldn't stop the coldness gripping their bodies.","[Master, someone has indeed been bought off. However, the method they are using is extremely clever.","Recently, a method to refresh the mind has become popular in Nanzhao, which is smoking dry tobacco. Nanyue then figured out a way to mix opium paste into the shredded tobacco.","They even thought of adding this substance into the charcoal fires used for heating in the military camps.]","Yue Fuguang sneered coldly, \"Why is it Nanzhao again? Don't they have a bit too many ideas, and they never ponder over anything good.\""]},{"number":411,"title":"Chapter 411: A High Official in the Court Has Contracted","paragraphs":["\"Although smoking dry tobacco is not as harmful as opium, the damage it causes to the body is completely incurable given the current medical standards of these mortals!\"","Ji Hongming, who had seen a white jade tobacco pipe and exquisite shredded tobacco on his gift list during the New Year, exchanged a glance with Ling Yinghua, who had already started smoking. They both saw lingering fear in each other's eyes.","It turned out this thing did more than just refresh the mind; it actually caused irreversible damage to the body!","What was even more terrifying was the possibility of someone mixing opium into their tobacco... They didn't even dare to imagine the consequences.","The Junior Preceptor had once said that those addicted to poppies were worse than pigs and dogs. If they were to fall victim to it, they wouldn't even be fit to be human anymore, let alone serve as officials!","[Over the years, Nanzhao has become increasingly dependent on Nanyue. Their country is just like the former Great Yan, having been infiltrated so thoroughly it resembles a sieve.","Behind the Empress's several children are the shadows of the Nanyue Emperor and his nobles.","Therefore, Nanzhao's resources will naturally be utilized by Nanyue.]","\"Do Lan Xuan'er and Gan Tang know about these things?\"","[Because of the Empress's favor, Lan Xuan'er is deeply ostracized by her siblings. As for Gan Tang, she is the only legitimate princess of the late Emperor, and her elder brother was once the Crown Prince.","Although Gan Sheng outwardly showers her with favor, he secretly guards against her at every turn.","In the original timeline, her ability to eventually ascend the throne after Great Yan was destroyed relied not only on her own formidable political maneuvering but also on her Prince Consort, who held heavy military power, and the later God of War, Ling Yuanhang.","Currently, both of them are excluded from court politics and remain unaware of the plot against Great Yan.","However, there is a person in the diplomatic mission who not only knows but is also one of the executors of this plan.]","\"Who is it? Are they related to the two of them?\"","[Master, do you remember a maid beside Lan Xuan'er? The one who was the most active when exposing the illicit affair between Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi.]","Yue Fuguang thought hard. In her memory, aside from the bare white buttocks and long, snowy-white legs, all she could recall were the brilliant expressions on the faces of the people who had barged in to watch the scene.","It seemed there really was a maid in green beside Lan Xuan'er. The only reason she had noticed that woman at the time was because her expression had been a bit strange.","\"Little Zhu, what about her? Is there a problem?\"","[Master, you would never guess it. This maid in green is named Qing Lan, and she is cousins with that double agent, Li Qun.","Li Qun came to Shangjing City in secret this time to execute internal affairs, so he naturally needed to seek his cousin Qing Lan's help.","This Qing Lan is not only someone else's spy placed beside Lan Xuan'er but also a double agent recruited by her cousin Li Qun.","The clever idea of adding ingredients to the charcoal fire was something she came up with for Li Qun.]","The Crown Prince and the other officials were clearly becoming restless. Since it was just about time for lunch, they each found an excuse to step out.","Watching their retreating figures, Yue Fuguang quietly asked the system, \"Little Zhu, have all those tobacco shreds and charcoal been transported to the military camps?","Are there any soldiers who have already become addicted to the drug?\"","If there were, no matter how outstanding they might be, they could no longer be kept in the army. After all, anyone who understood the nature of this substance knew what it meant.","[They have arrived at the military camps and been put into storage. However, because it hasn't been too cold over the past few days, the army has used very little charcoal. This newly stored batch hasn't been distributed yet.","As for the tobacco shreds, they are only supplied to a select few military generals, and no one has fallen for the trick yet.","But Master, while the military is fine, the same cannot be said for the imperial court.]","\"What do you mean? Has an official in the court gotten addicted?\"","Yue Fuguang was somewhat worried. They were all her hardworking subordinates. If it were one of the capable ones, she would feel a bit of heartache. She might have no choice but to use potions from the system shop to repair their bodies and cure their addiction.","Although drug addiction was something that had no permanent cure back in her hometown, for an entity like the system, it was a trivial matter.","The few men who had just stepped outside the courtyard suddenly halted their steps. Their biggest worry, the military, was temporarily safe, but before their hanging hearts could fully settle, they heard these words. This was hardly any better than something happening in the army!","[Leaving others aside for now, the pouch currently hanging at Ling Yinghua's waist contains tobacco shreds, and they are shreds that have been soaked in opium.]","\"Lord Ling? I don't think I've ever seen him smoke. Could he already be addicted?\"","On this side, the several men all turned their gazes in unison to the pouches hanging at the waist of Chancellor Ling, whose body had already begun to tremble slightly.","Despite the freezing weather, Ling Yinghua's forehead was beaded with sweat. With a trembling hand, he snatched a blue pouch embroidered with a green bamboo pattern from his waist.","It seemed to take all his strength to shakily open the pouch, revealing the brown tobacco shreds inside that emitted a strange odor.","\"Lord Ling, be careful!\" The Crown Prince grabbed the swaying Ling Yinghua to keep him from falling and smoothly caught the pouch that had almost dropped to the ground.","Ji Hongming also leaned over to look at the contents of the pouch. At the same time, the voice of the divine artifact echoed in their ears. To Chancellor Ling, who currently felt like he was drowning, this voice was no different from a life-saving breath of immortal air.","[He has only smoked that spiked tobacco once, so it's not a big problem. But if he were to smoke it a few more times, it would be hard to say!]","Ling Yinghua slumped heavily onto the stone bench in the courtyard. It was not until the cold sweat stung his eyes that he belatedly remembered to wipe it away.","[But...] Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. Sure enough, there was always a turning point. She served herself some soup while listening to what followed.","After today, who knew how many would cry and how many would laugh.","[Ever since the trend of smoking dry tobacco was brought to Great Yan by those scholars and literati, it has actually been elevated into an elegant pursuit by people with ulterior motives. When gathering to chat, many people not only brew tea and warm wine, but also take a few puffs together. They even elegantly refer to it as 'swallowing clouds and blowing mist'.","Among the court officials, there are quite a few who pose as lovers of culture, and this Ling Yinghua is one of them. The supposedly top-grade shredded tobacco in his pouch was a New Year's tribute from his students.","Many among the court officials and scholars have already started smoking this specially made tobacco.]","Yue Fuguang sighed inwardly. How many people are already addicted?","She felt helpless too. It was not that she did not want to expose things in advance, but ever since their revelations caused history to severely deviate from its course, many of the original system tasks would no longer happen due to this shift.","Therefore, the task board had long since changed. Because the new future was uncertain and still being created, many of the current tasks were now trigger-based.","If it were not for this Wu Chengbin, she figured it would have taken her quite a while longer to discover the problem with the court officials.","[There are five or six court officials and over twenty scholars in the capital. They are...]","Yue Fuguang listened to the string of names the system reported to her. She recognized all the court officials, but aside from Wu Chengbin, she had not heard of a single scholar. They probably were not anyone famous.","However, in terms of numbers, it was fewer than she had expected, which was a blessing in disguise.","The system clearly guessed her thoughts and added, [It is also fortunate that those literati only brought over the so-called 'elegant pursuit' of smoking. At that time, the tobacco was still normal.]"]},{"number":412,"title":"Chapter 412: Are You Trying to Kill Me","paragraphs":["The poisonous tobacco was later secretly ordered by Gan Sheng to be brought into the capital by Li Qun, in cooperation with South Yue spies, who added extra ingredients and mixed it into normal tobacco.","Because there have been many literary gatherings lately, scholars like to puff away when they get together, which is how they got addicted. Fortunately, it hasn't been long, and they can still be saved.]","Upon hearing the names one by one, the Crown Prince quickly memorized them. He summoned his personal hidden guards and ordered them to send the information directly to Emperor Mingxi through a special channel.","This special channel was specifically added to handle any unusual situations because Yue Fuguang was participating in the spring examinations this time. He hadn't expected it to come in handy so soon.","By the time they finished their tasks and returned, Yue Fuguang had already eaten and drunk her fill, and started observing the candidates writing furiously below.","Three days passed quickly amidst brilliant essays born of hard thought and the ever-thickening scent of ink.","Yue Fuguang had shut off her sense of smell since the afternoon of the first day, so she hadn't gone down to patrol during the subsequent exams.","However, when the second round of exams just started, standing in Wenxin Hall and seeing the distorted faces of the students in the distant cells near the latrines, her sympathy was inevitably touched a little.","Having taken the college entrance examination herself, she couldn't help but sympathize with those unlucky people. If they failed not because of a lack of talent, but because the stench ruined their train of thought, they would truly regret it to death.","With her narrow-mindedness, she would definitely curse the heavens, the earth, and her fellow candidates whenever she thought of it.","Little Zhu, the smell in this examination hall is really not pleasant. Help me find the Qingming incense.","[Master, you want to burn incense? These students are in luck. This Qingming incense not only clears away foul and murky air but also refreshes the mind. It is a great thing for those who are using their brains intensely.]","After Yue Fuguang took the Qingming incense from her sleeve and lit it, the entire examination hall was soon filled with an indescribable, ethereal aura. The candidates, who had been taking exams for three consecutive days and were physically exhausted and mentally sluggish, gradually regained their spirits as they smelled the faint fragrance wafting into their noses.","Thinking that this second round of exams included math questions she had set herself, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but be curious about how the candidates were answering. Unable to hold back any longer, she finally stepped out of Wenxin Hall for the first time and began her first patrol.","As Yue Fuguang, who was less than one and a half meters tall, walked through the crisscrossing corridors, she attracted immense attention wherever she passed.","As she walked, Yue Fuguang paid attention to the favorability column on her system panel. System, I have done meritorious service for the Great Yan Dynasty after all. Look, how are there still negative numbers in the favorability ratings?","Remember to mark them. No matter the reason, such people can never be allowed to step into the imperial court.","Yue Fuguang wouldn't let off those who harbored malicious intentions towards her just out of pity for their years of hard study.","Those with a negative favorability toward her were the ones who wanted her dead. Do not blame her for being ruthless; naturally, she had to clear out such people one by one as she found them. If she didn't get rid of them, was she supposed to save them for the New Year?","Did they think they were Xie Zhiyao or Bei Ye, people who were actually still useful!","[Master, Xue Baoshan, Cao Wei... these people bear malice toward you. They are either sponsored by aristocratic families or are the brats of major landlords themselves.","[Your high-yield seeds are life-saving rations for the common folk, but it is a different story for the wealthy. Between your seeds and the new land distribution policies, the commoners who originally had no fields and were forced to work as tenant farmers—enduring the exploitation of giving up fifty to sixty percent of their harvest to landlords—can now directly rent land from the imperial court for a mere thirty-five percent tax. They even have the opportunity to own their own land.","Because they planted high-yield crops in their fields, they do not have to sell their sons, daughters, or themselves when faced with a natural disaster like the current one.","You must understand that if it were not for those three types of high-yield seeds providing a safety net for ordinary households, the usual outcome would be the poor selling their land if they had any, or selling their children and borrowing from loan sharks if they did not.","It would never be like it is now, where almost the entirety of the Great Yan Empire has planted one to two seasons of these crops, leaving nearly every household with some surplus grain.","Even if a few specific prefectures failed to plant them in time, the imperial court now has the capacity to provide relief, ensuring that the people do not starve to the point of selling their lands and children.","It is safe to say that you have completely severed the methods by which these wealthy individuals enriched themselves off the backs of the poor. Tell me, do you think they hate you?]","Yue Fuguang walked at a leisurely pace, observing the conditions of the examination candidates as she replied in her mind, \"So, in previous years, this would be the exact time they bought up people and land, issued usurious loans, and made a fortune off the blood and sweat of the impoverished masses?","\"And unfortunately for them, this cycle was broken by the appearance of the high-yield grain. Therefore, they have developed a murderous intent toward me, the one who brought out these seeds?\"","[Correct. Most people are wary of your status and position, only daring to hide their hatred in their hearts. However, there are some who are used to acting like local tyrants. Arrogant and conceited, they want to use the imperial examinations as a stepping stone for the younger generation of their clans to rise in power.","Once they reach the royal court and gain a voice, no matter how good your relationship with the Emperor is, they will find ways to drive a wedge between you and the imperial family.","This is especially true for the candidates sponsored by the noble and aristocratic families. They inherently share countless ties with the nobility. Before being purged by the Emperor, these aristocratic families also sensed the impending crisis for their clans.","Thus, they promised massive benefits to certain individuals with two main goals: first, to help the surviving descendants of their families stage a comeback; and second, to take revenge on you by any means necessary.]","\"Strike back and take revenge on me? Just them?\" Yue Fuguang sneered inwardly. If she had just arrived in this world, she might have been afraid. But now, her only fear was that they wouldn't come at all.","However, knowing that they hated her actually made Yue Fuguang breathe a sigh of relief. She couldn't bear to lay a hand on those who loved her, but she felt absolutely zero psychological burden when dealing with those who hated her.","Pulling them up by the roots and completely destroying them would no longer cause her any hesitation.","[Master, have you forgotten that there are still people who want to stand in the royal court one day and drive a wedge between you and the Emperor!]","The Crown Prince, Ji Hongming, and a host of other ministers couldn't help but frown. Alienating the Grand Tutor from His Majesty? Weren't they trying to dig up the very roots of their Great Yan Empire?","Setting aside the fact that, for certain unspeakable reasons, neither they nor His Majesty could ever develop a rift with the Grand Tutor, they would never even give these individuals with ulterior motives a single chance to step into the royal court.","As for the saying that cutting off a person's future is like killing their parents and forging a blood feud... if it weren't for the current lack of hard evidence preventing them from immediately arresting and punishing these people, the schemers would be losing their lives, not just their futures.","Ji Hongming memorized all of their names. Once he returned, he would absolutely have the Court of Judicature and Revision and the Secret Spy Agency investigate the backgrounds of these people thoroughly. If they were involved in any illegal or undisciplined activities, they would absolutely not be spared.","Yue Fuguang clasped her small hands behind her back. \"What is there to worry about? If the Emperor truly listens to slander and grows suspicious of me, I will simply leave.\"","[Master, you just want to go out and have fun. Are you tempted by the invitations from those other countries?]","Neither the system nor the Crown Prince and his companions received an answer from Yue Fuguang. However, the more she kept silent, the more convinced they became that the Divine Artifact had hit the nail on the head!","Over on the other side, the Crown Prince and Ji Hongming, who were patrolling the examination grounds, could not help but quicken their pace toward Yue Fuguang. Seeing the sweat on the Crown Prince's forehead, the guards beside him assumed he was simply tired and hot from walking, and hastily offered him a handkerchief with deep respect."]},{"number":413,"title":"Chapter 413: Poisonous","paragraphs":["The Crown Prince waved his hand in refusal. How could a mere handkerchief soothe his nervous mood?","If the Junior Preceptor truly entertained the thought of strolling around neighboring countries, his royal father and the assembly of officials would absolutely never agree.","However, even all of them combined might not be able to change the Junior Preceptor's mind. Since they were powerless to stop her... The Crown Prince's gaze shifted toward the east, a cold glint flashing briefly in his eyes.","According to the news brought back by the spies, the heavy rains in Dongyi had indeed stopped on the exact day the Junior Preceptor predicted.","More than half a month had passed, and the floodwaters in the Dongyi lands had yet to fully recede, while the number of people freezing and starving to death everywhere continued to rise.","Perhaps before the Spring Festival this year, the Junior Preceptor could go to Dongyi... no, to the Great Yan's Four Islands of the Eastern Sea for a stroll.","He had to find a way to leak this information to the Junior Preceptor to keep her calm and patient, ensuring she absolutely didn't get the idea to visit Beili or Xiqiang.","Traveling abroad was nowhere near as fun as staying in one's own country!","The cold glint only flashed briefly across the Crown Prince's face before he quickly put on a genial smile again. When the candidates in the examination cells saw him, their faces were filled with reverence.","They thought to themselves, \"The rumors are indeed true. The Crown Prince truly looks like a lenient and benevolent heir apparent. In the future, he will surely be a wise and kind ruler.\"","Clang!","Just as Yue Fuguang was about to walk out of the \"Yi\" block of examination cells, the sound of a heavy object hitting the ground came from behind her.","She and the group of officials behind her turned their heads in succession, while the guards beside her had already drawn the sabers at their waists.","Entering the examination venue this time, Yue Fuguang had only brought Cuizhu, Shen Chunying, and Yu Huaixian. Although the commotion behind them was suspicious, Yue Fuguang did not think it was an assassination attempt.","Not to mention that her system hadn't sounded an alarm, carrying out an assassination in the examination venue was truly not a good choice.","Yue Fuguang took the lead and walked back. After taking only a few steps, she saw a student in one of the cells collapsed on the ground.","Yue Fuguang approached. A guard in the examination venue, seeing that the Junior Preceptor wanted to check on the student's condition, tried to help lift the person up.","\"Don't move!\" The words \"it's poisonous\" were swallowed back just in time as her gaze swept over the candidates in the surrounding cells, who looked tense yet couldn't hide their gossipy expressions. In her heart, she couldn't help but silently criticize them: at a time like this, a moment that determined their destinies, these few actually still had the mind to enjoy the drama.","Did they feel they had victory in the bag, or did they think their imperial exam prospects were hopeless and were just throwing caution to the wind?","Regardless, she could not cause a panic.","Thus, she beckoned Yu Huaixian over, whispered a few words in his ear, and then pulled a jade bottle from her sleeve, pressing it into his hand.","She then turned around and spoke in a voice that was neither too loud nor too soft, but just enough for the surrounding cells that had witnessed the situation to hear: \"It is nothing serious. He likely didn't rest well and overworked his mind, causing him to faint.\"","She waved her hand at Yu Huaixian, who had already dismantled the examination desk to use as a makeshift stretcher, and the guard who had initially tried to help. \"Carry him to the front and find the examination academy's physician for treatment.\"","Cuizhu thoughtfully placed the candidate's unfinished exam papers and answer sheets into his examination basket and took them along.","With her young lady's abilities, as long as this person wasn't dead right now, he definitely wouldn't die. He might even be able to return and continue the exam in a little while.","Yue Fuguang had the person carried away, completely unaware that she was falling right into someone else's trap.","\"Chen Kang, what time is it?\"","In a luxurious courtyard on the outskirts of the capital city of Shangjing, a wealthy-looking man in his fifties lay on a rocking chair with his eyes closed, humming a small tune as he asked the personal attendant serving beside him.","The young man in his twenties named Chen Kang looked up at the water clock placed in the corner of the study, bowed, and softly replied, \"To answer Master, it is the end of the Shen hour!\"","Chen Kang looked through the window at the sky outside and sighed in admiration once again. The current Junior Preceptor Yue truly lived up to her title as a divine maiden. These glass windows were not only bright, but looking outside from inside the room was also incredibly clear.","He had followed his master to the residences of some officials and noble families; the glass inlaid in the houses of those families was even larger than the ones in his master's room.","While Chen Kang was thinking about what a pity it was for the fine houses and the precious glass of those noble families whose homes had been confiscated, he softly asked the person on the rocking chair who seemed to have fallen sound asleep, \"Master, it is getting late. Shall I have the meal served?\"","Normally, this was their master's mealtime. For some unknown reason, not only had the master stayed in the study the entire day, but he had even refused to leave when his most favored eighth concubine came to invite him.","\"No rush. Go and see if Chen Zhong has returned.\"","Chen Kang really wanted to say that he could see very clearly through the glass window that, apart from a few servants in the courtyard, there was no sign of Chen Zhong, who had been out all day and had yet to return.","Thinking was one thing, but his mouth didn't hesitate for a second as he replied, \"Yes, this lowly one will go to the estate gates right away to welcome Steward Chen.\"","His words had barely landed, and before he could even take a single step forward, he looked up and saw the courtyard gates being pushed open from the outside by guards. Dressed in gray clothes and looking hurried, Chen Zhong was taking large strides into the courtyard, heading straight for the study.","\"Master, Steward Chen is back!\"","Upon hearing that the person had returned, the master quickly sat up from the rocking chair. After glancing outside through the glass window, he waved his hand at Chen Kang and said, \"Go and invite Mr. Bai.\"","Walking two steps toward the desk with his hands behind his back, he added, \"Take all the servants in the courtyard away with you. Apart from Mr. Bai, do not let anyone come within half a step of the study.\"","\"Yes, Master.\" Chen Kang nodded and quickly left. This \"anyone\" naturally included himself.","By the time Chen Kang opened the door to leave, Chen Zhong had already reached the entrance of the study.","The two brushed past each other. In the moment the door closed, Chen Kang could still faintly hear a few words.","\"Master, there is news!\" Chen Zhong carefully opened the door again and glanced out into the courtyard. After confirming no one was there, he carefully closed the study door.","The master pointed to a chair below his desk and said, \"Sit down and speak.\"","Chen Zhong expressed his thanks and sat down carefully. The exhaustion and tension on his face made him look significantly older. At just over forty years old, he looked about the same age as his master.","Without even taking the time to drink a sip of water, Chen Zhong said impatiently, \"Master, the city has been under martial law these past two days. This lowly one made inquiries from various sources and found out that those few families have been raided and their properties confiscated!\"","He stretched out three fingers, pointed toward the west, and finally, his fingers landed toward the east.","The layout of Shangjing City was such that the west belonged to the noble and the east to the wealthy. For a family with some background like theirs, even just trying to ask about affairs in the west required quite a bit of effort.","The master's hand, originally resting on the armrest, slowly tightened. His other hand pressed against the table as he asked with a stern face, \"Did they not even spare the branch families?\"","\"Master, for those involved families, regardless of whether they were branch or main lineages, they have all been locked up in the Ministry of Justice's prison.\" Chen Zhong swallowed hard and continued, \"Even the families on good terms with them, and... and families with relatives who participated in the hunting assassination, were all arrested. Their lands and properties were confiscated, and their entire households were thrown into prison.\"","Upon hearing about the hunting assassination, the master couldn't help but stand up abruptly. He paced back and forth in the study. \"Didn't the main family say before the new year that they had shouldered all the blame and wouldn't implicate anyone else?\"","Over the past two or three months, the branch families had remained unaffected. People like them had thought this disastrous calamity was about to pass."]},{"number":414,"title":"Chapter 414: Machination","paragraphs":["Unexpectedly, after so many days, they still hadn’t escaped. The emperor hadn’t let them go—he had only lulled them into a false sense of security before uprooting everyone involved.","One had to admit that the emperor and those officials were truly skilled in their methods. Who would have thought they would strike during the national examination?","No wonder those family heads, after Old Man Song was arrested and the plan to rig the imperial exams fell through, insisted on poisoning the spring examination grounds. They must have long anticipated that the emperor wouldn’t let them off. Even if they were to die, they would drag the two prominent figures down with them!","The master glanced at the water clock again. According to the plan, the man should be showing signs of poisoning by now. He wondered if anyone had noticed and had him carried away for treatment.","Chen Zhong had no idea his master’s mind was already on the examination hall. He continued, “I hear the Grand Court and the Ministry of Justice are jointly investigating. They’ve discovered that those collateral branches and in-laws are sheltering direct-line descendants. Now, all three families in the capital have been thrown into prison.”","He cautiously peered outside before adding, “Before I came back, I saw several teams of imperial guards riding out of the city at full speed.”","So it seemed that even those who had fled outside the city wouldn’t escape.","Chen Zhong looked at his master. Was their Chen family truly going to follow those people down a dead-end road? Could the Chen family possibly stand against the royal family and that powerful figure?","If his master were to report the matter now and distance himself, perhaps he could still save his own skin.","Just as Chen Zhong was debating whether to urge his master to reconsider, the door pushed open, and in walked the strategist the Chen master had hired, a man known as Mr. Bai.","Chen Zhong stopped talking and sighed inwardly. With this man around, the master had already passed the point of no return.","Mr. Bai entered, and Chen Zhong tactfully stood up and excused himself.","As he closed the door, Chen Zhong could faintly hear Mr. Bai’s slightly raspy voice say, “The seed has already bloomed...”","Chen Zhong wiped the tears that had unknowingly fallen from the corner of his eyes and shook his head. People like themselves were destined to become mere fertilizer for someone else’s ambition. It was a pity for his own children and grandchildren back home, and for the young master who had studied so hard in the mansion.","“Mr. Bai, are you certain this won’t implicate us?” Chen master asked, still uneasy. After all, his own son was among the examinees. If the court investigated, he would be considered a victim.","But he couldn’t help fearing the worst. That Junior Preceptor Yue was notoriously unpredictable—over the past two years, almost every plot involving her had failed.","“Rest assured, master. You are the victim. Who would suspect you?” Mr. Bai said. Sacrificing a son who was not favored was a small price to pay for a fortune.","“Mr. Bai, I... I have a whole family behind me. I’m truly terrified!” The Chen master, who had appeared calm in front of Chen Zhong, now put on a pitiful face before Mr. Bai, hoping to squeeze out a little more advantage.","As expected, seeing the Chen master still looking unsettled, Mr. Bai feared he might reveal something later and continued to reassure him. “Once the plan succeeds, all of the Wang family’s hidden assets on the west side of Lotus Mountain on the outskirts of the capital will be yours!”","Facing the emperor’s relentless pressure and encroachment, the aristocratic families wouldn’t fail to prepare a contingency plan for a comeback. Hiding away some wealth was easy for them, as long as it was done secretly enough not to be discovered by the authorities.","Chen master felt a surge of joy but kept a grateful expression on his face. His words, however, said something else entirely: “I am deeply grateful for Mr. Bai’s generosity! It’s a pity about my son. If he somehow survives, he would have made a fine local magistrate someday.”","He quickly glanced at Mr. Bai’s expression before continuing, “But for the greater cause, sacrificing one man is worth it.”","The man called Mr. Bai, dressed in a white silk robe, appeared to be in his thirties. His features were ordinary, but he carried the air of a scholar.","Hearing Chen master’s words, his hand, which had been stroking his beard, paused slightly. A flicker of mockery and contempt passed through his eyes before he picked up his teacup and took a light sip.","“Master Chen is magnanimous. His Highness and that certain figure will not forget your family’s contributions,” he said.","Setting down the cup, he chuckled lightly. “The results of your eldest son’s assignment will come soon. As long as the person inside...” He made a cutting motion toward his own throat, “...all involved will be greatly rewarded. Better days are ahead for you and me.”","This time, using the aristocratic families as cover, if they could take down both Yue Fuguang and Xie Zhiyan in one fell swoop, it would be worth sacrificing even the last remnants of the ancient clans.","Consider it their burial offering!","Yue Fuguang: Should I say thank you?","Xie Zhiyan: I’m doing quite well, thank you. I don’t plan on dying just yet!","Xie Zhiyan, who was doing quite well indeed, was now shocked by what Yue Fuguang had just said to him. He stumbled back half a step, nearly losing his balance.","Minister Ji, already in his forties and approaching fifty, had fallen into a chair in utter shock. He tried several times to stand up, but his legs were too weak to support him.","“Little Aunt, what do we do now? If the virus spreads as you say... we... and all the examinees, even the entire capital, will be doomed!”","Yue Fuguang pulled out another white jade bottle and handed it to him. “Relax. With me here, what you fear won’t happen.”","“Everyone who has come into contact with Zhou Bo must take this antidote pill.”","With that, she walked over to the unconscious man lying on a wooden board. In her mind, the system’s data on Zhou Bo quickly surfaced, along with a freshly triggered quest.","Zhou Bo, age twenty-five, from Pingliang County under Xingzhou’s Jinyi Prefecture. He had a wife, Madam Chen, a son, and a daughter. He was the third child in his family, with both parents and siblings still alive.","A man with family, a career, and prospects would never willingly poison himself just to take down her and the Crown Prince.","The system’s quest was simple: Stop the spread of the “White Flower Blight.” The poison, or virus, that Zhou Bo was infected with was precisely this vile White Flower Blight.","It was so vicious because anyone poisoned by it would initially fall into a coma. Once the “flowers” began to bloom on their body, they would wake up. At that point, the “flowers” would float into the air like countless seeds, spreading to others.","These “flowers” were nearly invisible to the naked eye.","Anyone poisoned by it would die within three days, their flesh blooming like flowers before reducing them to bare bones.","[System, are you sure you didn’t offend the task-issuing core system? Besides the long-term and main quests, almost all our side quests this past year have been this type of emergency.","If I didn’t have my points and methods, who else could complete a quest with a ninety-nine percent mortality rate, ninety-nine percent transmissibility, and the potential to wipe out ninety-nine percent of the population once it spreads?]","Even if their unconventional approach to completing quests had altered history too much and caused most side quests to change or even vanish entirely, shouldn’t new quests be triggered sooner than this last-minute panic?","The system transformed into a shimmering bead and slid into Yue Fuguang’s palm, rolling around and acting cute. [Host, absolutely not! How could a unit-friendly system like me possibly offend the Jammed... I mean, the auxiliary system!]","The system spun in her hand, nearly slipping up and blurting out the nickname it had secretly given the auxiliary system.","“Little Aunt, if only the people here take the antidote, what about everyone else?”"]},{"number":415,"title":"Chapter 415: The Person Behind the Scenes","paragraphs":["Yu Huaixian and his men carried the person back all the way, passing by examination rooms A and B. If the poison truly spread through the air, then those examinees were also in danger!","Seeing that even after the assassination attempt on the Crown Prince, he could still worry about the examinees, Yue Fuguang felt some relief. It was good that those in power were finally looking downward instead of only thinking about how to report upward.","\"We were lucky today. His poison was discovered in time, and as it happened, I had burned Qingming incense. This incense has an inhibitory effect on early-stage toxins—or rather, poisonous vapors.\"","If she hadn't been unable to bear the smell of the examination hall today and decided to light the incense, then suddenly taken a whim to go downstairs for a look, the poisonous bloom on this man's body would have grown further, and even Qingming incense wouldn't have been able to suppress it.","It was simply destiny at work!","No, for the sake of points, this matter had to be resolved quickly. Yue Fuguang glanced at the procedure steps displayed on her system while simultaneously inserting needles into Zhou Bo.","Her clumsy technique made the Crown Prince, standing a step behind her, watch with a pounding heart.","Was Yue Fuguang herself not nervous?","She wanted to say she was terrified!","But this was part of the system's mission, and she had no choice.","Who could argue with a point-giving system? You couldn't afford to offend it!","\"System, if a single pill could solve this poison, why does the mission require me to use silver needles? If I accidentally stab him to death, who takes the blame?\"","[Host, our pills are exclusive to us. After we leave this world, how would the people here cure themselves if similar cases arise?","Host, give a man a fish, and you feed him for a day; teach him to fish, and you feed him for a lifetime.]","Hearing the system start preaching again, Yue Fuguang quickly changed the subject. \"Little Zhu, tell me what's up with this Zhou Bo.","This 'White Blossom Blight' on him is refined from corpse poison. It's no accident—how could an examinee preparing for the exams get infected?","The toxin has an incubation period of three to five days, which aligns perfectly with the exam period. This is too coincidental!\"","Whenever the White Blossom Blight emerged, it claimed tens of thousands of lives. In this ancient era, it was often mistaken for an epidemic plague, and few knew it was originally a poison. Its antidote was hard to prepare, but it was most afraid of fire.","This led some rulers, upon detecting an epidemic, to burn affected people alive without regard for their lives—a cruel yet expedient solution in an age of backward medicine. By accident, this also eliminated the White Blossom Blight. Ironic, wasn't it?","[Master, among the candidates in this examination hall, one is Zhou Bo's friend. His surname is Chen, given name Mingyu. Zhou Bo married a woman from the Chen family, who is Mingyu's fifth cousin once removed.","Zhou Bo came to the capital to prepare for the exams and was staying in a small residence owned by the Chen family. Both were examinees and often discussed their studies together, so they were close.","But neither Chen Mingyu nor Zhou Bo knew that they were both merely sacrificial pawns in this conspiracy.]","\"So the poisoner is connected to these two. Are they enemies, relatives, or friends? Why didn't Chen Mingyu get poisoned?\"","When Zhou Bo's poison activated, Yue Fuguang had already used the system to scan the entire examination hall and confirmed that only he had been poisoned.","[It was a relative of Chen Mingyu, but practically an enemy.]","The Crown Prince had returned to his desk and began silently reviewing the files of the two men, focusing closely on Chen Mingyu's information, reading it line by line.","Chen Mingyu was from the capital, the fifth son in his family, born to a concubine. His legitimate elder brother, Chen Mingren, was a same-year jinshi of the sixth year of Emperor Mingxi's reign. Their father, Chen Fengzu, had been a low-ranking seventh-rank official before being implicated in the corruption case of Fu Hong and was dismissed in the winter of the fourth year of Emperor Mingxi's reign. He was currently idle at home.","If they were merely dismissed, it meant he was not heavily involved—perhaps merely implicated. Was this resentment toward the court the reason for today's revenge?","The Crown Prince shook his head. Chen Fengzu was just a minor seventh-rank official. Although his family had some wealth, carrying out such a bold scheme required not only courage but also capability and connections.","\"Was this familial intrigue?\"","[Chen Mingyu was a concubine-born son, but he surpassed the legitimate eldest son, on whom his father had placed all hopes, in scholarly pursuits.","The future head of the Chen family was being outshone by a son born to a merchant's daughter. This bred jealousy not only in the principal wife and the eldest son but also in Chen Fengzu himself, who feared the eldest son wouldn't be able to control the younger one, leading to family discord.","So when implementing this poison plot, Chen Fengzu followed some of his wife's and eldest son's suggestions.","Originally, according to Chen Mingren's plan, the one lying here should have been Chen Mingyu. But later, Chen Fengzu felt some reluctance and, after listening to his advisor, swapped the victim for the visiting relative Zhou Bo, who was staying with the Chen family. Meanwhile, Chen Mingyu had to be present in the examination hall as a link to make the Chen family appear uninvolved.","Thus, when the court launched a strict investigation, the Chen family would appear as the aggrieved party, not the suspects.]","\"What a clever scheme! There must be someone behind the Chen family. Who is it?\"","Earlier this year, Emperor Mingxi had already executed and imprisoned the main branches of the aristocratic families involved in the hunting grounds assassination, but some collateral branches and in-laws were still under investigation.","She looked out the window. Based on the trials conducted by the Secret Intelligence Bureau and the Grand Court, the clean-up of the remaining figures should have begun outside by now. She wondered if, at the brink of life and death, they had enough strength left to stir up more trouble.","Only after coming here and delving deeper did Yue Fuguang understand the saying: a lean camel is heavier than a horse. Even an aristocratic family fallen into the mud still possessed resources far beyond what ordinary commoner families could match.","[Master guessed right. On the surface, the Chen family seems to be making the dying struggle of the aristocratic families, attacking you and the Crown Prince as revenge against the Emperor.","But secretly, behind them, someone from Panshan Mountain is supporting them, perfecting the plan and covering up their tracks.","That person is now hiding in the Chen household. Ostensibly, he is an advisor Chen Fengzu hired. In truth, he used the aristocratic families as a cover to embed himself in the Chen family, overseeing and assisting in the execution of their plan.]","Yue Fuguang sneered inwardly. Dragging her along as a scapegoat? They'd better not choke on it!","The Crown Prince raised an eyebrow. At least those people had planned to trap both him and the Grand Mentor together. If he had faced them alone, it would have been far more dangerous!","His father, the Emperor, was truly farsighted to appoint the Grand Mentor as the deputy examiner for this spring's provincial examinations. Without her, not only the tobacco incident but also the White Blossom Blight would have been a certain death sentence!","As for Panshan Mountain being involved again, neither of them, nor Ji Hongming and the others quietly working nearby, found it surprising.","The six kingdoms: aside from floods in Dongyi, droughts plagued all other regions. If this continued, chaos would soon engulf the world.","An organization like Panshan Mountain, which thrived on turmoil, naturally couldn't resist causing trouble. Their specialty? Overthrowing dynasties!","\"It's Panshan Mountain again. Are they targeting only Dayan this time, or do they have plans for the other kingdoms?\"","Dayan was hardly a soft target anymore. Attacking it alone seemed unlikely!","[Master, you may not know yet, but Dongyi has already descended into chaos because of Panshan Mountain's intervention.","In the original timeline, with Sima Jing's covert but strong support, Panshan Mountain's schemes would have failed.","But now, without Sima Jing, Dongyi is in complete disarray, consumed by power struggles. No one is dealing with the dead or calming the people.]"]},{"number":416,"title":"Chapter 416: The Struggle for Supremacy","paragraphs":["\"When it gets hot in April and May, the plague will surely rise. By then, the Eastern Barbarians will be a true hell on earth.\"","\"In that case, I must guard my Emerald Isle well.\" After taking over Chrysanthemum Island, Yue Fuguang decisively renamed it Emerald Isle, hoping that by next year, the barren island would be covered in green plants, becoming a vibrant piece of emerald lying on the vast blue sea.","\"As for the other countries, a few days ago, during the North Li Festival of Missing Relatives, nobles were assassinated. The news should have reached the emperor's hands by now.\"","\"Today is the twelfth of February. Great Yan is holding the spring imperial exams, and at the same time, it's the birthday of the Goddess of Flowers in Southern Yue and Southern Zhao. Something will happen tonight.\"","\"Only Western Qiang remains, and their turn will come within the next two days.\"","Yue Fuguang clicked her tongue. Damn, this Panshan organization's actions were no different from that old dowager empress who declared war on eight countries at once!","Were they too arrogant, or just courting death?","No matter how mysterious they were, no matter how deep they hid, if all six countries united desperately to dig them out, they wouldn't be completely without a chance of victory.","The only variable was that the countries might suspect each other and fail to work together. That gave Panshan the chance to grow strong, dare to challenge all six countries at once, and not fear full-scale retaliation.","Yue Fuguang's guess was right. Panshan's methods were covert and measured, making it truly impossible for them to be hunted down by a unified six-nation alliance.","\"System, can you still not find out where Panshan's nest is, or who their leader is?\"","It shouldn't be like this. The system was already at level six. Couldn't its data search cover all six countries?","\"Host, first of all, I am a merit system. Merit systems do not provide such services.\"","\"So the system just doesn't have this function.\" Or was it just that her merit system didn't have it? Yue Fuguang suspected the latter.","The system ignored Yue Fuguang's grumbling and continued defending its own 'inability.' \"Secondly, the gossip system was too severely damaged. It's difficult to repair.\"","\"Besides, if the auxiliary system finds out we've merged dual databases, the gossip system will definitely be completely blocked. Then we won't be able to use it at all!\"","What System 07 didn't mention was that during the repair of the gossip system, it had unintentionally recovered a fragment of data—scattered records about past events.","After reading that data, it felt it should behave more cautiously. The best course was to persuade the host to lie low as much as possible.","After all, the more the gossip system was repaired, the greater the chance the auxiliary system would detect data fluctuations. That was why it had recently been reluctant to use the gossip system to query matters requiring too much algorithmic computation.","If it hadn't been for the merit energy transformed from incense offerings shielding them, the dual-database merger would have been exposed long ago.","After all, quite a few taskers had failed in this mission. Why was it that when it came to her host, tasks were completed quickly and well?","With roughly similar identities and starting points, the outcomes were vastly different. Not only would the systems verifying the tasks investigate, but the failed taskers would also pay attention.","But because the host had not yet 'graduated' from the first minor world, bound by system rules, it could not tell her yet.","Kept in the dark, Yue Fuguang still asked persistently, \"Is it because we're too far from Panshan's nest that you can't find it? If we get closer, might we be able to dig them out?\"","The system thought about it for a moment and found it reasonable. \"Indeed, distance is one limiting factor.\"","Yue Fuguang felt relieved. According to her plan, when she started sowing next month, she would definitely begin a nationwide touring performance... that is, a touring rain-making session. That would be her chance.","While Yue Fuguang and the system were discussing Panshan, the Crown Prince hadn't been idle either. He urgently reported Zhou Bo's matter, the Chen family, Bai Huaku, and Panshan's schemes in detail to Emperor Mingxi.","By the time Emperor Mingxi received the message from the Crown Prince, the unconscious Zhou Bo had already woken up and could return to his examination cell to continue his tests.","As for the Chen family, except for Chen Mingyu, who was still in the examination hall, everyone else had been thrown into prison.","The third and final session of the exams finally passed without further incidents. Yue Fuguang silently breathed a sigh of relief—she hadn't triggered any sudden tasks.","When she finally returned to her Bright Moon Pavilion, it was already the seventh day after the spring exams.","Although she hadn't participated in grading papers over the past few days, as the deputy chief examiner, the decisions on who to admit and how to rank them had to be discussed and decided with the Crown Prince.","After several days of continuous effort from everyone, over three thousand exam papers were finally fully reviewed. Yue Fuguang had followed the entire process from start to finish.","Today was the last day of grading. Inside the grading chamber, candlelight flickered. Sealed paper scrolls lay spread across the desks.","Several examiners sat around, having reached a critical moment in determining the rankings.","Twenty exam papers lay before her and the Crown Prince. The examiners largely agreed on the other rankings, but the debate over the placement of three candidates was exceptionally fierce.","Yue Fuguang could see that Minister of Rites Ji Hongming was so agitated that he was nearly spraying saliva onto the face of the official opposite him.","Having studied at the Hongwen Academy for three years, Yue Fuguang's skill with classical texts was mediocre due to her lazy and erratic attendance. Still, she asked a key question, \"Gentlemen, regarding the policy essay on managing drought relief, how did all three of them write?\"","In her view, flowery language didn't matter. She preferred pragmatic people—those suited for governance.","As for the rhetorically brilliant and exceptionally talented, they could be thrown into the Hanlin Academy to compile books or teach. That would be good enough.","Empty talk harmed the nation. Having literary talent without the ability to govern a region meant only that a person could study well, not that they were the talent the court needed—someone capable of governing the country and benefiting the people.","\"Your Excellency,\" Ji Hongming stepped forward first, bowed, and said, \"The essays of the top three candidates are all exceptionally written. It is only in their strategies for managing the drought that their views differ sharply, leading to a deadlock.\"","He paused for breath, swept a glance at the other examiners, and continued slowly, \"All three policy essays address the drought topic, but their underlying frameworks are entirely different. That is the crux of our dispute. As to who should take the top spot, we await the decision of Your Excellency and His Highness the Crown Prince.\"","Before Ji Hongming could continue, another examiner, Minister Hu, clasped his hands and said, \"Your Excellency, I believe this particular paper should be ranked first. Its writing, every word and sentence, aligns with the teachings of the sages.\"","\"The measures it proposes—reducing meals, offering sacrifices to heaven, punishing corruption, selecting virtuous officials... are all perfectly proper, with no errors...\"","Before he could finish, Ji Hongming coldly interjected, \"Yet if you look at a thousand years of disaster relief memorials, they are largely the same. In an ordinary year, this would be a stable, superior strategy. But this year's drought is not limited to one province or one region. Nor is it confined to our Great Yan alone. I fear this approach suffers from failing to move beyond clichés.\"","Minister Hu's face turned ugly at being interrupted. Seeing Minister Hu defeated, Minister Wang quickly said, \"Your Excellency, I recommend this paper for first place.\"","\"Its writing is grand in vision, pointing directly at the core issues. It proposes using official positions to attract merchant investment, with the people building and officials supervising. It aims not only to manage the drought but to reshape the entire landscape. We...\"","\"However,\" before Minister Wang could finish, Minister Hu sharply interrupted, \"A nationwide survey, a decade-long dedicated effort, merchant shares and government funds—all require enormous resources. It involves systemic reform and upsets entrenched bureaucratic interests. I fear it is more than the current court can bear. The argument is most valuable, but also most dangerous.\""]},{"number":417,"title":"Chapter 417: Seeking a Son-in-Law from the List of Successful Candidates","paragraphs":["Grand Councilor Wang shot a glare at Grand Councilor Hu, but after some thought, he found his argument somewhat reasonable—it was difficult to implement and would take time, and given the current drought, the Great Yan Empire could not afford to wait.","Ji Hongming, seeing that the two had both backed down, spoke unhurriedly: “Only this one—every word is grounded in reality, not a single false statement.","Labor, grain, funds, canals, wells, and silver all have clear provisions, and it seems it could be immediately dispatched to the prefectures and counties for implementation. Therefore, I recommend it as the top-ranked paper.”","Grand Councilor Wang flicked his sleeve in rebuttal: “However, his essay lacks a certain artistry, missing the sage ideal of ‘governing by non-action.’ Moreover, the policy of ‘relief through labor’...”","He glanced cautiously at Yue Fuguang, who sat in the presiding seat, and continued, “...was originally proposed by the Junior Preceptor’s people. He is merely picking up crumbs from the Junior Preceptor’s table.”","By now, Yue Fuguang understood the three men completely. Grand Councilor Wang favored essays that were elegant, ornate, and bold in speech.","Grand Councilor Hu was conservative, preferring essays that were balanced, moderate, and substantive in content.","Minister Ji, much like herself, valued practicality above all.","Yue Fuguang had already made up her mind, but she still asked the Crown Prince: “Your Highness, what do you think? Which one should be the top scholar?”","The Crown Prince pondered for a moment and said, “Minister Ji’s paper is like coarse grain—it sustains life; Grand Councilor Hu’s paper is like ritual etiquette—it steadies people’s hearts; Grand Councilor Wang’s paper is like strong medicine—it cures illness, but it may be too potent.”","Seeing the others lost in thought, he continued, “At present, holding a ritual sacrifice to heaven could calm the people. But if the rain still does not come after the sacrifice, what will the court do then? Distant water cannot quench a near fire.”","He pushed open the window and stared into the pitch-black night sky. The bright moon was hidden, and the stars were twinkling—tomorrow was sure to be a clear day.","“A ruler must understand that writing’s value lies in its feasibility, not in its recitability. If we select Paper C as the top, we win posthumous fame; if we select Paper A, we save the people of today.”","Yue Fuguang nodded. Exchanging a glance with the Crown Prince, she picked up the three papers on the table and said, “Paper B is mediocre—it can be placed in the second rank, for those who maintain the status quo; Paper C is florid in style yet substantive—it can be placed at the end of the first rank, to be preserved for the future; only Paper A is immediately actionable—let it be crowned as the top.”","With Yue Fuguang having the final say, she left the rest to others and did not wait until dawn before taking a carriage back to her residence.","On the day the list was posted, she did not go to watch the excitement. Back in the sixth year of Yuankang, she had gone once to watch, and she could only say that the scene of examination candidates waiting for the list surpassed the desperation of expectant fathers pacing outside a maternity ward.","Those who passed cried and laughed, almost insane. Though not as mad as Fan Jin in the story, it was true that civilized men lost all pretense of civility.","The failed ones turned pale and dejected. In short, tears filled the scene—successful ones cried with joy, the unsuccessful with grief.","She had even seen an old man with gray hair carried away by his family. But even that family was lucky—though the father failed, his son barely scraped by, earning a spot as an associate scholar.","“Seventh Sister, it’s a pity you didn’t come today. You should have seen those families trying to snatch the sons-in-law at the list—they nearly came to blows over a single scholar!”","Yu Ningxuan picked up the tea on Yue Fuguang’s table, took a sip, and continued, “This batch of scholars—every unmarried one—was snatched up to be a son-in-law!”","Hearing that the classic scene of “snatching sons-in-law at the list” had occurred this time, Yue Fuguang was indeed intrigued. “Then it must have been even more lively. Why didn’t anyone try to snatch a son-in-law in the last examination?”","Yu Ningxin chuckled at Yue Fuguang’s question. “It wasn’t that no one went hunting for sons-in-law in the last examination. They all held back because they knew in advance that our younger sister would be watching the excitement.”","Yu Ningxuan nodded in agreement. “Wasn’t it chaotic? Imperial censor Zhang and Vice Minister Liu each grabbed one arm of the same young graduate and pulled. I actually saw tears streaming down the young graduate’s face—I couldn’t tell if it was from excitement or pain.”","“If Academician Liu hadn’t suddenly stepped in to mediate and then snatched the prize for himself, those two families might have come to blows.” Yu Ningxuan wore an expression of pure delight at the spectacle. “By the time we left, Imperial Censor Zhang and Vice Minister Liu had already stormed over to Academician Liu’s house. I bet the fight among those three families is still going on.”","Yue Fuguang was very curious about the man at the center of this dispute. Who could be so sought after? He must have either outstanding talent or good looks.","She had stayed in the examination hall for a full nine days, and with her excellent memory, she had remembered most of the candidates by name and face—especially the talented and the handsome ones, who left deeper impressions. As she sifted through her memories of the unmarried young men, she turned to Yu Ningxuan, who was nibbling on pastries. “Second Sister, which graduate are they fighting over? I might even know him.”","Yu Ningxuan paused for a moment, then nodded eagerly. “Right, right! How could I forget? Dear Sister, you are technically their chief examiner.”","Yu Ningxin chimed in with a smile. “This year’s examination has drawn more families hunting for sons-in-law under the announcement board than usual. Maybe it’s all because of you, little sister, being the chief examiner!”","Yu Ningxuan agreed with a nod. As for the crown prince, who was the head examiner... the emperor was still in his prime, so not everyone was eager to have such a person as their mentor. Even if the crown prince’s position as heir was stable for now, how many throughout history had actually ascended the throne from that role? And even those who did—how many were secure in the beginning?","But her little sister, the Junior Preceptor and Prince, was different. She not only held a noble position, but she was also known as a divine maiden, with poetic talent unmatched across all six kingdoms. Anyone with sense would want to be her student.","With this thought, Yu Ningxuan’s face glowed with pride. She broke into a wide smile. “I heard from the onlookers that the graduate being fought over is the tenth-ranked scholar of this year, named Zhao Pengfei. Judging by his clothes, his family is ordinary. Still, he’s young and good-looking—much better than those widowers.”","In this year’s examination, even widowers with children were being snatched up by lesser families eager to form marriage ties. That was rare in previous years. Perhaps it really was because of their little sister’s reputation as their mentor.","Zhao Pengfei? Yue Fuguang recalled him without much effort. He was indeed among the younger candidates and was handsome among the unmarried ones. No wonder someone was rushing to claim him as a son-in-law.","As for the three families, Yue Fuguang had a vague impression they were all well-off. But people of that standing normally wouldn’t marry a legitimate daughter off to a mere new graduate whose future was uncertain.","Still, in Yue Fuguang’s view—dominated by modern ideas about marriage—Zhao Pengfei was hardly an ideal match.","“Little Zhu, what do you think of this Zhao Pengfei?” Hearing Yue Fuguang ask a question to which she already knew the answer, the system couldn’t help rolling its eyes.","But despite the eye roll, the system always answered when asked. [Master, which aspect do you want to know? Ability or character?]","When it comes to ability, setting aside other factors, Little Zhu currently rates as above average.","As for character, Zhao Pengfei—having passed the imperial examinations at a young age—is somewhat arrogant due to his talent, and he shares a common flaw of most mortal men in this era: he is overly chauvinistic and possesses a strong desire for control."]},{"number":418,"title":"Chapter 418: Praying for Rain","paragraphs":["As for his family, his birth mother had died early, and after he passed the imperial exam at the county level, his father remarried a wealthy merchant's widow who had returned to her natal home. So not only did he have half-siblings from his father's side, he also had a stepbrother and stepsister with no blood relation to him.","Upon hearing this, Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin didn't even furrow their brows. This kind of small household was still considered simple; the troubles in wealthy families were far more complicated than those of the Zhao family.","Yue Fuguang observed their composed expressions and noticed how elegant they had grown, so she couldn't help asking, \"Have the elders in your family brought up the matter of marriage for you two?\"","The elders in their family were open to advice. In this generation, whether boys or girls, they were marrying a year or two later than was typical. Especially Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin, who were closer to Yue Fuguang—one was seventeen, the other sixteen. By conventional standards, they were already at marriageable age, yet neither had a prospective family arranged. She wondered what the elders had in mind.","When talk turned to marriage, Yu Ningxin shyly lowered her head, while Yu Ningxuan said casually, \"Your second uncle and aunt said that my betrothal still needs your final approval, little sister. They said only the talented man you endorse is the right match.\"","Among the dozen or so children in their generation, only the eldest elder brother and second elder brother had married, and both unions were certified by their younger sister. The elder brothers and their wives really did get along well, and there were no messy concubines or chambermaids in their households.","To be honest, the brothers in the family were all kept busy running errands for their younger sister; they had no time for those messy thoughts. Elegant pastimes like \"a beauty adding fragrance to the ink\" didn't exist in their home.","Yu Ningxin's face flushed slightly as she smiled softly. \"Father and Mother share the same sentiment. They also think the matches you select are more reliable.\"","Faced with their trusting gazes, Yue Fuguang pressed her hand to her forehead. The Yu family elders had been scared stiff by the tragic fates in store for the younger generation in the original timeline—each one's marriage more miserable than the last.","She could help vet potential spouses, but in the end, the elders should select the candidates. Otherwise, having her, a person who seldom went out, pick husbands for them—she really didn't have many good prospects.","\"Alright. If either of you takes a fancy to anyone, just tell me. I'll help you evaluate him!\" Anyone's deeds could be thoroughly investigated from childhood to the present.","\"We're in no rush to marry, and we haven't set our sights on any young man yet.\" Yu Ningxuan was very open and straightforward.","Under her influence—or rather, the family's influence—the young men in the capital had also been marrying later in recent years. If no suitable marriage prospects could be found in other families, raising a good husband for the two elder sisters from scratch wasn't out of the question.","Yue Fuguang's thoughts made her rub her hands together eagerly. Seeing her expression, the two sisters laughed and said, \"Little sister, don't trouble yourself. We have never worried that the daughters of the Yu family won't find good in-laws!\"","As Yue Fuguang's sisters, they weren't concerned about failing to secure good husbands. If all else failed, they could always bring a son-in-law into the family.","After the palace examination, when the new top scholar led his fellow successful candidates on a horse parade through the streets, it was already the end of the second month. The days grew warmer by the day, with the sun hanging high—not a hint of rain in the sky.","Because of the drought, this year's parade for the new scholars was greatly diminished in splendor.","Time quietly slipped into the third month. Yue Fuguang still hadn't found a good match for her two sisters, nor had she found any suitable candidates to raise as husbands; but news came from court first: the Emperor was planning a sacrificial ceremony to pray for rain.","The Dayan Empire had been suffering drought for over six months. The water reserves stored earlier in various regions had mostly been poured onto the fields for spring sowing. If there was still no rain, not to mention whether the newly planted crops could sprout and grow—the people's drinking water, consumed daily and used at will, wouldn't last more than a few months.","So even though Yue Fuguang had long mentioned a three-year great drought, the petitions from both court and countryside left the Emperor no choice. Even just to show the people his attitude, the rain-praying ceremony was absolutely necessary.","As for the \"Edict of Self-Blame,\" the Emperor had conducted a thorough self-criticism back in the second month. Heaven still hadn't forgiven him!","\"Master, the Emperor won't be able to bring down a single drop of rain. What's all this fuss for?\"","Emperor Mingxi: Do you think I don't know I don't have that much face? But if I don't go through these paces, not only won't the uninformed court officials agree, but I also can't account to the common people!","For centuries, whenever a major natural disaster struck, which imperial household hadn't prayed to heaven? Whether it worked or not was secondary—at least it showed the right attitude!","\"Just treat it as a 'show' staged for the world, and it won't be hard to understand.\"","Even as she said this, Yue Fuguang knew she couldn't stay idle any longer. Ever since she removed those who doubted her title as Goddess from her congregation, the remaining believers were mostly relatively devout.","One must be gentle with one's own fans. Besides, she had already collected enough storage pearls. It was time to summon the dragon—to call down the rain.","\"Master, the Emperor can't do it, but you can. Do you want to take charge?\"","The system's question suddenly silenced the heated discussion in the court hall. Xie Zhiyan reacted first, stepping forward immediately. \"Your Imperial Father, I believe...\"","But Yue Fuguang didn't bother listening to what the Crown Prince said. She thought for a moment. Just as everyone assumed she wouldn't respond, they suddenly heard her speak. \"Given the divine power I've recovered so far, it's impossible to cover the entire territory of the Great Yan in one go.\"","\"Wouldn't that be perfect? We can take the chance to go out and play. To be honest, this capital city is just too dull!\"","Those who were constantly watching Yue Fuguang's expression immediately saw the Young Master's eyes light up.","So, while the rulers and ministers of Dayan pretended to be busy discussing an auspicious day for the prayer ceremony, they overheard the answer they had been eagerly awaiting.","Yue Fuguang's voice was calm, but loud enough to stir most of the people in the hall.","\"Your Majesty, leave the rainmaking to me.\"","Upon hearing this, Emperor Mingxi was so excited that he abruptly rose from his dragon throne. He took a step towards Yue Fuguang before asking with half-certainty, \"Fuguang, did I hear you correctly? You say to leave the rainmaking to you? You... you can bring rain?\"","\"Praying for rain? As if He deserves the honor. Isn't that something anyone with a pair of hands can do?\"","Yue Fuguang looked at the Emperor's flushed face and his clenched fists, and couldn't resist teasing, \"Your Majesty, I'm not trying to pour cold water on you, but no matter how many times you pray, it's useless.\"","\"So... let me handle it. I guarantee I'll bring the rain.\"","Faced with Yue Fuguang's blunt words and her attitude that showed no deference, Emperor Mingxi was not angry but delighted instead. He let out a few hearty laughs, sweeping away the months of pent-up gloom in his heart, before saying, \"Fuguang is right. I also feel that this rain-praying ceremony might not succeed.\"","He sat back on his throne, sighed rather helplessly, and said, \"Nevertheless, to reassure the common people, even knowing it's futile, I have to grit my teeth and go through the motions. I can only hope Heaven shows mercy.\"","He looked at Yue Fuguang seriously and said, \"To be honest with you, Fuguang, I've already drafted my second 'Edict of Self-Blame.' If this prayer fails, I'll have to issue it.\"","Yue Fuguang toyed with the beads in her hand and raised an eyebrow. \"Your Majesty, you are in luck. I have some skills in this field. If all goes well, I can likely relieve Dayan of this drought.\""]},{"number":419,"title":"Chapter 419: Seeing Off","paragraphs":["Emperor Mingxi naturally knew that as long as Yue Fuguang was willing to act, Great Yan would be secure, and he couldn’t help asking, “Fuguang, what do we need to do for the rain prayer?”","He wondered if her process was the same as his own, in which case, aside from the dragon robe and what the Imperial Observatory and the Ministry of Rites had prepared, those could be given to her use.","Yue Fuguang shook her head. “My rain doesn’t require as much trouble as Your Majesty does.”","[Exactly. Begging Heaven, It won’t send rain anyway. Better we do it ourselves!]","Yue Fuguang and her system had naturally guessed that the world’s Heaven had some request of them, so they grew bolder and bolder, not holding back when ridiculing it.","Besides, they weren’t wrong. Bound by certain rules, Heaven could do nothing at all. The “landlord” truly wasn’t as effective as they were—the monks from afar who found it easier to recite sutras.","When everyone heard this, they understood, but Emperor Mingxi still couldn’t resist asking, “Is there anything we should do?”","Yue Fuguang paused to think. “Your Majesty, with my current limited power, I cannot make rain fall simultaneously across all of Great Yan.”","“So Fuguang means you wish to leave the capital?” Emperor Mingxi immediately guessed her plan. Wasn’t she only taking this on to get out of the city?","“Absolutely not, it’s out of the question!” Ling Yinghua exclaimed in agitation. “Chaos is brewing across states, and they’ve long coveted the Grand Mentor. If they confirm the Grand Mentor has the power to bring rain, they will surely scheme. Far from the capital, how can we ensure the Grand Mentor’s safety?”","Rain was important, but the Grand Mentor was more important! If Heaven wouldn’t send rain, Great Yan could tough it out for two or three years—it wasn’t enough to cripple the state. But without the Grand Mentor, they...","“Minister Ling is right. The Grand Mentor’s safety is paramount. I beg Your Majesty to reconsider!” Wu Yuanjing also stepped forward to echo Ling Yinghua.","Minister Wang Shouchen of the Honglu Temple weighed the pros and cons and also stepped forward. “I concur with the two ministers. The Grand Mentor’s safety must be the first priority.”","Because Great Yan had prepared in advance, their situation was far better than that of neighboring states. They had not yet reached a desperate point. The Grand Mentor was one of a kind in the world; lose her and she’d be truly gone. There was no need to risk her.","Yue Fuguang looked around. Only the conservative older faction opposed her, while the younger, more vigorous officials kept their heads down—neither supporting nor opposing, making their stance clear.","“I understand what you venerable ministers worry about. Not only are my personal guards all formidable fighters, but Your Majesty can also dispatch more soldiers to accompany me.”","[Besides, we’re within Great Yan’s borders. What’s there to fear? Those emperors can’t send tens of thousands of troops infiltrating just to grab her, can they?","If so, it only means the emperor and his courtiers are incompetent!]","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers, cursed as incompetent by the divine artifact again, looked aggrieved. They were only worried about the Grand Mentor’s safety. If the drought dragged on for two or three years, those desperate emperors might indeed mobilize armies just for one person!","The Grand Mentor still didn’t realize her own importance!","Emperor Mingxi took one look at Yue Fuguang, whose face clearly read “I want to get out of here,” and knew he couldn’t dissuade her. For the sake of the people and Great Yan, he said no more. With a grand wave of his hand, he declared, “Ministers, say no more. Let it be as Fuguang proposes. As Great Yan commands the nation’s strength, how can it fail to protect one person?”","He swept his gaze over the ranks. “Shen Jian, lead your thousand Feather Forests. Wei Shouyi, lead your fifteen hundred New Army to escort the Grand Mentor, ensuring her full safety.”","“My dear minister Huo, order all regional garrisons to be on high alert. Every place the Grand Mentor passes must guard her with full loyalty. Should any harm befall her, the civil and military officials there will answer with their heads!”","Then he looked toward the civil officials. Feng Tang and Wu Yong almost simultaneously stepped forward, volunteering, “We beg Your Majesty’s permission to accompany the Grand Mentor!”","Emperor Mingxi did not grant permission on the spot. Instead, he turned to Yue Fuguang for her opinion. “What does Fuguang think?”","Wherever Yue Fuguang went, she would inevitably have to deal with local officials. Given her nature, she would surely find such matters tedious, so she needed someone to handle these chores—someone with a rank high enough to keep those regional magnates in line.","Emperor Mingxi could already imagine that once she went to the provinces, those officials, grinning with flattery, would be even more eager than they were for imperial princes and princesses. Feng Tang and the others might not be able to hold them back.","But Yue Fuguang was quite satisfied with the two choices. She nodded. “I find both of them suitable.”","“Your Majesty, rest assured, we will protect the Grand Mentor!” Feng Tang and Wu Yong, delighted at her approval, quickly pledged allegiance to Emperor Mingxi.","Seeing this, Emperor Mingxi decided he would later give Feng Tang a talisman and a sword. With those, no one would dare act rashly.","Shen Jian and Wei Shouyi, standing in the ranks, watched the two officials’ ingratiating faces and gritted their teeth behind smiles. What did they mean by “we will protect the Grand Mentor”? That was clearly their duty! Did these two literati think he and his soldiers were mere decorations?","Yue Fuguang was a woman of action. From deciding to depart to the entourage leaving the upper capital’s city gates, it took only three days.","On the sixth day of the third month, in the eighth year of Yuan Kang—auspicious for travel, relocating graves, and sacrifices.","Yue Fuguang stood atop her carriage, waving farewell to the women of the Yu family. “Grandmother, Mother, go back now. Don’t worry, Cuizhu and the others will take good care of me.”","Yue Fuguang did not claim she would take care of herself. In the eyes of Yu family women, their darling child was perfect in every way except for self-care, which was far inferior to loyal servants like Cuizhu.","The sky had not yet fully brightened, and the morning mist still lingered at the foot of the imperial city wall. Yue Fuguang’s entourage arrived at the city gates, where banners fluttered far into the distance, stretching from the gates to the outskirts beyond.","Yue Fuguang looked out through the window. At the Vermilion Gate, several thousand soldiers in full armor stood silently on both sides of the city road, their light-steel armor and halberds gleaming coldly in the morning light.","Amidst the dark sea of soldiers, the imperial yellow stood out prominently, followed by purple and red robes, while the blue and green robes were lost in the crush of people.","The Yue flag, bearing her surname, unfurled gently in the breeze. Embroidered with golden and silver threads, the moon and rolling clouds glittered in the first light—a fiery gold impossible to ignore.","Yue Fuguang suspected the emperor might come to see her off, but she hadn’t expected such a grand spectacle. She silently grumbled that the emperor was skilled at winning hearts as she adjusted her dress and stepped slowly off the carriage.","“Your Majesty, Honorable Ministers,” Yue Fuguang greeted the crowd with a nod.","Behind the emperor, she spotted her grandfather and father, their faces a mix of pride and infinite worry. So that was why her grandfather hadn’t seen her off at the mansion gate—he had come all the way to the city gate.","“Fuguang, this journey will be long. The road will be hard. Above all, take care of yourself, and never harm your own well-being just for the sake of rain!” Emperor Mingxi exhorted her like an elder.","“Indeed, Grand Mentor, please, put yourself first!”"]},{"number":420,"title":"Chapter 420: Perform a Magic Trick","paragraphs":["In the eyes of Emperor Mingxi and his court, Immortal Lord Yue Fuguang had descended to the mortal world, now bound by flesh and blood like any other. Though she received incense offerings and worship, she was ultimately still a mortal being.","To perform divine deeds with a mortal body was no simple matter—it wasn’t like the small-scale antics of summoning a thunderclap or a drizzle back in the day. She would have to traverse the entire Great Yan Empire. Such exertion could truly harm her foundation, and if that happened, they would have suffered a great loss!","“Your Majesty, rest assured. Since I dared to take on this task, I have full confidence that I can accomplish it,” she said.","The Great Yan had been preparing for this drought—lasting over two years now—since two years ago. And she, Yue Fuguang, had begun her own preparations even earlier than that!","This rain wouldn’t just fall once or twice. Fortunately, the power of the incense offerings enhanced her abilities, allowing her to accomplish divine feats through her own strength. Otherwise, if she had to rely entirely on the Cloud Rain Talismans from the system shop like she initially planned, she would have ended up at a massive loss!","Emperor Mingxi, hearing her confidence, nodded repeatedly. He turned and took a purple-gold emblem inscribed with “As if the Emperor himself were present” from Eunuch Qian, personally hanging it on the bronze ring of Yue Fuguang’s carriage.","“Fuguang, this journey of yours is akin to my own imperial tour of the realm. With this emblem, you have the authority to execute local officials first and report later.”","Yue Fuguang’s fingers lightly brushed the smooth tassels hanging from the emblem, and she chuckled lightly. “With your words, Your Majesty, I won’t hold back. If I end up moving against your beloved ministers, don’t come asking me to spare them later.”","Her journey wouldn’t simply be about summoning rain.","She had, after all, managed to clean up the Great Yan court to a certain degree. At least now, important decrees wouldn’t be leaked to irrelevant parties before they were announced.","But the provincial regions were a different story. As the old saying went, “The emperor’s power doesn’t reach beyond the county.” With poor transportation and blocked information in this ancient world, local magistrates all acted like petty tyrants in their own territories.","Another saying went, “A county magistrate can ruin a family; a prefectural governor can bring down an entire clan.” Who knew how many scourges were waiting for her to eliminate, or how many parasites were waiting to be rooted out?","This journey would serve as clearing out hidden dangers at home before the Great Yan could expand its borders. Otherwise, if the provinces were unstable, no matter how much territory they conquered, none of it could be held.","Emperor Mingxi’s face bloomed with a smile at her words. He waved his hand with great boldness and said, “Fuguang, act boldly. I’ll have your back in everything!”","Wei Ping and Cai Xuan, watching the exchange between His Majesty and the Grand Tutor, couldn’t help but twitch their eyelids. Their mouths twisted, and if the occasion hadn’t been so formal, they might have rushed over to grab the Grand Tutor’s robe and begged her to go easy, whispering, “Ancestor, please break the news slowly and clean house gently. Our workload is already endless!”","The aristocratic families’ cases still weren’t closed. The investigations into opium and White Flower Blight were ongoing. If major cases from the provinces got dragged in, they really would be worked to death in their posts!","Yue Fuguang caught the weary faces of the two ministers in her peripheral vision, their expressions far more haggard than their peers. She decided to take a sustainable approach. After squeezing them dry for so long, it was time to offer a sweet reward.","“Little Zhu,” she thought. “The provinces of Great Yan aren’t clean. I’ll need Cai Xuan and Wei Ping for a long time yet. In their current condition, they might not hold up much longer.”","【What does my master intend to do?】","Cai Xuan and Wei Ping both mentally nodded like crazy. Yes, yes! The Grand Tutor has finally seen our hardships! We beg you to take it slow!","“Give them each one Health-Building Pill. And honestly, Emperor Mingxi works them so hard, just look at how aged they’ve become!”","The warm bond between ruler and minister lasted only a moment before Emperor Mingxi found himself suddenly slapped with a huge, invisible pot as a scapegoat.","An aggrieved Emperor Mingxi thought: These two have been run ragged, and honestly, the only one in the entire court who doesn’t realize why is this very ancestor!","Human joys and sorrows were not the same. Emperor Mingxi bore the blame, while his two loyal ministers received Health-Building Pills—specially granted to them by Yue Fuguang alone. Those two really had faces as thick as a dog’s hide!","Emperor Mingxi squinted sideways at Big Cake Face and Pot Helmet Face, who were desperately suppressing their grins. His heart was full of disdain.","Wei Ping and Cai Xuan, however, couldn’t care less about their emperor’s expression at that moment. Their hearts were pounding, their hands trembling. Happiness had come too suddenly—all they could do was clench their fists and grit their teeth to barely suppress the urge to leap with joy.","Feng Tang, standing beside them, caught sight of their twisted expressions. He couldn’t help but roll his eyes and hissed through his teeth, “Wipe those looks off your faces. Careful—if the emperor catches on, he’ll tear you both apart!”","The two lowered their heads, pinching their own thighs while silently grumbling that the censor’s mouth truly spoke not a single likable word—except, of course, when addressing the Grand Tutor.","Before they could complain much longer, a sudden warm current surged from the soles of their feet, slowly spreading through their entire bodies.","When the warmth rushed into his head, Wei Ping felt the wrinkles on his face smooth out ever so slightly. He had no mirror to check his own reflection, but cleverly used Cai Xuan as one. Staring at him was like looking at himself.","The two locked eyes in a “deeply affectionate” gaze, drawing looks of envy, jealousy, and eye-rolling disgust from their fellow officials.","Emperor Mingxi was envious, but he still had to maintain the dignity of a sovereign. He only cleared his throat lightly to make everyone rein in their faces that practically screamed they’d trade places with her.","Lord Chong: Your royal face isn’t much better than ours!","“Your Majesty, I’m off then!” Yue Fuguang acted as if she hadn’t noticed the extra longing for the Body-Strengthening Pill in their gazes.","Emperor Mingxi nodded, the morning light falling perfectly on his face, which was etched with reluctance and the fear that she might never return. “Fuguang, take care on your journey. Most importantly... come back soon!”","Yue Fuguang then looked at the officials behind the emperor, who wore equally worried expressions. What did they take her for?","A runaway?","She had long wanted to travel beyond the capital, but this time she was heading out for serious business, not for fun.","Yue Fuguang turned and climbed into her magnificent carriage. Emperor Mingxi naturally gave her a hand.","She thanked him with a smile, and just as her figure was about to disappear inside the carriage, she suddenly turned back to the emperor with a mysterious grin. “Your Majesty, let me show you a magic trick.”","Emperor Mingxi looked puzzled. Magic? Did she mean illusion?","Before he could ask, Yue Fuguang turned her back, waved at him, and called out in a louder voice, “Move out!”","The carriage slowly began to move. The wheels rolled over the official road, producing a dull, steady rumble that drowned out the soft clatter of the Imperial Guard’s armor.","Passing through the towering city gates, she left behind the majestic capital of Shangjing, the farewell party, and all those complicated gazes.","“Wind, arise!”","“Clouds, arise!”","Everyone heard Yue Fuguang’s calm voice drifting from the carriage as it faded into the distance, the words ringing clearly in their ears.","As her words fell, a cool wind sprang up out of nowhere, and rolling clouds surged in on the wind.","In an instant, pitch-black storm clouds shrouded everything within sight.","Commoners who had stayed indoors pushed open their windows to look outside; some even reached out their hands to feel the faint moisture the wind carried.","“Rain, come!” Yue Fuguang’s fair little hand pointed toward the sky."]},{"number":421,"title":"Chapter 421: What a Heavy Rain","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang’s hand seemed to open a valve in the clouds of the sky, and the rain fell in wisps and threads, growing heavier, pattering and splashing as it drenched this long-parched earth.","“Father, Mother! It’s really raining!”","“Hahaha, it’s raining!”","“Heavens, finally it rains!”","Amid the wind and rain, Yue Fuguang’s divine manifestation flickered in and out of view, truly like a compassionate goddess overlooking the mortal world from above.","“Father, Mother, it’s not the heavens—it’s the Divine Lady!” Everyone, even three-year-old children in the capital, knew why the Divine Lady had left the city. Now that the heavens had sent down rain to moisten the land, surely the Divine Lady had revealed her power!","“Father, Mother, look! Isn’t that the Divine Lady standing in the sky?” The sharp-eyed child saw the solemn and majestic divine manifestation through the curtain of rain.","“Little one, don’t point at the Divine Lady—that’s great disrespect!” His parents quickly pulled him down to kneel.","“Wah wah wah, this old man bows in gratitude for the Divine Lady’s great grace!”","As soon as Yue Fuguang’s divine manifestation appeared, the common people streamed out of their homes, tilting their heads in awe to gaze at the heavenly form.","“So this is what the Divine Lady looks like? She’s six or seven parts like the statue enshrined in my home!”","“To see the Divine Lady’s heavenly countenance in these few days, this old man can die without regret!”","“Divine Lady...”","Lying in the carriage with her eyes closed, Yue Fuguang faintly heard a jumble of murmured wishes, laughter, and weeping.","Within the capital and the surrounding areas covered by rain, the people, after kowtowing in thanks to the divine likeness, laughed or cried aloud under the downpour soaking their heads.","The emperor, still standing at the city gate in the rain, waved away Qian Gui, who wanted to hold an umbrella over him. He stood silently in place, watching Yue Fuguang’s departing carriage until it became a blurry black speck at the end of the official road, feeling a hollow ache in his heart.","The rain pattered down, and the wind, heavy with moisture, stirred the jade tassels on his crown, producing an extremely soft, clear sound like jade pieces tapping together. This soft note, mingled with the laughter, weeping, and prayers directed at the divine manifestation from the distant city, composed a melody named Hope.","Behind Emperor Mingxi, the assembled officials also looked up at the heavenly form above. The rain struck their faces in this long-awaited, life-giving downpour, and no one spoke.","Only the Yu family—father and sons—gazed into the distance at the vanishing carriage. After a moment, they let out, almost inaudibly, a long sigh that only they themselves could hear. That breath blended into the joyful rain, leaving no trace. Their daughter Yue Fuguang might claim she had given up on Dayan, yet over the past few years, in countless small ways, she had done much for Dayan and its people.","Yue Fuguang: For points, for the mission, I don’t hesitate to say one thing and do another!","Among the clamor of shock and joy, none were more stunned than the envoys from the other kingdoms who had come to see her off. They knew Yue Fuguang was no ordinary person—they had seen her summon thunder, rain, and ice before—but those had been small in scale. This time, the volume and range of the rain far surpassed anything before.","If she truly traveled all the way across Dayan like this, then... then wouldn’t Dayan’s drought be resolved?","And that bright figure in the sky—that was called a manifestation, wasn’t it?","This was power only a deity possessed. Though they had already believed in their hearts that Yue Fuguang was a divine lady descended to earth, even if she had a divine origin, she still had a mortal body. Yet what she had done now far exceeded what any mortal could do.","They thought they had already held her in very high regard, but now their understanding was shattered once more.","The delegates from North Yue exchanged glances, seeing deep fear and endless worry in each other’s eyes.","If the people of the other kingdoms learned that the Divine Lady of Dayan truly possessed supernatural power, then... would they still be willing to remain subjects of North Li, West Qiang, South Zhao, or South Yue?","If it were them, what choice would they make?","Thinking of the fervor among their own people toward Yue Fuguang, a chill of ice settled in their hearts.","At this moment, they truly feared that if Yue Fuguang raised her arm to rally their subjects, the consequences...","Just as the answer was about to surface in their minds, Emperor Mingxi’s voice reached their ears: “Minister Huo, send a few teams in different directions to find out how far this rain has spread.”","“Your humble subject obeys!” Huo Ying accepted solemnly, watching the emperor and the line of officials’ carriages fade into the distance.","He turned back and scanned the city gate, which had resumed its usual order. Apart from the deep and shallow wheel ruts in the mud, it was as if nothing had happened—and yet, as if a turning point in an era had just passed through here.","The rain, and especially heavy rain—something as vital as life itself to Dayan’s people—spread to surrounding prefectures and counties within two days.","Along with the news of the rain came word that the Junior Preceptor Yue Fuguang was touring the realm on behalf of the emperor.","The rumor that wherever her carriage passed, heavy rain would fall grew wider and wider.","Before her convoy had even left Quanzhou, where the capital was located, the news had already flown ahead of her like wings.","Yue Fuguang spread clouds and summoned rain as she traveled. Though she had energy-storing beads to rely on, she still had to occasionally chant and direct wind and clouds—without clouds, even a fake deity like her couldn’t conjure something from nothing.","So the most tired parts of her body, aside from her rear end from sitting in the carriage, were her pale, delicate hands from making hand seals.","Fortunately, she had promoted cement soon after arriving and strongly supported paving the important sections of Dayan’s official roads. Over the past two years, the results were significant; otherwise, this journey would have been far more miserable!","“Chunying, why has the carriage stopped?” Yue Fuguang had drifted off to sleep amid the rocking and swaying, but the halt woke her.","In less than five days out, she had quickly mastered the art of conserving her strength while effectively summoning rain. At present, she could ensure abundant rainfall within fifty li of her position, so she would only bring the rain down after the convoy had traveled some distance. They shouldn’t have gone twenty li yet in this short time.","“Milady, we’ve entered Qiyang County. The roadsides are lined with commoners, and a few are blocking the way ahead.”","Shen Chunying rested her right hand on the sword at her waist, scanning the dense crowd of people kneeling silently on either side of the road.","For now, she sensed no ill intent from them, but her heart remained on guard, without the slightest relaxation.","Though her lady was bringing rain to do good deeds and save the people, there was no guarantee that troublemakers might not sneak among the crowd to cause chaos.","“Do you know why the people are blocking the road?” Yue Fuguang wondered silently if this was a classic case of petitioning the emperor while blocking her path—a trope she had seen plenty of in films and TV shows. Should she take up their case or not?","“Milady, Minister Yu has already gone to inquire and should be back soon,” Shen Chunying replied.","Her words had barely fallen when they saw Yu Mochun and Yu Huaixian hurrying back.","Over the past two years, Yu Mochun had been training with the guards, recovering the martial skills he had let lapse in earlier years, becoming much stronger than when Yue Fuguang first met him.","Seeing sweat on his brow and his less-than-pleased expression, Yue Fuguang wondered if the situation ahead was tricky.","No matter how tricky—she had the convening authority as her mandate, and even high-ranking officials would be executed if they committed crimes!","For an instant, Yue Fuguang imagined countless scenes of corrupt officials oppressing the people, and a flash of murderous intent flickered through her mind."]},{"number":422,"title":"Chapter 422: What Are You Asking Me to Forgive","paragraphs":["Recently, the oddly-behaved System 07 rolled over in its space, turning its pristine white orb into a flattened pancake. It sensed Yue Fuguang's fleeting killing intent but chose not to intervene, closing its eyes to its own troubles—brooding over how to explain things to its host.","Unaware that her system harbored secrets, Yue Fuguang asked Yu Mochun, \"Fourth Uncle, what's happening up ahead?\"","\"Fuguang, there are some villagers blocking the road, seeking your forgiveness,\" Yu Mochun replied, wiping sweat from his brow. The heat was unseasonably intense.","What? Yue Fuguang almost had to clean out her ears. What was all this nonsense?","Seeking her forgiveness? Forgiveness for what? She didn't even know these people!","Could it be the Zhou family? No, that couldn't be. The grass on their graves was already overgrown. Even if they had reincarnated, they couldn't have become adults yet, let alone be blocking her path now.","\"Forgiveness for what?\" she asked.","Just then, the withdrawn System materialized in her hand. Its shimmering body rolled once before speaking telepathically: [Master, I know. They were once your worshippers. Because they angered you, they can no longer offer sacrifices to your statue. Now, they're blocking the road to atone and beg you to revoke your decree, allowing them to worship you again.]","Sure enough, what Yu Mochun and Yu Huaixian said next confirmed the System's words. Finally, Yu Huaixian said indignantly, \"These people use you when it suits them and discard you when it doesn't. They show no respect. In my opinion, you shouldn't forgive them.\"","Hearing that this was the issue, Yue Fuguang felt little emotional stir.","After all, in her homeland, useful gods were enshrined high, while those who proved ineffective—some even had cannons aimed at their temples—were not unheard of.","Of course, the God of Wealth was an exception. Whether effective or not, people would kneel for hours before his statue. Blasphemy? That simply didn't exist!","Still, understanding the situation was one thing, but Yue Fuguang didn't consider herself a magnanimous person. She lacked the tolerance to forgive easily. If they only realized their mistake today because of the lack of rain and begged for forgiveness, what about next time? What if they sought wealth, children, or other blessings, and she couldn't fulfill their wishes? Would they betray her again?","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Second Cousin is right. Since they cannot worship me, let them find another god to serve.\"","She smiled and waved her hand. \"There are many gods here—ones far more effective than I. There's no need to cling to one deity.\"","Her voice, light and serene, seemed casual but carried over two miles, sounding as though she were whispering directly into everyone's ears.","The villagers lining the roads bowed their heads lower, while the people kneeling to atone turned pale and mechanically knocked their foreheads against the ground in a dull thud, thud, thud.","Yue Fuguang sighed softly. \"I can no longer hear you.\"","Her words were gentle, carrying no stormy anger, no reproach or condemnation. Yet they were colder than any insult. It was as if she had removed a door from its frame, leaving only a wall where it once stood.","Those kneeling and chanting let their blood drip into the dust, flowing into the dry, cracked earth. But it was useless. The goddess could not hear them!","\"There's no need to kneel. Everyone, stand up.\" The villagers felt a gentle force lifting them to their feet.","As the creaking carriage passed by, her voice called out, \"Wind, come!\"","And a breeze swept through their coarse clothing and tangled, withered hair. Strands of hair brushed against their faces, blurring their vision but sharpening their hearing.","Then came, \"Clouds, come!\"","They felt a shadow suddenly gather above their heads. The scorching sun that had dried their hearts and cracked the earth was hidden behind thick, layered clouds.","The world darkened. As the wind surged and clouds rolled, the majestic presence of the goddess manifested. Before the crowd could recover from their shock, a not-so-loud command—\"Rain, come!\"—rang in their ears like thunder.","Instantly, wind and rain poured down in sheets, raindrops hitting the dry, hardened soil, forming coin-sized patterns like copper coins.","These patterns merged together, moistening the earth, and the villagers, like the newly planted crops, welcomed a rebirth.","\"Thank you, Goddess, for the rain!\"","\"Thank you, Goddess, for the rain!\"","\"Thank you, Goddess, for the rain!\"...","Along the path Yue Fuguang's convoy traveled, the villagers fell like cut wheat, kneeling in the direction of her carriage and pressing their foreheads into the mud. Sweat and rainwater mingled to drench the land beneath them.","Some attentive individuals even carried incense and candles, lighting them on the spot to offer prayers. Curiously, despite the heavy wind and rain that should have extinguished the flames, the incense lit successfully. Three slender trails of smoke rose gracefully in the downpour, faintly coalescing into the shape of the character \"abundance.\"","Seeing this, every villager rushed home as fast as they could, a single thought echoing in their minds: \"Offer incense!\"","They, too, had to present incense to the goddess! They, too, needed a bountiful harvest in their fields!","Having accomplished all this, Yue Fuguang took credit but also finally reaped rewards. Someone remembered to replenish her ammunition—no, rather, to replenish her incense offerings.","Without a massive influx of incense energy, her power would only last for a single round trip. Moreover, her abilities still had infinite potential for growth.","As Yue Fuguang walked, she brought down the long-awaited rain upon the land of Dayan. The path she tread, winding many times around Dayan, would later be called the Rainy Path by the people, also known as the Goddess Road.","This was years afterward, when Yue Fuguang, the goddess, had long left this world, yet traces of her presence remained. Whenever someone walked this road, the elderly would recall the goddess, recount how her rain had saved them, and tell more legends about her.","But that was a tale for later. For now, Yue Fuguang had only just completed the rain-making task over one prefecture. To avoid harming the crops in the fields, her carriage moved faster than usual.","After the convoy left Quanzhou, it headed straight for Yingzhou. On this day, Yue Fuguang and her party arrived at Yingchuan Prefecture in Yingzhou, named after the Yingchuan River that flowed through it.","Unfortunately, after more than half a year of drought, this jade-belt river had dried up, leaving only black silt and countless cracked fissures, like ugly scars on the river’s body.","When Yue Fuguang passed by, she paid special attention to this river. By the time her group headed toward Yingchuan City, where they would stay for the night, this mother river, over thirty miles from Yingchuan Prefecture, had begun to revive with faint signs of life.","Seeing that it was nearly time for the evening meal, the party, knowing Yue Fuguang must be hungry, quickened their pace.","Suddenly, the fast-moving carriage slowed down and came to a halt. Before Yue Fuguang could ask, He Jin approached the window and reported in a low voice, “My lady, we are about to enter Yingchuan City ahead. Huang Xie, the prefect of Yingchuan, has gathered all the officials and local gentry to await you at the Ten-Mile Pavilion.”","“Huang Xie, the prefect of Yingchuan?” Yue Fuguang recalled the file on this man she had once read.","Huang Xie, aged forty-six, was a jinshi of the fifth year of the Fengshuo era, the same autumn the Great Yan emperor changed.","As soon as Emperor Mingxi ascended the throne, this man was assigned as a county magistrate in the provinces. His official career went smoothly, and he was promoted to prefect of Yingzhou just two years ago. He could be considered a minister of some weight in Emperor Mingxi’s eyes.","Yet despite this, Yue Fuguang, tired from the journey, had no intention of stepping down to exchange pleasantries with them."]},{"number":423,"title":"Chapter 423: Seeing the Roadblocker Again","paragraphs":["She cast a distant glance and saw a group of blue and green robes behind the red official attire, followed by wealthy local gentry in brocade finery and spirited young scholars. Not far from them was a dense crowd of commoners, all in gray cloth clothes, their faces dusty and weary.","Their spirits were far poorer than those of the officials and gentry ahead—their lips were chapped, and as they looked toward her carriage, a faint glimmer of light appeared in their otherwise dead eyes.","Yue Fuguang waved a hand and said, \"Go tell Prefect Huang that this Junior Preceptor is tired. It will be fine if I see him tomorrow.\"","He Jin smiled with a curtsy and went to deliver the message. Her superior was now too lazy to even bother with polite excuses. With the drought urgent, their journey was pressing, and they were set to leave at dawn the next day—there was no time to meet this Prefect Huang.","When Huang Xie heard He Jin’s words, his expression remained gentle and deferential. He bowed toward Yue Fuguang’s carriage and said, \"The Junior Preceptor has labored tirelessly to relieve Yingzhou’s drought. The entire Yingchuan Prefecture is deeply grateful for this life-saving grace.\"","Shortly after Yue Fuguang’s carriage passed the Ten-Mile Pavilion, it stopped again.","Someone had blocked her carriage once more!","Before Yue Fuguang even asked, Dai Yuxing, who led the vanguard, hurriedly reported, \"My lord, a father and son ahead are blocking the road to file a complaint?\"","\"A complaint?\" Yue Fuguang had assumed it would be someone begging for forgiveness. She hadn’t expected to run into a genuine road-blocking grievance this time. That was something she had to hear!","Suddenly, she felt neither tired nor hungry. \"Have you asked what they are accusing and whom they are accusing?\"","As she spoke, Prefect Huang and his men, who had stepped aside to clear the path, noticed the commotion and rushed over in haste.","Huang Xie had some connections in the capital. He and Zheng Ziling were peers and close friends, exchanging letters from time to time.","Though Zheng Ziling, bound by certain unknown forces and the emperor’s gag order, dared not reveal too much in his letters, a few hints were enough for Huang Xie to grasp the Junior Preceptor’s standing at court.","Moreover, from crop varieties to technologies, everything this person had introduced had earned the reverence of the entire Dayan dynasty. Now, having single-handedly alleviated the drought across Dayan, her status was incomparable—","To put it in Zheng Ziling’s words, if the Crown Prince and Yue Fuguang fell into a river together, His Majesty would certainly save the Junior Preceptor first.","So, knowing that Yue Fuguang would pass through Yingchuan Prefecture, Zheng Ziling had written ahead to Huang Xie, urging him to take excellent care of her hospitality and, if possible, latch onto her good graces without hesitation.","Huang Xie was someone who heeded advice. He hadn’t climbed to his current position solely on capital connections—he was competent and willing to listen, not stubborn or arrogant.","Hearing faintly that someone had blocked the Junior Preceptor’s carriage, Huang Xie’s heart tightened. \"Slow down, my lord—mind your step!\" his attendant cried as Huang Xie nearly stumbled.","When he finally rushed to the front with his men, he saw from afar an old man and a young boy kneeling before the Junior Preceptor’s guards. He felt a bit more at ease.","As Huang Xie stopped to wipe his sweat, an official in blue robes behind him couldn’t help saying, \"My lord, these riffraff dared to block the Junior Preceptor’s carriage on the road. Should we send people to drive them away? If we anger Lord Yue, none of us can bear the consequences!\"","The official wore an expression of deep concern for Huang Xie and the others. Some nodded in agreement, while others were not so convinced.","The Junior Preceptor was who she was; if the prefect said he wouldn’t see her, so be it. If she didn’t want to deal with those blocking the road, who could object?","Given her current standing among the people, even if Prefect Huang, as the local magistrate, intervened, his words would carry less weight than a single sentence from her.","Thus, someone remarked, \"Sir Sun is mistaken. There must be a reason the commoners are blocking the road. Let us wait and see how the Junior Preceptor handles it.\"","\"But the Junior Preceptor wouldn’t even meet with us. She must be exhausted from the journey. We shouldn’t trouble her with trivial matters.\"","Huang Xie carefully folded his handkerchief into a square, tucked it into his sleeve, and said calmly, \"Judge Yao speaks sense. Whether she handles it or not is up to her. As her subordinates, it’s not our place to make decisions for her.\"","He turned to glance at Sir Sun, whose eyes kept darting ahead. Brushing dust from his clothes, Huang Xie added, \"Sir Sun, speculating about your superior’s intentions is a grave taboo in officialdom.\"","With that, he turned around, his stern face immediately breaking into a genial smile as he strode toward Yue Fuguang’s carriage.","At that moment, Yue Fuguang had just stepped down from her carriage and was walking ahead. Spotting Huang Xie and the string of officials trailing him, she arched an elegant brow. From this spot, though still a few dozen meters from the kneeling father and son, she could see most of the scene.","That Prefect Huang could remain so composed meant either he was unshakably confident, or that the grievance had little to do with him.","\"Yingchuan Prefect Huang Xie pays respects to the Junior Preceptor!\" Huang Xie bowed deeply. Though she was a prince, court and commoners alike preferred calling her the Junior Preceptor.","In the Dayan dynasty, there were still five or six living princes, but only one Junior Preceptor—her status beyond compare.","\"Paying respects to the Junior Preceptor!\" the crowd behind him bowed in unison.","Yue Fuguang’s expression was calm. She raised a hand slightly and said, \"Rise, everyone.\"","Turning to Huang Xie, she added, \"Since Prefect Huang is here, join me up front to see what grievance this father and son have within Yingchuan Prefecture.\"","Huang Xie wiped his brow with his sleeve and hurried to catch up. That one sweeping glance from the Junior Preceptor felt like it had seen through his very bones.","Ziling was right, he thought. This woman is an ancestor—just serve her well and never try to play tricks before her, or the consequences would be dire.","How dire exactly? He didn’t know yet, but just two steps later, he nearly stumbled again and began to vaguely sense the clue.","\"Master, this Prefect Huang is a bit soft and bloated. It’s not even hot yet, and he’s sweating profusely. No wonder his kidneys are weak!\"","\"Little Bead, what’s Huang Xie’s background? Is any of this ahead related to him?\" Yue Fuguang didn’t care about his kidneys—she cared if he was breaking the law.","\"Master, Huang Xie’s teacher is the retired Grand Secretary Xu, the Crown Prince’s maternal grandfather.\"","\"So he’s a natural member of the Crown Prince’s faction. Did the Crown Prince help with Huang Xie’s promotion?\"","In this era, a teacher’s lineage was as binding as family, so Yue Fuguang logically lumped Huang Xie with the Crown Prince’s party.","But behind them, Huang Xie, who had overheard everything, was sweating even more after nearly falling.","One voice he was certain belonged to the Junior Preceptor. But whose was that childlike voice? There were no children nearby! He couldn’t be seeing ghosts, could he!","Huang Xie started sweating again."]},{"number":424,"title":"Chapter 424: Injustice","paragraphs":["Out of the corner of his eye, he caught a glimpse of Yao Huijing, who calmly steadied him, and Sun Chengming, whose face was full of unease as he kept glancing at the father and son pair. He could be certain that these two hadn’t heard those voices.","Huang Xie’s heart began to pound with doubt, and his steps grew increasingly unsteady.","He naturally missed the Yao Tongpan, who had just helped him up, glancing at him with a puzzled expression.","Yao Tongpan couldn’t help but mutter to himself: What’s wrong with Lord Huang today? First he almost trips, now he’s drenched in sweat. Could what happened earlier really be related to him?","Yao Tongpan swept his gaze toward the light cyan figure ahead of him. Right now, he really wanted to withdraw the hand that was supporting Prefect Huang and ask if it was still possible to cut ties with Lord Huang!","[He was promoted to Yingchuan Prefect in the early days of the fifth year of Prince Yuan’s reign, thanks to a recommendation. At the time, the master happened to be in the Hongwen Academy, so she wasn’t aware of this.","This Huang Xie is also a close friend of Zheng Ziling. He suffers from kidney deficiency and once asked Zheng Ziling to find him a doctor in the capital to prescribe medicine.]","「At his age, he’s still kidney-deficient? This old guy’s private life must be unsavory, right?」Huang Xie clearly heard Yue Fuguang’s voice turn cold, and his heart was full of bitterness he couldn’t express.","He desperately wanted to say: Lord Junior Master, is it possible that this humble official’s condition is congenital?","[Master, Little Bead found out that this Huang Xie has one wife, three concubines, and one bed-servant. He’s trying to nourish his kidneys because he wants to have a son.]","「He sure hasn’t neglected himself! At his age, he’s still obsessed with having a son. Doesn’t he already have sons?」Of course, Yue Fuguang wouldn’t openly mock Lord Huang’s desire for a son in this ancient setting. Even if there wasn’t a throne to inherit, there were still family assets and connections to pass down.","This mindset was common even in the modern era, with its advanced technology and liberal thinking, let alone in ancient times, where technology, ideology, and productivity were all underdeveloped.","They truly had property and ancestral graves to inherit, and in this context, only male heirs could carry that burden. Without a male heir, the only option was to adopt a male relative from the clan to take over one’s wealth and continue the ancestral line.","This feudal ritual dross was something even the current Yue Fuguang couldn’t change in the short term, no matter how much she wanted to.","Whether it was decrees or systems, if they sprang from a single person, they would likely vanish with that person’s departure.","Without a change in the underlying thought patterns of the masses, even if some people heeded her now, the old thinking would violently rebound the moment she left.","She was a selfish person, not noble enough to stay in this world permanently for anyone’s sake.","[Sons? Of course he has them—more than one. Unfortunately, the big account is ruined, and the medium account is wasted. So he’s in a hurry to create another small account to train.]","Huang Xie didn’t understand their talk of “big accounts,” “medium accounts,” and “small accounts,” but he guessed from the context that they were referring to his sons.","In a few moments, the group had already reached the front of the line.","The father and son kneeling on the ground looked at the leading girl, whose bearing and aura resembled the deity statue they had enshrined in their home by seven or eight parts. They realized she was the Divine Woman they had come to seek.","“Commoner Cao Xiwang from Taohua Village, Pinglang County, Yingchuan Prefecture, with my foolish son Cao Xiaojun, pay homage to the Divine Woman!”","The pair kowtowed heavily to Yue Fuguang, raising a cloud of dust. When the surrounding commoners saw Yue Fuguang’s true face, their expressions lit up with joy, and they fell to their knees to kowtow in unison.","Cao Xiwang wore coarse cloth clothes that had been washed gray, covered with patch after patch. He appeared to be in his fifties, but the system indicated his age was only forty-one.","His face was weathered and bitter—the kind of premature aging that came from exhausting all one’s energy on making a living and bending under the weight of daily labor. This was the appearance of ninety percent of the commonfolk present.","His son, who looked to be in his teens, wore the same ragged clothes. His dark-skinned face flushed to a blackish-red from excitement when he saw her, and only his eyes were startlingly bright.","Yue Fuguang had no way to change the habit these people had of kneeling and kowtowing at every turn. She simply waved her hand and said, “Stand up, all of you!”","Then, addressing Cao Xiwang and his son, she said, “Cao Xiwang, if you have a grievance, speak it aloud while standing.”","She didn’t know exactly where Taohua Village was, but Pinglang County was over a hundred miles away. In a place with underdeveloped transportation, where some people never left their home county in their entire lives, that was truly a long distance.","Yue Fuguang turned and sat down on the chair that Dai Yuxing had brought over for her, turning the Ten-Mile Pavilion into a temporary hearing court. If only she had a table in front of her and a gavel to slam, it would feel even more authentic.","When she arrived, she had already learned the general outline from Dai Yuxing, but to grasp the details, she still had to hear it from the parties themselves.","“Divine Woman, my old self... my family’s grievance is immense!” Before he could even finish his sentence, Cao Xiwang choked up and began to sob.","Cao Xiwang tasted the saltiness of his tears on his lips, then wiped his face hastily with his sleeve. Through intermittent sobs, he recounted his family’s grievance.","The matter was actually simple, and quite common in this ancient society: Cao Xiwang’s eldest son, Cao Dajun, had married a famous local beauty in the spring of last year.","Since their wedding, they had been a loving young couple, and their life was steady and happy. But it all fell apart because of one person’s appearance.","\"My Lady Divine, that Sun Jizu, relying on his uncle who holds a high office in the prefectural government, has been committing all kinds of evils in our neighborhood—bullying men and abusing women, stopping at nothing.","That day, he brought a pack of wicked servants to my village to collect rent. When he saw my daughter-in-law's beauty, he insisted on taking her back as his eighteenth concubine.","When our family refused, we were beaten viciously by the Sun family’s thugs. After they snatched my daughter-in-law away, my son Dajun went to the yamen to file a complaint. But before he even reached the gate, he was set upon by some ruffians who appeared out of nowhere, beating him mercilessly without asking a single question.\"","At this point, Cao Xiwang’s tears fell again. \"When the villagers brought my son home, he lay in bed for over three months before he could even stand.","The day after he was back on his feet, my son and I went to report the crime again.","On the first day, the county magistrate claimed to be busy and refused to see us. The second day was the same. We went every day for ten days straight and never once got to see the magistrate—not even a single other official.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded, then suddenly turned to the sweating Huang Xie and asked, \"Prefect Huang, is it the norm in this Great Yan Dynasty for county magistrates not to show up for their duties?","Or perhaps the magistrates of Yingchuan Prefecture are special, drawing their salaries from the imperial treasury while sitting idle and accomplishing nothing?\"","\"N-no, no, Lord Junior Preceptor. All officials in Yingchuan Prefecture abide by imperial decrees. The magistrate of Pinglang County is an exception. He does not represent the entire Yingzhou officialdom.\"","\"That's right, Lord Junior Preceptor. We all attend to our duties diligently every day, and our devotion to the state is plain for heaven and earth to see. That magistrate of Pinglang County, Hao Ren, is merely an anomaly!\"","\"Or perhaps Magistrate Hao had his reasons for acting this way?\" one official cautiously glanced at Yue Fuguang’s expression, trying to defend Hao Ren.","Yue Fuguang paused her handling of the 'system' and let out a scornful laugh at this. \"An anomaly? And reasons?\"","She raised her eyebrows and swept her gaze lightly across all the officials present, her cold voice piercing into everyone's hearts. \"What a fine example of officials shielding one another! Your Yingchuan Prefecture has truly opened my eyes, Lord Junior Preceptor.\""]},{"number":425,"title":"Chapter 425: Half a Fellow Patient","paragraphs":["A playful smile curled at the corner of her lips. “I would also like to ask all of you—which uncle is this Sun Jizu who supposedly holds a high position in the prefectural city?”","She ignored the others and fixed her gaze on Huang Xie. “Lord Huang, think carefully before you speak. I have a bad temper and limited patience. Since the emperor has granted me the authority to act as I see fit, I imagine he wouldn’t object if I were to behead one or two officials to set an example.”","The fleeting murderous intent made the backs of everyone present break out in a cold sweat. No one dared utter another word.","Her chill grew more pronounced. “Lord Huang, I assume I don’t need to elaborate on your crime of negligence, do I?”","With that, she turned away from Huang Xie and addressed Cao Xiwang. “Cao Xiwang, continue.”","Seeing that the young palace tutor was questioning him and recalling how those lofty officials—whom he and his son had begged on their knees to meet—were now trembling in fear, Cao Xiwang’s long-hanging heart finally eased. He silently prayed that his son’s life might yet be saved.","“Later, my son went alone again. He finally met with Magistrate Hao, but Hao said the evidence was insufficient and refused to take the case.","My son wouldn’t accept it and went back several more times. The last time was on the twentieth of the first month. He went to the county office and never returned.”","Cao Xiwang knelt once more. “I went with my two sons to the county office to look for him, but the clerks not only claimed they’d never seen him, they also accused us of offending our superiors and beat us. If my second son hadn’t taken a blow for me,","I would have died at their hands that day. My second son’s leg was injured in the beating, and he still lies in bed, unable to move.","Since then, the land we rented was suddenly taken back, and people kept coming to our home to cause trouble. My wife fell ill and has been bedridden ever since.","To pay for my second son’s leg treatment, we’ve been stripped of everything. Even the grain we harvested last autumn was mostly stolen by thieves who sneaked in during the night.","Young tutor, someone is trying to drive my family to death!”","“Are you certain that Cao Dajun entered the county office and never came out?”","“I am certain. My son Cao Dajun is now locked up in the death row of the county jail!” If not for a kind-hearted person who told him of his son’s situation and pointed him toward this path of justice, he, an uneducated commoner, would never have thought to come here.","His son was in death row—if he wasn’t rescued before autumn, he would be executed.","“Death row?” Yue Fuguang turned back to Huang Xie. “Lord Huang, how is this justified? In your Yingzhou Prefecture’s jail, can death row be used to imprison innocent civilians who have broken no law?”","She had initially assumed this was just a simple tale of a tyrant landowner bullying the weak, protected by corrupt local officials.","But Cao Dajun’s ordeal hinted at something far more sinister.","Normally, prisoners executed after autumn had their cases reviewed and approved by the Ministry of Justice before they were taken out for beheading.","If Cao Dajun had been placed in death row, that meant they were preparing a substitute for a condemned man...","Clearly, Huang Xie, a veteran official who had seen all sorts of intrigue, thought the same. Not only was his face covered in cold sweat, but his puffy cheeks were now turning deathly pale.","If a death row prisoner had been replaced under his jurisdiction, it would be a grave scandal in officialdom. The people and events behind it couldn’t be dismissed with a simple charge of negligence.","If that happened, his mentor and the crown prince might also be implicated.","“Young tutor, I am hearing about this matter for the first time. I will immediately send men to investigate! I will give you and Old Cao an answer.” A flash of ruthlessness crossed his eyes. Since someone was trying to harm him, he would not sit idly by.","Yue Fuguang shot Feng Tang a knowing glance. Out here, it wasn’t like the capital, where one look from her would send Wei Ping and Cai Xuan into action.","Now, she had to rely on her own people to keep watch and prevent any clever scheme from unfolding.","“In that case, Lord Huang, why don’t you tell me—who is this supposed uncle of Sun Jizu?”","Huang Xie paused briefly. From the corner of his eye, he caught sight of someone whose complexion was even paler than his own, then bowed. “In response to the young tutor, if I recall correctly, Prefect Sun’s brother does indeed have a nephew named Sun Jizu.”","The reason he remembered so well was that Prefect Sun and he were somewhat kindred spirits in suffering. Though his own kidney condition was poor, he still had two sons and three daughters.","Prefect Sun was worse off. With one wife, six concubines, and countless chambermaids, he had only managed a single son and a daughter. The son had been frail since birth and died at three years old.","The Sun family had three brothers, but Sun Jizu was the only male heir among their offspring. The whole family doted on him excessively, fostering a domineering personality.","Prefect Sun treated this nephew like his own son. More than once, he had seen Prefect Sun bring the boy to stay with him for extended periods.","But he never imagined Sun Jizu would become so lawless back home. As the prefect, he was indeed guilty of negligence.","“Prefect Sun?” Yue Fuguang swept her gaze across the officials and quickly identified Sun Min, the vice prefect whose rank was just below Huang Xie’s.","“Sun Min, is what Lord Huang said true? Did this matter in Pinglang County involve your nephew? How much do you know?”","Her gaze was icy. “I will give you only one chance to tell the truth. If you fail to treasure it, I will not hesitate to have your entire family escorted to the capital for the emperor himself to question.”","At the mention of his family being taken to Beijing, Sun Min’s face turned ashen. Trembling, he fell to his knees. “Young tutor, please hear me! My nephew is still young and ignorant. Everything was done by servants on his behalf to curry favor.”","He pressed his forehead hard into the dirt, his voice choked with tears. “Please, for the sake of his youth and foolishness, grant him another chance.","From now on, I will discipline him strictly. The Sun family will compensate all the losses Old Cao has suffered!”","His head remained bowed as if he would never rise. Yue Fuguang shot him a cold glance, feeling not a trace of pity for such a man.","“Young and ignorant? Are you saying Sun Jizu, a twenty-three-year-old giant baby, is young and ignorant?” She slammed her teacup heavily onto the table, the sharp clang echoing through the hall.","“Sun Min, do you know that Cao Dajun’s wife, Li Yoniang, has already hanged herself from the disgrace she suffered? How do you plan to compensate for a human life?","With silver? How much of your Sun family’s wealth was extorted from the common people?”","The Sun family had once been wealthy, but had later declined. By Sun Min’s father’s generation, they were mere small landowners. It was Sun Min’s success in the imperial exams and marriage to a daughter from a side branch of a prestigious clan that had earned them their current status.","Now she recalled that Sun Min’s wife seemed to be an aunt-by-marriage of Princess Bai, Bai Nianzhu, wife of the third prince. When Emperor Mingxi had executed the entire Bai clan and had their property confiscated, it only targeted the Bai family itself.","Married daughters, including Bai Nianzhu, were left untouched.","“Young tutor, you must see clearly. My Sun family has always followed the law. Our property was earned through the honest toil of my two brothers through legitimate means.","Li Yoniang’s death was an accident. I and my family will fully compensate both the Cao and Li families.” Yue Fuguang took a measure of satisfaction from Sun Min’s stubborn denials—men like that were far easier to execute without a guilty conscience."]},{"number":426,"title":"Chapter 426: Do You Know You're Breaking the Law","paragraphs":["\"Obtained through righteous means? All accidents?\" This was another great joke Yue Fuguang had heard this year!","As the day grew late, she didn’t want to waste time with Sun Min. She looked him straight in the eyes and said, \"Was Hao Ren’s actions carried out on your orders?\" An invisible pressure bore down on him, her voice coldly echoing in his ears. \"Think carefully before you answer!\"","Sun Min couldn’t lift his head under the invisible weight. His official robe was covered in dust, his forehead nearly pressed into the dirt. His voice was choked with suppressed emotion, filled with deep remorse. \"Reporting to you, my lord, it was I who ordered Magistrate Hao to refuse to take up this matter.","But I did not know that Magistrate Hao had locked Cao Dajun in death row. I only wanted the Cao family to back down, not to kill him!\"","\"Little Bead, how much of what Sun Min says is true?\"","[Master, Sun Min did indeed order Hao Ren to detain the man. Their original plan was to send Cao Dajun to the black mine as forced labor.","However, Hao Ren has another master behind his back. He hid this from Sun Min and arranged a new fate for Cao Dajun, which is why he was locked in death row. If we hadn’t shown up today, he would have been beheaded this autumn in someone else’s place!]","Huang Xie heard this voice again, and with such precise knowledge, his guesses about the young master’s origins grew deeper.","A flicker of inner conflict crossed his eyes. He didn’t know if he should report his discovery to this mysterious and seemingly godlike young master.","His men had just informed him that as the young master’s party passed by the Yingchuan River, torrential rain had fallen, restoring the river to seventy percent of its original flow.","Such power—could this woman truly be a celestial goddess descended to earth?","Yue Fuguang was unaware of Huang Xie’s inner turmoil. She only looked down at Sun Min, who knelt before her, and said word by word, \"I heard you originally planned to send the man to the black mine as forced labor?\"","\"Sun Min, tell me, where is that black mine? As a court official, you knowingly concealed the illegal mining of a national vein without reporting it. Sun Min, do you know your crime?\"","Her voice was not loud, but every word struck Sun Min’s heart like a thousand-pound hammer. He felt momentarily dizzy, sensing that a great calamity was upon him.","If his nephew’s matter jeopardized his career, ordering Hao Ren would at most cost him his post. But now, this black mine business could genuinely cost him his life!","He just couldn’t understand—only he and Hao Ren had plotted this. How did this woman know? Could it be that Hao Ren had grown tired of living and betrayed them both?","Regardless of Sun Min’s guesses, Yue Fuguang’s hammer fell heavily. \"Sun Min, how much benefit have you taken from privately digging these mines? In such a dire situation, why not confess everything now?\"","At this question, Sun Min’s kneeling body involuntarily leaned backward. His eyes opened wide in terror as he stared at Yue Fuguang in disbelief.","He had a stake in the black mine, and even Hao Ren didn’t know that. How had Yue Fuguang found out?","The black mine couldn’t have been raided. Yue Fuguang had only entered Yingchuan Prefecture today, and it was nearly a hundred miles to the mine’s location.","Besides, he had received last month’s dividend only yesterday. The messenger said everything was fine there and the mine would never be compromised. Clinging to this belief, Sun Min waved his hands repeatedly and defended himself. \"My lord, please be clear! On the matter of Cao Dajun, I am indeed guilty, and I am willing to accept the law’s punishment.","But as for the black mine you mentioned, there is absolutely no such thing. I truly know nothing about it!\"","He turned his face, full of entreaty, toward Huang Xie, who stood by with a scrutinizing gaze, and said mournfully, \"Lord Huang, you know me.","My Sun family’s only male descendant is that boy Jizu, and the whole household has indeed spoiled him too much.","I only make mistakes in matters concerning that child. But aside from that, I would never, and dare not, be involved with a black mine!\"","Huang Xie, hearing this excuse, couldn’t help but twitch his lips. If he hadn’t heard that mysterious voice’s revelation, he might actually have believed Sun Min’s sophistry.","He had only today seen through this self-righteous Sun Min, discovering that his brazenness was even thicker than his own.","Was making a small mistake with your own nephew the only issue? Don’t you realize you broke the law?","And that black mine—Sun Min was too greedy and too bold. How could he not see the changing winds in officialdom over the past two years?","The rampant practice of oppressing the people, extorting bribes, and skimming a layer off every penny had diminished greatly—all starting from the very official sitting before him.","Instead of lying low, he had committed a crime. He had not only brought ruin upon his own family but also saddled Huang Xie with a dereliction of duty. What bad luck to be his colleague!","Huang Xie, because of Sun Min, had already accumulated several charges of oversight in a short time, leaving him numb inside.","He grumbled inwardly, but said aloud, \"Lord Sun, with the young master present, you’d better honestly confess all your crimes. Otherwise, once you’re sent to the capital, the ministers of the Supreme Court and the Ministry of Punishments won’t be as easygoing as the young master.\"","It could only be said that no wonder Huang Xie had risen to the post of Prefect of Yingchuan—he knew how to speak. Even at this moment, he didn’t forget to flatter Yue Fuguang.","He cupped his hands toward her and said, \"I believe the young master will neither wrong an innocent person nor let a guilty one off.","Young master, if the Yingchu Zhou Prefecture needs assistance in any matter, please do not hesitate to ask.\"","He glanced back at the dense ranks of the Imperial Guard and the Right Guard New Army, and especially when he spotted Shen Jian in the crowd, his pupils involuntarily contracted.","He had met this man when reporting to the capital at the Crown Prince’s residence. As the eldest son of the princess and the emperor’s own nephew, such a person serving as the young master’s guard showed how favored she was by the royal family!","His friend Ziling had indeed spoken truly!","Yue Fuguang did not stand on ceremony and replied directly, \"There happens to be a matter here that requires your men, Lord Huang.\"","She waved over Shen Jian. \"General Shen, select five hundred soldiers to accompany Lord Huang’s men to Tiger Ridge at Ten Mile Slope. Someone is privately mining iron ore there.\"","As she spoke, Yue Fuguang feared they might waste time finding the place, so she had the system produce a map for her.","Shen Jian took the map, bowed respectfully, and left to carry out the order. Meanwhile, Huang Xie on the side was utterly stunned. That black mine was actually an iron mine!","What could iron be used for? Besides making farming tools like sickles and hoes, it could also be used to forge weapons, armor, and swords for rebellion. This was a grave crime!","Could there be someone under his jurisdiction harboring rebellious intentions?","Huang Xie’s legs went weak. He felt like kneeling on the ground alongside Sun Min for a rest!","Yue Fuguang settled into the garden prepared by Huang Xie. After dinner, she asked He Jin, who had just returned from outside, \"Are Cao Xiwang and his son properly settled?\"","\"Rest assured, my lord. Lord Feng has arranged for the Cao father and son in the outer courtyard’s side rooms. To guard against any mishap, General Wei Shouyi has specially assigned four soldiers to protect them.\"","He wondered if someone would truly try to silence the two men tonight.","If anyone did come, the faction behind Hao Ren would indeed be no simple matter."]},{"number":427,"title":"Chapter 427: Outside the Plum Garden","paragraphs":["Substituting a condemned prisoner for execution, no matter the era, was a capital offense. Pulling off such a feat was not something a county magistrate could simply order.","A magistrate might wield considerable local power, but the county yamen also included the assistant magistrate and registrar—entrenched local powers. A magistrate, as a transferred official, would not dare take such a risk without certain assurance.","The fear was that Cao Dajun was not the first to be substituted.","\"By my reckoning, the men General Shen sent to Pinglang County should arrive tonight,\" Yue Fuguang said, glancing at the darkened sky outside. \"Tomorrow, we’ll likely be able to bring the suspects here for questioning. We’ll stay here for one more day.\"","She could already foresee that once today’s events spread, her reputation as the emperor’s surrogate surveying the realm would be solidified.","From now on, not a few commoners would likely seek her out to plead their cases.","Yue Fuguang retreated to the inner chamber and sat cross-legged on the bed. These days, she felt her abilities had grown somewhat.","With some effort, her rain now covered an area of about thirty to fifty miles. Fortunately, the current Dayan Dynasty was much smaller than her homeland’s territory; otherwise, it would take her forever to cover it all.","The next morning, He Jin reported that the courtyard outside the mansion was packed with citizens of Yingzhou Prefecture. Yue Fuguang had slept well the night before, nourished by the incense offerings, and her spirits were fully restored. She stretched lazily. Another day for a major push!","As Yue Fuguang walked out with He Jin, Shen Chunying, and the others, she asked about the arrest of the criminals. \"Has General Wei returned?\"","\"General Wei came back around early morning, bringing in 153 bandits and rescuing over 500 miners.\"","Over 500—that must have been a sizable mine.","\"Have the rescued miners been taken care of? Do we know who these miners are?\" Were they all like Cao Dajun—offended someone and were sold off to the mine by enemies?","Yue Fuguang shook her head, thinking it unlikely. He Jin’s following words confirmed her suspicion.","\"Rest assured, Magistrate Wu Yong registered their information this morning. But I heard from General Wei that some claimed to be from Hegou Village in Pinglang County.","The entire village was in that mine. Same for the villagers of Pinggu Village—whole villages were taken, wiped out wholesale.\"","Shen Chunying added, \"According to those people, the elderly, weak, and sick from both villages died off last winter. Now all that’s left are the able-bodied young men. But the black mine didn’t give them enough food, and the work was brutal—they’re all in terrible shape.","Dai Yuxing said that if not for the Lady, these people would never have survived the spring with so little food and water.\"","Their Lady truly was a goddess—she had saved countless lives again.","Yue Fuguang caught the reverence in He Jin and Shen Chunying’s eyes and chuckled lightly. She asked about another matter: \"How many came last night?\"","\"Master, I know that. Twenty-eight came last night. All but one lookout were caught.\"","Twenty-eight assassins sent just to kill those two men—the mastermind behind Hao Ren was no simple matter.","And the fact that the common folk of Pinglang County were taken as forced labor to neighboring Pingchuan County, entire families wiped out at once—this was no trivial affair.","When the villagers of two entire hamlets suddenly vanished, Yue Fuguang was certain not a single petty official in Pinglang County had failed to notice. To them, these people weren’t villagers—they were walking taxes in the form of poll taxes and corvée labor.","That no one up or down the chain investigated only reaffirmed how deep the rot ran. Pinglang County wasn’t just a problem with its magistrate; every party with a stake was complicit.","\"System, how much do you know about Pinglang County?\"","When it came to information unrelated to her mission, the system faced various restrictions. For instance, about Pinglang County, the system could only pull data on the case connected to Sun Min, who had appeared before her.","To learn anything else, she needed to interrogate Hao Ren in person.","\"Host, I’ve already told you everything I know! I haven’t held back a bit!\"","The system wished it could do more, but the data wasn’t allowed.","\"I suspect the backstory behind Hao Ren isn’t simple. Maybe this will even trigger a side quest.\"","Little did Yue Fuguang know how prophetic her words were. By now, she had already led her people to the front courtyard of Plum Garden.","The courtyard was crowded. Inside, Feng Tang was chatting with Huang Xie, who had come for the morning roll call. Behind them stood the assembled officials of Yingzhou Prefecture, Magistrate Wu Yong, and his staff.","When they saw her approach, they broke off their conversations and eagerly came forward to greet her.","\"Lady, the front gate is packed with citizens of Yingzhou Prefecture. Would you like to step outside and have a look?\"","Feng Tang knew Yue Fuguang’s temper well. Although she never spoke of it, he had sensed that she was far more approachable to commoners than to some officials.","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Let’s go see.\"","She looked up at the late morning sun—bright and blazing, the sky a clear azure. But not a single soul in Yinchuan Prefecture was happy about such weather.","\"It’s time to send down rainfall and relieve Yingzhou City’s drought,\" Yue Fuguang said casually. Yet her offhand remark stirred the hearts of the officials behind her.","The Junior Preceptor was still willing to look after Yingzhou Prefecture—they were finally reassured.","Eagerly, they followed Yue Fuguang out through the front courtyard and stood at the main gate. The gates of Plum Garden swung open before them. Before Yue Fuguang even stepped over the threshold, she looked up to see the area beyond the gate, ten meters away, packed with commoners in every kind of dress.","Their spirits seemed much better than yesterday, and their clothes were noticeably cleaner.","Observing Yue Fuguang’s unspoken question, Huang Xie quickly whispered, \"Lady, perhaps you didn’t know. Last night, when the citizens heard that the Yinchuan River outside the city had risen, many brought their families by night to fetch water.\"","Word about the Yinchuan River spread quickly. While Yue Fuguang was still hearing the Cao family’s case the previous day, many onlookers had already learned about the heavy rain thirty li away that had filled that stretch of river.","Yue Fuguang nodded and stepped out through the gates.","Seeing her appear, the crowd readied to kneel. Before them stood a living goddess—how could they not kneel and offer incense?","It was then Yue Fuguang noticed that besides incense, the citizens were holding fruit, pastries, and small livestock. They were indeed offerings for a rite!","Were they about to begin worshipping her like this—a living person? Goodness, have you no manners?","Incense was one thing, fruit and pastries tolerable, but the man holding a roasted suckling pig and the one carrying a roast chicken were especially eye catching!","Although she had found such scenes unremarkable on her journey, there she had been inside her carriage. As long as she didn’t lift the curtain and the horses were fast, she wouldn’t have to witness their incense offerings.","But now the situation was completely different. Persistent as she was, she still preferred it if they kept up their incense burning subtly, out of her sight. A bit more propriety wouldn’t hurt!"]},{"number":428,"title":"Chapter 428: Interrogation","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang forced a smile as she raised her hand to stop those who were about to kneel. \"No need for such formalities, everyone. I already know what you seek and wish for.\"","She was now speaking to her followers in her divine identity, so referring to herself as \"I\" was perfectly appropriate.","As Yue Fuguang finished speaking, without waiting for the crowd of commoners to react, she pointed toward the clear blue sky and said, \"Wind, come!\"","It had to be said that the ancient sky was remarkably clean—blue during the day without a single cloud, and at night, stars hung heavy in the sky, again without a trace of cloud.","Otherwise, given her current abilities, she wouldn't be able to cover only a range of sixty to seventy li with rainfall.","A sudden gust of wind blew up from the ground, stirring dust and sand into spirals that made many people shut their eyes involuntarily. Yet more squinted, covering their mouths, forcing themselves to witness the entire miracle happening right before them—a sight worth remembering for a lifetime to brag about.","With Yue Fuguang's next words, \"Clouds, come!\" the sky immediately stirred with wind and clouds, and within moments, dark clouds obscured the sun and the blue sky they had grown tired of seeing.","Every single person present, upon seeing this, became even more convinced that the deity they worshipped daily was real!","If anyone ever told them that the divine maiden was fake or her miracles were invalid, they wouldn't believe a word—they'd drive such a person away!","In the eyes of these people, Yue Fuguang saw the most fervent reverence.","At the front of the crowd stood a plump squire holding a roasted suckling pig. Without waiting for anyone else, he knelt first, lifting the pig high above his head. Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow, thinking: With such a stout figure, how did he manage to move so nimbly? Wasn't he tired holding that pig all the way?","As she uttered another word, \"Rain, come!\" raindrops fell without warning, pelting down noisily. The ground before the squire was immediately dotted with coin-sized rain marks spreading across the dusty road.","The quiet crowd erupted into movement the moment the first raindrop fell—again the familiar mix of crying and laughter.","Some opened their mouths to catch the rainwater from the sky; others clasped their hands together, murmuring prayers.","\"The divine maiden has brought rain!\"","\"Thank you, Lady Goddess, for granting us rain!\"","...","The rain grew heavier, and more people knelt on the ground. If someone resisted kneeling, it wasn't allowed—they insisted on burning incense and making wishes before her.","When Yue Fuguang heard someone again begging her to bless them with a son or to find a good family-in-law for their daughter, she could barely hold it together.","Feng Tang noticed her discomfort and said, \"My Lady, General Shen just sent word. He is escorting the officials of Pinglang County and is expected to arrive before noon.","Would you like to interrogate those from the illegal mine before that?\"","Seizing the excuse Feng Tang offered, Yue Fuguang immediately went along, taking the lead toward the outer courtyard's main hall. She didn't forget to instruct Dai Yuxing, \"Yuxing, bring the ringleader to the hall. Have General Wei interrogate the rest.\"","Those people, though neither the main culprits nor leaders, after long association, would surely know some hidden secrets.","\"He Jin, have the accompanying doctors check the health of those rescued and treat the sick promptly.\"","\"As for medicinal herbs?\" She turned to look at Huang Xie.","Huang Xie, quick to catch on, immediately responded, \"My Lady, the Yingzhou prefectural office will cover the cost of the herbs. Lord He Jin, just provide a list of whatever medicines you need.\"","Magistrate Sun, who was behind him, also said, \"Prefect, let me handle this matter. I guarantee it won't delay the Junior Preceptor's affairs.\"","Yue Fuguang had only just settled into the flower hall and hadn't even finished a cup of tea when Dai Yuxing entered with five people.","He clasped his hands toward the seated Yue Fuguang and said, \"Sir, the five ringleaders of the illegal mine have been brought here. These five were originally bandit chiefs from a neighboring mountain, but later someone recruited them and set them up to run a private mining operation.\"","With a single sweep of her gaze, she saw that even as they tried to act tough and refused to kneel, Dai Yuxing kicked each of them behind the knee, one by one, and with a thud-thud-thud, they dropped to the ground.","The leader was a man in his thirties of medium build—neither burly in frame nor brawny in face.","His features were ordinary, except for a pair of eyes that set him apart. When this man looked at others, there was a kind of bloodthirsty, brutal gleam hidden in his gaze.","He thought that by staring at her—a mere child of around ten-something years—with such murderous venom, he could intimidate her.","But Yue Fuguang merely let out a light snort of disdain. Ah!","The cold sneer still echoed, and the man suddenly felt as if needles had stabbed through his eyeballs. Though there was no blood, the pain in his eyes made his entire body tremble. His hands instinctively covered his eyes, but no cry of agony could escape his throat.","She turned her attention away from that man, focusing on the four behind him.","These four were all in their twenties or thirties. The suffering of their leader had left them bewildered, but instinct made them fearful. Their gazes as they looked at Yue Fuguang were mixed—some startled, some fearful, and all tinged with a hint of complex curiosity.","Among the four was a surprisingly attractive young woman in a deep red dress. She was tall, with a well-proportioned figure, and the way she moved suggested she was trained in martial arts—though it remained to be seen how her skills compared to those of Shen Chunying and the others.","Judging by her stance, she seemed to be the third-in-command.","In front of the woman stood a man in his twenties, dressed like a scholar. Behind her were two others: one weasel-eyed, scraggly and short, and the other tall and burly, built like a dark, beefy giant.","Without beating around the bush, Yue Fuguang asked directly what she needed to know: “Who is your master?”","“And where do all these iron ores get shipped?”","It wasn’t that she looked down on these men—common bandits might discover a mineral vein, but with no one above to protect them, they couldn’t manage it on their own.","In the end, they’d face the same fate as savages in the mountains: either be exploited or be recruited to serve some noble as enforcers.","These five clearly followed a similar pattern, especially since Dai Yuxing had already noted that they’d been taken under someone’s wing.","“The Junior Preceptor overestimates us. The mine was discovered by our Black Tiger Stronghold, and it’s been us who’ve dug it ourselves,” came the reply. “As for where we sell it... Well, most of the time, buyers come from different places. So long as they pay silver, we just sell it. We don’t bother with where the goods go or what they’re used for.”","Yue Fuguang’s question was met with a brief silence, but to her surprise, the one who stepped forward to answer wasn’t the chieftain—though his eyes had stopped hurting, they were still streaming tears—but the young scholar behind him.","Interesting, she thought, taking a sip of tea to mask the spark of amusement in her eyes. Her gaze slid toward the young scholar. “You dig and sell on your own? And you don’t know who the buyers are?”","The sneer at the corner of her mouth grew wider. \"Do you think I, the Junior Master, am young and easy to bully, or do you believe you've covered your tracks cleanly?","Sun Min, Hao Ren... I imagine you're all quite familiar with these names.\"","As Yue Fuguang recited each name, not only the young scholar, but also the older man and the woman instantly changed their expressions when the name Hao Ren came up.","The gaunt man even couldn't help shrinking back, looking even more shifty. Among the five of them, only the burly, dark-complexioned man seemed oblivious to the situation."]},{"number":429,"title":"Chapter 429: Interrogation, Lesson","paragraphs":["He kept glancing toward the courtyard outside. What was out there? Rain!","By now, a pool of water had formed on the ground, with raindrop bells occasionally appearing and bursting.","Yue Fuguang calculated the time and rainfall, estimating that in another hour, the drought in Yingchuan Prefecture would be temporarily alleviated.","“The esteemed officials you, sir, have mentioned are the renowned local authorities. In these parts, everyone knows who they are. We are merely lowly men engaged in capital crimes. To protect ourselves, we can even forget our own parents, but we must know every influential official above.”","The young scholar’s words seemed reasonable — those in the underworld naturally needed to know the big names in the legitimate world who held power above them.","Yue Fuguang followed his lead and said, “So you find out their preferences and secrets, then cater to them to lure them onto your pirate ship?”","The moment her words fell, she clearly sensed a momentary relaxation in the expression of the young scholar and the woman.","“No.” Yue Fuguang shook her head thoughtfully, “It wasn’t you who pulled them aboard, but they who actively absorbed your bandit stronghold. You people are just servants keeping watch for them. Am I right or wrong, Grand Tutor?”","Sure enough, no sooner had she spoken than everyone present changed color. The leader, who had just calmed down slightly, now looked fierce and vicious again.","Especially upon hearing the word “servant,” his gaze toward Yue Fuguang became filled with venomous hatred.","Yue Fuguang found it tiresome and said flatly, “Since you don’t want your eyes, then you don’t need them!” She lightly flicked her sleeve, and a breeze swept past. The leader’s vision went dark again, and he could no longer see.","This man couldn’t stand the word “servant.” She was tempted to say she had shown restraint by not calling them “watchdogs”!","A man like that leader, who never learned from punishment and only relied on brute force, was at most the muscle of the stronghold. When it came to planning and strategizing, she was more inclined to suspect the scholar and the woman — these two were peculiar.","“Ah! My eyes! I can’t see!” He rolled on the ground clutching his eyes. “What did you do to my eyes!”","In grief and fury, he tried to lash out in Yue Fuguang’s direction, but because he had staggered around dizzily earlier, he was facing the scholar instead.","“You false goddess! Give my eyes back!” He shrieked harshly, nearly shaking the ancient dust off the roof of the hall.","“How irritating!” Yue Fuguang said, and in an instant, the mining leader lost his voice. His mouth gaped open and shut, but no sound came out.","Then He Jin stepped forward, gently tapped a few spots on his body, and the man stiffened on the ground, unable to move.","Yue Fuguang had casually stripped the leader of his sight with a mere gesture, once again terrifying those around her. How did she make someone go blind and lose their voice instantly? They hadn’t seen clearly the first time, but this time it was obvious — she simply waved her light, wide sleeve. It was so casual that it barely stirred the air.","Hidden weapons? Impossible!","Even experts like them, using internal energy to launch hidden weapons, couldn’t deprive someone of sight without causing injury.","Even poison wouldn’t take effect that fast!","Hei Likui and the short, thin man instinctively turned their eyes toward the man and woman standing in front, as if seeking their advice.","[Master, are you about to strip his five senses?]","“This man is both stupid and malicious, and he shows no respect to me. I’ll just make him behave for a while.”","Yue Fuguang could see from their reactions that the mining leader was nothing but a puppet. The real decision-makers were indeed the young scholar and the woman behind him.","Though silent, the woman remained calm and clearly had a mind of her own and the authority to decide.","These five people seemed to be a group, but judging by their style, they belonged to two different factions.","“Little Pearl, investigate the backgrounds of that scholar and the woman. They’re clearly the real pair.”","“Which of you will tell me who the mastermind is? And where was the iron ore transported?” Yue Fuguang’s earlier feat had clearly intimidated them. Being unable to see or speak brought them more fear than having a knife at their throats.","[Master, I found out. The young scholar and that woman are indeed not from the same group as the three Black Tiger bandits.","A year ago, someone discovered the iron mine and took over the Black Tiger stronghold. Then these two joined. The moment they arrived, authority fell into their hands. They are the trusted agents sent by the behind-the-scenes master to keep watch.]","“Who is that mastermind? What’s his connection with Sun Min and Hao Ren?”","[The mastermind is the head of the Yu family. This Yu family is a prominent clan in Yingzhou. Although not as powerful as the great and minor noble families, they have many members and considerable local influence.","The collapse of those great and minor families gave those lower-class clans the opportunity they were waiting for.]","Yue Fuguang commented, “So when the tiger is away, the monkey tries to be king? The noble families have fallen. Aren’t these people afraid they’ll follow the same fate?”","[Master, hundreds of years of habit. Back then, the great families like Zheng, Wang, Kong, Bai, Cui, Yang, Yuan, Li, and the minor ones — none of them gained power without someone else falling.","In their eyes, what is happening now in the Great Yan Dynasty is just a new round of redistribution. The imperial authority needs new forces to stabilize itself. The idea that noble families should rise again hasn’t vanished from their minds.]","Yue Fuguang was speechless. “It’s human nature to want a seat at the table for your own benefit, but taking this path is only narrowing your own options!”","Yu family? Huang Xie was startled when he heard this. He had no doubt about the mysterious voice calling Yue Fuguang “master”; he believed it easily.","Last night, after returning home, Huang Xie had thought it over. Finally, the hints in the private letters from Ziling and the Crown Prince now made sense.","The Yu family had many members and great influence in Yingzhou, but what was their purpose in discovering an iron mine without reporting it? Did they harbor rebellious ambitions?","But no. Although the Great Yan Dynasty was suffering from drought, with the living goddess, Chancellor, by their side, the dynasty’s fortune was too strong to be shaken by a mere Yu family.","Wait. The Yu family might have influence in Yingzhou, but outside it, few knew of them.","In reality, few Yu family children held court positions. The most powerful one was just a county magistrate.","If he remembered correctly, the county where the young Yu man served was Hao Ren’s hometown!","So there was someone behind the Yu family?","While Huang Xie was busy speculating, Yue Fuguang was more direct. “I heard your Black Tiger stronghold has close ties with the Yu family of Yingzhou.","You are bandits; the Yu family is a local notable. How did you two end up entangled?”"]},{"number":430,"title":"Chapter 430: Identity","paragraphs":["Her voice was calm. \"Don't use the business relationship as an excuse. I'm sure you don't even believe it yourself.\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang mention the Yu family, the young scholar unconsciously leaned back a little. Although it was just a small movement, everyone present could tell that this question had hit the nail on the head.","\"Your Excellency also said that the Yu family is a prominent local family. How could we, a bunch of bandits, have anything to do with such a family?\"","There were already faint beads of cold sweat on the scholar's forehead. \"As I said before, we don't know the identities of the buyers who purchased the ore. As long as they pay in silver, anyone is our customer. Maybe there are people from the Yu family among them?\"","Yue Fuguang didn't comment on his nonsense. She slowly took a sip of fragrant tea and then continued, \"Since you sell to anyone who pays in silver, you must have earned a lot of silver.","Where did all that silver go? My people only found some loose silver in your lair!\"","Saying it was loose silver was an exaggeration, but to be honest, there wasn't much profit.","\"This...\" The young scholar was at a loss for words. He never expected that his confident words just now would become the biggest flaw in his lie.","\"Your Excellency, please see clearly.\" The woman behind the scholar crawled forward on her knees for two steps. \"I'm in charge of the accounts and silver transactions in the stronghold.","That day, when your Excellencies raided the mine, I saw that the situation was wrong, so I burned all the account books!\"","She knocked her head heavily on the ground, with tears all over her face. She looked so pitiful.","Unfortunately, Yue Fuguang was not the kind of person who would show pity for a beautiful woman, especially since this woman's identity was not simple.","She tapped the table lightly and said, \"The account books are gone, but what about the silver? Don't tell me you burned it too. Silver isn't like paper money. If you want to lie, come up with something more believable to fool this junior grand preceptor.\"","There was a clear look of mockery in her eyes, as if she was watching them perform. The woman felt a momentary panic of being seen through.","She gathered her courage and said, \"Part of the silver was squandered by a few of us.\"","She glanced at the other four people. But then she thought that some of the miners who were captured first were still alive, and it was possible to calculate approximately how much ore had been mined in the past year.","It was simply impossible that a few people had squandered so much silver. She gritted her teeth, and a faint blush appeared on her face. \"Most of it was secretly taken by me and given to... my lover!\"","\"Your lover? Hao Fangting, the son of Hao Ren?\"","\"How do you know about A Ting, Your Excellency?\" The woman suddenly looked up, with panic and suspicion in her beautiful eyes. An exclamation blurted out. By the time she realized what she had said and tried to cover her mouth, it was too late.","\"You don't need to worry about how I know. All you need to know is that I already know all your details.","I should also thank the person who told me the truth.\"","Her eyes swept over the five people, and some things were self - evident.","\"Is it you, Zhou Wu, who informed on us?\" The woman turned to question the wretched man kneeling behind her. He looked so sneaky and unreliable.","\"You ugly thing, trying to take advantage of me but failing, and now you want to ruin me and A Ting!\"","Her voice was full of anger and resentment, and her eyes looking at the man were filled with venom. \"You useless thing, that's all you're capable of!\"","\"I didn't. It wasn't me! Snow Lady, I don't care about your dirty business with that Hao Fangting!\"","The wretched man was being scolded by the woman called Snow Lady, and in a fit of anger, he shrank back and defended himself. Unfortunately, the angry woman didn't believe a word of it.","\"Stop arguing!\" The young scholar saw that these two idiots were starting to fight among themselves because of a vague remark from the other side, and he couldn't help but speak up to stop them.","\"Master Yu, what a great air you're putting on!\" Yue Fuguang looked at him, with a sneer on her lips. \"I'm not sure whether I should call you the second in - command, Xu Shangu, or Master Yu Qi, Yu Wei?\"","As soon as the name Yu Wei was mentioned, the young scholar's body trembled. Most of his energy seemed to be sucked away by this address, and he slumped to the ground, silent, no longer having the stubborn attitude of refusing to confess.","\"Yin Hongxue, no, I should call you Li Qingxue. You're from a side branch of the Li family in Xinzhou, one of the eight great families. You were engaged to Hao Fangting of the third branch of the Hao family in Xinzhou since childhood.","The Li family was raided by the imperial court. You happened to be staying at your maternal grandfather's house, so you managed to escape.","Later, in order to avoid the imperial court's investigation, your grandfather sent you to Yingchuan Prefecture where your fiancé's family worked. After a conspiracy between the Hao father and son, they sent you to manage the accounts in the black mine.","The reason you were able to manage the accounts is that your grandfather is a side branch of the Yu family in Xinzhou and has always had a close relationship with the first branch of the Yu Mansion.","There has always been a lot of strife between the first branch and the third branch where Yu Wei is from. You're not just the accountant, but also sent by the first branch to keep an eye on Yu Wei. Am I right?\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. She had seen too many struggles between the legitimate and illegitimate children in the great families of Dayan.","Even siblings born of the same parents could fight like enemies for the sake of interests, let alone half - siblings with the difference between legitimate and illegitimate status. Those so - called brothers were just rivals in the fight for family property.","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but wonder if the idea of having more children bringing more blessings was really right.","Even with Emperor Mingxi suppressing things, there were always old men in every family who liked young women. It was quite funny that the Yu family was already on guard against each other before even starting to fight for the family fortune.","When Yu Wei learned that this cousin was also tasked with monitoring him, a cold light shot out from his small eyes.","But now he was like a fish on the chopping block, in no position to take revenge on Li Qingxue!","Humph! So after learning the truth, Yu Wei just got angry for a moment.","\"Yu Wei, Li Qingxue, who of you will tell me where the Yu family transported all the iron ore and what they used so much iron for?\"","Although the actions of the Yu family were dangerous, it didn't really matter to Dayan at present, so this matter was not within her mission scope.","The information provided by the system was also limited. It could be said that Yue Fuguang was just bored during her journey and wanted to have some fun in handling this case.","She also wanted to expose this matter to remind the emperor and his officials of Dayan. Even if the great and small families fell, there were still many prominent local families in Dayan. They shouldn't let their guard down and allow these guys to grow stronger and become hard nuts to crack.","Yu Wei and Li Qingxue glanced at each other and then turned their heads away. It seemed that neither of them was going to speak first.","Yue Fuguang looked outside and saw that it was almost lunchtime. She didn't want to waste any more time with them and directly said, \"I'll only give you one chance. Otherwise, go to the prison and reunite with your families.","If you don't say anything, there are others who will.\"","As soon as her words fell, Shen Jian walked into the yard in military uniform. He handed his sword to the guard and walked straight into the hall. Without looking at the people kneeling on the ground, he bowed to Yue Fuguang and said, \"Your Excellency, Junior General Shen Jian is here to report.\""]},{"number":431,"title":"Chapter 431: What Crime Has Been Committed","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang saw that aside from a weary expression and some mud splatters on his clothes, he was otherwise fine, so she relaxed and asked, \"General Shen, did everything go smoothly on this trip?\"","\"Reporting to Your Honor, all went smoothly. We successfully rescued Cao Dajun and arrested Hao Ren along with all the officials of Pinglang County and their families. I brought Hao Ren and his two sons back first to report; the rest will arrive in Yingzhou City a bit later.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded, highly approving of Shen Jian’s arrangements. \"How is Cao Dajun’s health? Is his life in danger?\"","The daughter-in-law of the Cao family had already died from humiliation. If the eldest son’s health were also compromised, Yue feared Cao Xiwang might not be able to bear it.","\"Your Honor, rest assured. Cao Dajun’s life is not in danger; he just needs proper rest and recovery.\" However, due to the severity of the torture he endured, his body was damaged, and he might no longer be able to perform heavy manual labor as before.","But Shen Jian thought such minor details weren’t worth troubling the Grand Tutor with. He had already left money for Cao Dajun’s medical treatment, enough to help the family get through this crisis.","\"Since you’re here, bring the Hao father and sons up now,\" Yue Fuguang said. Upon hearing that Cao Dajun was out of danger, she set the matter aside. She believed that after the Sun family’s assets were confiscated, Prefect Huang would provide sufficient compensation to the Cao family.","There was also the Yu family, a major local clan whose members held considerable land. Once those were freed up, countless landless commoners would benefit.","Yue Fuguang intended to finish the interrogations all at once; eating could wait.","Shen Jian went to retrieve the prisoners. When Li Qingxue heard that Hao Ren and his sons had been captured, her face turned even more sour than Yu Wei’s.","Half of her energy and spirit drained away. She had thought that if she stalled long enough, Ating might hear the news and escape in time. But she had not expected that this famous Grand Tutor Yue would be so meticulous, having sent men to Pinglang County early on.","Li Qingxue stared earnestly toward the door. When she finally saw the familiar, handsome figure appear at the courtyard entrance,","her hanging heart died completely—or rather, there was a secret flicker of relief inside. Although she wished Ating could survive alone, now that he was trapped alongside her, she thought perhaps they could die together. If they accompanied each other on the journey to the Yellow Springs, they might even reunite in the next life.","If Yue Fuguang knew what she was thinking, she would call her infatuated and naive—a hopeless romantic through and through.","Not to mention that both of them had blood on their hands, which might make it uncertain whether they could even be reincarnated.","Moreover, this Hao Fangting was no good man. On one hand, he kept his beautiful, devoted fiancée dangling before him, using her to carry out shady deeds.","On the other hand, he was entangled with his delicate maternal cousin, and without his fiancée’s knowledge, he had secretly pledged himself to the cousin, promising to take her as a secondary wife in the future.","Hao Fangting’s plan was to enjoy the pleasures of a wife and a concubine at the same time.","If it had been the Li Qingxue of the past, she would never have agreed. But after the Li family fell, she became a pariah. Had he not taken her in and given her refuge, her current status would mean she should even be grateful to become his concubine.","That’s exactly what Hao Fangting thought behind the scenes.","Now, playing the lovestruck hero, Hao Fangting’s face filled with heartache when he saw the beautiful but haggard Li Qingxue, showing no trace of his earlier schemes. It could only be said that wearing a mask and acting had become second nature to him.","The Hao father and sons, shackled at the ankles, now had disheveled hair, their fine clothes wrinkled and stained with mud.","Their shackles clanked loudly as they moved.","Seeing Hao Fangting so beaten, stripped of his former elegance and grace, Li Qingxue’s tears uncontrollably streamed down her face. Her Tinglang had never suffered such hardships before!","\"Ah Xue!\"","\"Tinglang!\"","‘Holding hands, gazing at each other through tear-filled eyes, they were speechless, choked with sorrow.’ Yue Fuguang’s mind involuntarily recalled those words as the two exchanged soulful looks.","\"Hao Ren, do you admit your guilt?\" Yue Fuguang had no desire to watch the passing lovers’ longing glances and directly pressed Hao Ren below.","\"Your Honor, this subordinate admits guilt!\" Hao Ren, seemingly aged years overnight, saw his would-be daughter-in-law Li Qingxue and the four others.","His pupils shrank, a weight like a thousand-pound stone pressing down on his heart as his kneeling body trembled slightly.","But as his eldest son spoke with Li Qingxue, he hurriedly racked his brain for a way to save himself.","When Yue Fuguang asked if he knew his crime, Hao Ren’s eyes flickered. As a man well-versed in Dayan law, he confessed immediately.","As expected, after his confession, the Grand Tutor asked the question he had anticipated.","\"Then tell me, what crimes have you committed?\"","Yue Fuguang naturally noticed the flash of calculation in Hao Ren’s eyes, but she didn’t mind there was a saying: brute force can break ten ingenious moves. She held the upper hand, so she would play along with these people for a while.","\"Your Honor... I should not have shielded the nephew of Prefectural Vice Commissioner Sun and wrongfully imprisoned Cao Dajun. I should not...\"","His eyes shifted to Li Qingxue, who was kneeling aside, her face wet with tears. \"I should not have, out of lingering affection, harbored the descendant of a criminal.\"","He seemed to gather his courage as he raised his head to look at Yue Fuguang, “Your Excellency the Grand Mentor, please see clearly. The betrothal between our two families was decided long ago. If not for the death of Fang Ting’s mother, which required him to observe a period of mourning, the two would have been married long ago.","When Your Excellency saw that His Majesty did not punish the daughters who had already married into other households, I presumed that Li Qingxue, who was already my Hao family’s future daughter-in-law...”","Hao Ren bowed deeply, pressing his forehead to the ground. “Thus, it was out of foolishness—I was unable to endure my son’s persistent pleas—that I officially recognized Qingxue as our daughter-in-law.”","Behind him, his two sons, Hao Fangting and Hao Fangyuan, also knelt and kowtowed.","But Yue Fuguang remained unmoved. She slowly stroked the teacup in her hand and said coldly, “And what else?”","Hao Ren was stunned for a moment, then gritted his teeth. “I also accepted lavish gifts from Vice Prefect Tong, as well as tributes from the gentry of Pinglang County.”","“Continue!” Yue Fuguang urged him when he paused.","Hao Ren then confessed one by one some offenses of varying severity, even recounting how, during the imperial examinations, he had placed a cursed doll to harm the classmates ranked above him. But he did not utter a single word about his connection to the illegal mine.","When Yue Fuguang pressed him on why Cao Dajun had been thrown into death row, he merely claimed it was a mistake by the prison guards and that he had known nothing about it.","[Host, I’ve discovered that this Hao Ren is not the biological son of the Hao family. And the iron ore from the Yu family’s mine has not been transported far.]","The timely information from the system gave a boost to Fengtang, Huang Xie, and the others who overheard it.","[Host, they sent everything to the neighboring Xin Prefecture, where the Yu family owns an estate spanning several large mountains at the border between the two prefectures.","The Yu family set up a smelting site on the mountain. The iron ore was turned into pig iron and sold to the Ouyang family. You may not know this family, but if I mention the Tong family, it may ring a bell.]","The Tong family? Two years ago, Emperor Mingxi had already purged most of the former imperial clan members who had plotted rebellion.","However, from what the Tong family themselves had revealed, there remained another branch of the Tong clan within the Great Yan territory—including the youngest son of the last emperor."]},{"number":432,"title":"Chapter 432: Misplaced Origins","paragraphs":["He had sent people searching for over two years without finding him. Had he changed his name and fled?","\"Little Bead, what is the identity of this Hao Ren? How does this matter involve the Tong family? And what about the Ouyang family? Could they be the last branch of the royal Tong family His Majesty has been searching for all these years?","They changed their names and surnames to avoid the court's investigation!\"","At the mention of the Tong family, everyone present, including Shen Jian, Feng Tang, and Huang Xie, felt a jolt of excitement. If they could successfully apprehend them, Huang Xie, for one, could redeem himself for several charges of negligence. The merit would even outweigh discovering the iron mine and exposing the Yu family, as Wei Shouyi’s survey had shown the Yu family’s iron ore reserves to be modest. A minor clan like the Yu family couldn’t forge anything significant in three years.","[Master, there’s some juicy gossip here—want to hear it?]","Hearing about gossip, Yue Fuguang couldn’t help but quickly open the system task panel. Sure enough, when Hao Ren appeared, the system triggered a new task. That meant Hao Ren carried something that could affect the rise or fall of Dayan or become an obstacle on her path to completing her mission.","\"You call it juicy gossip—how could I not want to hear it?\" Yue Fuguang squeezed the system object in her hand. She had to admit, the system’s manifestation, the \"Realm-Breaking Pearl,\" was not only beautiful to look at but also smooth to the touch, with a slight elasticity. Playing with it was truly stress-relieving.","Feng Tang, Shen Jian, and Wei Shouyi caught a glimpse of the divine artifact, a shimmering, flowing pearl being toyed with in the Young Master’s hand—squashed, stretched, and rolled around. Seeing this, they couldn’t help but chuckle inwardly.","This usually arrogant artifact, which scolded anyone it pleased and even made His Majesty cautious, now had to obediently sit still in the Young Master’s hands, just like everyone else, letting her do as she wished.","[Master, please don’t squeeze so hard. I can barely speak. Do you still want to hear the gossip?]","Hearing the system’s complaint, Yue Fuguang reluctantly stopped. \"Alright, I won’t squeeze. Talk quickly!\"","[Master, this Hao Ren was originally named Tong Jiaren, a grandson of the last emperor’s youngest son. During the previous emperor’s purge of surviving remnants of the former dynasty, the entire Tong family relocated.","At just over three years old, Tong Jiaren got separated from his family during the move. Fortunately, a loyal old servant protected him. Unable to find the Tong family, the boy and the old servant spent years wandering in hardship.","Then, when he turned ten, just as he was worrying about not having an identity to study openly, he was mistaken by chance as the long-lost son of the Hao family, Hao Ren.]","\"You mean Hao Ren assumed the identity of the Hao family’s son?\"","[Exactly. Hao Ren is a genuine Tong by blood. He successfully passed himself off as the Hao family’s lost child not only because he was of similar age and appearance, but also because, like the Hao family’s missing son, he had a butterfly-shaped birthmark on his left wrist.]","\"How coincidental!\" Yue Fuguang voiced the thought on everyone’s mind.","Meanwhile, Hao Ren, kneeling in the hall, had begun confessing his journey from an upright official to a lawbreaker. In short, his refrain was that everyone else was to blame; he had only strayed due to various temptations.","Yue Fuguang sneered inwardly. Did Hao Ren really think she was just a naive twelve-year-old girl?","His words were half-truths. She was too busy savoring the gossip to bother with him—she’d just treat him as background noise.","Not just Yue Fuguang, but the others paid little attention to his words. After all, the gossip was far more reliable than anything Hao Ren said.","Only Yao Tongpan, tasked with recording the case, diligently kept writing, transcribing Hao Ren’s every word without missing a detail.","[Master, this coincidence is both coincidental and not so coincidental.]","\"What do you mean? Is there more to it?\"","[The Hao family was originally nobles of the former dynasty, producing high-ranking officials and noblewomen. They only declined in the Dayan dynasty.","Tong Jiaren’s grandmother was a secondary consort to the last emperor’s youngest son. Those with Hao family blood share a unique birthmark, which he inherited from his grandmother, the former consort.]","Everyone silently nodded. Yue Fuguang remarked, \"I see. So Hao Ren and the Hao family truly were destined to be connected.\"","[When Hao Ren passed the imperial exam at twenty and gained some local fame, he was recognized by the Tong family, who had changed their surname to Ouyang.","It was then that Hao Ren secretly reunited with his birth family, though publicly he still carried the Hao family’s identity.]","\"And what happened to the real Hao son? Is he still alive?\"","[Master, don’t you think Sun Tongzhi bears some resemblance to Hao Ren in certain ways?]","Yue Fuguang paused, her teacup hovering in midair. She immediately caught the system’s implication—but how could such a coincidence be possible?","These two were accomplices in crime—how could they have such deep ties! She had encountered Sun Tongzhi last night but received no mission prompt, so the problem must lie with Hao Ren.","Prompted by the system, Yue Fuguang unconsciously glanced at Hao Ren kneeling on the ground and compared him to Sun Tongzhi, whom she had met only the previous evening.","Sun Tongzhi had a thick beard—the most luxuriant facial hair of any official Yue Fuguang had seen in Dayan. Even the rugged Wei Shouyi didn’t have such dense whiskers. Because the beard covered half his face, Yue Fuguang could only detect a few similarities between the two men from their eyes and brows.","\"Little Bead, could it be that no one noticed Sun Tongzhi and Hao Ren’s resemblance because of his bushy beard concealing half his face?","Does Sun Tongzhi even know he isn’t a Sun family member?\"","Given his wholehearted devotion to the Sun family, doing everything to protect their only grandson even in violation of the law—aside from his rotten character—he truly seemed to have gone to great lengths for the Suns. This suggested he might really be unaware.","[Master, Sun Tongzhi was kidnapped before he turned three. His memories were all of growing up in the Sun family.","The Sun couple, childless for years after marriage, bought him as their son. When he turned six, they had two sons of their own.","A common folk belief holds that an adopted son brings good fortune for biological children. So even after having their own sons, the Sun couple treated their eldest, though not as well as the biological ones, fairly decently overall.","They supported his studies, arranged his marriage, and once he passed the imperial exams, they became even more caring, especially since his two younger brothers achieved nothing.","So Sun Tongzhi never truly doubted his identity.]","\"Sun Tongzhi doesn’t know his own identity, but does Hao Ren know?\" Yue Fuguang asked the key question. The others sized up Hao Ren in their minds. Perhaps influenced by his Tong family background, they felt he was somehow devious.","[Hehehe, Hao Ren actually does know. He found out through the Ouyang family’s connections. Originally, Hao Ren and the Ouyangs feared his identity might eventually be exposed.","So they planned to find the real Hao Ren—and kill him to eliminate the threat.]"]},{"number":433,"title":"Chapter 433: There's a Mine at Home","paragraphs":["Who would have known that after years of searching, by the time Hao Ren finally got concrete information, Sun Tongzhi had already become an official and had married a woman from a branch of the prestigious Bai family. His official rank and status were higher than Hao Ren, who was a rising star.","Since he couldn’t find a clean way to get rid of him for the time being, Hao Ren thought of a scheme—he planned to drag Sun Tongzhi into the mud.","As it turned out, Sun Tongzhi was no paragon of virtue. After a few years of corruption by the Ouyang Family, he was easily pulled into the mire, covered in filth.","“How deep was his involvement in the iron mine business?”","Feng Tang and Huang Xie exchanged glances. That was the real issue. The crimes Sun Tongzhi committed by abusing his power for his nephew’s sake paled in comparison to his complicity in the iron mine affair.","[Sun Tongzhi was Hao Ren’s—or rather, the Ouyang Family’s—biggest protector in Yingzhou Prefecture. He received dividends from the iron mine.","Although he didn’t know exactly what Hao Ren was doing with the iron ore, he dimly suspected it was for some illegal purpose.","At the very least, he guessed it was being sold to people planning rebellion or to foreign forces. But it never occurred to him that a mere county magistrate wanted to rebel himself.","If he had known it was that kind of capital offense, he would have done whatever it took to distance himself.]","In earlier years, when the Dayan Dynasty was in decline and its fall seemed obvious, there might have been officials entertaining treacherous thoughts, hedging their bets.","But in the past three years, Dayan had grown strong, showing signs of becoming the leading nation among the six. Wanting to rebel was about as realistic as wishing for a fart to turn into a feast!","What Sun Tongzhi didn’t know was that the Ouyang Family—or rather, the Tong family—had a burning desire to restore their former kingdom, no less urgent than Murong Fu’s obsession with reviving the Great Yan, and perhaps even more desperate.","“Isn’t Hao Ren dragging Sun Tongzhi down with him just biting the hand that feeds him?”","If she saw it correctly, Hao Ren was the most promising member of the Hao family’s current generation. Sacrificing a more talented relative for his own selfish gain was nothing short of repaying kindness with enmity.","The Hao family: We’re so lucky to have you!","[The Hao family had poured all their resources and connections into Hao Ren, which was how he had come to hold the position of county magistrate of a first-tier county. Naturally, he didn’t want to lose that support.","After the Yu family discovered the iron mine, they initially relied on their own servants for small-scale secret mining. But once Hao Ren found out, he coerced and bribed the Yu family, promising his eldest son and daughter-in-law positions, forcing his way into a stake.]","“So Li Qingxue was really a fool. She thought she was managing the estate, but in reality, she had already been sold out.”","[No kidding. Her dear Hao wasn’t just involved with his cousin behind her back, but her father had also arranged another marriage for him.","After Hao Ren meddled in the mining operation, he secretly ordered his men to cooperate with the Ouyang Family, abducting people from three villages deep in the Pinglang County mountains to work the mine.","Unfortunately, one of those villages was completely wiped out.]","Wu Yong’s hand froze. He had spoken with those captured villagers. Some of them had indeed said that the villagers from one hamlet had all vanished. It turned out Hao Ren had ordered it.","“As for the living, let them be settled well. For the dead, let Hao Ren go down and personally apologize to them.”","[Master, the Ouyang Family smelted the iron ore into swords, knives, and armor. They also colluded with the Southern Yue.","Before finding the Tong family treasure, the Ouyang branch relied on Southern Yue’s financial support for their daily expenses.","You see, they were once royalty and had grown used to a life of luxury. They couldn’t lower themselves to live like commoners. So, they were naturally grateful for Southern Yue’s backing. In fact, because of the Southern Yue influence, they had gradually split into two factions: one advocated for restoring the kingdom; the other wanted to attach themselves to Southern Yue, helping them conquer Dayan in exchange for credit and favors.]","“Is currying favor with a conquering lord that easy? Aren’t they afraid Southern Yue will kill the donkey once the mill is gone?”","[In the original timeline, not long after Southern Yue invaded Dayan, this branch of the Tong family was slaughtered by bandits, wiping out their entire clan.","Master, most of the three high-yield crop varieties that Southern Yue now possesses were smuggled out in secret caravans via the Ouyang Family.","Were it not for the strict government control over border trade and land production outputs over the past two years, making it impossible for the Ouyang Family to smuggle large amounts of seeds, Southern Yue might already be planting them on a large scale.","I also detected that, under cover of the drought, the Ouyang Family used grain to exchange for seeds from the common people, intending to send them to Southern Yue in a few days.]","Once the Guoshi seeds were mentioned, everyone present—except Yue Fuguang—started to feel restless.","Dayan’s current strength and stability, even in the face of internal drought, were half due to the contributions of these three high-yield seeds.","If other countries got their hands on them on a large scale, wouldn’t Dayan’s advantage be eliminated?","The men, who had long coveted their neighbors’ lands, could not let that happen!","Just as Shen Jian was itching to march out and wipe out the Ouyang Family right then, a single sentence from the system froze him in place.","[Master, in this whole affair, the Yu family appears to have been coerced by Hao Ren and the Ouyang Family behind him, but in truth, they did it all deliberately.]","“How so, Little Bead? Is there a story within a story?” Yue Fuguang said, realizing from the system’s tone that it had unearthed new information.","Though it spoke with confidence, what it was about to reveal couldn’t have come to it much earlier than it came to her.","[Master, guess who stands behind the Yu family?]","Who? Wei Shouyi, who was in charge of arrests, furrowed his brow and stroked his beard as he thought. To him, the Yu family was just a provincial landlord-gentry clan. Yesterday, when Huang Xie led the welcoming party for the young master in Yingchuan City, the head of the Yu family had been among them.","He was a coward. When taken into the prefectural prison last night, he spilled everything like beans from a shattered bamboo tube without even resorting to torture.","He was just a bloated, soft steamed bun, rich but weak and timid—did someone like that dare to toy with him, an imperial envoy?","Yue Fuguang squeezed the system again. “I won’t guess. You tell me yourself who’s behind them—”","She paused for a moment before blurting out her own theory: “Is it one of Dayan’s neighbors, or Peak Mountain? It can’t be Netherbloom and Heavenly Pavilion—those two guilds of executioners and assassins, right?”","[Master, don’t underestimate the small Yu family. Although their clan numbers less than a thousand, behind them stand the two major forces of Peak Mountain and Netherbloom.]","“Peak Mountain and Netherbloom? What could they see in an unheard-of family like the Yu family?”","[Because the Yu family has mines! The iron mine we’ve found so far is just a small bait to lure out Hao Ren and the Ouyang Family behind him, even Southern Yue.","They have larger mines elsewhere that they’ve never revealed—actually, no, it’s not that they didn’t reveal them. Even among the Yu family themselves, only a handful know the actual locations.]","“What do you mean? They don’t know where their own mines are?”","What difference did that make from hiding money so well that you yourself forget where you stashed it?","Impossible, don’t you think?"]},{"number":434,"title":"Chapter 434: Child Character Scorches the Mouth","paragraphs":["“Master, the Yu family’s ancestors were once serving as mountain surveyors under the Imperial Metals Office. During the years of dynastic change, the political situation was unstable—who knew if the Xie family could hold onto the throne?","Back then, an ancestor of the Yu family used his position to survey several rich mineral deposits but concealed them and failed to report them. His original plan was to preserve them for his descendants.","Only a few successive heads of the Yu family and a handful of core members had a rough idea of this. As for the specific location of the mines, because that ancestor who discovered them died suddenly without passing on the details, the secret remains unsolved to this day.","Yet somehow, though the Yu family guarded the secret tightly over generations, the news of their hidden rich mines still reached the ears of the Panshan and Youtan sects.","They used human-skin masks to replace members of the Yu family’s direct lineage, all for the purpose of investigating the mines.”","“Little Bead, since you say it’s a rich mine, tell me, how rich is it? And what kind of mine did the Yu family’s mountain surveyor find?”","Indeed, Feng Tang, Huang Xie, and the others were equally curious, while generals like Shen Jian and Wei Shouyi speculated—could it be an even larger iron ore deposit?","Wei Shouyi now deeply regretted how, yesterday, when he met that cowardly head of the Yu family, he had so easily believed his words. If only he had applied a few more lashes with his saltwater-dipped whip, maybe the man would have confessed then and there!","On reflection, he shuddered: had it not been for the great artifact spirit’s love of gossip, tracing the clues like a vine, uncovering one shocking revelation after another, wouldn’t he have failed in his duty?","“Your Grace, this guilty official has confessed everything he can!” Just as everyone was straining to hear more, they were interrupted by Hao Ren’s words.","Disturbed in her gossip, Yue Fuguang showed no annoyance. Instead, she swept a curious glance over the Hao father and son. “County Magistrate Hao, are you sure you’ve confessed everything?”","Her fair fingers tapped lightly on the table, one after another, neither heavy nor gentle, yet each tap struck Hao Ren’s heart like a sledgehammer.","Seeing Yue Fuguang watching him with such amused interest, Hao Ren’s heart began to waver. His hands, pressed against the ground, trembled slightly. He had no idea just how much the Junior Preceptor knew about his background and secrets.","Every single one of those secrets was enough to cost him his head. Hao Ren dared not admit it, nor could he gamble on it.","Yue Fuguang noticed him lowering his head, gritting his teeth in silence, and her patience wore thin. “Don’t want to talk? Then let me, the Junior Preceptor, say it for you!”","Feeling weary from sitting, she stood up and walked a few steps, stopping three meters away from them, looking down at them from on high. “County Magistrate Hao, shouldn’t I really be calling you County Magistrate Tong Jiaren?”","At the name Tong Jiaren, Hao Ren could no longer pretend. He jerked his head up, staring at Yue Fuguang in terror, his mouth opening and closing as if to speak, but no words came out.","Behind him, his eldest son fared even worse. Hearing the surname “Tong,” he prostrated himself on the ground, trembling uncontrollably.","Over the years, he knew all too well how the imperial court dealt with members of the Tong family—either rotting away in some sunless prison for life or being dragged to the vegetable market to be beheaded.","Given the extent of his involvement, his fate was inevitably the same as his father’s: to lose his head.","Watching his father and eldest brother, the Hao family’s second son looked utterly bewildered. He had handled some trivial matters involving the mines, but what did “Tong” have to do with any of this? County Magistrate Tong Jia—was that his father? Did that mean they weren’t surnamed Hao at all, but Tong?","When the second son thought of the most infamous members of the Tong clan... then looked at his elder brother, who looked like he had lost his own father, and his actual father, whose expression was darker than if he had buried a son, his body couldn’t stop shaking!","In his heart, he screamed: I don’t want to be surnamed Tong! I’m not one of those Tong people!","Li Qingxue, witnessing her future father-in-law and lover react so violently to the name “County Magistrate Tong,” understood all too well with her sharp mind.","As a former member of the prominent Li clan—even if just a branch daughter—her family had thoroughly investigated Hao Ren and his lineage before agreeing to the betrothal.","As the magistrate of an upper-ranked county under Yingchuan Prefecture, Hao Ren’s son managing to marry a Li branch daughter was a testament to the allure of the Hao family’s past prestige. After all, the Hao family had once been a distinguished clan with considerable legacy.","Li Qingxue knew that Hao Ren had been kidnapped as a child.","Her thoughts raced as she linked things together: perhaps this Hao Ren was not the child the Hao family had lost, but one deliberately swapped in by the Tong family!","Their goal, too, was to seize the Hao family’s wealth and connections, much like the earlier incident with the yu clan.","One had to say, women had such vivid imaginations. While her speculation wasn’t entirely accurate, it wasn’t far off from the plans that the Ouyang family and Hao Ren had later conceived.","Hao Ren’s face stiffened, twisted as he forced a feeble defense. “The Junior Preceptor jokes. This guilty official is surnamed Hao, from a great clan of Yingzhou.”","As for the surname “Tong,” he didn’t even utter it, as if the word burned his tongue.","“Is that so?” Yue Fuguang mused. “Then why do I hear that your birth parents were members of the former imperial clan? Oh, they’ve changed their surname now. What was it...”","She paced a couple of steps before the Hao father and son, then suddenly snapped her fingers, as if recalling something. “Ah, right—it’s Ouyang, isn’t it, County Magistrate Hao?”","Hao Ren's hands clutched the hem of his robe in a death grip, his head bowed low as he used silence to resist Yue Fuguang's interrogation. He dared not look up, afraid she would see the terrified, twisted expression on his face.","Yue Fuguang paid no heed to his reaction. Instead, she turned to ask Huang Xie, the prefect, who was still trying to process the cascade of shocking news he had just received.","\"Prefect Huang, are there any wealthy families or prominent clans with the surname Ouyang in Yingzhou?\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang’s question, Huang Xie immediately rose from his chair and bowed in response. \"Your Excellency, there is a landowner who moved here from elsewhere and settled on the outskirts of Yingchuan Prefecture. His surname is indeed Ouyang.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded and waved her hand. \"I’ll trouble Prefect Huang to send someone familiar with the situation to accompany my men in raiding the entire Ouyang clan.\"","Over the past two years, she had witnessed so many household raids that ordering one herself hardly weighed on her conscience. Perhaps the Ouyang family included innocent people, but distinguishing good from bad was the court’s job. Hers was simply to complete the system’s tasks and earn points. Selfish as it might be, what wouldn’t she do for her own sake?","\"General Shen, I’ll need you to handle this,\" she said. For capturing remnants of the former dynasty, who could be more suitable than Shen Jian, the emperor’s own nephew?","When Hao Ren heard the hurried footsteps of Shen Jian leaving, his face turned completely ashen. He knew who Shen Jian was—after all, he and his father had been arrested by the very same man.","Hao Ren closed his eyes in despair. Thinking back on everything they had done over the years, he knew the Ouyang family was finished. Their actions had left them no escape.","Yue Fuguang waved her hand to have Hao Ren and the others taken away. She had never expected him to tell the truth anyway. She had only used him to test the system, and sure enough, it triggered a task. Moreover, using him as a pretext had led to the Tong family being exposed, completing half of her mission.","Once the irrelevant people had been dismissed, only Yue Fuguang, Feng Tang, Huang Xie, and the other officials remained.","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and then asked Wei Shouyi, \"General Wei, how is the interrogation of the Yu family going?\"","Wei Shouyi recalled that the Divine Artifact had mentioned a rich mine, yet there had been no further update, and he couldn’t help feeling a bit anxious."]},{"number":435,"title":"Chapter 435: Helian Mountains","paragraphs":["He hesitated for a moment before saying, \"Your Excellency, I have heard that a distant ancestor of the Yu family discovered a rich mine, but when I inquired about this matter, the descendants of the Yu family flatly denied it.\"","He cautiously glanced at Yue Fuguang's expression before continuing, \"In my humble opinion, they did not appear to be lying.","Thus, I am currently uncertain about the truth of the rumor.\"","[If you’re uncertain, just keep asking. Although the eldest Yu doesn’t know the exact location of the mine, he still knows that his ancestors had a mine.","Besides, the Yu family hasn’t been idle over the years. How do you think that iron mine was discovered? It was found by accident while the Yus were searching for mines using their ancestors’ work notes!]","Yue Fuguang suddenly understood. So that was how it happened. She said to him, \"That iron mine was bought by the Yu family the year before last. What a coincidence—buying the mountain one day and finding the iron mine the next!\"","It turned out they had seen the egg first before buying the chicken.","\"So, where is this rich mine located, and what type of mineral is it?\" she said.","The others heard the topic finally come back around and silently breathed a sigh of relief in their hearts.","[Master, you absolutely won’t believe this, but the mine is located in Xinzhou, just below Yingzhou. Two of the deposits are hidden in the Helian Mountains. We’ll pass by that area in a few days if we keep traveling.","As for the mineral, the main one is a silver mine, and next to it is a modest gold mine. Gold and silver together are indeed considered a rich mine for mortals!]","The others silently nodded in their hearts. A gold and silver mine—even if the reserves were modest, it could still be counted as a rich mine.","[Master, how do you plan to tell the Emperor and the others? Or are you just going to pretend this never happened?]","Everyone’s hearts sank. If the Junior Preceptor didn’t intend to tell His Majesty the truth, even if they had the skill to find the location, given the current attitude of the Great Yan court, no one would dare to mine it.","They had lacked the nerve before, and now, with the Divine Maiden who could alleviate the drought, who would dare to defy her wishes?","Even if the Emperor harbored such an intention, Feng Tang rubbed his bare arms and thought—let’s see how the Censorate would tear into His Majesty!","As for Wei Shouyi, though a military man, Mingxi Emperor and Huo Ying trusted him to accompany Yue Fuguang as a guard precisely because he was a man of rough edges yet careful.","Thus, he couldn’t help but think more deeply. They had been out for nearly a month, and news of the localized heavy rainfall in Great Yan had already reached their neighboring countries.","Just now, he had received a message from Zheng Zicheng: several countries had sent many people to infiltrate Great Yan. Because of the Divine Maiden’s rain-making, even their long-planted, dormant spies throughout Great Yan had been activated.","Their goal was simple—invite the Divine Maiden to their own countries!","Right now, the Junior Preceptor was like a piping hot, fragrant pastry. Great Yan couldn’t do enough to honor her, so who would dare to cross her at this time?","Yue Fuguang didn’t know the myriad thoughts running through their minds, but she could roughly guess what they were thinking. She said casually, \"When we get there, I’ll see how things are. The Emperor has plenty of money now anyway. Telling him a day earlier or later won’t make a difference.\"","So she intended to tell them, just not immediately. The others felt a bit more at ease.","The afternoon passed leisurely for Yue Fuguang. After the entire Ouyang clan, over a hundred people, were arrested, she ordered Shen Jian to have them, along with Hao Ren and others, escorted back to the capital for trial.","Sun Tongzhi’s prison cart naturally accompanied them.","When they set off the next day, Yue Fuguang was surprised to see Cao Xiwang and his son among the crowd, silently kowtowing to see her off.","She had thought that Cao Xiwang, after learning of his eldest son’s rescue the day before, had returned to Pinglang County that same day.","\"We respectfully bid farewell to the Divine Maiden!\"","\"We respectfully bid farewell to the Divine Maiden!\"","Yue Fuguang once again looked towards the people of Yingchuan City. Regardless of age or gender, they were burning incense and kowtowing to send her off. The feeling of her scalp tingling had faded.","But if anyone looked closely, they might notice her body stiffening slightly as she climbed into the carriage.","However, in such a solemn and serious occasion, even her own guards dared not look up at her, so no one noticed their Divine Maiden’s awkwardness. Her idol image was preserved.","Yue Fuguang’s party first traveled east from Yingzhou, sprinkled water over Yunzhou and Qingzhou, and then headed south.","As she had expected, after Cao Xiwang successfully stopped her carriage on the street to file his complaint, such incidents occurred frequently along the way.","To avoid slowing down the journey, Yue Fuguang didn’t personally handle cases anymore. Instead, she ordered Feng Tang and Shen Jian to select experienced subordinates to stay behind and oversee the local yamen in handling the cases involved.","After all, disaster relief was as urgent as putting out a fire. The crops in the fields couldn’t wait. Didn’t the tired faces of the traveling party and the lack of rest show how pressed for time they were?","Due to technological limitations and other reasons, the water stored by the common people of Great Yan was only a drop in the bucket for the current drought.","That was why her carriage and party were greeted with reverence by the local people at every stop.","The incense and worship they received along the way was enough to let her traverse the entire map of Great Yan once more.","Sometimes, Yue Fuguang gazed at her luxurious carriage, drawn by five white horses and traveling through the rain, and an image popped into her mind unbidden—the water trucks from her hometown back in her original world, spraying water as they wove through city streets.","Admittedly, the system had its moments. Just as the image of a water truck came to her mind, the system played a catchy tune for her for free.","Wait, wasn’t that the same music that the national water trucks from her country all used?","\"System, you’re taking it too far!\"","What about her divine maiden image? Playing such catchy music made things feel weird, even if it did remind her of home!","She even had a conditioned reflex to dodge upon hearing that tune!","[Host, don’t you find it familiar and touching? Does it bring back memories of how fast you used to run to avoid the water truck?]","How fast? Not that fast—she just ran to find shelter as soon as she heard the music from a distance!","[Host, look, isn’t that the Helian Mountains up ahead?]","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes at the system’s clumsy change of subject but didn’t say anything. After all, there was a major task waiting for them ahead!","\"System, can you pinpoint where those people are hiding?\"","Their party had entered Xinzhou from Xuzhou. Xuzhou, like Yingzhou, bordered Xinzhou. Part of the Helian Mountains’ lower range lay at the border between Xuzhou and Xinzhou.","They were now close to the middle section of the Helian Mountains.","As they entered Helian County, it happened as usual. From a distance, they could see townsfolk lining the streets.","After leaving the county and entering the rural roads, even more villagers stood by the roadside, looking at her carriage with even greater reverence and piety.","[Host, some of those people are mixed in among the crowd. Can you spot a few using your own eyes?]","She had to spot them herself?","Yue Fuguang looked out through the sheer curtain. With her current eyesight, the curtain didn’t obstruct her view."]},{"number":436,"title":"Chapter 436: What Did They See","paragraphs":["Her gaze swept across faces weathered or young, curious or devout. Due to dehydration, everyone’s complexion looked unwell—chapped lips, wind-bitten skin. The hair of men, women, and children, whether coiled or loose, was either caked with dust or greasy and matted, the result of too long without water to wash.","Yue Fuguang couldn’t tell from their clothes or expressions which among them were commoners of Dayan. But suddenly a glimmer sparked in her eyes. Delicate, pale fingers reached out the window. “Wind, come! Clouds, come!”","A whirlwind rose from the ground, lifting the carriage curtains embroidered with lotus blossoms. As the fabric whipped in the wind, Yue Fuguang saw the vast swaths of dark clouds swept in by the gale.","“Rain, come!” Her voice, neither loud nor soft, reached the ears of the people lining the road, following the wind and clouds.","They looked up at the sky, which had long withheld rain. For the first time in over half a year, the blazing sun was no longer overhead. In their dull and vacant eyes, a light seemed to flicker, reflected in the thickening clouds that now filled the sky—and in the warm, drizzling rain that soon fell upon them, drop by drop.","This was the life-saving water they had begged the heavens for, over six months, to no avail.","“Long live the Divine Maiden!”","“Long live the Divine Maiden!”","The people along the road opened their mouths to welcome this sweet dew, their eyes truly lit by the rain striking their bodies. Those who could rekindle their hope for life because of this rain were her own people. As for those who weren’t lit up...","Yue Fuguang rubbed her wrist. That only meant one thing—this rain hadn’t fallen on their own fields!","“Little Pearl, I think I’ve spotted which rats are hiding among the people!”","Good heavens, quite a crowd had come. That single rain had exposed those spies with their top-notch disguises! The one who came up with this idea must be a huge... well, a clever little thing!","Everyone knew that local folk, after a long drought, would be overwhelmed with joy and awe when they saw blessed rain falling from the sky. If you didn’t cry with excitement, people might say you were reserved. But to show expressions of shock, envy, and grim determination? That was another story.","If it were raining on your own land, why would you envy anyone? As for the look of grim determination... Yue Fuguang really wanted to snort at them.","When Dai Yuxing, He Jin, and the other guards heard Yue Fuguang’s words, they wordlessly moved closer to her carriage. Yu Huaixian leaped onto the carriage, replacing the driver. To be safe, he insisted on personally driving for Yue Fuguang.","Meanwhile, Wei Shouyi, Shen Jian, Feng Tang, and Wu Yong silently signaled the front-clearing and rear-guard guards to prepare for first-level combat readiness.","Along the way, they had left behind many escorts to help oversee the petitions of the common people blocking the road. By now, Yue Fuguang’s guard had dwindled by more than two hundred since they set out.","But she swept her gaze over the bad guys hidden among the crowd. A hundred or so of them. Advantage is mine!","Just as the thought “advantage is mine” zipped through her mind like a shooting star, she looked up and saw the dense red dots marked by the system in the distant mountain forests.","[Master, see that? Not only are their people mixed in with the commoners, but there are plenty in the forest ahead too. I’ve roughly counted—close to a thousand.]","Yue Fuguang stared at the red dots and asked, “Even if they’ve hidden a thousand in the mountains, isn’t a ratio of 2.3 to 1 still in my favor?”","Exactly. Shen Jian and Wei Shouyi rested their hands on their sword hilts, staring at the distant rocks. In their hearts, they thought: the soldiers under their command are no pushovers. Each one is a soldier handpicked by them, no worse than those spies.","[Master, look at the positions of those hidden among the people. They’re clearly planning to take Dayan’s civilians as hostages.]","Yue Fuguang carefully replayed the scenes she had just witnessed. She frowned—the system was right. Beside them were either elderly people, children, or frail women—all easy to control and basically unarmed.","If these people actually threatened her with ordinary civilians, then, to protect her image and avoid harming innocents, she really would have to hold back.","“So what do you suggest we do now?” She could let them go for the moment, but these people were clearly here to “invite” her. And now that they had seen her rain-controlling ability firsthand, they would never give up on such a treasure.","After all, everyone else was suffering from drought. Only Dayan had stored water and now could make artificial rain. One gain, one loss—Dayan’s national strength had suddenly leaped up two tiers compared to its neighbors. Which other state could just sit by and do nothing?","[Master, why don’t you demonstrate your power a little? Scare them off?] If the spy weren’t so close, the system itself would have loved to strike them with lightning.","Yue Fuguang had originally wanted to “control with voice,” but she noticed some people had their hands resting on those next to them.","If things went wrong, these people might panic and lash out. Even one death would sully her divine image.","She absolutely could not let anything that might harm her reputation happen before her eyes!","When dealing with mortals, the Divine Maiden must achieve total dominance.","“Little Pearl, what do you think I should do to scare these mortals?”","It wasn’t like she was going to jump out right now and perform some martial arts display. That would be embarrassing and ridiculous!","“Master, only immortals can fly. How about you give it a try and fly?”","Fly, huh? Yue Fuguang stroked her chin, seriously considering how feasible the system’s suggestion really was.","She couldn’t fly on her own, but inside her storage ring she had not only an interstellar flying hoverboard and flying shoes she bought from the marketplace, but also a pair of flying boots from the cultivation world.","The hoverboard was the first to be ruled out. Sitting down didn’t have the same imposing presence as standing—though, technically, the hoverboard was meant for standing. Yue Fuguang admitted she didn’t have the courage!","Besides, she had an idea for an entrance “effect.”","It had to be the cultivation world’s “Step-by-Step Lotus Boots.” These shoes not only allowed mortals to soar through the sky by consuming spirit stones but also created a lotus with every step, making the wearer appear ethereal and divine—a perfect way to max out the “awe factor.”","That was precisely why these boots, with only those two functions, were outrageously expensive. If it weren’t for a 90% off sale and her desire to make a grand impression, Yue Fuguang would never have spent 28,000 for shoes originally priced at 280,000.","Yue Fuguang had no idea that, after hearing the system’s suggestion and waiting in vain for her reply, the crowd couldn’t help but wonder: had the young master already regained more of her abilities as a celestial being?","After all, for mortals, the sky was a place they could never reach, yet it often appeared in their dreams and fantasies.","Was there any human who didn’t long for the ability to soar through the heavens?","That longing was perhaps even greater than their hope for rain—if not more!","“Alright, then,” she said.","The crowd heard Yue Fuguang’s words, and in the next moment, a radiant light shot out from her carriage. That brilliant, shimmering glow stood out starkly against the dark, rain-soaked wilderness, catching everyone’s attention.","Those who had been kneeling with their heads bowed were suddenly blinded by the flash of light. When they looked up, they witnessed a scene they would recall countless times for the rest of their lives, each time unable to stop themselves from gasping in awe.","Even in their old age, whenever the elders of the Helian Mountains talked about the goddess of those days, they would inevitably bring up the sight they had seen that day.","What had they seen?"]},{"number":437,"title":"Chapter 437: One Step, One Lotus","paragraphs":["They watched as, amidst the pouring rain, the goddess’s chariot blazed with multicolored radiance. The goddess, clad in flowing rainbow robes, stepped out from the chariot one step at a time. With each step she took, a beautiful lotus bloomed beneath her feet.","Those lotuses also shimmered with light—some white, some cyan, some gold, some red... The goddess walked step by step toward... the sky!","The rain falling from the heavens parted around her, not a single drop touching her beautiful celestial gown.","The common folk had only ever heard that immortals could fly, but this was the first time they had witnessed a goddess walking on empty air, lotuses blooming with every step.","“We pay homage to the Great Goddess!”","“We pay homage to the Great Goddess!”","Cries of worship rose and fell one after another in Yue Fuguang’s ears.","“Rise, all of you!” Yue Fuguang’s voice came from the sky, ethereal and distant, carrying an innate, mysterious divinity and authority. Whether they were near or far, the voice seemed to speak directly into their ears.","“We thank the Great Goddess!” Before the people could rise on their own, they felt an invisible force lifting them up.","Some obeyed and stood up, and the force disappeared. Others instinctively tried to resist, unaware that the more they struggled, the tighter the binding power became.","Yue Fuguang suddenly realized that her entrance could only intimidate for a moment. So, taking advantage of the moment when these people’s minds were shaken and their control over those around them relaxed, she used the lifting force to capture them all at once.","Thus, the scene along the road became one where over a hundred people among the crowd struggled desperately against the invisible bonds.","Those around them stared wide-eyed, not understanding what was happening. These “villagers” seemed to be pulled and dragged by an unseen force, quickly lifted into midair.","Then, with a loud bang, they were dropped like dumplings into an open space in the middle.","Mud and water splashed everywhere, and cries of agony rang out incessantly.","Yue Fuguang looked down at the crowd below; from the moment she acted to the moment she pulled out all one hundred-plus people, only a few breaths had passed.","But that was enough time for the people below to snap out of it. Yet, surprisingly, among the tens of thousands of people lining the road, not a single one stepped forward to question the reason.","Were they frightened?","That reaction wasn’t right. With tens of thousands of people, shouldn’t at least one or two have rushed out to demand why she was arresting people for no reason? Shouldn’t they have said something like, “Even immortals must be reasonable”? After all, in the early days of the drought, many had criticized her as “ineffective.” Could it really be that there wasn’t a single self-righteous saint or saintly figure among them?","If so, she was indeed quite lucky today?","Little did Yue Fuguang know that the news of her refusing to forgive believers had already spread far and wide. Every local person kneeling here today had been carefully selected by the local magistrate as the most devout followers.","Otherwise, if an entire county had heard that the goddess was passing through, even if not everyone came out, there would certainly have been more people than this.","Yue Fuguang thought the county just had a small population, unaware that there was not a single rebellious local among them.","As for the people from outside, the county magistrate stood among the crowd, his gaze cold as he looked at the unfamiliar faces bound like zongzi by Shen Jian’s men.","Although he couldn’t tell what was wrong with these people, if the Young Preceptor had singled them out for arrest, they must have some problematic identity.","He stepped out of the crowd, bowed to Yue Fuguang in the air, and said, “Your subordinate, Feng Su, magistrate of He Lian County, pays respects to the Young Preceptor.”","“Magistrate Feng, are you puzzled as to why I am arresting these people?”","“Your subordinate knows that the Young Preceptor must have a reason for arresting them. I will not ask. However... is there anything this county can do to help?”","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow at his response and finally took the time to study this magistrate of a lower-tier county.","Feng Su, a second-class jinshi graduate from the tenth year of Tianyou, was thirty-eight years old this year. He was of medium build, with a slightly dark complexion. He had served as magistrate of He Lian County for five years. Because he had no connections in high places, even though it had been nine years since he passed the imperial examinations and was appointed as a magistrate in the provinces, he was still just a minor magistrate.","Moreover, every place he had been assigned to was a lower-tier county.","But judging by his governance record, while unremarkable, it was still decent and competent.","The words he spoke suggested that this man had both intelligence and emotional intelligence. What he lacked was merely an opportunity—and opportunities were something Yue Fuguang had in abundance.","“These people are enemy spies.”","Yue Fuguang’s words were light and calm, but to those present, they struck like thunderbolts.","Not just Feng Su, the county chief, but even the common folk of He Lian County knew what enemy spies were.","Although He Lian County was still somewhat far from the border, when it came down to it, Xinzhou was a border region of Dayan, with some land bordering Nanyue.","The people living near the border had truly suffered from Nanyue’s depredations. Every single year, there would be several skirmishes at the border.","The area here was suffering from a drought, and it was said that the neighboring country of Nanyue had also not seen a single drop of rain in over six months. The people there were barely surviving.","Could these men be those wolves from Nanyue, knowing that their goddess could control rain, and coming to snatch her away?","Among the people, there were not a few clever individuals, including many scholars. A quick thought led them to guess that these men harbored ill intentions.","“Great Goddess, are these men here to snatch... snatch away...?” A man dressed as a scholar, his blood running hot with anger, boldly shouted out his question. But when he got to the end, realizing what he had impulsively done, he instinctively shrank back in timidity.","He had read the goddess’s poetry countless times and revered her deeply, so he suddenly felt that asking such a question would be an act of blasphemy.","Yue Fuguang watched his face gradually turn red, his eyes darting around in embarrassment as if looking for a crack in the ground to crawl into.","But the rain-soaked earth, now swollen with water, offered him no such refuge.","“You guessed correctly. These men are indeed targeting me.”","The confirmation of his guess caused an uproar across the crowd. The once-silent wilderness, filled only with the sounds of wind and rain, suddenly came alive with the most rustic curses from men, women, the elderly, and children.","Taking the mothers of the targets as the center, relatives as the radius, fathers as the fulcrum, and ancestors as the goal, Yue Fuguang deeply experienced the diversity of linguistic expression.","Some bold men even wanted to rush over and kick the bound one hundred-plus men.","“Silence!”","As soon as Yue Fuguang called for silence, it was like pressing the pause button on this torrent of national cursing. When the people realized what they had said to the goddess in their fury, they were terrified and knelt to beg for forgiveness.","Hadn’t those words defiled the ears of a divine being!","“We beg the Great Goddess for forgiveness!”","“We beg the Great Goddess for forgiveness!”","Yue Fuguang waved her broad sleeve, and a gentle breeze swept through. As the people began to bow, the breeze supported them and straightened them up.","“When the world suffers a great drought, traitors and thieves inevitably run rampant, and petty schemers covet the lands of Dayan. I only wish for you all to remain ever vigilant and never give the enemy an opportunity to take advantage.”","“We will uphold the goddess’s decree!”","“We will uphold the goddess’s decree!”","Yue Fuguang brushed aside the faint embarrassment that flickered through her heart and instructed Feng Su, “Magistrate Feng, you should thoroughly spread the news of this matter among the uninformed citizens of He Lian County.”"]},{"number":438,"title":"Chapter 438: Reaction in Southern Yue","paragraphs":["\"Xinzhou is the first line of defense for Dayan. Your tasks are very heavy.\"","Yue Fuguang looked toward the distant mountains and forests. So many had sneaked in without any sign being detected, which meant that both the officials and border troops in Xinzhou bore responsibility.","\"Rest assured, my lord. I will ensure the common people are well informed.\" That day, the goddess had brought rain, appeared before the crowd, and left lotus blooms in her wake—such treatment had never been seen elsewhere.","Without needing him to say more, within a single day, the people around Hexian County would all know.","The reason it spread only to surrounding villages was not due to limits of communication, but simply that a commoner could only travel so far in one day!","Feng Su assumed the Grand Preceptor would return to the carriage and continue onward. But in the blink of an eye, the goddess had once again lifted her foot and walked toward the Hèlián Mountains. The people below followed, running along the lotus path that bloomed under Yue Fuguang's steps.","Lotus flowers paved the road as she walked for two miles, soon reaching a spot not far from the foot of the mountain.","[Host, do you plan to handle all the ambushers by yourself?]","Yue Fuguang sighed helplessly. \"With my current persona, I cannot afford any flaw in my abilities.\"","For a divine being, you could be bad-tempered or unpredictable, but you could not lack divine power. What was divine power? Raising the dead and making bones bloom with flesh were the basics.","\"If I let Shen Jian's men go up to capture them, there will inevitably be injuries and deaths. Those I can heal, I can save. But the dead... I cannot bring back.\"","A deity who could not resurrect the dead would suffer greatly in the faith of the people.","It wasn't that she was overly cautious, but people were simply practical. They could not do it themselves, yet they demanded that others always succeed!","She herself was human. Did she not know the human mind?","In the end, it meant that a god could never show a health bar in front of mortals!","The people who had stopped looked up. They saw the goddess lightly touch the void with her delicate hand. Thunder rumbled. Purple lightning snakes swam through the rain. The sky began to crack from the center, like a thin sheet of ice struck by a stone.","The cracks were not black but dazzling gold—a burning gold that made you dare not look directly.","Every fissure spread, making sounds like shattering glass—slow, crisp, one after another, mingling with the rumbling thunder like a heavy hammer striking the hearts of the tens of thousands watching below.","Unconsciously, the crowd was forced to close their eyes from the blinding golden light. When they opened them again, they saw that the golden glow had turned into threads of gold, falling like shooting stars and vanishing into a mountain peak in the distant Hei Lian ranges.","Soon, everyone realized those golden threads were not mere lines—they were ropes of gold binding people holding sharp blades, dressed in black with masked faces and unknown identities.","The thunder continued to roar overhead, like an angered deity warning the world.","Yue Fuguang brought the captives down the mountain and tossed them onto the ground. Without another word, she flew into the carriage like a flash of light.","\"Shen Jian, leave some men to deal with this. The rest will depart now.\"","Her plan was to traverse Xinzhou in three days, heading from the border city of Lancheng to Xingzhou.","Her abilities had grown stronger. A single rainfall could now cover over a hundred and fifty miles—such progress far exceeded her own expectations.","Yue Fuguang looked back at the people of Hexian County still seeing her off. Along the journey, the rain had made the common folk revere her as a true deity. With her incense offerings flourishing, was it any wonder her abilities grew so quickly?","Having entered Xinzhou just two days prior, Yue Fuguang did not yet know that news of her arrival had already spread. Not only had the people of Xinzhou heard of it, but the neighboring nations of Nanzhao and Nanyue—suffering from severe drought—had spread word from village to village. People from counties near both borders were gathering in groups and heading toward the Dayan border.","\"Third Sister-in-Law, are you heading to Sanshui Gully too?\" An elderly woman, her face sallow and lips cracked from severe dehydration, sat resting with her family under a half-dead tree. Looking up, she spotted fellow villagers coming into the woods.","\"Aunt Hu, you're going to Sanshui Gully as well?\" The woman called Third Sister-in-Law glanced around and lowered her voice.","Although the road to Sanshui Gully was full of travelers, and everyone knew each other's purpose, the officials above had issued a ban, so she instinctively kept her voice down for fear of being overheard.","\"Isn't that right! I've been worshiping the goddess for over two years. I heard that in one more day, she'll reach the border. So my family and I must go to the nearest place to offer her incense!\"","Aunt Hu shifted her seat and motioned for Third Sister-in-Law, who was holding a seven or eight-year-old girl, to sit on a stone beside her.","Her husband and son went off to chat with Third Sister-in-Law's husband and sons.","\"Auntie, do you think we could beg the goddess to send rain for our fields too?\" Third Sister-in-Law's land had only been watered once the previous month with water carried from the mountains. After that, not a single drop had touched it. Watching the crops wither from drought, she was frantic, her lips covered with blisters, but there was nothing she could do.","The mountain streams had dried up. Even drinking water had become a problem, let alone irrigating the fields.","The water they had stored was limited. In a few days, they might even have to slaughter the chickens and ducks—not because they wanted meat, but because there wasn't enough water to keep them alive.","Aunt Hu knew what she was thinking. Who didn't want the goddess to send sweet rain for their fields? Having lived for forty or fifty years, Aunt Hu could see plainly that drought was rampant everywhere—this was no temporary disaster.","Aunt Hu had once been the daughter of a scholar. Being literate, she saw further and understood more than most ordinary women.","The goddess was the deity of Dayan. The people of Nanyue also worshiped her, but whether the goddess herself acknowledged them—her foreign believers—was uncertain.","Yet, seeing the misery on Third Sister-in-Law's face, Aunt Hu held back discouraging words, saying only, \"I've heard the goddess is still young, in her growing stage. Her rainfall has limited range. We're far away. Even if she wanted to bless us, it would be difficult!\"","She then pointed toward the Nanyue capital. \"The emperor and officials won't allow it.\"","Of course, Aunt Hu and Third Sister-in-Law did not know that their emperor and officials had colluded with their neighbor to try to \"invite\" the goddess they worshiped into their own country.","But the plan had failed. The emperor and his ministers were now like ants on a hot pan, burning with anxiety.","\"Your Majesty, Xiao Yi and all his men were captured on the spot. Even General Qin Hu and his thousand one hundred soldiers were taken by Yue Fuguang alone! According to intelligence gathered from our scouts...\"","Han Qinbao, Minister of War of Nanyue, knelt before Emperor Gan Sheng and described the scene in detail.","When they first received the report, they were terrified. The intelligence described that rain, how Yue Fuguang had single-handedly stopped a thousand troops with absolute dominance, made the arrests, and... walked with lotus flowers blooming beneath her feet. Every detail made them break out in cold sweat."]},{"number":439,"title":"Chapter 439: Final Battle","paragraphs":["The fact that the Grand Yan's Junior Preceptor Yue could control the rain was already giving them headaches. While doing everything possible to silence the people, they had also long planned to use extreme measures to \"invite\" her to the Southern Yue Kingdom.","Now they were being told that the Divine Maiden could not only control the rain but also possessed superhuman strength, capable of soaring through the sky and diving into the earth!","Upon receiving this news, the Minister of War and the other officials took a while to compose themselves at the government office. Only after their legs stopped trembling did they call each other to report the matter to the emperor.","Such news would likely be impossible to keep secret. In a few days, as merchant caravans traveled between the two countries, the information would inevitably leak in.","What? Close the trade routes?","Even if the emperor agreed, the officials who had all invested in the various merchant caravans would never consent!","They would use the argument that \"the ancestral laws cannot be abandoned\" to silence the emperor and claim that \"refraining from eating for fear of choking\" was unacceptable.","The Minister of Personnel shot a glance at Han Qinbao, who was constantly wiping sweat, stepped forward, and reminded the grim-faced emperor, \"Your Majesty, the immediate priority is how to minimize the impact of this matter!\"","From what they knew, given how much the Grand Yan court cherished Junior Preceptor Yue, once they learned that Southern Yue had attempted to seize her, the Grand Yan ruler and his ministers would surely retaliate fiercely.","Putting themselves in their shoes, if their own kingdom had such a treasure and a neighbor coveted it enough to act, even if the attempt failed, they would still tear a chunk of flesh from the neighbor as the bare minimum. Otherwise, how could they explain themselves to the treasure herself and to the people?","Gan Sheng’s face darkened as he lifted his eyes to glance at the old ministers below. These old relics were all holdovers from his father's reign, arrogant because of their seniority, showing him only superficial respect as the emperor.","If their power weren’t so deeply entrenched in the court, he would have long since purged these presumptuous old fools!","Despite his inner fury, Gan Sheng kept his voice cold, displaying the virtuous demeanor of a wise ruler accepting good counsel. \"Then, my esteemed ministers, do you have any good solutions to resolve this?\"","The plan to \"invite\" Junior Preceptor Yue to Southern Yue had been jointly discussed and approved by all of them. Although Gan Sheng had pushed quietly and overtly, everyone present had supported it, so no one could escape responsibility.","Did the Southern Yue ruler and his ministers want to kill Yue Fuguang?","The answer was naturally yes. Over the past three years, they had spent two of them attempting every method to eliminate her.","Unfortunately, after more than ten large and small operations involving a hundred operatives, they hadn’t even managed to touch a corner of her clothing.","Gan Sheng had to admit that Yue Fuguang was even harder to kill than the emperor himself!","\"Your Majesty, the immediate priority is to send an envoy with generous gifts and a state letter to Grand Yan.\" A purple-robed elder with graying hair stepped forward.","He bowed and continued his advice, \"Your Majesty could inform the Grand Yan emperor that Southern Yue wishes to spend a great sum to invite Junior Preceptor Yue to help solve our kingdom’s drought.\"","\"Unacceptable!\" A middle-aged man in a red official robe stepped forward, bowing deeply with extreme respect. \"Your Majesty, I, your humble minister, believe there are issues with Chancellor Li's proposal.\"","\"Oh?\" Gan Sheng suddenly showed interest, leaning forward with a smile as he looked at the man. \"Minister Fei, tell me, what is unacceptable about Chancellor Li's proposal?\"","\"Your Majesty, our previous actions have already infuriated the Grand Yan ruler and his ministers. Even if we now seek to mend relations, knowing that we tried to 'invite' Junior Preceptor Yue to Southern Yue, the Grand Yan emperor will not easily agree.","Consider this, Your Majesty: if Grand Yan were Southern Yue, would Your Majesty allow a treasure of the kingdom to take such a risk?\"","The others inwardly shook their heads.","Fei Yongxing lifted his head, gazing at Gan Sheng with blazing eyes. \"And ask yourself, Your Majesty, if our kingdom possessed a being like Junior Preceptor Yue who could communicate with the gods, and neighboring countries were suffering disasters, what would you do?\"","There was no need to ask. Not only Gan Sheng but all the Southern Yue ministers thought the same: \"Strike while the iron is hot!\"","Helping? Impossible!","\"Minister Fei means that Southern Yue and Grand Yan are destined for war?\"","Under his rule over the past few years, Southern Yue had grown increasingly strong. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have laid all kinds of plans to swallow Grand Yan.","But given Grand Yan’s recent development, a direct clash would cost Southern Yue dearly.","Gan Sheng’s gaze unconsciously shifted toward Nanzhao. This operation had also involved Nanzhao, which the Grand Yan emperor surely already knew.","Nanzhao could no longer completely wash its hands of the matter. That meant this war couldn’t be fought by Southern Yue alone.","\"This is only my humble guess,\" Fei Yongxing continued, elaborating his thoughts to the emperor. \"Your Majesty, our kingdom is currently suffering from disaster, with livelihoods in ruins. In contrast, Grand Yan enjoys prosperity thanks to Yue Fuguang and the high-yield crops she provided.","Under these circumstances, with the enemy strong and us weak, starting a war would be extremely disadvantageous!\"","\"Then what does Minister Fei suggest?\" Although Gan Sheng found the words \"enemy strong and us weak\" grating, it wasn’t the time to argue. Fei Yongxing was still useful for now—he would settle this account later.","Unaware that his words had landed him on the emperor’s blacklist, Fei Yongxing earnestly offered his strategy for the king’s sake, blurting out a single word without hesitation: \"Delay!\"","\"Delay?\" Before Gan Sheng could respond, Chancellor Li immediately seized the chance to interject, his eyes flashing undisguised contempt. \"How does Minister Fei plan to delay? Do you think the Grand Yan ruler and his ministers are fools?\"","Fei Yongxing gave a perfunctory bow to Chancellor Li. \"Chancellor Li is discerning. What I mean is to delay temporarily while we intensify border deployments.","Our people envy Grand Yan for having water, don’t they? My king, we can use their hopes to inspire the youth to enlist. Once we take Grand Yan, will Southern Yue still lack water?\"","Fei Yongxing was smug, believing his plan was brilliant—\"the people’s will\" could be used after all!","Chancellor Li regarded the complacent Fei Yongxing with a noncommittal expression. \"Still, Minister Fei, what are you planning to use to delay? And how long can this 'temporary' delay last?\"","No one knew how long the drought would continue. If, as their intelligence suggested, it lasted two or three years, and internal conflicts weren’t diverted outward, civil unrest would be inevitable.","Shifting that conflict outward wasn’t a bad idea in theory, but the Grand Yan ruler and his ministers were no pushovers. Grand Yan was no longer a soft target to be bullied!","A sharp glint flashed in Fei Yongxing’s eyes, and he knelt with a look of utmost loyalty, kowtowing to Gan Sheng. His voice trembled slightly as he spoke, \"Your Majesty, my plan may require some sacrifice from the long princess.\"","\"Atang?\" Gan Sheng raised an eyebrow. He hadn’t expected Gan Tang to be involved here.","\"Minister Fei, tell me what is needed of the long princess.\" He patted the armrest of his dragon throne gently, his voice more gentle than ever before. \"Although she is a woman, the long princess is one of the rare, intelligent, and courageous princesses of Southern Yue’s imperial family.","Born into royalty and nurtured by the people's tribute, she understands righteousness and devotes herself to the kingdom. If there is something she can do for the good of Southern Yue, as long as it is not too difficult, I will consent on her behalf.","Minister Fei, speak your mind freely!\""]},{"number":440,"title":"Chapter 440: Peace Marriage","paragraphs":["Premier Li and the other veteran ministers, hearing this, couldn't help but roll their eyes. The emperor and his trusted confidant, Fei Yongxing, were surely up to no good.","Their actions at this moment seemed more like a performance staged for the ministers' benefit.","Premier Li and the others sat like clay statues, eyes fixed, noses aligned with hearts, silent and still. They lowered their heads, watching coldly as the emperor and the \"brilliant\" Fei Yongxing put on their show.","Fei Yongxing felt this was his moment of glory—a loyal minister serving his sovereign. Encouraged by Gan Sheng's gaze, he finally revealed his true intent. \"Marriage alliance!\" he declared loudly.","He blurted out the words \"marriage alliance,\" his face swiftly adopting an expression of pain and reluctant resolve, his eyes brimming with tears. He was so emotionally charged, you'd think it was his own daughter being sent away.","Premier Li sighed inwardly. What an act from that old scoundrel Fei!","\"A marriage between two kingdoms is no trivial matter,\" Fei continued, smiling with an air of absolute control. \"Your Majesty, we can use this negotiation period to make our deployments.\"","Though heavy troops had always guarded the border, those forces were clearly insufficient if war truly broke out.","The Southern Yue could even launch a surprise attack while the wedding procession entered Dayan, catching them off guard.","Premier Li's lips curled into a mocking sneer, but it vanished in an instant.","By now, they all understood. The emperor and that scoundrel Fei had joined forces to remove the Eldest Princess, that obstacle in their path.","As the only legitimate offspring of the late emperor, Gan Tang naturally had her followers.","Neighboring Nanzhao had a female emperor, and Southern Yue, separated from Nanzhao by only a single mountain, wasn't as hostile to women in power as other kingdoms.","When the late empress, the Eldest Princess's mother, was alive, she had intended to arrange a marriage with a military noble family. Though the plan was dropped after her untimely death,","the Eldest Princess was still surrounded by many outstanding young men—sons of civil officials and elites from military families.","The emperor feared that if the Eldest Princess truly married a military noble as her consort, it would strengthen her power. So he was trying to drive her out of Southern Yue in a roundabout way.","As for Fei Yongxing, news had it that his sons were among the most attentive suitors around the princess.","Both his eldest and second sons were smitten with the princess. Last year, during the literati delegation to Dayan, the second son of the Fei family had nearly sneaked along.","Rumor had it that he’d failed only because the eldest son had sabotaged him.","How could Fei Yongxing, who prided himself on being the emperor’s most loyal subject, tolerate that?","For the sake of his own family, he would even scheme against a royal princess. If he didn’t have the emperor’s secret backing, then this Fei Yongxing had some nerve!","Gan Sheng, who had just sworn to agree on the princess's behalf, now put on a troubled face. He rhythmically tapped the armrest of his dragon throne. The ministers kept their heads down, offering neither support nor opposition.","Though it involved state affairs, at its core it was still the royal family's private matter. Since they weren't sure if the emperor had orchestrated this beforehand, they chose to stay silent.","\"A distant marriage alliance does indeed wrong Ah Tang,\" Gan Sheng said, his face full of reluctance, his voice laced with sorrow. \"But it concerns the very survival of Southern Yue. We can only let her bear this burden.\"","Gan Sheng looked around at the officials, his tone resolute. \"Ah Tang is still in Dayan. I'll write her a letter immediately, explaining the situation. Knowing her sense of duty, for the sake of Southern Yue, she will surely agree.\"","Gan settled the matter on his own, but before concluding, he still asked, \"Dear ministers, what do you think of this plan? Do any of you have suggestions for the Dayan marriage candidate?\"","By now, Premier Li had basically figured out the emperor's intentions. When asked for a candidate, he pondered briefly before replying, \"Your Majesty, as far as I know, the only adult, unmarried sons of the Dayan emperor are the Fifth and Sixth Princes. In my opinion, the Fifth Prince, Xie Zhiquan, is quite talented and keeps a low profile. He would be a suitable match for the Eldest Princess.\"","Gan Sheng nodded. \"Then choose the Fifth Prince to marry my Ah Tang.\"","Far away in the capital city, Shangjing, Gan Tang, who was currently reading the biweekly Shangjing Gazette, had no idea that her dear imperial brother was planning to sacrifice her marital happiness to buy time for Southern Yue to attack Dayan.","And Yue Fuguang, who was already approaching the border, had no clue that her failed 'kidnapping' attempt had sparked Southern Yue's idea of a marriage alliance—an alliance that would ultimately affect her sister's marriage.","Yue Fuguang, still sprinkling water along the way, was now less than two hundred li from the border.","She quietly took out colorful plastic pendants from her storage ring—the ones inscribed with 'The Five Kings unite all under heaven' and 'The Divine Maiden descends, destiny lies in Dayan.'","[Host, are you planning to use these worthless plastic trinkets to stir up trouble among the neighboring kingdom's commoners?]","\"System, watch your wording! Besides, plastic is such a rare thing here; I'm the only one in this world who has these. As the saying goes, rarity makes value. These people won't be able to make plastic for centuries. Are you telling me a piece like this isn't worth more than gold of equal weight?\"","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes, picked up a pastry from the small table, bit into it fiercely, and continued, \"More importantly, it's not the material that matters, but the words carved on it. Given how superstitious these people are about gods and fate, these plastic plaques might not sway the nobles, but they'll definitely influence the common folk.\"","She planned to teach these kings—who ruled by keeping their people ignorant—a lesson. If they chose to stupefy the masses, they'd have to swallow the consequences.","Yue Fuguang pulled out a few drones from her storage ring. Tomorrow, when she reached the border, she would fly them across. The opposite side was a Southern Yue village. If she dropped the plaques in different spots, at least one would be found.","The things were so unusual that whoever found them would find it hard to keep them hidden. If a commoner got their hands on something so 'precious,' they'd surely sell it for money. Circulation would ensure the message spread.","As for hiding them in fish bellies or burying them, that would be too troublesome and lacked control. Using drones was more direct.","Whether it would work or not—this was just something she'd do in passing. She didn't care much about the outcome.","\"Look! It's really raining on the other side!\" On the Southern Yue side, only a small river, about a dozen meters wide, separated them from the Dayan border.","The river had dried up due to the drought. The riverbed was cracked, and even the mud at the bottom had turned into ash-white powder.","On both sides of the river, the Dayan bank was a muddy, barren wilderness. Originally, this land had belonged to Southern Yue, but near the end of last autumn, it suddenly fell under Dayan's control—a full thirty li of territory.","On the Southern Yue side, there were a few connected hills and wastelands. A few li further down the mountain path, a handful of small villages appeared.","It was high noon on the Southern Yue side, the sun blazing overhead. People from nearby towns and villages, having heard that the Divine Maiden would pass through this area, had brought their families and had been waiting on the Southern Yue hills for a day or two.","Families like Widow Hu and Third Brother's—who lived farther away—had arrived a day or two early.","Hills on the Southern Yue side were full of people, and the Dayan side was no less crowded.","The county magistrate and village head had long told the locals that the Divine Maiden was still several dozen li away."]},{"number":441,"title":"Chapter 441: Plastic Badge","paragraphs":["The goddess herself would not personally visit the border town, but that could not stop the common folk from leaving their homes, gathering in every alley and street, finding a spot that seemed agreeable, and kneeling down to burn incense.","They had only burned their incense halfway when, above their heads, the bright sun that had shone moments before was suddenly replaced by flashes of lightning and rolling thunder, dark clouds gathering thickly. A fierce wind howled, yet it did not extinguish the still-burning incense.","\"Father! Mother!\" some young lads cried out, unable to help themselves at the sight.","\"What are you yelling for? You kneel properly, you brat!\" the father grabbed his son, who was trying to rise in agitation, and pressed his head down. Thump, thump, thump—he kowtowed three times before the three sticks of incense.","The dust kicked up covered the dark-haired boy's face from head to toe, but he only grinned foolishly.","There were many such households. Those who had already been kneeling and mumbling their wishes, upon seeing the flying sand and stones and the approaching downpour, straightened their kneeling postures even more, kowtowing to the incense and candles with even greater reverence and piety.","In no time at all, the rain poured down in torrents. On the Dayan side, with the river wasteland as the boundary, it was as if the heavens had sprung a leak.","Yet on the Nanyue side, the sky remained clear and vast, the sun hanging high overhead, bright and blazing.","If someone stood on a high place and looked down, they would see a dry river dividing the two sides—one bright, one dark; one sunny, one rainy; one teeming with life, one dead—like the two sides of yin and yang.","High above the curtain of rain, several drones pierced through the storm, flying silently across from Dayan into the airspace of Nanyue.","Yue Fuguang operated the drones, deliberately heading toward inhabited villages and towns, as well as fields that showed clear signs of cultivation.","[System, what do you think of this place?]","She pointed to a road that was not very wide and asked the system. This road appeared to be the main route connecting nearby villages. Because of the drought, it was thick with dust, covered in footprints—clearly a path often traveled.","The drones Yue Fuguang used were small models produced by the system, each only about fifty to sixty centimeters in size, with a maximum flight range of two hundred li. The place she had just pointed to was about one hundred and twenty to one hundred and thirty li from her current position, about forty to fifty li inside Nanyue territory.","She thought it best to start from the border area, affecting the Nanyue common folk first. Here, the mountains were high and the emperor far away. By the time word fermented and reached the emperor's ears, some time would have passed.","And in that time, the words of \"heaven's decree\" would have spread widely among the common people.","For what spreads fastest among the common folk? The answer, of course, was the more bizarre and strange the tale, the larger the audience. Those who heard it would inevitably share it with their family and friends.","07, who was operating six drones at once, took a glance at the scene Yue Fuguang had pointed to and fully agreed with her choice. [I think it works! As for the remaining plaques, we'll drop one every ten to twenty li.]","Of the twelve colorful plastic plaques, a few were bound to be picked up by someone.","Though 07 had complained earlier, anything customized by the system's store could not be of poor quality. Once one of these things was found, its discovery could not be hidden.","While Yue Fuguang was busy with her mystifying tricks, she did not realize that across the river, witnessing the scene of a torrential downpour on just one side, the Nanyue common folk—whether from their intense longing for rain or something else—had quickly moved from shock.","Soon, the people of Nanyue who had awoken from their daze brought out incense and candles, and some even brought out small statues of Yue Fuguang.","Facing her statue, they began murmuring fervently and kowtowing with devotion! The incense they burned was so thick that from a distance, an uninformed observer might think the drought was so severe that the forests themselves had caught fire.","In the crowd, a child stared at the heavy rain on the other side of the river and couldn't help licking his cracked lips. He asked his parents naively, \"Father, Mother, if we lived on that side of the river, would we have water to drink too? Enough to never run out, so we could even water the fields and never go hungry?\"","The child even thought that if the wind were stronger, it might blow some of the rain from the sky over to their side.","The child's innocent words stunned his parents. This was a question they had never considered. All they had ever hoped for was the goddess's mercy, that while blessing the people of Dayan, she might also show compassion for them, these pitiful souls.","But... but if they had really been people of Dayan, then surely, they would have received the goddess's favor.","Thinking this way, the father still instinctively scolded, \"What nonsense are you talking, child?\" He was afraid that someone with ill intentions might report his daughter's childish words.","But was it really nonsense? Everyone who heard those words fell into silent contemplation. Some people's gazes already began shifting back and forth between the two sides, as if searching for something.","The rain on the Dayan border fell from morning to night. The parched earth finally drank its fill, and the people of Nanyue watched the spectacle all day long.","When the wind ceased and the rain stopped, as they made their way home, thousands of people filed down from various hills in small groups.","Among them were the elderly and children, yet not a single person spoke. All of them trudged along in silence, heads bowed.","The children, held by their parents' hands, seemed to sense that their mother and father were in low spirits. Even when they needed to pee, they only dared to ask their elder sister to take them to the side of the road.","Suddenly, a child felt the dry, gray-white grass beneath his feet not as the familiar softness, but rather a hard object digging into his sole.","He picked it up casually, making a motion to throw it away, when his sister called out from behind, \"Erwa, wait!\"","The elder sister, about eight or nine years old, snatched the object from her five- or six-year-old brother's hand and examined it closely. The moment she saw it, she couldn't help shouting, \"Father! Mother!\"","Upon hearing their daughter's cries, their parents did not take it too seriously. The area was full of people, so the kids couldn't be in any real danger.","\"Erwa, if you're done peeing, come back right away. If you keep fooling around, watch out for your little bottom!\"","\"Father, I haven't peed yet!\" he said, instinctively covering his small rear. Judging by his quick movement, it had suffered plenty for his mischief.","\"Father, come quick and see what treasure I found—\" the word \"look\" was still on his lips when his clever sister clamped her hand over his mouth.","If she hadn't, maybe nothing much would have come of it. But her nervous reaction, combined with the little boy's mention of treasure, immediately drew the attention of those nearby.","Before the children's parents could react, a busybody approached with a friendly smile. \"Little one, tell uncle what treasure you've found, so I can have a look too.\"","He pulled from his bosom a piece of yellowish malt candy the size of a fingernail. It was not only small but looked slightly melted.","Still, none of that dimmed Erwa's desire for the candy.","\"It's a colorful plaque, like a rainbow in the sky!\" He took the candy without putting it into his mouth right away. Instead, he glanced carefully at his sister.","This was treasure they had found together. He was a man, after all, and he wouldn't be selfish and eat it alone. Swallowing his saliva, he waited.","\"Daniu, what's going on?\" The children's parents ran over. The father still wasn't convinced about the supposed treasure their son had found. What valuable thing could a child really discover by the roadside?"]},{"number":442,"title":"Chapter 442: The Melon-Eating System Seems to Be Locked","paragraphs":["\"Father, younger brother found a beautiful little plaque!\" As soon as she saw her parents, the little girl finally took out the plaque she had been clutching protectively to her chest.","Her father took the plaque, less than two inches long, and the few people gathered around couldn't help but gasp when they saw its striking colors and patterns. Yue Fuguang had designed these plaques through the system, making them aesthetically pleasing and collectible—they weren't just inscribed with words.","The plaques were also engraved with landscapes, flowers, birds, and fish. Among the twelve plaques, no two patterns were the same. And those two prophetic lines were like inscriptions on the front and back of a painting, though the characters were golden, impossible to miss.","\"This... this... what is this?\" The child's father had initially thought it was one of those jade plaques used by wealthy nobles.","But when he weighed it in his hand, the heft was off. He had never seen jade before, but common folk weren't fools—jade was made of stone, and stone had weight. Yet this plaque, neither large nor small, felt strangely light in his hand.","\"Brother, that thing in your hand... the material doesn't seem like jade, does it?\" A middle-aged man, dressed noticeably better than those around him, leaned in slightly, his eyes glued to the plaque.","The colors were vivid, the luster fine, but it didn't look like jade at all, nor was it the priceless glassware that was hard to come by.","\"Kind sir, do you recognize this?\" the child's father asked, holding the unknown treasure with a look of anticipation.","The middle-aged man shook his head. \"Never seen it before.\"","\"Oh! The characters on it...\" A young man in a long gown pointed at the lettering, his face full of shock.","\"What about the characters?\" The child's father, illiterate, only thought the golden characters looked beautiful.","\"The goddess descends upon the world, destiny lies in Dayan!\" The upward-facing side bore the floral design. Prompted by the scholar, the middle-aged man finally noticed those eight small characters and read them aloud without thinking.","His voice wasn't loud, but those who heard it couldn't help but freeze. A goddess? This beautiful plaque spoke of a goddess descending to the world!","\"A goddess! This plaque mentions the divine lady!\" The crowd around them buzzed with discussion. Whether they understood the full meaning of those eight characters or not, they remembered this phrase and added their own interpretations.","They had just witnessed the goddess bringing rain to bless Dayan with their own eyes.","So was this a prophecy from heaven? Destiny in Dayan? What about their Southern Yue? Did heaven no longer care for them?","Some, more simple-minded, felt that heaven simply wanted nothing to do with their fate.","But the middle-aged man and the young scholar in green, being a man of wealth and a man of learning respectively, couldn't help but think more deeply.","The scholar in green pursed his lips, then suddenly bowed to the commoner. With considerable politeness, he said, \"Big brother, I am Huang Wei from Weicheng Academy. May I have a look at the back of this plaque?\"","The commoner, seeing a courteous scholar, found it hard to refuse. He was counting on learned men to help him figure out what this treasure was, and how much grain he could exchange it for.","\"Not at all, not at all. I was hoping you could, young master, take a look and tell me what this treasure is!\"","Hearing this, the middle-aged man's eyes flickered.","Huang Wei took the plaque. It was light to the touch, smooth in texture. Turning it over, he saw a landscape painting with six small golden characters: \"When the five kings have finished, the four seas will be one.\"","\"This... what does this mean?\" The commoner scratched his head. He could barely grasp half of the first line, but this one he didn't understand at all.","\"Brother, come, let's talk privately.\"","The middle-aged man spoke up, inviting both the commoner and Huang Wei, who held the plaque, to a spot away from the crowd by the roadside.","\"Brother, I'm not looking down on you, but with the words on this plaque, keeping it in your hands—you won't be able to handle what comes with it. How about...\"","At that moment, Yue Fuguang, still on her way to Xingzhou, had no idea that her dropped plastic plaque had been found on the very first day, turning a poor family's fortunes around overnight, making them moderately well-off.","In the following days, lucky people successively found several more. Yes, \"found\"—ever since the second similar plaque was accidentally discovered, folks within a hundred miles of the Southern Yue border gained an important way to make money: searching for these beautiful jade plaques.","And those two prophetic lines spread far and wide, even faster and farther than Yue Fuguang had initially anticipated.","This even sparked numerous disputes over the unique material of the plaques. Before the Southern Yue military could fully seal the border, many Southern Yue people—carrying packs and families—could be seen crossing into Great Yan.","Whether inspired by the little girl's words or by the prophecies, many clever and decisive individuals had already slipped into the bordering cities of Great Yan before the Southern Yue court could react.","It was only two weeks later that Yue Fuguang learned of this through a confidential letter from the Crown Prince.","Yue Fuguang waved the letter triumphantly. \"System, see? You said those plaques were worthless, but look at what they've accomplished!\"","She was brimming with pride at this moment. If she weren't still in the carriage surrounded by people, she would have loved to put her hands on her hips and laugh uproariously at the sky.","System: What's there to be so proud of? It was all thanks to my help!","But thinking back on its own past, the system inexplicably felt a wave of guilt. Its backbone wouldn't straighten, and it couldn't muster a single bold retort.","Right now, the system feared nothing more than its host asking about the data repair progress!","[Yes, yes, yes, host, you're the greatest, the most resourceful, with the bearing of a great general, you strategize far away and win battles...]","The system began blowing rainbow-colored flattery at Yue Fuguang without restraint...","Yue Fuguang enjoyed the praise, but a growing sense of unease gnawed at her. Was it her imagination, or had the system been acting strangely lately? It always seemed to be hiding something from her.","Should she try to probe a little?","\"Little Tong, how's the data recovery going? I'll still need your information support for our actions against the other countries. You can't let me down.\"","System: !!! The very thing I feared!","[Host, the data recovery has hit a bottleneck. It seems... it seems to be locked.]","\"Locked? What does that mean?\"","[It means... because we've already reached level six and will soon level up to seven, the higher management system has taken notice. Our attempt to repair the data might have been discovered. The Merit System is fine, but the Gossip System seems to have been locked!]","Yue Fuguang's heart sank. The reason she could complete her tasks so smoothly now was entirely thanks to the Gossip System. If she couldn't dig up gossip and expose secrets, she couldn't very well show up as the goddess and openly chat with the ministers and the king of Great Yan over tea and snacks, spilling dark secrets about corrupt officials like one of those gossiping old women under the locust tree at the village entrance, could she?","That would ruin her image—too cringeworthy to imagine!","\"Being locked means we can't continue repairing the data? Will it affect our current usage?\""]},{"number":443,"title":"Chapter 443: That Bastard Xie Laowu","paragraphs":["Although the melon-eating system still had quite a few issues, compared to being completely unusable, she suddenly felt that the current situation was not unacceptable.","The colorful pearl that the system had turned into was in Yue Fuguang’s hand, and it suddenly flickered rapidly, as if letting out a tiny sigh of relief. [Of course it can be used!]","Afraid that Yue Fuguang would keep dwelling on this, it quickly assured her, [Host, rest assured, Tongtong will definitely try to recover the data, but it might just take a bit longer.]","Yue Fuguang’s eyes shimmered as she said with great confidence, “Tongtong, I trust you to get things done!”","Yue Fuguang’s rain-making brigade had marched through Xingzhou and Yizhou, traveling across a large part of the Dayan Dynasty.","“Second Brother Xian, have you found out who sent them?”","During the midday break, Yue Fuguang took the opportunity to ask Yu Huaixian about the identity of the assassins from the night before.","Along their journey, if one were to call it smooth, there were always those reckless enough to launch assassination attempts or sneak attacks. The largest-scale incident was the one with over two thousand people from Nanyue.","Since then, it seemed like a switch had been flipped—over the past half month or so, there had been no fewer than five sneak attacks or assassinations, large and small. Some involved over a hundred people, others just a few dozen. All of them had perished without returning. Yet, despite such a record, those hiding in the shadows did not seem to have been intimidated.","“System, do you think I was too merciful last time? That’s why these people keep coming one after another to annoy me?”","[Hst, showing mercy is fine, but be careful—too much killing will cost you merits!]","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes. “This isn’t the same as when you had me expose the aristocratic families. You weren’t saying that back then!”","[That’s different!] The system felt wronged. [That was a system mission. When we act according to the mission, the main system bears the responsibility, and the karma does not fall on us.]","Yue Fuguang’s eyes flickered. System 07 had just used “we,” implying that whatever she did, it would also share the consequences.","Seeing that Yue Fuguang was silent, the system continued. [Host, since you want to walk the path of immortality in the future, you cannot carry too much karma. Otherwise, when you face tribulation, not only will the lightning be harsher, but the heart demon tribulation will also be a hurdle.]","Yue Fuguang thought: I say one thing, and you fire back with several sentences. The system definitely has something on its mind! It definitely didn’t tell me everything last time.","As Yue Fuguang and the system bickered, Yu Huaixian had also organized his words. “With someone like Lord Feng, who is a master of interrogation, even an iron mouth can be pried open.”","Yue Fuguang nodded in agreement. Over the past two years, Feng Tang had indeed improved his ‘professional skills.’","“We learned from one of them that they were originally bandits from the neighboring mountain stronghold. The stronghold had only fifty to sixty people, surviving by robbing homes and looting. Barely making a living.","A little over a year ago, a group of people arrived at the stronghold. Although they were about the same in number, they all had real martial skills.","These locals were forcibly absorbed into the group. The stronghold’s leader was killed, and the second-in-command became the third-in-command. Everyone there followed the orders of those newcomers.”","Yu Huaixian took a sip of water and continued, “It’s said that those people were brought in by the new second-in-command. The lower-ranking members didn’t know the background of those people.","As for this raid on us, they were forced to do it by those people—calling it a sort of ‘testing our strength.’ The leader was that unlucky third-in-command.”","Yu Huaixian grimaced with regret at this point. “It’s too bad that unlucky second-in-command died instantly—he jumped around the most and was struck down by Commander Dai in one blow.","If we had left him alive, we might have gotten some useful information out of him.”","Yu Huaixian looked at Yue Fuguang eagerly, and she understood his expression perfectly, but she had to pretend she didn’t.","Times had changed. Her melon-eating system had been locked, and querying information unrelated to system missions consumed too much energy—it simply wasn’t worth it.","“Do you all think their story about ‘testing our strength’ is believable?” After all, they were in the open while the enemy was in the shadows. Didn’t anyone with a keen interest across the whole realm already know the size and combat power of the rain-making squad?","Why were they still sending people to die in waves?","And each time they sent people to die, they wouldn’t sacrifice their own, just useless cannon fodder. What was the point?","“Lord Feng doesn’t think it’s believable, so he’s still interrogating the others along with Lord Shen.”","After speaking, Yu Huaixian quickly pulled a letter from his sleeve and handed it to Yue Fuguang. “This just arrived!”","Yue Fuguang took it and saw it was from her family—her grandfather’s own handwriting. She hastily opened it and began reading.","The moment Yue Fuguang finished the first page, her expression turned cold. By the time she read further, Yu Huaixian and Shen Chunying felt the temperature around them plummet. Though it was the warm April of spring, it suddenly felt as if winter had struck.","Shen Chunying exchanged a glance with Yu Huaixian. He shook his head helplessly, earning a glare from her at his uselessness.","Finally, unable to bear the pressure from his colleagues, Yu Huaixian nervously took a peek at Yue Fuguang’s expression and asked cautiously, “Fuguang, what’s wrong? What did Grand Uncle’s letter say? Is something wrong at home?”","Yue Fuguang coldly downed a cup of tea to suppress her anger, then said furiously, “That bastard Xie the Fifth has actually proposed to marry Fourth Sister!”","“Xie the Fifth? Who’s that?” A confused look spread across Yu Huaixian’s face. He couldn’t recall such a figure for a moment. Whoever dared to propose to their family’s Xinjie had some nerve.","After all, over the years, several families had set their sights on Fuguang’s studying companions. Not to mention the other three families, but their own Yu family’s two girls had grown increasingly outstanding over the past two years. There were hardly a few eligible young men in the entire capital who could match them.","“That bastard Xie Zhiquan!” She said, so that was why that guy was so afraid of her—he had been coveting their family’s ‘cabbage’ all along.","Shen Jian and Feng Tang, who had been about to walk over, silently withdrew their big feet. The two dragged each other away in a different direction and slipped off.","Throughout the whole dynasty, no more than three people dared to call a prince a bastard. Even Shen Jian’s mother, the Grand Princess, found it inappropriate to curse her own nephew like that.","If she did, what did that make her, her imperial brother the emperor, her late father the former emperor, and her mother the empress dowager?","Yu Huaixian immediately wanted to slap himself when he heard “Xie the Fifth” was the fifth prince. Why was his mouth so fast?","How long had it been since they left? How could he forget that their divine girl always referred to the emperor’s sons by their rankings, just to keep things simple?","Yu Huaixian happened to be facing in the direction where Shen Jian stood. He had seen with his own eyes that Shen Jian and Feng Tang had intended to come over earlier.","The moment they heard Fuguang yelling at a prince, the two promptly slipped away.","Shen Jian was practically part of the royal family. Seeing Fuguang scolding his own cousin like that, he probably wouldn’t take offense, right?","Yu Huaike stiffly forced himself to ask, “How did the Fifth Prince suddenly decide to propose to Xinjie?”","Did princes have the final say in their own marriages? And since when did the royal family announce ‘proposals’? Wasn’t it custom for them to just issue an imperial decree betrothing whoever they fancied?","He didn’t dare to ask what the emperor’s stance was.","But guessing by his speculation, the emperor was probably secretly delighted. If the emperor had no hand in this, he wouldn’t believe it at all."]},{"number":444,"title":"Chapter 444: Nothing to Do with Us","paragraphs":["Given their statuses, in the past, Sister Xin, as a concubine’s daughter from the Yu family’s main branch, would have been considered overreaching even as a secondary consort to the Fifth Prince.","But now, with Yue Floating Light in the picture, especially when the marriage proposal came from the cousin who was closest to Floating Light, Yu Huaixian felt that even the Fifth Prince was barely worthy of a Yu family girl.","“Hmph!” Yue Floating Light let out a cold snort. Even from afar, Shen Jian’s heart trembled; he instinctively knew trouble was coming.","He silently prayed that the Grand Tutor would only take out his anger on that scoundrel Xie the Fifth and not vent it on him, a distant cousin.","Xie Zhiquan: Distant?","Shen Jian: Distant!","Xie Zhiquan: Cousin, you have a red mole the size of a mung bean on your left waist.","Shen Jian: !!!","“I think he’s using Fourth Sister as a shield to avoid marrying into the Southern Yue kingdom!”","“Gan Tang is also a princess—smart and beautiful. How is she not good enough for him?” If anything, Xie the Fifth was getting the better deal.","Yue Floating Light took a furious bite of tender venison, but the meat didn’t taste as good as before.","Yu Huaixian was utterly confused. How did this involve marriage alliances? Seeing his cousin’s cheeks puff up with anger, he couldn’t help but find it amusing. Floating Light’s fiercely protective nature was oddly endearing and heartwarming.","“Even the imperial family won’t have much to say about it.”","“It’s just that I don’t know what the elder grandfather’s stance is.”","He glanced cautiously at Yue Floating Light’s expression. “Why is our family entangled with Southern Yue? If the Fifth Prince proposed to Fourth Sister just to avoid the marriage alliance... Floating Light, what do you plan to do? Will you agree?”","Yes, he was asking her directly. He guessed that the letter from Elder Grandfather was meant to seek Floating Light’s approval.","If she didn’t agree, with her influence, even the Emperor himself might lose face arguing with her.","Yue Floating Light: Isn’t the real question whether I agree or not? Shouldn’t you be asking Fourth Sister, who is the one actually involved?","Yu Ningxin: Who I marry doesn’t matter. The choice has to be made by Seventh Sister. She trusts that whoever Seventh Sister picks won’t lead her into a trap. It guarantees fewer detours.","“What am I going to do? Beat his dog head to a pulp!” Floating Light wasn’t sure if Xie Zhiquan’s interest in Yu Ningxin, who was talented in her own right, was purely her own quality or also influenced by her presence.","One day, she would leave this world. Once she did, would their feelings suffer as a result?","If Xie the Fifth had his eye on Fourth Sister merely to cling to her own connections, she would never agree to this match under any circumstances.","Yu Huaixian instinctively shrank back. At that moment, his younger cousin’s fierce expression was genuinely intimidating.","“Southern Yue probably proposed a marriage alliance to mend relations after that sneak attack earlier. They nominated Gan Tang and Xie Zhiquan as the pair!","That wicked Xie didn’t even let the night pass before running to the Yu family to ask Grandfather for marriage!”","“Does... does His Majesty know?” Yu Huaixian couldn’t hold back his curiosity any longer.","An inter-kingdom marriage was no trivial matter. However, if they could swap Fourth Sister for Princess Gan Tang, the Emperor would likely agree.","Emperor Mingxi: Agree? If Floating Light doesn’t mind, I’d gladly pack Xie the Fifth up and send him to the Yu family tonight. Exchanging an unimportant son for a tighter bond with Floating Light seemed like an excellent deal!","Yue Floating Light narrowed her eyes. “He is the emperor—the whole world is his, including his sons. Who would believe he was oblivious?”","Back in the capital city, Emperor Mingxi felt an inexplicable chill and sneezed twice in a row. First sneeze means people are missing you, second means scolding, third means being remembered. Someone was cursing him?","“Your Majesty, shall I fetch you an extra robe?”","The emperor waved his hand. “By my reckoning, Floating Light should have received Minister Yu’s letter by now.”","Given her fiery temper, he was bound to be dragged down by that brat Prince the Fifth!","Yet, despite thoughts of the chaos, the emperor wore a smile. No wonder that boy had refused repeatedly over the past two years whenever he pressed him to select a primary consort. So the little scoundrel had long set his sights on the Yu family’s Fourth Girl.","Before, he was scared of Floating Light, so he didn’t dare speak up. Now, if not for Southern Yue nominating him as a son-in-law, he’d probably keep stalling!","Eunuch Qian Gui overheard the emperor mention Yue Floating Light, glanced at his master’s face, and smiled. “The Grand Tutor should be nearing Yizhou soon. By our pigeon’s speed, the message should have arrived.”","The capital Mingxi was in Quanzhou, bordering Yizhou. If the Grand Tutor’s route didn’t cut through Yizhou into Lianzhou, Qian Gui honestly feared she’d lose her temper and ride straight back.","The emperor didn’t voice his concerns aloud, but his anxiety was no less than Qian Gui’s. After some hesitation, he asked, “Qian, do you think Floating Light will blame me for my Fifth son’s actions?”","Achoo, achoo! Just then, the emperor sneezed twice again. Qian Gui quickly handed him a cup of hot tea.","Emperor Mingxi took a sip and lamented, “Can you believe it? My Fifth son went to propose to Minister Yu without even telling me! Floating Light won’t think I sent him, will she?”","Then his tone turned vindictive. “Gan Sheng that worthless cur—first trying to kidnap Floating Light, and now proposing a marriage alliance just to buy time!”","He sneered. How naïve. Did he really think the dagger was already in their hands? Did he believe that the Great Yan would miss this golden chance for war—an excuse served on a platter?","Qian Gui quickly comforted him. “Your Majesty, please calm down. Don’t let those unworthy people sour your spirit.” He said nothing further. Having served the emperor for over two decades, he knew His Majesty just wanted a sounding board, not actual advice.","If he truly wanted counsel, there were plenty of ministers in court eager to help.","“Qian, you’re right. One day, I’ll drag Gan Sheng to the capital to kneel and repent!”","He downed the last of his tea with a soft sigh. “I’m just worried that Floating Light might misunderstand me.”","He had met the Yu family’s Fourth Girl—a refined, capable young woman who managed Floating Light’s affairs. A far cry from typical sheltered ladies—she more than deserved his Fifth son.","“Your Majesty has already sent a letter to the Grand Tutor. By our timing, it should arrive half a day after Minister Yu’s.”","Qian Gui didn’t know the letter’s contents, but he could guess: His Majesty would disavow any involvement in the Fifth Prince’s proposal.","Sure enough, who knew the emperor better than Eunuch Qian? That evening, Yue Floating Light hadn’t moved from her spot. She sat in the same place, reading the emperor’s freshly arrived letter. She scanned his familiar handwriting, surprised he had written so many sheets without getting tired.","From her perspective, those seven or eight pages conveyed just one message: Xie the Fifth acted entirely on his own volition, and even his father only found out afterward.","Earlier that day, still simmering with anger over the familial letter, Yue Floating Light hadn’t bothered to change location. She had simply ordered rest for the night.","It wasn’t a threat; she was just being stubborn.","But anger aside, she wouldn’t sacrifice her points. Her mission still had to be done."]},{"number":445,"title":"Chapter 445: Arriving at Sancha Di","paragraphs":["This decision was also made because after such a long journey, everyone in the entourage was exhausted from top to bottom. She herself was in a foul mood, and thus saw this as a good opportunity to rest for half a day.","That was how Yue Fuguang saw it, but Shen Jian, Feng Tang, and Wei Shouyi had no idea about her reasoning!","Now, including the small fry Wu Yong, the core members of the \"sprinkling squad\" had all gathered. The four of them sat in Shen Jian’s tent, eyes locked on each other, none willing to speak first.","What could they say? Could they say that the Young Mistress had done something wrong?","In their hearts, they shook their heads furiously. To put it bluntly, the Young Mistress bringing rain to Dayan was a monumental favor and act of grace. Even if she did nothing at all, who would dare to complain?","It didn’t affect her standing in their hearts in the slightest.","They had all witnessed toil along the way with their own eyes. Dayan owed the Young Mistress far too much.","Shen Jian looked at the three colleagues whose mouths were as tightly shut as clam shells and had to start a topic himself. \"Lords, once we finish with Lianzhou Precture, only Hezhou and Jizhou remain. At our current pace, it should take no more than half a month for us to return to the capital.\"","Following Dayan’s seasonal temperatures, Yue Fuguang's team had gone south first and then north—though slightly delayed, the impact on the planted seeds was minimal.","Now they had reached the northernmost border of Dayan, encompassing Lianzhou and Hezhou, where not only were large tracts of her fiefdom located, but the borders of both prefectures also formed the location of Sanchadi.","The three of course understood Shen Jian’s implication. The Young Mistress might not care about others, but these two prefectures were her own people.","\"The Young Mistress has had a long and difficult journey. It would be good for her to rest a few more days,\" Feng Tang said, gazing toward the distant fields. They had been meticulously tended by farmers. That morning, after the crops in the fields had drunk their fill of rain, a faint hint of green was already beginning to show.","\"We all know how much the Young Mistress values the Second Miss and the Fourth Miss. Yet the Fifth Prince came to propose marriage without so much as a prior word.\" Wu Yong grew more dissatisfied as he spoke. \"Isn't that a breach of propriety?\"","Strictly speaking, as a minister, he was overstepping by commenting on a member of the imperial family.","But deep down, all three—including Shen Jian—agreed with Wu Yong. Although the Fifth Prince held the status of a prince, to the nation he was less significant than a single finger of the Young Mistress.","In Wu Yong’s view, it was the Fifth Prince who had truly overstepped!","\"As I see it, the Young Mistress doesn’t only value the Second Miss and the Fourth Miss. Even your sister, Minister Wu, and Minister Feng’s son are also highly regarded,\" Wei Shouyi said with a smirk.","Wei Shouyi was currently wearing a smile. In just a few more days, they would reach Sanchadi. His son had been away from home for two years guarding this place. As a father, he didn't say much, but he deeply missed the child.","He spoke of the Young Mistress cherishing those from the study group, but his mind was on the people of Sanchadi—also her own folk, people toward whom they must act cautiously, especially regarding marriages.","Those of their generation would be best advised to inform the Young Mistress in advance.","Yue Fuguang had no idea that her actions that day had led Wei Shouyi and the others to such a misunderstanding. If she knew, she would surely think herself more wronged than Dou E.","Was she the kind of person who meddled in the marriages of other people’s children? She wasn’t a matchmaker, looking after who married whom.","Why was she so angry today? It was simply because she feared that her fourth sister, in consideration of family ties, might meekly accept Fifth Prince Xie’s proposal rather than offend someone from royalty.","Over the past few years, even with her, a celestial master, overseeing the Yu family, and her grandfather and great-uncle watching, no one had dared to grow arrogant or dismiss the emperor’s authority.","Yue Fuguang’s self-interest lay elsewhere. She couldn’t control others, but when it came to her own people—especially the women—she wanted to spare them the bitterness of marriage as much as possible. At least in the choice of a spouse, they should enjoy the greatest possible autonomy.","Given their family's status, there was simply no need to trade the girls’ marriages as bargaining chips.","At this point, Shen Jian felt that the four of them seemed to be talking about different things yet somehow about the same matter.","Shen Jian tentatively asked, \"Should we jointly submit a memorial to His Majesty?\"","They were toiling hard outside, and they hoped that certain people in the capital could restrain themselves. Daring to stir up trouble behind the scenes while the Young Mistress was away?","Even without the Young Mistress saying much, those around her couldn’t help but overthink things!","The Young Mistress was contributing to the nation, yet a prince who enjoys the people’s offerings was ‘sneaking around and stealing her home base.’ What exactly did he think he was doing?","\"Minister Shen, your proposal is workable!\" Feng Tang’s eyes lit up. He had once thought that Shen Jian, being the emperor’s nephew and the Fifth Prince’s cousin, might not be on their side. It seemed he had been mistaken.","Although they had seen the Young Mistress receive His Majesty’s letter, there were matters they needed to voice regardless. It was their duty as ministers.","His Majesty must not let his guard down just because the Young Mistress had left the capital. And he must not assume that, having helped Dayan resolve the drought, she’d not one day leave in displeasure!","The memorial those three, alongside Feng Tang, drafted to the emperor was earnestly cautionary and brimming with sincere advice—one wonders if, when Emperor Mingxi read it the entreaty, he would angrily accuse them of rebelling against heaven and order.","On the other side, the two members of the Yu family—Yu Mochun and Yu Huaixian—were also writing letters home themselves.","They could see clearly what Fuguang valued in Sister Xin: it wasn’t opposition to the betrothal herself per se; rather, she did not want Sister Xin to resign herself to a forced acceptance out of a variety of reasons.","\"Uncle-Four, tell Great-Grandfather, he must not consent early to this marriage. At least wait until we return,\" he said.","Vuguang had sent letters home and to around her midday and then started two personal letters to her family and Xin themselves—to Sister Xin. The family home therefore not make any quick marriage decisions with announcement; truly ruthless, this Fifth Prince.","If only he had fine alternatives, like going for a placatory marriage tiebinding with another region... After serving closely with Yue Fuguang and her staff all the time, Huaixian had actually met Ambassador Princess Gantang, from the south state. Excluding the identity southern her herself, she was more than asufficient counterpart for Fifth Prince.","To the eyes: Five Prince in every dimension. So there He had a fine match; why drag a youth of Huai himself carry as much grievance as see in far-off rebegin lifting see—But when, three days of dis, when at last they could make out in ways a fitted black armor armored broad steel-gripped a thorough figure in dark black iron plate-could in what when rugged-and his long lance hand such outright confident--from long gone days short ended the soul faint He just made sight come across figures by black right comes at they able break fangs dissolve: Right and at this, of down miles having left home this past not formere strong. Kind is but youth of soul, own presence has: standing distant. Just as gentle heart same as burning: When the giant with stead ran horse, who goodly hands a chain dismount darted. Looked whose bosom wells free spring show o'er against shining down bright they see: \"Finally uncle, lead eldest-blood!\"","\"You put stronger gone from past...\"","Mochun says, \"Blackened: thick grew the frame real should bright you.\" Along His full lips skin turned from much sunlight, dabbing prickle something that gave no thick grey tone just was recently above less growing.","They known branch lay younger children: among about careful manner of s, person clear distaste for beyond rank van. This clan boon one of first brothers away Qing? That why until yesterday age lines only them else grew produce."]},{"number":446,"title":"Chapter 446: Meeting","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang: It's not that I don't like seeing people with beards; it's because that bearded guy isn't clean!","Especially when she watched that bearded man drink porridge—probably few modern people could tolerate it.","\"Fuguang!\" Yu Boming, sharp-eyed, spotted the curtain of Yue Fuguang's carriage moving and quickly shouted toward the carriage.","\"Second Brother!\" Yue Fuguang's head poked out from the large window, waving at Yu Boming as if waving at the sky.","With each wave of her small hand, the winds and clouds in the heavens pressed down a little more.","Yu Boming looked up at the sky, which had instantly darkened. The scope was far wider than what he had seen three years ago. \"Fuguang, can you cover all one hundred and eighteen miles of the Three Fork Land in one go?\"","Yue Fuguang nodded at Yu Boming, her eyes sparkling. \"Covered!\"","Whoosh, whoosh, whoosh!","Before Yu Boming could say more, the rain poured down in torrents. Wind and rain pelted them, blurring their vision.","But in Yu Boming's eyes, Yue Fuguang remained the most dazzling light in the world. Sincerely, he gave her a thumbs-up. \"My little sister is truly amazing!\"","Yue Fuguang couldn't help lifting her chin. The wind and rain bent around her, and she, too, thought she was pretty impressive.","Seeing how the wind and rain avoided Yue Fuguang, Yu Boming's eyes brightened even more. \"Zheng Feng and the others are waiting ahead. Would you like to meet them, little sister?\"","They had heard at Three Fork Land that the Divine Maiden, starting from the capital, had been blessing the land with rain all along the way without stopping. Even when she passed through prefectures and counties, local officials had welcomed and seen her off from a distance, leaving few who could catch a glimpse of her.","Knowing that Yue Fuguang still had to head to He and Ji Prefectures next, Yu Boming asked this.","\"You've been stationed here for three years; of course, I must see the soldiers.\" She smiled at the much sturdier Yu Boming. \"Second Brother, I'll stay here for two days. Arrange accommodations for the people I brought.\" These were her foundation. How could she not meet them after coming this far? Anything less would chill the hearts of her subordinates.","Though Yue Fuguang had never once come to Three Fork Land in all these years, her will had been fully carried out here.","When Yu Boming heard that his sister would stay for two days, his eyes lit up instantly, and his smile stretched from ear to ear. \"Don't worry, little sister. I'll handle everything perfectly!\"","\"Little sister, let's go!\" Yu Boming laughed heartily. Riding his horse, he charged ahead, his red cape flying in a straight line behind him, then being weighed down by the rain. His horse's hooves splashed through the puddles that had just formed on the ground, throwing up muddy water.","No one knew what Yu Boming said to Cai Bing, Wei Yan, and the others, but by the time Yue Fuguang stepped out of her carriage, it was surrounded by a group of former idle rich young men, now grinning from ear to ear.","No, after three years of tempering here, those former troublemakers from the capital, once the bane of everyone's existence, had grown into some of the most promising young talents of their generation.","Though they hadn't yet outshone their forebears, they were no worse than the heirs carefully groomed by their respective families.","The moment they saw Yue Fuguang, everyone immediately straightened their expressions and bowed to her. \"Greetings, Minister of Education!\"","\"Greetings, Minister of Education!\"","Rainwater streamed down their faces, but it could not extinguish the sparks burning in their eyes.","\"You may all rise.\"","She waved her hand, and the rain falling on them seemed blocked by something, sliding slowly down an invisible barrier.","\"This...\" Cai Bing looked up in amazement, even reaching out a finger to poke at the space above his head.","\"It's like we're the same as the Minister of Education!\" Huo Sui's eyes sparkled as he gazed at Yue Fuguang. \"So the rumor that the Minister of Education is the Divine Maiden incarnate is true!\"","Though they had long known the truth, this was the first time they could say it so openly.","Yue Fuguang waved her hand again, and the wet clothes on everyone instantly became dry and comfortable.","Under the astonished and worshipful gazes of the crowd, Yue Fuguang slowly descended from her carriage.","These two tricks were new abilities she had recently developed. She felt they weren't merely due to absorbing incense offerings.","System 07, hiding in its system space, looked at Yue Fuguang showing off and felt immensely envious. Why could its host, with a mortal body, do things like a deity, while it could not even restore its own data?","System 07 turned over, suddenly recalling Yue Fuguang's early talk of \"renting a place,\" and now fully agreed with that idea.","Having earlier been unable to find peace, it now felt perfectly comfortable lying down!","With a single thought, a glowing, radiant orb appeared in Yue Fuguang's hand. System 07 thought that if it was going to lie low, it first needed to pacify its host.","[Host, do you want me to add some special effects?]","Yue Fuguang didn't know what kind of special effects System 07 meant, but she felt things were already good enough for her. She didn't need anything bigger.","\"Better not. I think even without the mind-reading, there's not much to worry about now.\"","With her current abilities, who would dare to question her identity? Influenced by her homeland's chronic fear of insufficient firepower, Yue Fuguang now, with a certain degree of self-protection, felt her Divine Maiden persona was unshakable.","Yue Fuguang followed Zheng Feng, Bao Qianjun, and the others to the drill ground where the Yue Army camp was located.","The drill ground stood at the outermost edge of the camp, next to a large mountain. At this moment, wind and rain mingled, making the mountain look gray and indistinct.","In the drill ground, which could hold tens of thousands of people, stood over ten thousand soldiers in a dark mass. Yue Fuguang walked slowly onto the high platform, her gaze sweeping over them.","From their clothing and armor to their weapons, from the external matters to the individuals themselves, her first impression was that despite the prolonged drought, the Yue Army maintained decent discipline and morale. The soldiers' spirits were high.","\"You have all worked hard stationed in this remote place for so many years!\" Her voice was not loud, but it overpowered the howling wind and pounding rain.","As soon as she finished speaking, she intended to say a few more words of encouragement, when suddenly she heard a soldier in the front row, his face full of emotion, tears or rainwater glistening in his eyes. He shouted with all his strength, \"No hardship! Willing to die for the Minister of Education!\"","Wang Dashan, from Quanzhou, An County, had just received a letter from his parents a few days ago. It said that their hometown had suffered a drought—not a drop of rain in over five months. The village stored water early on, but the drought was too severe. What they had saved was only enough for drinking. When they tried irrigating the fields, the water they spared from their mouths barely wet the surface, let alone filling the cracked earth.","His parents had made the most desperate plan: if it came to it, they would save the water for the children. After all, they had lived a long life; dying wouldn’t be so bad.","Wang Dashan remembered that when he read this part, tears had soaked the thin letter paper, blurring the words.","He turned the page, as if turning over a major hurdle, and stepped into a new beginning."]},{"number":447,"title":"Chapter 447: Are They Checking Out My Body","paragraphs":["On the third day after her parents refused to drink water, the Spirit Maiden descended. She brought sweet rain, reviving the withered crops in the fields and saving the lives of their entire family.","So when Wang Dashan declared, “I would die for the Young Mentor,” his words were heartfelt and genuine, as pure as the drought-stricken land of Sancha that had seen no rain for half a year.","As his voice rang out, even the wind and rain seemed to pause for an instant, and the silence that followed grew even deeper.","That was because Yue Fuguang had just, by the same method, halted the wind and rain in this very place.","That she succeeded on her first try surprised even Yue Fuguang herself. She had simply wanted to test her abilities, and to her astonishment, it worked. Upon closer reflection, it seemed she hadn’t expended much energy at all.","The word “domain” flashed through her mind, but before she could dwell on it, the soldiers who had witnessed the sudden stillness of wind and rain in this small pocket of the world first stood in shock, then, just like Wang Dashan, began shouting at the top of their lungs: “I would die for the Mentor!”","“I would die for the Mentor!”","“Mentor, my name is Li Erniu, and I would die for you!”","The crowd’s faces darkened; many wanted to drag this Li Erniu, who had broken formation, out of the ranks.","Someone started kicking Li Erniu from behind, while others began blurting out their names. “My name is Zhao Dazhu, I would die for the Mentor!”","“Thank you, Mentor, for bringing rain to our hometown folks. I, Qian Youcai, would die for the Mentor!”","“I...” One after another, names and place names—all places Yue Fuguang had traveled to, passed through, and blessed with rain—filled her ears. Listening to their simple, unadorned words, she felt the same sincerity as those curling incense offerings and rustic expressions of gratitude.","Her mission seemed to have taken on a deeper meaning.","When the crowd finally fell silent again, Yue Fuguang’s voice remained as calm as before. “I have taken all your words to heart!”","She swept her gaze across the gathered soldiers, recalling the secret letter she had received from the emperor yesterday. The 150,000-strong army had already been secretly mobilized while Dayan and Nanyue were discussing a marriage alliance. War between the two kingdoms was imminent.","And when that time came, the land of Sancha would no longer be a place of peace. With Dayan and Nanyue at war, Beili and Xiqiang would not simply stand by.","Given the chance, they would surely come in for a bite, and Sancha, as tempting as a piece of fat, would be their first target.","These young soldiers, in the near future, would face their first true battle. “A great drought plagues the entire realm; only Dayan has rain. By now, Dayan must be seen as a fat target by others. Even if they have no opening, they will create one to take a bite.","You are Dayan’s first line of defense. As they say, ‘A thousand days to raise an army, one day to use it.’ The first battle here will fall to you!","Are you afraid?”","“No fear! No fear!”","“No fear! No fear!”","“Fight back!”","“Fight back!”","Yue Fuguang nodded. “Good. You are all fine sons of Dayan!”","A twelve-year-old girl, standing before soldiers who were at least seventeen or eighteen, praising them as fine sons like an elder—it might have looked odd to an outsider.","Yet neither the speaker nor the listeners found anything strange about it.","On the contrary, at her words “fine sons of Dayan,” the already ramrod-straight soldiers unconsciously straightened their backs even more.","War in the age of cold weapons was a meat grinder, and she couldn’t help but add a few words of advice. “I only hope you stay calm and train hard. As the saying goes, ‘Better to sweat more in peacetime than bleed more in battle.’”","“We will remember your teachings, Mentor! More sweat in training, less blood in battle!”","Yue Fuguang cast a look of approval at Wei Huaping. Truly, like father, like son—he had summarized it perfectly!","Wei Shouyi, watching his son standing at the very front of the ranks, resolute and steadfast, felt immense pride swelling in his heart as a father.","He and Shen Jian, along with the others, had also received the emperor’s secret letter about the impending war with Nanyue. They knew that Sancha would soon be coveted by Beili and Xiqiang because of the conflict, perhaps not through a full-scale war, but through constant skirmishes.","“Today, there’s an extra meal for the entire army. It’s on me!” After all, she had already performed enough ‘miracles’—adding one more, like ‘sleeves that hold the universe,’ wouldn’t matter.","“Thank you, Young Mentor!”","“Thank you, Young Mentor!”","The crowd cheered with excitement, but their formation remained orderly. Only then was Yue Fuguang completely satisfied.","Setting aside the actual combat effectiveness of this army, the discipline and bearing they displayed were clearly not something trained overnight just to impress her.","“Dismissed!” At her command, the soldiers filed out in an orderly fashion.","[Host, does this seem a little familiar?]","For a moment, Yue Fuguang felt dazed. “Mm.” A single word summed up all the complicated emotions churning inside her.","Yue Fuguang followed the others to the meeting hall.","“Zheng Feng, Wei Huaping, Bao Qianjun—you’ve all done very well.”","From the state of these soldiers, it was clear that Zheng Feng and Wei Huaping had put considerable effort into training and discipline.","And seeing that all ten thousand-plus men were strong and healthy, she knew her silver had been properly used by Bao Qianjun to feed the troops.","“And Second Brother, Wei Yan, Cai Bing, Huo Sui, Lin Huaijing...” She called them out one by one, and each named wore a look of delighted surprise.","“I would die for the Mentor!” Cai Bing shouted, sounding like a young hothead.","Huo Sui secretly reached behind his back and pinched Cai Bing’s arm. Always jumping the gun, stealing my lines—what am I supposed to say?","The two, who used to fight at every meeting and once nearly killed each other over a woman, had now become “booze buddies.”","“Just do your jobs well—no need to die for me.” Yue Fuguang smiled as she watched them pinch and nudge each other, wondering faintly if one day they might actually end up developing feelings for one another.","Well, never mind. She wouldn’t meddle in other people’s ‘relationships.’","“I am clear in rewards and punishments. Since you’ve done well, you’ll be rewarded!” She swept her hand across the large table before her, and in an instant, a dozen small wooden boxes appeared upon it.","The crowd accepted her ability to conjure objects out of thin air—well, “accepted” was generous.","Everyone’s eyes went wide and their jaws dropped in astonishment. If it weren’t for Yue Fuguang’s status and gender, Wei Yan and the most mischievous among them would have turned her upside down to search for the trick.","Right now, their eyes held not only wonder and reverence but also a blatant plea—do that again!","Yue Fuguang ignored their wordless, conflicted faces as they almost asked and then held back, while Yu Boming had already been pushed to the front by his companions.","Yu Boming: This is my sister’s secret; there’s no way I can ask for you!","“This one is for General Zheng Feng.” Starting with Zheng Feng, Yue Fuguang distributed the small boxes to everyone at the table.","[Master, what did you put in there?] the system asked, though it already knew.","Everyone had already noticed the shimmering, radiant orb in the Mentor’s hand. So this was the true form of the divine artifact?","No wonder it was called the World-Shattering Orb—just by its appearance alone, it was clearly extraordinary.","[Master, look at these people—their eyes are turning green staring at Little Bead. Are they coveting my body?]","The crowd: !!! Don’t come any closer! JPG"]},{"number":448,"title":"Chapter 448: Also a Master of Poisoning","paragraphs":["\"With beads as beautiful as these, anyone can see they’re priceless treasures. No wonder they couldn’t help staring.\"","Everyone: Right, right, right. We’d like to live a few more years. Who would dare covet the divine lord’s possessions? Is the bond of the nine clans not deep enough, or do they not want to be reborn as humans in the next life?","\"Little sister, what’s inside this box?\" Yu Boming hurriedly changed the subject, afraid of hearing something even more terrifying.","\"Just some pills and protective talismans.\" Her gaze fell on the box. \"Take good care of them. They’re life-saving items.\"","Those who had been about to open and inspect their boxes immediately hugged them tightly, still glancing at each other.","\"What are you looking at? Don’t you have your own?\" Huo Sui shot a glare at Cai Bing, and the two of them looked ready to squabble like a couple of chickens pecking at each other again.","\"Master, what are we having for dinner tonight?\" Wei Yan shoved the two of them aside, letting them bicker somewhere else so they wouldn’t block the brothers from enjoying some good food.","\"For food, you’ll have to ask the head chef. I only provide the ingredients.\"","With another wave of her hand, she summoned over a hundred baskets on the spot. They were filled with fruits, vegetables, meats, eggs, and aquatic products—everything imaginable. Of course, this still wasn’t enough to feed the entire army.","So she roused the stunned crowd, who had been rendered speechless and could only mutter incoherently. \"Get some people to move these to the kitchen. Chef Wu will know what to make based on the ingredients.\"","Chef Wu was a direct apprentice of the cook from her own small kitchen, so he was no stranger to these ingredients.","\"Master, what’s this?\" Zheng Feng picked up a spiky, stinking object and asked Yue Fuguang.","\"Ugh! What is this? Why does it stink so much?\" The ever-curious Huo Sui leaned in and then immediately recoiled, overwhelmed by the stench of the durian.","Cai Bing sniffed the air. \"Stinks? I think it smells pretty good!\"","\"Cai Bing, are you deliberately picking a fight with me?\" Huo Sui raised his fist, ready to throw down with him.","\"Fight outside!\" Yu Boming kicked Huo Sui in the rear, sending him stumbling, which instantly shut him up.","Brushing the dust off his backside, he pinched his nose and came closer again. He didn’t believe Cai Bing. After a few more sniffs, it was still foul.","Yue Fuguang watched the expressions of the group—some grimacing from the smell, others finding it tolerable—and couldn’t help but chuckle. \"This is a tropical fruit called durian. It’s known as the king of fruits.\"","\"King of fruits? Then it must be delicious!\"","\"Well... those who like it will adore it, but those who don’t won’t be able to stomach even a bite.\" Yue Fuguang glanced at the nose-pinching Huo Sui. \"It’s very sweet. You’ll know once you try it.\"","She took the durian from Zheng Feng and gently pried it open, revealing the yellow flesh inside.","Huo Sui quickly backed away, while Wei Yan and Cai Bing couldn’t help leaning in for a closer look.","\"Not only is the fruit rich in nutrients, but the shell can also be used to stew chicken.\" Though, she added silently, eating too much might give you a case of internal heat.","\"Would anyone like to try some?\"","\"Yes, yes, yes!\" Wei Yan grabbed a piece for Yue Fuguang first, then handed some to Zheng Feng, Yu Boming, Wei Huaping, and the others before eagerly taking a piece for himself.","\"Mmm, so sweet!\"","\"Delicious! Master was right. No wonder it’s called the king of fruits. This is the sweetest and best fruit I’ve ever had!\" Cai Bing ate with an expression of pure bliss, making Huo Sui frown from the side. He felt like the guy was messing with him.","Seeing Cai Bing, and thinking of his pie-loving son Cai Xian, Yue Fuguang chuckled again. \"This fruit can also be used to make pastries and pies.\"","\"Pies?\" Cai Bing, true to being Cai Xian’s father, widened his small eyes at the mention of durian pies.","\"It’s like this kind of pie.\" Too lazy to teach them how to make pizza, Yue Fuguang bought a few from her shop instead.","As everyone ate, all the baskets were moved out in no time. She waved her hand and summoned another hundred and twenty baskets.","Gazing at the now-packed hall, she nodded to herself. This should be enough for one meal.","[Master, don’t just focus on eating. Someone’s sneaking up!]","\"Someone’s sneaking up? Who? How far?\"","[About fifty li away, near Chengping Mountain. They’re dressed like bandits, but based on their weapons, they’re from Beili and Xiqiang.]","Chengping Mountain happened to sit at the border of Sandi, Beili, and Xiqiang. To the south was Dayan, to the north was Beili, and the western ridge extended into Xiqiang territory.","Chengping Mountain wasn’t large, but it inconveniently straddled three kingdoms.","\"Beili and Xiqiang? Are they trying to copy the Southern Yue scoundrels? Little Zhu, are these people coming for me too?\"","[Definitely! Master single-handedly solved Dayan’s drought crisis. Who wouldn’t want to take you back? If those two kingdoms keep drying up, their farmlands and pastures will be ruined. You’re their only hope now.]","Zheng Feng and the others had silently risen, hands resting on the hilts of their sabers. If anyone wanted to take the young master away, they’d have to step over their bodies first.","\"How many are there?\" Yue Fuguang glanced at the sky. It was just past noon. Fifty li away, even if they were all on horseback, by the time they arrived and launched an attack, it would be at least evening—shouldn’t delay her dinner plans.","[Fewer than eighteen thousand, but just enough to outnumber the garrison at Sandi.]","\"What are Beili and Xiqiang thinking? If they’re disguising themselves as bandits, they should at least make it believable. What kind of bandit leads an army of over ten thousand?\"","[Maybe they think that if they succeed in taking you, Mingxi Emperor will find out anyway. If they fail, this is just their fig leaf for diplomacy.]","In short, Dayan was already at odds with Southern Yue over words, and war could break out at any time. Even if they failed today, unless the Mingxi Emperor wanted to go to war with both kingdoms, he’d have to pretend ignorance and blame the incident on the bandits of Chengping Mountain.","Yue Fuguang guessed that those real bandits had probably already been recruited by them by now.","\"The emperor is itching to go to war with them over the Southern Yue incident. If something happens today, no matter how he handles it, it’ll be bad for Dayan.\"","[Master means we should stop this from happening?] The two of them had calculated that, with Dayan’s current military strength, a full-scale war—even with Yue Fuguang’s help—would be a pyrrhic victory.","So for Dayan, the best path to unification was to pick off the enemies one by one, or at most fight two at a time. Given time, they’d deal with the rest.","\"Right. Now’s not the time to take on Beili and Xiqiang.\"","Wei Shouyi and Shen Jian exchanged a glance. They had braced themselves for a bloody battle, but the young master wanted to prevent this war. But how? Those were over ten thousand men.","[Master, your abilities haven’t even recovered a ten-thousandth of their full strength. How do you plan to stop that many?]","Yue Fuguang stroked her chin. Too many people—she’d have to use area-effect tactics.","But she didn’t want to incur the karmic burden of taking over ten thousand lives all at once, so she couldn’t resort to anything too drastic.","\"What if I gave them poison? Not lethal, just something that robs them of their mobility.\" After weighing her options, poisoning seemed the most efficient method.","She had indeed been infected by those several countries—whenever she wanted to stir up trouble or attack someone, the first thought that came to her was poison!","Without even realizing it, she had become quite an expert at poisoning!"]},{"number":449,"title":"Chapter 449: Is It Aiming at Me Again","paragraphs":["When Zheng Feng and Shen Jian heard about dysentery, their hair stood on end. Although the Imperial Hospital of the Great Yan Dynasty had developed a potion to combat dysentery, they had been hearing about how severe this disease was since childhood. Once an epidemic broke out, it wouldn't stop until it had taken tens of thousands of lives.","Moreover, the medicine couldn't guarantee a 100% cure for all patients. What if it spread to their area...","\"No, it's too contagious, and it's too close to the Three - Forked Land. It's very easy for us to be affected here. As for croton, its medicinal effect is too short - lived.\"","Everyone heaved a sigh of relief. Only after they relaxed a bit did they realize they were hungry.","Just then, the kitchen started to serve the dishes one after another.","Shen Jian quickly invited everyone to take their seats. \"Sorry for the poor hospitality, Your Excellency the Junior Grand Tutor. Please have some simple meals with the other gentlemen first. We'll entertain you properly tonight.\"","Yuefen looked at the ten dishes and two soups on the table. They were all her favorite dishes. It seemed that even after Chef Zhang had been here for three years, he still remembered her preferences.","Yue Fuguang waved her hand. \"Compared to what we've had on the road these days, this is already very good.\"","\"Little sister, you've had a hard journey. You should eat more today,\" Yu Boming said with a look of concern on his face. He also glared at his cousin Yu Huaixian at the next table.","He couldn't say anything to his fourth uncle as he was an elder, but he had to have a good talk with this cousin tonight. The family had asked him to follow Fuguang so that they could take care of each other. Since he couldn't even take good care of his sister's diet, Yu Boming had to teach this guy a lesson.","Yu Huaixian was so intimidated by his cousin's glare that he couldn't taste the ten - dish and two - soup meal in front of him.","They had been traveling for days, and they always gave the best to Fuguang, but it was still no match for being at home.","Feng Tang and Wu Yong also looked ashamed, especially Yu Mochun. Since he hadn't taken good care of Fuguang, he could already imagine that his father would scold him when they got back.","Yue Fuguang ignored the silent exchange of glances among the Yu family members and continued discussing the matter of poisoning with the system.","[Master, do you want the poison pills from the cultivation world?]","\"Using mortal medicine, it's difficult to control the medicinal effect, and it's easy to be detected. If we do this, we must achieve our goal without leaving any trace.\"","It would be best if the poisoned people, after failing to find the cause, could automatically assume that they had angered the heavens by trying to harm her, the \"Goddess\", and thus incurred divine punishment.","Even if they couldn't think of this on their own, Yue Fuguang would send someone to \"remind\" them.","[Master, Little Pearl rummaged through my inventory in the natal space. It seems that the Intestinal and Stomach Cleansing Pill is quite suitable.]","\"What kind of pill is this? I've never heard of it. Tell me about its specific medicinal effects.\"","[It's normal that you haven't heard of it, Master. This pill is used by low - level cultivators who can't control their diet to clean up the waste accumulated in their bodies from overeating mundane food.","For cultivators, taking this pill is just a way to expel toxins. But for these ordinary people without cultivation, they might vomit and have diarrhea for three days straight and be bedridden for ten to fifteen days.","During this period, they won't have an appetite. Some insightful people might even gain a clear mind and see through the mortal world.]","Yue Fuguang understood. This was just a laxative in the cultivation world, which was harmful to both the body and the kidneys of ordinary people.","Uh... They were having a meal, and talking about such a \"smelly\" topic at the dinner table might not be appropriate.","She quickly glanced at the others. They were still eating gracefully, seemingly unaffected.","If they hadn't been taking such long pauses between bites, she would have really believed it!","Actually, the others weren't affected by the \"smelly\" topic. They were a bit frightened by the mention of helping people see through the mortal world.","Damage to the kidneys? They'd rather take a few stabs!","\"Will it kill people?\"","[As long as the dosage is controlled, it will only damage their bodies.]","The laxative for cultivators was beyond what ordinary people could bear. Cleaning up body waste was a good thing for cultivators, but for vulnerable ordinary people, it was only harmful.","\"Just right. There's wind and rain outside. You use the wind to send the pills to them.\"","[Don't worry, Master. I guarantee they won't be able to leave the area of Chengping Mountain for the next few days.]","Hearing what the divine artifact said, those who had no appetite suddenly regained their appetites and were in the mood to chat and laugh.","Just after they had finished their lunch, a young general rushed in to report, \"Sir, when our team was on a routine patrol today, we found a large number of unidentified people near Chengping Mountain, about fifty miles away. We don't know the exact number, but we estimate there are at least over five thousand people.\"","Those people were well - hidden. If each patrol team hadn't been equipped with a telescope, they wouldn't have been able to confirm even the number of five thousand.","Hearing this, Zheng Feng was glad that his patrol team had discovered their traces. If they had let those people cross the border of Chengping Mountain without noticing, it would not only be embarrassing for him but also the entire Yue Army stationed at the Three - Forked Land would be held accountable.","Zheng Feng ordered seriously, \"Investigate further. Before you determine their number and purpose, don't get close to them. Once they cross the border, send a signal immediately.\"","He was afraid that if his men got too close, they might be affected by the Intestinal and Stomach Cleansing Pill of the divine artifact master and suffer undeserved misfortune.","After the man left, Zheng Feng turned to Yue Fuguang and asked, \"Your Excellency, what's your opinion?\"","Yue Fuguang straightened her expression and started acting. \"Could they be mountain bandits from Chengping Mountain?\"","Zheng Feng shook his head. \"Before we came here, there were indeed several bandit strongholds on Chengping Mountain. But I once led a team to wipe out two of the ones near the south.","The remaining three, two are in the territory of the Northern Li and one is in the territory of the Western Qiang. The total number of them definitely doesn't exceed a thousand.\"","The Chengping Mountain Range wasn't very large. If it weren't for the poverty here, which forced many people to make a living as bandits, there wouldn't have been so many bandit strongholds.","Similarly, because of the poverty, these bandits could only barely make ends meet. It was difficult for them to grow in strength.","\"Then it must be the official army dressed as bandits, coming after me!\"","Even without the thoughts Yue Fuguang had previously revealed, these people could guess what was going on. But to determine which side they were from, they had to engage in battle first.","\"Then do you think they're from the north or the west?\"","\"Is it possible that they've joined forces for the sake of this rain from the sky?\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's straightforward statement, Zheng Feng immediately stood up, bowed, and said, \"Your Excellency the Junior Grand Tutor, please forgive me. I'll take my leave first and go to arrange the defense line right away. I'll never let those people cross the border.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Go ahead. Keep vigilant. If they don't attack first, don't provoke them.\"","It was true that young soldiers were eager for military achievements. If she didn't give this warning, someone might not be able to hold back from attacking.","Bao Qianjun stepped forward and said, \"Your Excellency, there's still a long time until the dinner. You've had a tiring journey. How about I take you to your accommodation to rest for a while?\"","\"Thank you, Your Excellency Bao.\" Yue Fuguang followed Bao Qianjun out. By this time, the rain had weakened a bit. In the large courtyard of the Yue Army's camp, there were large and small puddles on the ground.","Wouldn't her shoes get wet if she went out at this time?"]},{"number":450,"title":"Chapter 450: Wind Without Worry, Zhuang Xiu","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang didn’t want to wet her shoes, so she instantly switched into the Lotus-Birthing Boots. Everyone saw that wherever the Grand Preceptor stepped, translucent lotuses bloomed one after another in the puddles.","“This... this...” The guards were somewhat used to it, having seen it before, but Bao Qianjun, Yu Boming, and the others had never witnessed such a thing.","“So the rumors are true!” the crowd murmured behind her, barely above a whisper.","Though they had already seen the Grand Preceptor summon wind and rain at will and conjure objects out of thin air, was walking through the air and birthing lotuses with every step not a bit too incredible?","They saw clearly that although it looked like she was treading on lotuses growing from the ground, those with sharp eyes realized she was actually stepping on empty air!","Could it be that the Grand Preceptor had truly already restored her divine soul and immortal body?","Bao Qianjun’s eyes were too easy to read. He stared openly at Yu Boming, hoping for an answer.","Yu Boming thought: Is it possible that I know no more than you do?","Except for returning home once in the first year, he hadn’t been back in nearly two years. All communication with his family had been through radio or letters.","No one in the family had ever mentioned that his younger sister had become so powerful! Was the whole family treating him as an outsider, keeping it all from him alone?","The Yu family thought: Is it possible that we’ve seen even less than you?","Bao Qianjun looked at Yu Boming, and Yu Boming looked at Yu Mochun and Yu Huaixian, the two family members.","Yu Mochun and Yu Huaixian silently turned their heads away—they, too, had only learned how formidable Yue Fuguang was during this trip.","As for whether she had regained her immortal body, they shook their heads inwardly. No, she was still the same Yue Fuguang connected to them by blood.","While the people behind exchanged glances, Yue Fuguang was walking and inspecting the Yue Army camp at the same time.","Earlier, in haste to reach the drill ground, they had taken the outer route. Now, heading toward the guest resting area, they began to slowly see the full layout of the camp.","The Yue Army camp was built on a small hill. Below was the drill ground, and further up lay the meeting hall, behind which were various offices, warehouses, kitchens, and mess halls.","Behind these two rows of buildings was a medium-sized courtyard, flanked on left and right by continuous rows of barracks.","Further back stood a courtyard with a small garden, enclosed separately. It had been specially prepared for Yue Fuguang when the camp was first built.","Yue Fuguang walked a full circle around the small garden, which only had a few bare saplings. There was also a small pond, previously dry but now filled halfway with water.","Shen Jian and others inspected the area carefully. Strictly speaking, this was Yue Fuguang’s territory, so hiding anyone here should have been impossible. But after the incident with those people from Chengping Mountain, they had to be thorough before allowing her to take residence.","[Master, the medicine has taken effect. Beili and Xiqiang almost started fighting just now!]","\"Oh? Does the medicine taking effect have anything to do with them fighting?\" She had calculated the timing earlier and thought that, given the ‘efficacy’ of the elixirs from the cultivation world, the enemy should have been incapacitated during their midday meal.","\"Little Zhu, is it that your elixir isn’t good enough? They should have been unable to get up long ago—how do they still have strength to fight?\"","[Master, it’s not that my medicine isn’t good; it’s just starting to work. They haven’t been fully debilitated yet! Just wait—by the latest tonight, I guarantee they’ll all be down!]","The system spoke with conviction, fully confident in the elixirs sold in its shop.","[Master, aren’t you curious about who commands the Beili and Xiqiang armies this time?]","\"What, does the commander this time have some special background?\"","She sensed a juicy story from the system’s words and couldn’t help but focus her mind, pulling up the system panel to check the mission information.","Sure enough, another mission had just been triggered. It seemed impossible to settle this matter without a few deaths.","Capture the chieftain to subdue his followers first. Though she couldn’t yet rip off the heads of Bei Ji and Xi Yan this time, dealing with their dispatched men and teaching them a lesson would be fine.","[Master, the leader of Beili this time is Zhuang Xiu, the elder brother of the Eighth Prince’s prospective consort—the future brother-in-law of the emperor. The leader of Xiqiang is Feng Wuhuan, the brother-in-law of Xi Xiang.]","\"That Feng Wuhuan is a member of the Feng family? What’s his connection to Feng Xiao and Feng Wuchang?\"","If this Xi Xiang’s brother-in-law was from the Feng family, then he was inevitably linked to the Fengyu Pavilion.","Although two years ago the Fengyu Pavilion appeared to have been uprooted in Dayan, its foundation remained. Without severing its extending tentacles, it couldn’t truly be destroyed.","Within Dayan, the Fengyu Pavilion had merely changed its skin like Xueshan, behaving more cautiously to avoid being caught red-handed.","It was like running a company in later ages—Dayan was a vast market, and the Fengyu Pavilion couldn’t really withdraw. They would just change their name and re-enter.","Like grass in the wild, they would grow again with the spring breeze!","[Feng Wuhuan is of the Feng family’s direct bloodline. He is Feng Xiao’s nephew and Feng Wuchang’s clan brother. However, since Feng Wuchang’s family was a collateral branch, he climbed up by latching onto the Marquis of Changxin and then stepping over him, gradually gaining status in the Feng family.","Both brothers played a significant role in Dayan’s fall.]","Mentioning Dayan’s fall—though there was no longer any danger of national subjugation—being ministers of Dayan, Feng Tang, Wei Shouyi, and Shen Jian couldn’t help but glance toward Chengping Mountain.","If possible, they would love to crush this Feng Wuhuan before he fully matured.","And that Feng Wuchang too—not one of them should escape.","The Grand Preceptor had said, \"A gentleman takes revenge from morning till night.\" They intended to carry that principle through to the end.","[Master, don’t focus only on Feng Wuhuan. That Zhuang Xiu is a ruthless character.]","\"Oh? Tell me, what has he done?\"","[Master, after Dayan fell, several countries carved up its lands and wealth. But instead of becoming stronger and more stable, these states were torn apart by internal strife and endless conflict.","That’s why the realm descended into three hundred years of chaos. By then, it wasn’t about one country or one region—the whole world changed, fighting endlessly, like singers on a stage rising and falling in turns.]","\"This turmoil was the pain of an era’s backwardness and also the pain of progress. Without dragging down those old aristocratic families, how could society move forward?\"","[But because of your appearance, Master, this pain might turn out differently.]","Let the nobles of the five kingdoms suffer a little—they and their ancestors had enjoyed good times for generations. It was time their descendants tasted some hardship.","[Master, Zhuang Xiu, as the Eighth Prince’s prospective brother-in-law, was deliberately groomed by the emperor. He was given military power, and whenever the chance arose, the emperor burnedished his credentials.","This time, his appointment as the general commanding Beili’s seven thousand troops was the Northern Ji emperor’s way of building his resume.","In the future, as one of the vanguard commanders attacking Dayan, he would risk his life for military merit and for every city.","Whenever there was a battle, he led the charge. Slight wounds wouldn’t make him leave the line. He had personally captured banners and led the first assault. His military achievements and injuries were countless. His personal valor rivaled that of Ling Yuanhang.]","\"So, this Zhuang Xiu is a talent after all?\" Too bad talent on the enemy’s side could not be spared."]},{"number":451,"title":"Chapter 451: This Son Cannot Stay","paragraphs":["A fool she could let off the hook, but a talent? Only one thought echoed in her mind: \"This man must not be spared!\"","Though it was somewhat cold-blooded, she had to bury anyone who could threaten her mission six feet under—this was a matter of stance, not of right or wrong.","[Master, there is one more thing you might wish to know.]","\"What is it?\"","[Master, do you know how Shen Jian died?]","\"Didn't he fall in battle in the eleventh year of Yuan Kang?\"","[Yes and no. There is also a melodramatic love story behind it. Would you like to hear it, Master?]","\"Is it about Zhuang Xiu and Shen Jian?\"","[Er... something like that!] After all, in this cheesy romance flick, Zhuang Xiu plays a significant role.","Shen Jian's scalp tingled at once, and a bad premonition arose in his heart. He even forgot to worry about his own death in the eleventh year of Yuan Kang.","If even the Divine Artifact called it a melodramatic love story, it had to be something that defied common sense—or even ethics!","Right then, Shen Jian was panicking. He signaled the crowd with his eyes to follow him outside, trying to stop them from feasting on his scandal.","If it had been anything else, no one would have refused the nephew of the Emperor, the eldest son of the Grand Princess.","But... gossip? Especially a melodramatic love story endorsed by the Divine Artifact? Absolutely irresistible!","So everyone, including the eldest among them, Bao Qianjun and Feng Tang, suddenly seemed to go blind. They bustled about in Yue Fuguang's courtyard, finding odd jobs to do, deliberately ignoring Shen Jian.","Yue Fuguang had been settled by Cuizhu and the others under the eaves to drink tea and listen to the rain. Since the inner chamber had been unoccupied for a long time, they needed to give it a thorough cleaning.","[Master, in the ninth year of Yuan Kang, Shen Jian was ordered to guard the border. It was then that he met the great love of his life!]","\"The great love of his life? If I recall correctly, Shen Jian was already married and had one son and two daughters.","A married man, a father of several children, and you call that the great love of his life?","Was this 'love' after his fame or his fortune?","And Shen Jian fell for her—was it for her face or her face? If it was lust at first sight, just say so. Don't insult the word 'love'!\"","Shen Jian covered his face, flushed red by Yue Fuguang's blunt and biting words. He felt that the melodramatic story hadn't even begun, yet his face was already burning with shame.","[Er... Master, is it possible she was after his life? But you're not wrong about Shen Jian being after her looks. Twenty-eight-year-old Shen Jian paired with Zhuang Yuyan, who wasn't even eighteen yet—that's an old ox chewing on tender grass.]","Hearing \"twenty-eight with eighteen\" called an old ox chewing tender grass, several men in the room who kept young concubines felt an inexplicable arrow pierce their knees.","By now, Shen Jian was no longer the only one blushing. As for the man himself, he had already retreated to a corner, resigned to his fate.","\"Indeed, 'great loves' are always tailor-made ambushes designed to suit your tastes.\"","[Shen Jian's great love began in the tenth year of Yuan Kang, during a festival at a border town's lantern fair, where they had a 'coincidental' encounter. Master, let me describe the scene:","That night, Shen Jian came out of a tavern with his comrades, already half-drunk. He refused their offer to escort him home, saying he wanted to walk alone.","With blurred vision, he wandered away from the bustling street and the laughing crowd, heading into a quiet alley.","The lanterns there were sparse, with only a few plain silk lamps hanging under the eaves, casting a faint, soft yellow light on the ground.","The noise of the lantern festival was cut off behind him, like the receding tide, leaving only distant echoes in his ears.","Drunk and parched, he searched for water in the alley.","Then he saw it—deep in the alley, a tilted lantern hung, its light dim, just enough to illuminate that small patch of space.","She stood at the edge of the halo, her head slightly lowered, as if looking at something.","In the distance behind her, fireworks burst and crackled, showering down to the ground.","Her profile was traced in soft lines by the dim lamplight, and scattered shadows from the lantern fell on her shoulder.","Shen Jian was stunned. He was a well-traveled man who had seen many beauties, but he had never seen a woman like this before.","There, where the lanterns faded, she seemed to sense something. Slowly, she lifted her head, her gaze crossing the thin veil of night and landing on him.","At that moment, the distant songs, the nearby lanterns, the fireworks across the sky—all became irrelevant background.","Their meeting on that beautiful night felt destined, like some kind of fate—that must have been what Shen Jian thought.]","The others were captivated by the system's description of the scene, while Shen Jian, the one involved, buried his head in his arms, finding nothing beautiful about it at all.","If it weren't for the fact that the cracks in the ground were all filled with rain, he would have dug one and buried himself in it.","But Yue Fuguang felt the scene perfectly matched the line from Master Xin's poem: \"I searched for her a thousand times in the crowd, and suddenly turned my head, to find her where the lantern lights were dim.\"","\"What you call fate and destiny is nothing more than someone else's deliberate design and intentional approach.\"","Shen Jian didn’t know what kind of beauty could have blinded his eyes. What he most wanted to understand now was how this mysterious woman had managed to take his life.","\"Master, Zhuang Yuyan is an assassin from the North Li Tianxing Tower and also a daughter of a branch family of the Zhuang clan. Her mother died early in her childhood, and within a month of her passing, her father elevated his beloved concubine to the position of legitimate wife.","With a stepmother, a stepfather was surely not far behind.","The Zhuang family was a prominent household, yet Zhuang Yuyan’s father seemed unable to properly raise a daughter. At just seven years old, Zhuang Yuyan had the title of a young miss but the fate of a servant.","In her own home, she lived worse than the favored maidservants.\"","Yue Fuguang: I know this script well!","This was exactly her starting point!","\"Later, her stepmother and biological father personally sent her to Tianxing Tower. At the time, Zhuang Yuyan believed she would learn a means to survive.","Unfortunately, when she grew older, she realized that the means of survival were far different from what she had initially imagined.","Killing people for money—how could that not be considered a craft?\"","\"So, Shen Jian is Zhuang Yuyan's target? Why would Tianxing Tower go through so much trouble to take Shen Jian’s life?","Wouldn’t a straightforward assassination or poison work just as well? Why use the beauty trap? Doesn’t that seem a bit slow to yield results?\"","\"Master, Zhuang Yuyan’s father is actually the half-brother of Shen Jian’s mother, the Grand Princess—that is, an illegitimate son of Emperor Mingxi’s father. Can you believe it?","Zhuang Yuyan’s branch is a distant offshoot of the Zhuang clan. The family line was continued through a woman taking a husband into her home. In fact, Zhuang Yuyan’s grandmother was an only daughter. She once accompanied her father on a trip to Dayan. When the father and daughter returned, they brought along not only a young man but also a baby boy.","Officially, they claimed she had taken a live-in husband. In reality, that so-called 'live-in husband' was just a cover. And that supposed 'grandfather'—his slave contract was firmly held in the grandmother’s hands.\"","To think that the nominal grandfather was actually bought—Yue Fuguang couldn’t help but marvel at how resourceful that father and daughter, Zhuang Xiu and his kin, truly were."]},{"number":452,"title":"Chapter 452: The Beauty Trap","paragraphs":["Those with experience know that taking in a son-in-law can easily result in one’s family being swallowed up whole, not to mention that disgusting practice of “restoring the ancestral name after three generations.” In any case, the tricks involving live-in sons-in-law have been abundant throughout history.","But if the live-in son-in-law is purchased, these troubles become much smaller.","“These mortals sure know how to have fun! Does this Zhuang Yuyan actually know who her father really is?”","Upon hearing the scandalous affairs of his so-called maternal grandfather, Shen Jian perked up immediately, even hoping the divine artifact’s spirit would say more, so that everyone would stop focusing on his own messy business.","As for the impropriety of a younger generation discussing an elder’s romantic entanglements?","Well, everyone knew that Emperor Mingxi and the Grand Princess, along with their children, harbored deep resentment toward their late father, even if they didn’t speak of it openly.","So taboos about respecting the honored dead? Nonexistent. Besides, who dared to silence those two?","[Before her grandmother died, she revealed the true background of Zhuang Zhidong—that is, Zhuang Yuyan’s father.]","“So the Zhuang family targeting Shen Jian, a son of the Grand Princess, was it revenge against the imperial family, or were they trying to restore their ancestral status?”","Knowing he had an emperor for a father—that he was a lost imperial prince who should have enjoyed limitless wealth and glory—yet now had to live as a marginal figure in his clan...","How could such a man not harbor hatred?","“Having his rightful identity as a prince stripped away, Zhuang Zhidong probably found it impossible to swallow that bitterness.” It was no different from a pauper losing out on several major fortunes—and not just in terms of money.","Yue Fuguang could even guess that Zhuang Yuyan’s father often fantasized in solitude: if he had grown up in Da Yan, perhaps the throne would have been his!","As for the brothers Emperor Mingxi had eliminated before and after taking power—those could conveniently be ignored.","[Master has guessed correctly. After learning of his true identity, Zhuang Zhidong became ambitious toward Da Yan. So he found himself some helpers, intending to reclaim what he believed was rightfully his.]","“His helpers were the people behind Zhuang Xiu?” In this era of clan society, appealing to the clan head was the most reliable way to secure one’s interests and find the most steadfast ally.","[Correct. He told the Zhuang clan head—namely, Zhuang Xiu’s uncle. Together, they set up a trap for Shen Jian.","Shen Jian fell for Zhuang Yuyan at first sight. In the border town, he doted on her endlessly; she could even enter his private study on occasion. Thus, the border defense maps quickly ended up on the clan head’s desk.","When Zhuang Yuyan was five months pregnant, she accompanied Shen Jian back to the Shen household in the capital. Shen Jian intended to use her pregnancy as an excuse to elevate her to the status of a legitimate wife.","But Emperor Mingxi was still clinging to life at the time, and the Grand Princess was still around—they naturally refused. In the end, Zhuang Yuyan became Shen Jian’s noble concubine.]","Yue Fuguang glanced sidelong at Shen Jian and said flatly, “This Shen Jian appears upright and reliable on the surface, but deep down he’s a complete scumbag traitor!","He coddles a woman he brought back from outside, wants to make her his legitimate wife—did he ever consider his actual wife’s feelings?”","Her contemptuous gaze seemed almost tangible. Even though Shen Jian had his back to her, he could clearly feel the weight of her stare, like needles pricking him.","To receive such a judgment from the Preceptor herself—how could he ever face her or his fellow officials again? Had this not come from the infallible divine artifact spirit, he would never have believed his future self could be so despicable!","“If I recall correctly, Shen Jian’s wife is the niece of Minister of Rites Zhang Zhongping—well-mannered, filial to her in-laws, raising their children properly, without a single fault.","Zhang Qingyu was the one who enabled Shen Jian to guard the border without any worries. And his repayment? Bringing back some ‘true love’ to disgust everyone. How ironic!”","By now, Shen Jian’s face had turned the color of pig liver. With every word Yue Fuguang spoke, his flush deepened. Thinking of his gentle and graceful wife, whose name was Madam Zhang, his face burned with shame.","Madam Zhang—she was the woman he had loved since youth. In the years since their marriage, their bond had been deep. How could he have lost his mind upon seeing Zhuang Yuyan?","[Master, you don’t yet know: Zhuang Yuyan’s mission was to control Shen Jian, then through him control the Shen family, and gradually extend her reach into the imperial palace.","When she failed to become his legitimate wife, Madam Zhang became an obstacle. So, when she was eight months pregnant, after confirming through a secret method that she was carrying a girl, she staged a fall in Madam Zhang’s courtyard, causing a miscarriage to frame Madam Zhang.]","“So, Shen Jian believed her?” Back in her hometown, Yue Fuguang had seen plenty of melodramatic love-and-hatred plots. She didn’t need the system to spell things out; she could fill in the blanks herself.","[When a man is blinded by ‘love,’ he’ll believe whatever his beloved says. Madam Zhang thus lost her management authority over the household.","The Grand Princess had no choice but to personally take over the household management, simply to prevent Zhuang Yuyan from getting her hands on Shen family affairs.]","Even though Zhuang Yuyan’s scheme was crude and full of holes, Shen Jian chose to turn a blind eye.","He believed all of Zhuang Yuyan’s accusations but refused to listen to a single word of Madam Zhang’s self-defense, refusing to trust her character.","“Hah, men. Damn their ‘love’!” As for whether cursing might damage her divine image?","At this point, Yue Fuguang didn’t care. She was a goddess—she could say what she wanted, curse if she pleased. Who said gods never swore?","Would you believe the legends, or would you believe her, the authentic divine being?","[Master, every cause has its effect. Zhuang Yuyan had thought she was carrying a girl, and so cruelly used that child to frame Zhang Qingyu.","Who knew that secret method was inaccurate? Only after the miscarriage did she realize it had actually been a male fetus.","Unfortunately, the saying goes: Seven-month fetuses may live, eight-month ones may not. The child died shortly after birth.]","“So Zhuang Yuyan killed her own son with her own hands? She must have been furious, right?”","[Furious is an understatement. When she learned that not only had she lost the male child, but she had also damaged her body and might never conceive again, she nearly went mad.","Her mission was to control the Shen family. Without a biological heir, how could she do that?","By this point, you could say her mission had already failed.]","“That severe? One miscarriage and she couldn’t bear children anymore?”","[In this era, childbirth is like passing through the gates of hell. For her, it wasn’t just the fall—she had also taken an abortifacient beforehand.","The male child she aborted actually had some karmic connection with Zhuang Yuyan. It had struggled to finally get its chance to be reborn, specifically to settle a past grievance.","Before it could even be born, she deliberately destroyed it. That resentment was immense. Her damaged body was simply the consequence of that cause.]","Upon hearing such an otherworldly topic again, Yue Fuguang couldn’t help but shudder slightly. Her past life’s obsession with ghost stories still haunted her.","Even with her new, mighty divine identity, she still felt a bit creeped out by these supernatural matters.","The others weren’t much better off either. It was still raining, the surroundings dim and gloomy. The temperature, once pleasant amidst the rainfall in late April, now seemed to have turned icy cold."]},{"number":453,"title":"Chapter 453: Who Died This Time","paragraphs":["Shen Jian silently edged closer to Wei Shouyi. He didn’t feel even the slightest connection to the unborn child—he only felt a vengeful spirit coming to claim his life!","“Then why did Shen Jian die instead of Zhuang Yuyan?”","Isn’t a vengeful spirit supposed to go after the one who wronged it? Though this whole mess started over a rivalry for favor, the scheme was Zhuang Yuyan’s alone. Debts have their debtors, and grudges their targets—shouldn’t ‘it’ have gotten the right person?","“Well, Zhuang Yuyan’s mission failed, and keeping Shen Jian alive no longer served her purpose. Instead, it just anchored her to the Shen family.","So in the eleventh year of Yuankang, when Shen Jian returned to the border town, Zhuang Yuyan followed him again.","At that time, along the border, the kingdoms of Bei Li and Da Yan were constantly clashing, with skirmishes big and small happening often.","Zhuang Xiu received word from Zhuang Yuyan, and the two of them colluded from within and without. Not only did they cause Shen Jian’s death, but they also cost the lives of over twenty thousand soldiers under his command.","Because of his status and personal skill, Shen Jian was a notable figure among Da Yan’s military commanders. In the end, he died at Zhuang Xiu’s hands. You could say Zhuang Xiu used Shen Jian as a shiny feather in his cap!","Shen Jian’s life became Zhuang Xiu’s stepping stone for advancement.”","“What a shame about those twenty thousand soldiers!”","Shen Jian: What about me? What about me? Plays peanut-dropping emoji.","Yue Fuguang: The scumbag deserves to die!","“Little Zhu, you mentioned earlier that the Bei Li and Western Qiang generals were fighting. What started it?”","“Master, I spiked the Bei Li soldiers’ lunch with one batch of my medicine, and then the Western Qiang troops’ drinking water with another.","Sure enough, the symptoms hit the two sides about the time it takes an incense stick to burn apart.","Just now, as soon as Zhuang Xiu noticed that it was only his own men falling victim, he suspected Feng Wuhuan was behind it.","Because of the medicinal pill’s effects, two men who used to be evenly matched are now getting utterly crushed, and Feng Wuhuan is being ground into the dirt. They’ve become mortal enemies for good.”","Yue Fuguang’s heart stirred. Mortal enemies—perfect. That makes it easier for her to meddle behind the scenes, successfully driving a wedge between the two kingdoms without getting caught.","“Little Zhu, arrange an accident so that both men’s deaths look like the other side’s doing.”","Wei Shouyi and Shen Jian’s eyes lit up. Bao Qianjun, who had been planning to report this to Zheng Feng, turned back instead. Since the Grand Preceptor already had a plan, they just needed to watch it unfold—daring not to interfere and mess up her scheme.","The next day, under Zheng Feng’s guidance, Yue Fuguang made a thorough inspection of the surrounding area. Although Three Forks was nominally her private territory, commoners weren’t banned from settling there.","Along the way, she spotted a few small villages that rented land, growing high-yield grain and various new vegetables.","A hundred-plus miles of Three Forks had even sprouted a small city of several ten thousand people, twenty miles from the Yue army’s encampment.","Yue Fuguang was pleased with Three Forks’ development—and equally satisfied with the progress of those on Chengping Mountain.","The system also showed her the pitiful sight of the Bei Li and Western Qiang allied forces, all suffering from purging and dehydration.","On the third day, just as Yue Fuguang was about to depart, she boarded her carriage to the clear, crisp sound of the system’s death knell.","“Master, Feng Wuhuan died last night.”","“Little Zhu, you work fast!” Though, for someone like her and the system, killing a person wasn’t hard, making it look like the other side’s doing still required some effort.","People weren’t brainless—simple framing wouldn’t fool two kingdoms so easily.","“Master, this time you’re praising the wrong person. Little Zhu hadn’t even put my brilliantly subtle plan into action yet, and Feng Wuhuan was already dead!","Alas! With Feng Wuhuan dead, my elaborate scheme to stir up discord has gone to waste!”","The system had even paid ten integrity points out of its own pocket to buy a brilliant borrowed-knife plan from a newly-met system friend. According to that system friend, its host came from the Xia Kingdom—in fact, the ancient ancestor of the system’s own host—and was brimming with stratagems.","Too bad, compared to her own host, that one was a bit poor.","“If it wasn’t you, then who did it? He couldn’t have just died from shitting himself out of weakness, could he?”","“Master, how did you know Feng Wuhuan died from diarrhea? That’s indeed his cause of death on the surface!”","“Then what’s the real cause? Who made the move?”","“Feng Wuyang, Feng Wuhuan’s cousin. But Feng Wuyang just gave a little extra water laced with Intestine-Cleansing Heart-Purging Pill to the already ill Feng Wuhuan, hoping to embarrass him—or at most make him half-dead from diarrhea.","Feng Wuhuan’s real death was from poisoning. The poison was slipped by a man named He Ming, who used Feng Wuyang’s hands to put it into the water given to Feng Wuhuan.”","“Who is He Ming? Why did he want to kill Feng Wuhuan? Got a grudge against him?”","“Master, you’ll never guess He Ming’s true identity!”","“True identity? Does he have another alias? Someone from another faction in Western Qiang? Someone from Bei Li? Don’t tell me he’s from Da Yan!”","“Hehe, he really is from Da Yan—a spy working for Zheng Feng’s father, Zheng Zicheng. His cover identity was a bandit from Chengping Mountain. This time, when the two-kingdom allied forces conscripted bandits, his stronghold was assigned to Bei Li, so he smoothly joined the Bei Li army.”","“So he became a Bei Li man, then poisoned a Western Qiang general? And used Western Qiang’s own people to do it!","This guy’s a genius!”","If anyone tried tracing that back, it’d be total chaos!","Yue Fuguang’s guess was spot-on. Shortly after her rainmaking team set out, frontline reporter System 07 continued its coverage.","“Master, Feng Wuyang thought his cousin’s death was caused by his own water dose and got worried he’d be implicated. So he took his men and went to confront Zhuang Xiu.”","“He plans to blame Feng Wuhuan’s death on Zhuang Xiu?” Yue Fuguang couldn’t help it—this Feng Wuyang was a real good guy!","“Exactly! Now that Feng Wuhuan is dead, those seven thousand men belong to him. Deep down, the guy’s thrilled!”","When Yue Fuguang’s caravan was fifty miles out and about to have lunch, the system piped up again.","“Master, the news that Feng Wuyang gave Feng Wuhuan poisoned tea has just been leaked. And by a fellow Western Qiang man, no less!","On the surface, this man is Xi Xiang’s planted spy in the army, but in reality, he’s from Bei Li—a subordinate of Beiyue.","He was trained by Xu Changyue, remember him, Master?”","“Of course I remember Xu Changyue, the cuckoo bird.”","“This man counts as part of Xu Changyue’s legacy to Bei Li. But his legacy didn’t fall into the emperor’s or his father Ji Xiang’s hands—instead, it was all scooped up by Beiyue.","And now, it’s finally been put to use.”","This turn of events went beyond Yue Fuguang’s expectations, but the direction was everything she’d hoped for.","By afternoon, when the system updated her again, Feng Wuyang had cleared himself of the murder suspicion and was subtly pointing the finger at Bei Li.","“Little Zhu, keep an eye on things. If He Ming is in danger of being exposed, you must rescue him.”","Yue Fuguang also used the radio in the carriage to have Wu Yong send a telegram to Yu Boming, telling Zheng Feng and the others to keep track of movements on Chengping Mountain and be ready to help He Ming if his cover was blown.","Through wind and rain, when Yue Fuguang set off again the next day, the system once more announced a death.","Yue Fuguang looked around at the familiar scene, the familiar pattern. “Who died this time?”"]},{"number":454,"title":"Chapter 454: One More Death","paragraphs":["As long as their own people are safe, anyone else dying is a blessing in their eyes.","“Zhuang Xiu, Master, Zhuang Xiu died last night!”","“Poisoned again?”","“No, this time it was a blade wound. A unique scale from a Western Qiang war armor was left at the scene.”","“So it was Feng Wuyang’s doing?”","“Hehe, that’s how it looks on the surface.”","In other words, there was something else going on beneath it all.","“Master, Feng Wuyang has a younger brother, and Zhuang Xiu has a nephew. So now, Zhuang Huaqing has already taken a group of men to the Western Qiang camp to demand an accounting.”","“That scale... was it really from Feng Wuyang?” Even if he wanted to kill Zhuang Xiu, he wouldn’t do it himself, would he?","The ancestors once said a gentleman does not stand where danger looms. Even if Zhuang Xiu were weakened by dehydration, with all his layers of protection, killing him would still be difficult. A man in power like Feng Wuhuan wouldn’t need to personally act, and the one framing him must have realized that.","“Of course it wasn’t from his golden scale armor. That scale came from one of Feng Wuyang’s trusted subordinates.”","“So the attackers really were from Western Qiang?”","“Feng Wuyang has an even worse temper than Feng Wuhuan and holds grudges. You see, Feng Wuhuan scolded him during the march for slowing them down, and Feng Wuyang felt publicly humiliated. Once he had the chance, he couldn’t resist taking revenge.","Yesterday, Zhuang Xiu’s accusation nearly succeeded, and he publicly exposed Feng Wuyang’s ‘attempt to murder’ his own clan elder. When Feng Wuyang returns to the Feng family, he’ll face severe punishment. His grudge against Zhuang Xiu runs deeper than a ten-year-old ghost’s resentment, and vengeance wouldn’t even wait until morning.","That very night, he sent his own men to sneak over.”","Yue Fuguang frowned at the system’s mention of a ten-year-old ghost. The system’s database was full of metaphors—why did it have to bring up ghosts? Had it forgotten that this world actually had real ghosts and the Court of Hell?","And some things were more persistent than even Cao Cao’s name.","“They didn’t succeed?” Otherwise, Feng Wuyang wouldn’t just be a scapegoat. That man was useless if he couldn’t even kill someone properly.","“Someone else killed him first. By the time his team struggled to sneak into Zhuang Xiu’s tent, the body wasn’t even cold yet.","What’s more, just as they were about to retreat, the Northern Li army discovered them. Their entire squad of twelve was trapped inside Zhuang Xiu’s tent.","If Feng Wuyang hadn’t sent people on a desperate rescue mission to win loyalty, none of them would have escaped.”","“With all that evidence, they’d be guilty even without the scale, right? Also, Little Zhu, didn’t they administer poison earlier? How did they still have strength to fight?”","“Master, some people ate more, some ate less—symptoms varied in severity. Still, over ninety-five percent of them were incapacitated. Otherwise, how could twelve men sneak into a seven-thousand-strong camp and have any survivors? It was because too many soldiers couldn’t move!","Also, Feng Wuyang’s assassins were all disguised. To leave no traces, they carried back the bodies of the three who died.","For the Northern Li side, without physical evidence, even if they knew who did it, they couldn’t force Western Qiang to admit guilt!”","“So, who actually killed Zhuang Xiu? Don’t tell me it was He Ming again!”","For some reason, Yue Fuguang felt this was very likely.","“He Ming had wanted to act, but he only arrived a little before the Northern Li assassination team. At that point, Zhuang Xiu was still barely alive, so He Ming waited until he was completely dead. He left behind the scale fragment he had snatched during the day’s scuffle as a planted clue.","He was also the one who deliberately raised the alarm when the Northern Li men were discovered.","Master, you’ll never guess—it was Bei Ye’s people who killed Zhuang Xiu. Not Bei Yue. It was Bei Ye’s team, the ones who love assassination the most.”","This was such a mess.","“System, does this mean our sowing of discord worked? The brothers Bei Yue and Bei Ye have both begun to target the Emperor and his Eighth Prince’s forces.”","From the current situation, this retaliation had already reached the point of disregarding national interests—good news for her.","“You’re right, Host. Not only have they planted their own people in the military, but in the imperial court as well, they’re counterattacking against the hidden forces of the Emperor and the Eighth Prince.","Lately, it isn’t just Northern Li. Over in Western Qiang, Xi Yuanshan and Xi Ling have also been orchestrating moves remotely, openly and covertly targeting Xi Xiang.","The other sons of Xi Yan have only recently caught on, thanks to the ‘suggestions’ from those two, and they’re slowly beginning to see Xi Xiang’s ambitions and schemes.","In fact, Xi Xiang can no longer play the pig to eat the tiger or quietly grow rich. The more chaotic they become, the better it is for our mission.”","“System, haven’t Bei Yue and the others returned to their country yet?” It was almost the end of April, nearly May. If they delayed any longer, they might as well not go back and just stay to attend Emperor Mingxi’s birthday celebration.","“Bei Yue doesn’t dare to return. You said the ‘bone-dissolving poison’ is in the hands of the imperial family. His people are still searching, and until he finds out who wants to harm him, he definitely won’t go back.","Besides, since he learned that you have an antidote here for all poisons, he’s even less willing to leave until he gets it.”","Given how Bei Ji is treating him now, once Bei Yue goes back, he’ll rarely have another chance to be sent to Dayan. Bei Yue knows this well.","“As for Bei Ye, without Bei Yue shielding him, going back means he’d be stuck as a pawn. Now that he’s certain his father only sees him as a tool, with no real father-son bond, Bei Ye is even more unhinged than Bei Yue, the true victim.","His revenge against the Emperor and that precious Eighth Prince just keeps getting more creative.”","Since the system became aware of some of the task worlds it had been in, it had noticed that this particular world seemed to use poison to deal with enemies more than any other.","Scheming and plotting took too long to kill people; poison and assassination were far faster solutions to getting rid of troublemakers.","Sometimes the system wondered: was this why ploys and strategies in this world weren’t as developed as in its host’s homeland? Even the Thirty-Six Stratagems didn’t exist here.","Compared to stratagems, poison and assassination were more straightforward—it’s just a shame they lacked elegance and narrative appeal.","“Xi Yuanshan doesn’t want to go back and face a father who treats him like a fighting insect or a consort bloated with ambition.","Xi Ling doesn’t want to return and face his origins—he’s probably guessed he might not be Xi Yan’s biological son. He’s terrified Xi Yan knows much more and fears he’ll be secretly executed by the imperial family on his return.”","The system ticked off each person’s reasons for not going back.","“As for Gan Tang, her excuse is even simpler. She stays in Dayan on orders from Gan Sheng, awaiting her marriage.","Though the marriage alliance between the two countries hasn’t been finalized, Southern Yue’s candidate is definitely Gan Tang.","On Dayan’s side, the Fifth Prince firmly refuses, but Emperor Mingxi seems quite happy trying to set him up with your Fourth Sister.”","Hmph, Yue Fuguang’s face darkened slightly, but she said nothing.","She believed that until she returned to the manor, her grandfather would never agree to this engagement. And the old emperor was savvy enough not to force the Yu family. So there was no need to rush."]},{"number":455,"title":"Chapter 455: The Emergence of the Drought Demon","paragraphs":["[The latest news I've received is that the emperor plans to have Sixth Master Xie, Xie Zhifei, marry Gan Tang. Although he is a year younger than Gan Tang, among the princes, he is the most suitable candidate.]","They certainly couldn't have the Crown Prince take her as a secondary consort—she is, after all, a princess, and a legitimate one at that. Before Dayan was unified, Xie Zhiyan didn't have the audacity for such a thing.","[As for Oshima and Yanji, the King of Dongyi has urged them several times to return east as soon as possible. But those two, upon hearing that the floodwaters in their homeland haven't fully receded and that a plague has broken out, flatly refuse to go back.]","Finally, there's Lan Xuan'er. In Nanzhao, her siblings have joined forces to prevent the Empress from recalling her, so she has stayed behind with the others.","Yue Fuguang nodded. Good heavens—every single one of them had a solid reason not to return to their countries. They were treating Dayan as their temporary refuge.","If those people knew that Dayan was bound for war with their nations, and that they would automatically become hostages at that time, he wondered if they would pack up and flee overnight.","Shen Jian and Feng Tang, along with the others, listened to the reports coming back from the system while traveling. Upon learning that the generals of Beili and Xiqiang had both died, they felt immensely relieved.","Shen Jian, in particular, secretly sighed in relief upon hearing of Zhuang Xiu's death, even though he regretted not being able to kill the man himself.","In this life, he would never walk the same old path!","The Junior Preceptor was right—having too many women in the household was indeed the root of chaos.","They were thoroughly engrossed in the conversation when, suddenly, the voices went quiet.","Those keeping an eye on the situation noticed that the Junior Preceptor, who had opened a window for some air, had somehow already 'fallen asleep' leaning against a soft cushion.","Just as Yue Fuguang and his group were about to leave Hezhou, the joint forces of Xiqiang and Beili were barely able to stand and walk. However, most of them, due to eating and then vomiting, had withered down to mere sticks over the past few days, so thin that a gust of wind could knock them over.","As for the deaths of Feng Wuhuan and Zhuang Xiu, the rulers of the two countries began bickering the moment they learned of it. With Dayan's spies stirring the pot behind the scenes, the two sides were on the verge of falling out completely.","At this point, a rumor spread through both armies and beyond: Dayan's Junior Preceptor Yue was a true Divine Maiden, not to be touched; anyone who did would be punished.","The inexplicable diarrhea that had struck both armies, along with the deaths of Zhuang Xiu and Feng Wuhuan, became irrefutable proof of this.","Yes, up to now, the finest physicians and poison masters of both nations had been unable to identify the poison or drug used.","The System cackled with laughter: Of course they can't find out. The ingredients in the Abdominal Clearing and Calming Pill don't exist in this world's botanical database.","Moreover, the Abdominal Clearing and Calming Pill is, strictly speaking, not a poison. It's just that it was used on the wrong targets—mortal bodies simply cannot withstand its potency!","\"Old Qian, has Fuguang reached Jizhou?\" Emperor Mingxi put down the border military report just delivered by Huo Ying and immediately thought of Yue Fuguang.","Because Dayan was set to officially launch an attack on Nanyue at midnight tonight, the Emperor felt a bit uneasy without Yue Fuguang at court to hold things down.","He gazed at the bright sky outside the hall—it was only early May, yet the heat was unbearable. Without Yue Fuguang's rain along the way, Dayan would be even hotter across the board, and they would have no spare strength to wage war on Nanyue.","Eunuch Qian carefully added some cool tea to the Emperor’s cup before replying with a smile, \"Your Majesty, if we calculate the time, Junior Preceptor Yue and his party should have entered Hezhou territory yesterday.\"","Setting down the teapot, he picked up an ink stick and began grinding ink slowly. In his heart, Qian Gui knew that ever since the Junior Preceptor had left the capital over two months ago, His Majesty had not slept a single peaceful night.","Emperor Mingxi glanced at the map on the wall, chuckled, and said, \"Jizhou is small. At Fuguang's current speed, he should reach the capital in less than seven days.\"","Qian Gui: Dayan is still in drought. Had His Majesty forgotten that even if the Junior Preceptor returned, he would soon have to leave again to alleviate the drought?","Never mind—Qian Gui didn't dare pour cold water on the Emperor while he was in a good mood. That would just be asking for trouble.","But thinking of the drought, Qian Gui suddenly remembered something. After some hesitation, he couldn't help but speak up. \"Your Majesty, this old servant recently heard a rumor and isn't sure if it should be mentioned.\"","Emperor Mingxi set down his cup. \"Oh? What rumor? Speak freely—I grant you immunity.\"","Qian Gui bowed and said, \"This old servant heard among the common folk that 'the great drought across the land, thousands of miles of barren earth, is a sign of the drought fiend's emergence.'\"","\"The drought fiend's emergence?\" Emperor Mingxi's lips curled into a cold smile. \"I have already issued a self-criticizing edict, and yet there are still those who won't give up, who wish to shake the foundation of our state?\"","It wasn't just one province of Dayan suffering from the drought. This so-called 'drought fiend' could appear anywhere, but not in Dayan.","Otherwise, it would give their enemies a reason to attack them.","Though they had already begun operations against Nanyue, they didn't want to open up a full-scale war on all fronts.","\"Have you traced where this rumor started, and who it targets?\" Dayan had a 'Divine Maiden,' which seemed like a blessed land. After all, a large number of Nanyue civilians had recently been fleeing across the border to Dayan.","The dirty nickname of 'drought fiend' should never have been thrown at them.","\"According to the Shadow agents, the news first originated among the people of Nanzhao. Your Majesty knows that Nanzhao is rich in shamans, and its populace believes in such things more.\"","Eunuch Qian cautiously glanced at Emperor Mingxi's expression before continuing, \"Somehow, the rumor spread into Dayan's borders. However, thanks to Junior Preceptor Yue steadying them, our people are not too worried about the drought fiend's influence.\"","\"So they still believe it,\" Emperor Mingxi said helplessly. He had no better solution for the ignorance of the common folk.","But Dayan now had thousands of civilian schools, and many people were willing to part with a few catties of grain or a few coins to let their children learn some characters and gain a bit of knowledge.","The next generation of Dayan's people had hope of not being as ignorant and foolish as their parents.","Emperor Mingxi's fingers tapped lightly on the desk. After a moment, his voice rang out, \"Old Qian, handle this matter carefully. Don't let the people do anything unwise because of it.\"","In the past, this would have been a perfect opportunity to eliminate rivals.","Nowadays, with Yue Fuguang at court, none of the civil and military officials dared to make waves. But among the common people, though Dayan's territory wasn't large compared to the six states, it was still sizable. With all kinds of people, he couldn't guarantee that no one, discontented with their comfortable lives, would use this to stir up trouble.","As it turned out, Emperor Mingxi's concerns were not unfounded.","While Yue Fuguang was still spreading rain in the far north of Dayan, in the far south—Flower City, a border town near Nanzhao, and its surrounding villages and counties—the rumor of the drought fiend grew louder.","In the streets and alleys of Flower City, a piece of news had been circulating for days.","This news seemed to sprout from the corners of teahouses and taverns, leap from porters' carrying poles, and crawl into everyone's ears through the mutterings of old women under village locust trees.","\"A great drought across the land, thousands of miles barren—this is a sign of the drought fiend's emergence!\" one person said mysteriously, sharing the gossip he'd just heard."]},{"number":456,"title":"Chapter 456: Sacrificing to the Drought Demon to Pray for Rain","paragraphs":["“A drought demon? That can’t be!” The dark-skinned, honest-faced man felt a chill in his heart at the mention of drought demons, instinctively afraid.","What is a drought demon? Since childhood, he’d heard the elders speak of it: when a drought demon runs amok, the heavens refuse to rain!","“Why can’t it be?”","The man shot him a look of annoyance, as if he’d never seen anyone so ignorant, then continued. “I’ve heard it’s not just here—other places are suffering from drought too. The wells have gone dry, and the cracks in the riverbeds are wide enough to swallow a man whole.”","He spat on the ground, but his mouth was so dry that there was barely any spittle.","These were all country working men waiting for odd jobs, except for the old man who had spoken first, a local loafer from the town itself.","They were huddled together in the shade beneath someone’s eaves, escaping the heat, and soon the conversation turned to the drought.","The only reason they still had water to drink was because, a month ago, the young preceptor had visited and brought heavy rain, temporarily alleviating the crisis.","But now a month had passed, the sky hadn’t rained again, and the weather was sweltering, with a blazing sun every single day. The fields were starting to dry up again. People whose hopes had been rekindled by the goddess’s rain now watched the water levels drop day by day, their hearts filled with panic.","A young man took up the thread. “Ain’t that the truth? They say someone’s even seen the thing at night—dressed in a floor-length blood-red gown, hair all tangled and face hidden. Everywhere it goes, the moisture just vanishes...”","Another man chimed in with “proof.” “Take the Big Bowl River in the next village. In just one night, the water level sank by a finger’s depth. They say that thing carried it all away!”","Gossip like this spreads faster than any horse. No way stations or fresh mounts needed—just one pair of lips and another set of listening ears.","Within a few days, these tales multiplied. “Evidence” cropped up everywhere along the border.","“When the drought demon appears, the world turns dry; for a thousand li, not a blade of green.” These words had become the ironclad “truth.”","When the officials of Huacheng heard about it, they were furious. “Ridiculous!” Assistant Magistrate Zhou Zhou Shencai nearly smashed his cup in his study.","Huacheng was a border town, a small one at that. There were troops stationed nearby, and since there was no prefect here, he, as assistant magistrate, was the highest official.","If this rumor caused any trouble, he’d be the first to bear the blame—a huge burden to carry.","What times these were! Dayuan and Nanyue were already at war, and if this gossip destabilized the border, his head would be as good as lost!","“I wonder when the young preceptor will pay us another visit?” Assistant Magistrate Zhou Shencai mumbled to himself for what felt like the hundredth time that day, thinking of Yue Fuguang.","Back on the distant frontier, Yue Fuguang was someone who could withstand being talked about constantly. If everyone in the world muttered her name every day, her ears would have grown calloused long ago.","“Master, I hear that the young preceptor has just reached Hezhou and Jizhou at best—still far from here,” his adviser, the magistrate’s secretary, tried to soothe him. “First things first, we need to squash this rumor. Mustn’t let it cause any chaos.”","Truth be told, Huacheng and its environs were short on water, but thanks to the young preceptor’s rainfall, things weren’t as dire as imagined.","The real puzzle was where all this anxious talk of drought had actually started.","Besides, over in Lanzhou, the fighting with Nanyue was already going hot. If they couldn’t help out, at least they shouldn’t disrupt things, or no one would have an easy time.","“Right, right!” Zhou Shencai clenched his teeth and muttered low. “Cracking down on these rumors can’t wait!”","He thought for a moment and quietly instructed his secretary, “Do this...”","Not far from Huacheng, the setting sun hung red as blood, staining the whole earth an anxious yellow, like pottery scorched in a kiln.","In the fields, the wheat sprouts bore a pale green with faintly yellowing tips. It was this slight yellowing that filled the steadied old farmers with worry.","The river, once topped up by the young preceptor, seemed to be leaking. Within half a month, the water level had clearly dropped, and in some places the dark gray mud was beginning to emerge.","Along the farm path, a bedraggled band of strangely dressed people approached from the distance, slowly coming nearer. These people were dark-skinned, with thick, calloused knuckles on their fingers—clearly ordinary country men and village women who had labored year in, year out.","What was most striking were the few among the group whose clothing obviously marked them apart.","This procession of over a hundred people was dressed mostly in rough, gray-black homespun. Only one man, about forty years old, had a shirt made of fine cotton.","The rest of them included a person of medium height, holding a staff carved with a snake's body and a human face, wearing a fearsome mask of a fanged green and red demon and a deep-red cape that covered him completely—so no one could even tell if they were male or female.","Following that figure were six men also draped in red and black capes, each wearing small demon masks.","Two carried bundles of firewood, two held knives, and two were shoving along a young woman with her hands tied, pushing and dragging her toward the riverbank ahead.","Behind these eight people pressed an ordinary crowd of locals: about a hundred men, their faces either wooden or blank, with only a few flushed with indefinable joy, a strange, blood-hued glint brightening their eyes.","At the very rear stumbled a few women who moved just as unsteadily as the captive girl ahead.","One of them had red-rimmed eyes and was murmuring to herself; if one listened closely, she was saying, “My poor daughter, she’s no drought demon, no drought demon. You can’t... can’t...”","As for what they couldn’t do, the last words weighed a thousand pounds or burned the tongue, leaving her choked with sobs that she could get out no more.","“We’re here!”","“Begin the ritual to pray for rain!”","At the narrow, piercing command from the masked man in the demon crown, a makeshift and utterly crude folk rain ceremony, from its participants to its offerings to every step, staggered its start.","But no matter how hard the men with the demon masks twirled and skipped, there wasn’t even a scrap of cloud at the horizon.","The commoners kneeling in the back whispered nervously to each other. “Dashun, would you say those prayer-callers up front just ain’t got the knack?”","“Last time when the Goddess spread clouds and summoned rain, it was simple: she waved her hand at the sky, and the wind brought in the clouds. Then she motioned again, said ‘Rain, come,’ and the rain galloped down for a whole day and night.”","Stealing another upward glance at the figures with their frantic and jerky dance steps, he shook his head. “I don’t buy a word of their talk about some drought-demon woman.”","Hard as things were, could they really be worse off than the Southern Yue kingdom beyond the next range?","They were short on water, yes, but not desperately so.","They still had water stored from when the Goddess came, and there was water held in the ponds and ditches, too. The land was a bit dry, but the crops were not worse than years gone by. How could the clan leader still trust a few good-for-nothing strangers’ half-truths?","“Datou, brother, keep it down! Don’t let the clan head or them lot get wind of it. Next thing they will set you to burning right alongside sweetmeat Xinghua!”","The young man named Dashun plainly feared the demon-masked men and warned his friend quietly even as he nervously snuck a peek in their direction.","“Fear ’em? If they can’t bring the rain today, let’s see if the clan leader will still believe those tall-tales!”","Datou said the toughest words, but the apology written in his eyes had already betrayed his bluster."]},{"number":457,"title":"Chapter 457: Returning to the Capital","paragraphs":["The woman named Xinghua was tied to a wooden stake, with two piles of gray-black dry firewood at her feet. In Liu Datou’s eyes, that was the color of death.","Several men had been dancing for nearly an hour, exhausted to the point of collapse, yet the light of the setting sun still bathed the land.","“A drought demon—there must be a drought demon at work!” The Ghost King’s voice was shrill as his bony finger pointed at Xinghua, bound to the frame. “Burn her! Burn her now!”","“Once the drought demon is burned, Heaven will surely send rain to bless us!” He raised his hands and knelt in worship toward the sky.","“Don’t burn my daughter! She’s no drought demon, she’s not!” Xinghua’s mother broke free from the grasp of several people and rushed forward.","She spread her arms like a hen protecting her chicks, standing in front of Xinghua.","Xinghua’s hands and feet were bound, her mouth gagged. Watching her mother, she could only sob muffled cries. No matter how she twisted, she couldn’t move an inch.","“Ignorant woman, stand back at once!” the Ghost King barked. “Do you dare to provoke Heaven’s wrath?”","He turned to the man in the fine cotton robe. “Clan Leader Liu, drag her away now. If you miss the auspicious hour and no rain comes, don’t blame me, the Heavenly Master!”","“Of course, of course,” Clan Leader Liu said with a fawning smile, signaling to the clansmen behind him.","Two young men stepped forward hesitantly, reaching for Xinghua’s mother, who was already half-mad with grief.","As the three struggled, the Ghost King grew impatient. He barked orders to his six subordinates. “Light the fire! Execute the drought demon!”","Whoosh!","Crackle, crackle!","The dry wood ignited instantly in the roaring flames.","The fire hadn’t yet reached Xinghua, but the smoke already stung her eyes, forcing them shut.","“Ah—Xinghua, my poor daughter!” Xinghua’s mother lashed out wildly at the young men holding her back.","“You devils! I’ll fight you to the death!”","“Wahhh—!”","“My daughter was about to be married! Why are you doing this to her?”","Her mother’s wails grew louder, while Xinghua’s struggles grew weaker. Soon, the flames had crept to her feet...","The fire burned for no one knew how long. The sun set, the moon rose, yet the blaze still hadn’t died.","This Xu Xinghua was not a member of the Liu clan, but she was a villager of Liu Village. The clan leader’s son had taken a liking to her beauty and wanted to take her as a concubine.","But Xinghua was already betrothed and about to be married. After the clan leader’s son was rejected by the Xu family, he sneaked into her chamber one night, attempting to force himself on her. He was beaten by Xu Xinghua’s father and brother and had been bedridden ever since.","The Liu clan made up seventy percent of the village. Clan Leader Liu was both the clan head and the village chief. He had Xu Xinghua’s father and brother sent off to forced labor, and with no men left in the house, he seized their daughter, claiming she was a reincarnated drought demon!","Liu Datou shook his head. He knew in his heart that this was the village chief using the rampant rumors to take revenge on the Xu family and to assert his authority in the village.","Lately, the villagers had been placing their faith instead in the Oracle, deferring all difficult decisions to her little by little eating away at the clan chief’s power. It’s no wonder he needed to use such brutal methods to intimidate the ignorant clansmen!","Some saw through Clan Leader Liu’s scheme clearly, but others genuinely believed in the drought demon story.","But after the “drought demon” was killed, the rain still didn’t come. Instead, the moon shone bright and clear over everyone’s heads.","“If the drought demon is dead, why hasn’t it rained yet?” someone in the crowd whispered.","“Yeah, why no rain?”","“Didn’t the Heavenly Master say it would rain once the drought demon was dead?”","One question followed another. The murmur of doubt grew louder until Liu Datou craned his neck and shouted, “Clan leader, you burned the drought demon to death—so why isn’t it raining?”","“That’s right, Clan Leader. If this isn’t Heaven’s punishment but that drought demon you named Xu Xinghua causing trouble, why isn’t it raining?”","“Maybe the drought demon still has accomplices. We need to search again more carefully!” Clan Leader Liu’s gaze swept over the crowd. Instinctively, everyone shrank back, and no one dared speak another word.","That night, some heard a woman’s sobbing drifting intermittently from the riverbank. Clan Leader Liu’s son, still bedridden from his injuries, suddenly fell into a high fever, crying that a female ghost had come for his life in the night.","By the next morning, the news had spread. Clan Leader Liu led the villagers to dig up the new grave that had been filled less than a day earlier. Inside the coffin lay the charred body of Xu Xinghua. It was said that the moment the coffin was opened, Xu Xinghua’s corpse was suddenly covered all over in white fuzz. They dragged the body out and burned it again on a pyre.","The incident was too bizarre, and many had witnessed it firsthand. Because it involved claims of a drought demon, word soon reached Magistrate Zhou.","Smack!","The sound of a teacup shattering came from Magistrate Zhou’s study. “I knew something would go wrong!” he growled through gritted teeth.","Village clan heads and elders administering their own private justice—it wasn’t unheard of in the past. As the saying goes, the emperor’s power stops at the county gate. Sometimes, a clan leader’s word carried more weight than the law from above.","But what times were these? Just two days ago, the Emperor decreed that spreading rumors of drought demons was a serious crime.","Magistrate Zhou had been monitoring the drought demon rumors for days and had already sensed something off. The rumors, which he had managed to suppress through careful maneuvering, had suddenly flared up again—and they were now pointing obliquely at the Grand Mentor!","Cold sweat broke out on his back the moment he realized this. He knew this wasn’t something a lowly magistrate like himself could handle.","Acting on the advice of his counselor, he wrote a secret letter that very night and sent it to the capital by eight-hundred-li urgent express. It had only been two days when the Liu Village incident exploded.","At that very moment, Yue Fuguang—still far from the capital—had no idea that a conspiracy targeting both herself and Dayan was already taking shape. And the whole thing had begun with a single man’s greed and an innocent girl’s brutal death.","More tragedies cloaked in the guise of drought demons to satisfy selfish desires were already unfolding in silence.","When she next passed through that region, it would be more than a month later. And men like Clan Leader Liu would soon meet a reckoning far sooner—and far more gruesome—than they ever imagined.","If only they had known... But in this world, there were never enough “if onlys.”","The main road to the capital, paved with concrete, was broad and smooth. On ordinary days, a constant stream of merchants and travelers jammed the road.","These days, the adjacent earth-track side road was almost never used.","But today was different. The Grand Mentor was returning to the capital. The main road had been temporarily closed to traffic to ensure his swift, unimpeded journey.","At the ten-li pavilion outside the capital’s outskirts, imperial guards stood at attention with halberds, flanking the main road all the way to the distant city gate.","Dark-colored banners with golden-threaded dragons shimmered in and out of sight under the early summer breeze.","Inside the pavilion, Emperor Mingxi did not sit on his mat. Instead, he stood on the steps with clasped hands, dressed in black robes and crimson leggings, his gaze fixed expectantly northeast.","By his side stood Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan and Eunuch Qian behind them. All three wore identical expressions, glancing toward the distance, dropping their gazes, then holding their breath.","Flanking them and outside the pavilion stood a crowd of officials in purple and red robes.","“Old Wei, shouldn’t the Grand Mentor’s carriage be here soon?” Cai Xian said, craning his neck. But the mountains and trees blocked his view, and he couldn’t see much beyond.","“Shouldn’t be long now,” Wei Ping answered, shielding his eyes with his hand. It was only early May—why was it so hot already?"]},{"number":458,"title":"Chapter 458: Your Majesty, Is My Family Doing Well","paragraphs":["Now that the Junior Mentor has returned, the drought near the capital will finally be relieved.","\"I heard the Junior Mentor can now cover over a hundred miles with her rain-making powers!\" said Huo Ying, the Minister of War, who rarely had a moment's rest since the war between Dayan and Nanyue broke out.","\"Isn't that so? Prefect Shen of Jizhou reported one hundred and fifty miles,\" added Dong Qianli, the Minister of Revenue, who was most sensitive to numbers.","\"I remember when she left the capital just over two months ago, it was only seventy or eighty miles.\" The Junior Mentor's growth rate had truly exceeded their expectations.","The Minister of Rites turned to Yu Chongshan and said, \"I have yet to congratulate you, Senior Mr. Yu.\"","Yu Chongshan, who had been craning his neck toward the northeast, absentmindedly clasped his hands in return and said, \"Congratulations to all, congratulations to all!\"","And indeed, it was cause for celebration. There was nothing wrong with that sentiment—if his granddaughter's abilities grew stronger, the beneficiaries were the rulers and subjects of Dayan and all its people.","\"Look!\" Yu Zhongchun suddenly pointed at the rolling dark clouds on the horizon and asked Yu Chongshan, \"Father, is that Fuguang approaching?\"","Yu Chongshan nodded. \"It must be Fuguang! Only our Fuguang, a true divine maiden, can be draped in clouds and rosy light, bringing wind and rain with her.\"","Suddenly, the thunderous sound of horse hooves rolled in from the distance.","Through the gaps in the trees, the crowd could not only hear the hoofbeats but also see a troop of iron cavalry bursting out from the forest.","At the front was a chestnut-red steed, its rider clad in black armor and holding a silver spear, his battle robe dusty yet still sitting ramrod straight. It was Shen Jian, the former Commander of the Forward Army.","\"He's here!\" Emperor Mingxi recognized his nephew Shen Jian and knew that Yue Fuguang's carriage would follow closely behind.","Without waiting for Eunuch Qian's assistance, the emperor quickly descended the steps, his imperial tassels swaying lightly. The forbidden troops on both sides of the road turned in unison, clanging their halberds to the ground, the sound shaking the wilderness.","In just moments, Yue Fuguang's luxurious carriage, drawn by five white horses, came into everyone's view.","Following the emperor, the civil and military officials also took the initiative to step forward.","The cavalry halted abruptly fifty paces from the rulers and subjects of Dayan.","Shen Jian dismounted swiftly. Without removing his armor, he unbuckled his sword, held it in both hands, and strode forward.","Kneeling on one knee ten paces from Emperor Mingxi, his iron armor clanged against the stone-paved ground. He declared loudly, \"Your subject Shen Jian, obeying the imperial decree to protect the Junior Mentor, has successfully fulfilled the mission!\"","Behind him, the hundred cavalrymen dismounted in unison, their armor clattering as they knelt in a row.","Shen Jian kept his head lowered, seeing only the hem of the emperor's black robe stop before him.","A hand landed on his shoulder, patting firmly through the layers of armor scales.","\"Well done, young man!\" the emperor's voice was low but clearly audible to all present.","\"Is Fuguang well?\" He raised his head, looking toward the carriage.","His gaze met Yue Fuguang's, who had just pulled back the carriage curtain and was preparing to step down.","Emperor Mingxi grinned at Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang: After not seeing this old fellow for over two months, he's becoming less and less restrained.","Yue Fuguang smoothed her sleeves and slowly stepped down from the carriage.","The moment her figure appeared, a thunderous chorus of welcomes echoed through the Ten-Mile Pavilion.","\"We welcome the Junior Mentor back to the capital!\"","\"We welcome the Junior Mentor back to the capital!\"","\"We welcome the Junior Mentor back to the capital!\" ...","Emperor Mingxi hurried forward a few steps to greet Yue Fuguang. \"Fuguang, the journey was arduous!\"","\"Your Majesty.\" Yue Fuguang clasped her hands in salute. Hard work it was truly hard work, and she would not be so insincere as to say otherwise.","The emperor carefully examined Yue Fuguang's complexion. Other than a bit of travel grime, she hadn't lost weight. His heart finally eased slightly.","Taking a small white jade bowl from the tray held by Eunuch Qian behind him, he said, \"You must be thirsty. I had the imperial chef freshly brew some iced sour plum soup.\"","Yue Fuguang gazed at the amber-colored sour plum soup in the jade bowl and found it rather surreal.","She had anticipated that the emperor would lead the civil and military officials to greet her at the Ten-Mile Pavilion outside the capital.","But wasn't the proper greeting to offer wine? Why had it become sour plum soup, and in a bowl of all things?","She took the jade bowl, sipped it gently, and praised, \"Chef Bao's skills have improved again.\"","Emperor Mingxi burst into laughter at her words. \"Isn't that so? I told you you'd like it, but the Crown Prince didn't believe me!\"","As he spoke, he cast a sidelong glance at Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan, who was a step behind.","\"Zhiyan pays respects to my aunt. Your journey was arduous,\" Xie Zhiyan said, bowing to Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang nodded to him. \"Crown Prince.\"","A crown prince bowing to a \"minister,\" and Yue Fuguang accepted it without hesitation, and no one else found it improper.","Even if some had found it improper in the past, having seen it so many times, they had long since been forced to accept it.","Besides, Yue Fuguang's latest exploits had brought immense merit to Dayan, and the empire still relied on her rain-making powers to relieve its woes.","After greeting the Crown Prince, Yue Fuguang spotted Qian Gui behind Emperor Mingxi and smiled at him. \"Eunuch Qian, it's been a while.\"","Qian Gui, looking flattered, quickly bowed deeply. \"This old servant pays respects to the Junior Mentor. You must be weary from the journey.\"","Yue Fuguang's gaze then fell on the princes and princesses behind Emperor Mingxi, with particular attention on the Fifth Prince, Xie Zhiquan, whom she eyed again and again.","Xie Zhiquan had been trying to hide among his brothers since Yue Fuguang stepped out of the carriage. But being tall, and with only a few fully grown princes, even hiding among the younger children couldn't conceal him.","When Yue Fuguang's gaze landed on him, he felt an overwhelming pressure like a mountain bearing down on him, as though a thousand pounds were crushing his shoulders.","Just as Xie Zhiquan's legs began to tremble and cold sweat soaked his back, Yue Fuguang let out a loud, deliberate snort and released the pressure.","Emperor Mingxi, standing nearby, secretly sighed in relief. If Fuguang truly decided to strike his son in anger, all he could do as his father was watch—could he take the punishment for him?","The emperor shook his head. He was still hoping to live a few more years; he dared not bear the brunt of Fuguang's wrath.","Fifth Prince was young; a few beatings wouldn't kill him!","Xie Zhiquan: You really are my dear father.","Emperor Mingxi: If you weren't my son for daring to covet Fuguang's sister, you'd have been dead eighty times over!","\"Fuguang, you must be tired. Why don't we head back?\" Emperor Mingxi cleared his throat lightly, changing the subject.","Yue Fuguang cast another side-glance at Xie Zhiquan and asked knowingly, \"Your Majesty, is everything well at my home?\"","Emperor Mingxi was taken aback by her question. Shouldn't she be asking Yu Chongshan about the Yu family's well-being?","Asking him—how would he know?","Ever since the incidents involving Sima Jing, the Murong family, the Prince of Qi, and the Prince of Ming, Emperor Mingxi had been wary of all high officials. The Yu residence was the one place where he dared not plant a single informant.","But when his gaze landed on Fifth Prince Xie, who was secretly wiping sweat, he immediately understood the implication. Fuguang was reminding him.","\"Minister Yu, come here.\" Emperor Mingxi waved at Yu Chongshan. \"Fuguang has just returned and is already worried about the family. Tell her what's going on to ease her mind.\"","Emperor Mingxi decisively kicked the ball to Yu Chongshan, otherwise he really wouldn't have known how to answer Yue Fuguang's question."]},{"number":459,"title":"Chapter 459: System, You've Changed","paragraphs":["The thing his son did—taking advantage of a man's service to the nation to make a move behind his back—was indeed dishonorable. But as a father, he couldn't help being selfish. Who wouldn't want to marry a girl from the Yu family as their daughter-in-law?","\"Your humble servant greets Your Majesty.\" Yu Chongshan first paid his respects to Emperor Mingxi, then looked at Yue Fuguang with a face full of affectionate smiles.","\"Fuguang, after this trip, you've lost weight.\" Yu Chongshan's face showed genuine concern. \"When you get home, have your grandmother prepare some nourishing food to help you recover.\"","Emperor Mingxi was speechless, but Yue Fuguang smiled faintly. Whether she had lost weight or not, she knew herself well enough.","However, there is a kind of cold in this world called \"your grandmother thinks you're cold,\" and a kind of thinness called \"your grandfather thinks you're thin.\" She understood all that.","\"Then let's head home quickly!\" Yue Fuguang saw that Emperor Mingxi was pretending to be clueless and decided not to pay any more attention to the royal father and son.","\"Fuguang, a welcome banquet...\" Emperor Mingxi stretched out his hand as if reaching for her. He had come to pick her up, but now that he had, she wanted to run away.","\"Your Majesty, with the drought crisis being so urgent and the common people already tightening their belts, it's not appropriate for us to indulge in extravagance. So, the welcome banquet should be canceled.\"","[Master, aren't you just saying that because you can't be bothered with the banquet?]","\"I'm tired after the journey, and who has the patience for some boring banquet? It's no fun at all.\" Yue Fuguang was completely unabashed. \"Besides, am I wrong? Along our journey, every commoner facing this drought is eating one meal and saving the next.\"","[Master, is it possible that they look gaunt and yellow not because of the drought, but because even without it, they wouldn't dare to eat their fill?]","Especially in ancient times, with few side dishes and little oil in the food, people relied heavily on staple grains. But with such low crop yields per acre, how many could truly eat and drink their fill?","Hence the saying: In times of prosperity, the people suffer; in times of decline, the people also suffer.","\"I don't care. I say we must not be extravagant, and that's that! At the very least, I don't want to see in Dayan what happened in the poem—wine and meat rotting behind vermilion gates while frozen bodies lie by the roadside.\" Yue Fuguang swept her gaze over Emperor Mingxi and his ministers. \"What does Your Majesty think?\"","Emperor Mingxi quickly nodded. \"Fuguang is right. The drought is critical, and the people are suffering. As those who are supported by the millions, it is indeed inappropriate for us to indulge in waste at this time.\"","He turned to Minister of Rites Zhang Zhongping. \"Zhang Aiqing, the Longevity Festival this year need not be held. Instead, we will distribute porridge for seven days, celebrating with the people.\"","During a drought, avoiding lavish banquets was the right thing to do. Although their Dayan had Fuguang to bring rain, and the people were still faring reasonably well, as emperor, he still had to set an example—influencing officials at all levels since those above set the trend for those below.","\"Your Majesty is wise!\"","\"Your Majesty is sagely—blessing to the people!\"","\"With Your Majesty, Dayan will endure for ten thousand generations!\" That came from someone bold enough to say it.","\"Your Majesty...\"","The officials' flattery rained down like drumbeats. Judging by Emperor Mingxi's delighted expression, he was clearly pleased by the praise.","Yue Fuguang casually pointed a finger toward the sky. Without needing to chant any incantations for wind, clouds, or rain, the rolling dark clouds immediately unleashed a heavy downpour.","Her intention was to cool down the emperor, who seemed a bit carried away. But unexpectedly, although Emperor Mingxi was instantly soaked to the bone, the feeling was like drinking iced tea on a hot summer day—his heart soared.","How could it not soar?","Every member of the Dayan court was drenched like drowned rats. When Eunuch Qian tried to hold an umbrella for the emperor, Mingxi waved him off.","He squinted up at the rain crashing down from the sky, watching the parched fields and woodlands quickly become moist, the grass, trees, and crops in the fields rapidly rejuvenating under the nourishment of the rain.","The Dayan courtiers gazed at Yue Fuguang's departing carriage. Some wore smiles, some faces full of reverence, and others expressions of complex emotion.","True to her nature, Yue Fuguang didn't go to the palace but returned directly to the Yu residence.","She was, of course, warmly welcomed by the entire family. \"Fuguang, are you tired? Do you want to rest first before eating?\" the old Madam Yu asked, holding her granddaughter's hand, looking her over. \"You've lost weight. This time you're back, you must take good care of yourself and get some nourishment!\"","\"Mother is right,\" added Madam Zhang, pouring Yue Fuguang a fresh cup of tea with a smile. \"I've had the estate send over plenty of fresh ingredients—all of Fuguang's favorites. Fuguang, how many days can you stay at home this time?\"","Though they lived within the deep confines of the inner courtyard, the women of the Yu family kept a close watch on the outside drought conditions. Especially after Fuguang left the residence, whenever they visited other households, the Yu ladies loved hearing the wives and madams praise how remarkable their Fuguang was, and how she had resolved droughts in various places.","Even the old Madam Yu, who rarely went out these days, had recently taken to making social calls. It was also the old Madam Yu and a few of her daughters-in-law who first caught wind of the rumors about the drought demon.","\"Mother, this time I can only rest for three days.\" With summer approaching, the drought would be at its worst. Fortunately, her abilities were growing, and her efficiency was more than double what it used to be.","[System, is there any way I can make it rain across all of Dayan in one go?]","The system rolled its eyes. Its host was daydreaming!","Even ordinary cultivators in the cultivation world wouldn't dare think like that. Yet here was a mortal trying to achieve it. How was its host more arrogant than the emperor these days?","[Host, do you remember that you're just a mortal of flesh and blood? Although Dayan isn't huge, it spans thousands of li. Even a cultivator at the Golden Core stage couldn't manage that in the cultivation world.]","The system had recently recovered some memories. It had traveled through many realms large and small before, but though the memories were blurry, it actually knew the answer to Yue Fuguang's question.","[The shop does have powerful talismans with large water volume, like the Water Dragon Talisman, but those are attack talismans—meant for destruction, not salvation. Host, you wouldn't be able to handle them.]","Ninety-nine percent of talismans in the cultivation world were related to combat. Expecting cultivators to create talismans for the common people's livelihoods? Dream on!","[What about other worlds, like wastelands or star systems? Don't those technologically advanced worlds have weapons for creating rain?]","[They do, but if you use their weapons to bring down rain, the pollution would slowly kill everyone here. Would you dare use that?]","Yue Fuguang was disappointed. She wouldn't dare use anything that wasn't environmentally friendly. She didn't want to do good and end up causing harm instead.","Her current situation was excellent; she couldn't afford to mess it up just because she wanted to be lazy.","[System, you've changed.] Yue Fuguang said it casually, but the system took it to heart. It had also noticed that it sometimes spoke differently from when it was first awakened. It would have to fix that.","\"Only three days? You're still so young—how can your body handle that? His Majesty...\" The usually sensible old Madam Yu couldn't help feeling resentful toward the emperor.","Fuguang might be a divine maiden descended to earth, but she was still just a twelve-year-old girl, running all over the country. How could her body take it?","At that moment, the old Madam Yu had forgotten all about the miraculous medicines her granddaughter had at her disposal.","Yue Fuguang took the old Madam Yu's hand and comforted her with a smile. \"Grandmother, it's actually because I wanted to go out and have some fun. Settling those droughts is just a side matter. Don't worry.\"","She then turned her gaze to the younger members of the Yu family sitting nearby, listening to the elders speak, letting her eyes rest especially on Yu Ningxin."]},{"number":460,"title":"Chapter 460: Marriage","paragraphs":["\"Grandfather, Grandmother, regarding that Fifth Prince Xie's proposal to our family, what exactly is going on? What are your thoughts, and what do Father and Mother think?\"","Hearing her own matters being discussed, Yu Ningxin felt only a momentary shyness before calmly waiting for her grandparents and parents to respond.","In another household, when matters of marriage were brought up, not only the person involved but even the unmarried younger members would actively or passively avoid the conversation.","But in the Yu family, this was not necessary. As Yue Fuguang put it, listening more and seeing more would benefit their future dealings and judgment of people.","Yu Chongshan said, \"Your grandmother, parents, and I are all of the mind that we should follow Little Four’s own wishes. But Little Four said she wanted to wait for you to return.\"","Yu Chongshan understood that Sister Xin wanted to hear Fuguang’s opinion. As the grandfather, he had also noticed that the children at home—not just Sister Xin, but also Xuan Jie’er and the other sisters—were different from the daughters of other households.","When it came to their own future marriages, they showed less shyness and more careful consideration. With this kind of foresight, and with their younger sister as their backbone, the girls of their family would not have a bad future.","Yue Fuguang smiled and waved Yu Ningxin over. When she came closer, she warmly pulled her to sit down. \"Fourth Sister, what are your own thoughts on Fifth Prince Xie? Just talk about what you like and dislike—there’s no need to consider anything else.\"","She added with a smile, \"With me here, no one can force our family to do something we don’t want to do!\"","Hearing this, everyone in the Yu family smiled. It was precisely because of this confidence that they had the nerve to refuse the marriage proposal from the Fifth Prince that day.","Afterward, Yu Chongshan even rushed to the palace to see Emperor Mingxi. Although his words were tactful, the main point was to tell the Emperor to keep his son in check.","Even if you are a prince, bypassing the parents to go directly to a subject’s home and ask for their daughter’s hand in marriage was against the rules.","Xie Zhiquan thought: It’s not that I didn’t want to tell my parents first—I didn’t dare to! If I had told them, this whole thing probably would have fallen through!","Emperor Mingxi thought: The Fifth Prince was right to act first and ask later. Otherwise, I wouldn’t have dared to bring it up either!","Anyone with eyes could see that Yue Fuguang did not want her sisters to marry into the royal family.","Yu Ningxin also laughed. \"Seventh Sister, I don’t know much about the Fifth Prince, and I don’t have many thoughts on it. So whether this marriage happens or not, I’ll follow your lead.\"","Yue Fuguang thought to herself: Oh no, don’t do that! I’ve been single for two lifetimes—following my lead on this is a terrible idea.","She could stand up for her sisters, but she didn’t want to interfere in their marriages. If she were some wise older sister with rich romantic experience, that would be one thing. But the problem was that she wasn’t. In her previous life, from middle school on, she had received plenty of love letters but never actually been in a relationship. All her knowledge came from novels and TV shows—fine for armchair theorizing.","If she actually tried to apply what she’d read or watched, the Yu girls would probably all end up single!","The system noticed its host’s lack of confidence and jumped in to save her. [Master, you can’t interfere too much in others’ romantic fate.]","\"I know that. But at least I can check their character and background—I won’t let anyone with bad intentions or a despicable nature ruin the Yu family’s girls.\"","[Don’t worry, Master. I’ve investigated Fifth Prince Xie thoroughly—from his birth to adulthood. I know how many times he wet the bed, whose milk he drank, and which palace maids he was closest to.]","\"So, does this guy have any issues?\" Actually, this was a flawed question—everyone has issues, big or small.","[The risk assessment is medium-low. His compatibility with Yu Ningxin is about eighty percent. He can be kept as a backup candidate.]","The system’s use of “backup candidate” left the Yu family momentarily speechless.","True, their family had some confidence—they dared to refuse a prince’s marriage proposal. But they had never actually considered treating the Emperor’s son as a backup.","If the censors got wind of this... well, the most powerful censor in Dayan was Feng Tang, one of their granddaughter’s biggest fans. So it was probably fine.","Emperor Mingxi: What about me?","\"Perfect. Investigate thoroughly every eligible, unmarried young man in the capital. Besides Fourth Sister, Second Sister and Third Sister are also of marriageable age.\"","The elders nodded mentally. Even those who had reached marriageable age—Yu Ningxuan, Yu Ningzi, and Yu Ningxuan—and the younger ones like Yu Ninglin, Yu Ningrong, and Yu Ningjin, all showed joy on their faces.","As long as Fuguang was willing to put some thought into their marriage prospects, their futures would be bright, and the risk of marrying badly would drop significantly.","Sitting quietly in the corner, the father and sons of the third branch of the Yu family all breathed a silent sigh of relief. Yue Fuguang still refused to acknowledge them.","But if she was willing to involve herself in the marriage arrangements of the two illegitimate daughters of the third branch, it meant she hadn’t completely given up on them yet. Could the father-daughter and sibling relationships still be salvaged?","Yue Fuguang: Keep dreaming (insert meme emoji).","\"Fourth Sister, take a good look around. If you find a young man who catches your eye—no matter his status—as long as he’s not engaged and has no one he loves, I can get him for you!\"","\"Fuguang is right. Fourth Girl, your own marriage is your own business. You must be clear about what kind of man you want to marry.\"","Several elders of the Yu family had been frightened by the failed marriages of several future grandchildren and had now become both open-minded and cautious about the younger generation’s marriages.","After Yu Laofuren finished speaking, Yu Chongshan added for the younger ones: \"The same goes for the rest of you. When the Yu family arranges marriages, we don’t care about family status or wealth, only character and ability.\"","Even if the granddaughters fell in love with a poor scholar, they would simply give them a larger dowry and offer more support.","As the Yu family discussed Yu Ningxin’s and the younger generation’s marriage prospects, the royal family in the palace was also talking about the same matter.","The Empress Dowager glanced at the Fifth Prince kneeling on the ground and asked Emperor Mingxi, \"The Emperor, what are your thoughts on the Fifth Prince’s marriage proposal to that Yu girl?\"","\"Empress Dowager, it’s not about what I think. It’s about what the Yu family—or rather, Fuguang—thinks.\" He glanced at the silent Xie Zhiquan. \"If Fuguang says no, then I can only blame my son for not being fortunate enough.\"","He had heard from his nephew Shen Jian that on the day Fuguang received the Yu family’s letter and learned what the Fifth Prince had done, she was so angry that she rested for half a day, and her expression was gloomy for several days.","Just now at the Shili Pavillion, he had also noticed how little Fuguang liked anyone trying to carry off her family’s cabbage.","The Empress Dowager nodded repeatedly at Emperor Mingxi’s words. \"My thought is, now that Fuguang is back, as the father, shouldn’t you apologize for your son’s recklessness?\"","\"The Empress Dowager is right. And I, as the lawful wife, have also been negligent. I’ve already prepared gifts of apology, just waiting for Empress Dowager and His Majesty to give the order to send them over!\"","Empress Xu and the Crown Prince exchanged a glance. Finding excuses to give gifts openly and legitimately to Fuguang—they had become quite skilled at it.","The Empress Dowager smiled with satisfaction. \"The Empress is very thoughtful. But the Fifth Prince’s behavior is far too reckless! Even if you had feelings for the Yu family’s Fourth Girl, you shouldn’t have gone to propose while Fuguang wasn’t at home!\"","She sighed. She knew why the Fifth Prince had done that, but some things still needed to be said.","\"Your grandson was reckless. Please forgive me, Imperial Grandmother, Imperial Father, and Empress Dowager!\"","Xie Zhiquan’s attitude of admitting his fault was sincere, but his relentless pursuit of Yu Ningxin remained unchanged. “Imperial Father, your son’s heart belongs to the Fourth Girl. I implore you to grant your blessing!”"]},{"number":461,"title":"Chapter 461: Factions","paragraphs":["Emperor Mingxi was exasperated by his son. Didn’t Fuguang say he was full of schemes? Why was he being so clueless now?","This wasn’t something he could simply bless and have done with. If it were that easy, he would have already married off every Yu girl to the imperial family.","“Fifth Prince, you must understand—this is not something I can simply grant on a whim!” Emperor Mingxi wasn’t afraid to reveal his own limitations in front of his son.","It was just impossible. If Fuguang didn’t nod, no one could change that.","“Father, your son swears that if I can marry Fourth Miss Yu, I will take no other concubines and will dutifully remain Your obedient son and Crown Prince’s loyal younger brother.”","His meaning was clear: even if he married a Yu woman, he would not let his wife’s family influence him to covet the throne.","As for taking no other women, the moment he realized his feelings for Fourth Miss Yu, he had secretly dismissed all his concubines and chambermaids.","Although the Yu family had never explicitly stated it, he knew the Grand Tutor’s temperament all too well. If his household wasn’t clean, he wouldn’t stand a chance of marrying a Yu girl.","“Father, we all know Little Aunt’s temper. Why not let the Fifth Brother find opportunities to interact more with Fourth Miss Yu? If Fourth Miss Yu also has feelings for him, given Little Aunt’s nature, she probably wouldn’t object,” Xie Zhiyan said.","Indeed, Xie Zhiyan understood Yue Fuguang well. As long as the two were mutually in love, Yue Fuguang—though protective of her sisters—wouldn’t meddle excessively in others’ fate.","“However...” Xie Zhiyan glanced at the excited Xie Zhiquan and shifted his tone, “For the sake of Fourth Miss Yu’s reputation, there must be boundaries. It’s best to meet only in appropriate settings.”","If the Fifth Prince got carried away and barged into the Yu residence demanding to see Fourth Miss Yu while the Grand Tutor was away from the capital, he would disgrace both the emperor’s and the Yu family’s honor.","No need to even guess—the moment the Grand Tutor returned, that would be the Fifth Brother’s doom. Even his father, the emperor, wouldn’t be able to save him!","Emperor Mingxi pondered briefly, then nodded in approval. “The Crown Prince is right. Fifth Prince...”","As the imperial family schemed over how to marry a Yu daughter into their fold, other high-ranking houses in the capital were also calculating their younger generation’s marriages, desperately searching for someone worthy of forming a match with the Yu family.","In fact, during Yue Fuguang’s three days at home, people seeking to gauge her stance never stopped coming to the Yu residence.","She simply lounged in her own courtyard, refusing to see anyone. However, she had made a preliminary selection of eligible young men and women in the capital and passed the compiled information to the Yu family head.","How they chose, and whom they chose, were no longer her concern.","For now, her attention was split—partly on the drought across various regions, but mostly on the war between Dayan and Nanyue.","Strangely enough, while the two countries were locked in fierce combat on the frontlines, peace negotiations through marriage were still ongoing behind the scenes.","You Minmin, the head of the Court of State Ceremonial, and his officials had spent five days negotiating with the Nanyue delegation. The Nanyue side insisted on choosing the Fifth Prince, while Dayan proposed the Sixth Prince, Xie Zhifei.","Clearly, Emperor Mingxi was still holding out hope that Xie Zhiquan might actually marry a Yu girl and was unwilling to use him for a political marriage.","[System, they’re already tearing each other apart on the battlefield—how do both sides still have the nerve to discuss marriage alliances?]","In ancient times, royal marriages between states were usually for political exchange, resource flow, military alliances, buying time to recover, or ending wars.","Yue Fuguang had read plenty about such practices in her hometown’s history, even able to recount famous examples. But given the current situation, Nanyue wanted a truce to catch its breath. After failing to kidnap her, they hastily presented a marriage proposal to Dayan, offering their legitimate princess as a show of sincerity.","But Dayan had just started its offensive, aiming to swallow Nanyue whole. They had no intention of ending the war through peace.","Even if Emperor Mingxi wanted that, none of the civil or military officials—who dreamed of leaving their names in history—would agree.","An arrow once shot never returns—that was Dayan’s reality now.","[Host, both sides are just wasting words and tea during negotiations. What’s the harm? You fight your war, we talk our talk. Who knows, it might work out!]","“What’s Gan Tang’s attitude? She’s still in Dayan. Even if she resists, it won’t mean much to Gan Sheng, will it?”","[Host, you haven’t seen her! Gan Tang is almost furious enough to die. Her hatred for Gan Sheng has reached its peak. If anything, Gan Sheng thinks he’s cleverly exiled a threat from Nanyue, but he may have brought himself an even bigger disaster.]","“What? Does Gan Tang still have the strength to oppose a ruler like Gan Sheng?” She had no men, no authority. Toppling a country’s emperor? Nearly impossible!","[Host, don’t forget—Gan Tang’s brother was once the Crown Prince.]","“So what? He’s been dead for years. Is he going to climb out of his coffin?” Yue Fuguang teased, mentally kneading the system.","[He can’t climb out, but a former Crown Prince would have networks. After his death, those loyal to him were either purged, switched sides, or finally wiped out by Gan Sheng when he took power.","But some forces remained loyal only to that faction.]","“You mean the Crown Prince’s six guards? After his death, they were disbanded or folded into the army. How many would still be loyal to a dead prince or his sister?”","Once someone is gone, so is their influence—a truth across all ages.","[Host, have you forgotten the secret forces the Crown Prince raised?]","“The Crown Prince’s shadow guards?”","[Host, consider this: the Crown Prince had likely sensed the emperor’s schemes against him. Historical records show that the emperor’s wish to replace him wasn’t exactly hidden. His favoritism for Gan Sheng, the son of his favored consort, was no secret either.","The relationship between the emperor and empress was also cold. The late emperor had little fatherly affection for the former Crown Prince. So, although never stated outright, every court official was an expert at reading the emperor’s intentions.]","“Was the emperor testing the officials’ stance?” As long as he never said it directly, he could advance or retreat as he pleased.","Not long before, Nanyue had gone through a coup; their brothers’ blood hadn’t yet dried. Power wasn’t solely in the emperor’s hands, so replacing the Crown Prince wasn’t a one-man decision.","[That’s part of it. So the shrewd former Crown Prince surely had secretly nurtured his own forces and left contingencies.","Assassins and shadow guards were the personal power he cultivated for himself, his mother, and his sister—forces thoroughly loyal to him, more trustworthy than the Crown Prince’s six guards appointed by the emperor.]","“So the former Crown Prince’s assassins and shadow guards are now in Gan Tang’s hands?”","If so, even with limited numbers—unable to fight in open battles—they could still pull off assassinations.","Precision strikes, if executed well, could produce unexpected results.","[Exactly. Though due to distance and other factors, I can’t fully monitor Gan Tang’s deployment yet. But from her recent actions, Gan Sheng is in for serious trouble.]"]},{"number":462,"title":"Chapter 462: Authenticity of News","paragraphs":["Gan Tang now hated not only Gan Sheng but also the father emperor who had caused the deaths of her elder brother and mother. She hated the Gan family clan, for they all knew what the former emperor had done. Not one of them had stepped forward to help the former crown prince, nor even spoken a single word in his defense.","What was worse, later her mother, the empress, also died, as did her elder brother’s only heir, her nephew—still so young—who perished as well.","Yue Fuguang’s heart stirred. Good, let her hate the Gan dynasty. As long as Gan Tang stopped trying to defend the imperial rule of her own family, with the forces she had at her command, she could do anything.","Little did Yue Fuguang know that her guess would soon come true. Just as she resumed her journey, Wei Shouyi, who had ridden posthaste to the border military camp, encountered a strange incident at the very outset.","Swish!","“Protect the General!”","When Wei Shouyi and his party were less than a hundred meters from the camp, a stray arrow suddenly shot out from an oblique direction.","Whoever had launched the sneak attack—whether too skilled or too careless—the arrow was aimed at Wei Shouyi, but the arrowhead ultimately struck the ground three meters in front of his horse.","“General, are you all right?” The guards quickly surrounded Wei Shouyi.","One of them shouted toward the camp ahead: “Brothers inside, we’re on the same side. This is General Wei Shouyi, newly appointed by His Majesty as General of the Southern Expedition. Please do not shoot again!”","“General Wei? Please wait a moment. We’ll report this to General Xu immediately.”","While the negotiations began, the guards on this side were not idle either.","One man dismounted and pulled the arrow out of the ground. It had been too dark to see clearly earlier, but now holding the shaft in his hand, he noticed something tied to the tail feathers.","“Bring it here for me to see.” Wei Shouyi sat upright on his horse, reaching out to take the arrow.","Seven days ago, after successfully escorting the Junior Preceptor back to the capital, he had been appointed General of the Southern Expedition by the emperor that very day. After seven days of hard riding, he had finally arrived tonight.","He had not expected to be greeted by a sneak arrow attack the moment he arrived. Wei Shouyi’s temper flared. Why would the people inside fire a sneak arrow at him, a general appointed by the emperor?","Had something gone wrong inside? Or had the gate guards been infiltrated by the enemy? No, that couldn’t be. With the identity of the person inside, betraying Dayan was impossible!","Could it be... All sorts of conspiracies raced through Wei Shouyi’s mind. Before he could erupt in anger, he noticed the suspicious look of the arrow.","Undoing the cloth strip wrapped around the note, Wei Shouyi took one look and realized he had wronged his comrades in the Southern Expedition camp.","Before he could examine it more closely, he saw the side gate of the camp swing open, and a procession of over a hundred men came out. Leading them was someone Wei Shouyi recognized: Xu Shu, the Supreme Commander of the Southwestern Route Army, the empress’s own brother, and the crown prince’s maternal uncle.","“Brother Wei, I failed to welcome you from afar. Please forgive me!” Xu Shu, around forty years old, wore full armor, a sturdy build, a guo-shaped face with a short beard, healthy bronze skin, and small but spirited eyes. His laugh was hearty and unrestrained. As a fellow Dayan military commander, he was an old acquaintance of Wei Shouyi.","“Your subordinate Wei Shouyi pays respects to General Xu.”","Wei Shouyi dismounted to greet him. Whether due to rank or Xu Shu’s status as the crown prince’s maternal uncle, Wei Shouyi had no choice but to treat the man with careful respect.","“We’re like brothers. No need for such formality.” Xu Shu warmly took Wei Shouyi’s arm. “Brother Wei, you’ve had a long journey. Please, come inside!”","“You first, General!” The two exchanged courtesies and entered the camp together.","“Brother Wei, are you saying this thing was deliberately shot to you just now?”","Once inside Xu Shu’s operations tent, Wei Shouyi gestured for Xu Shu to dismiss the attendants. Without even pausing for tea, he urgently pulled out the note he had just obtained.","He might not trust others, but Xu Shu had been certified by the Junior Preceptor as a loyal minister of Dayan, so Wei Shouyi felt completely at ease showing him the note.","“General, you’re right. Just as I was about a hundred zhang from the camp, a shot came from an oblique direction. I initially thought it was a warning arrow from the camp guards, but then I saw this.”","He pointed at the note. “I only glanced at it briefly and don’t yet know if the information is true. I ask General to enlighten me.”","Over the past month, Xu Shu had clashed several times with the Southern Yue army. Thanks to sharp weapons and advanced equipment—especially the unstoppable gunpowder—the Dayan forces had won every battle. Morale was now at its peak. Since Xu Shu commanded the front lines and the secret intelligence agency gathered information from behind Southern Yue lines for his reference, Wei Shouyi felt Xu Shu should know some insider details he didn’t.","Xu Shu stared at the information listed on the note and frowned. After hearing Wei Shouyi’s words, he thought for a moment. “To be honest with you, Brother Wei, there is some information on this note that I can confirm as truth with ninety percent certainty, but there are a few items I cannot be sure of.”","Wei Shouyi clasped his hands. “Please, General, speak plainly. Your humble subordinate may be unworthy, but perhaps I can think this through with you.”","“The Southern Yue army’s deployment and their defenses on the eastern and western flanks are largely consistent with what our scouts have uncovered.","As for the central army, their defenses are tight, and we haven’t been able to probe the true situation inside yet.","Xu Shu first acknowledged the two points before continuing, “As for the issue of the Southern Yue emperor’s failing health, the information my men brought back says that the Southern Yue court has canceled court sessions twice recently. As for the reason, some say the emperor is gravely ill, while others claim he’s too busy indulging in women to get out of bed.”","Xu Shu shook his head. “The Southern Yue Imperial Medical Institute is completely calm. The few skilled physicians who attend to the emperor’s pulse have been coming and going at their usual hours these past few days. To outsiders, it seems there’s nothing seriously wrong with the emperor’s health.”","He looked up and saw that Wei Shouyi was more inclined to believe the information in the note. He couldn’t help but ask, “General Wei, do you know who sent you that message?”","In truth, Wei Shouyi had been pondering this question ever since he received the note.","The first possibility he ruled out was officials from Da Yan. Whether it was the emperor’s spies or agents from the Secret Intelligence Department, their reports would either go directly to the throne or to the highest commander of the Southwestern Army, Xu Shu.","They wouldn’t resort to an anonymous arrow to deliver the message into his hands personally.","After all, he had only just arrived here and hadn’t even entered the military camp. How many people even recognized him?","“To be honest with you, General, I’ve been wondering the same thing, but...” Wei Shouyi shook his head helplessly. “I truly can’t imagine who would be so kind as to send me such earthshaking news.”","After all, if Gan Sheng’s cancellation of court sessions truly stemmed from health problems, it would be a golden opportunity for them to exploit.","At a time like this, with the Southern Yue court unstable and infighting over the throne inevitable, the Da Yan army might be able to seize the moment and take Southern Yue with minimal losses.","Seeing that Wei Shouyi’s expression didn’t seem feigned, Xu Shu pressed on, still unwilling to give up, “Brother Wei, don’t you have even one or two suspects in mind?”","If the source of this intelligence couldn’t be confirmed, Xu Shu wouldn’t be able to judge the truthfulness of some of its contents, and that would certainly affect his decisions going forward. With the source unknown, who would dare trust it easily?","Who could say for sure that this information wasn’t deliberately released by the enemy to mislead them?"]},{"number":463,"title":"Chapter 463: Give him a dose of his own medicine","paragraphs":["\"If the other party deliberately gives nine true and one false piece of information, and they believe it, wouldn’t they be falling right into the trap?\"","\"Grand General, you see clearly. The only ones who could know such secret information are either the top brass of Nanyue or that one.\" He pointed toward the capital.","\"You mean His Majesty?\" Their emperor not only controlled the Secret Intelligence Department but also had two separate spy networks overseeing internal and external affairs.","Wei Shouyi shook his head. \"What I mean is our young master.\" In Wei Shouyi's eyes, that person was omniscient and omnipotent.","Thinking of this, his heart stirred, and he immediately smiled, saying, \"Grand General, I might have a way to help scout out the deployment of Nanyue’s central army.\"","\"Oh? Brother Wei, are you serious?\" Xu Shu paused in the middle of pouring him tea.","\"This time I came, the young master gave me a miraculous tool for reconnaissance. With it, we might give it a try!\" Though he said \"might try,\" Wei Shouyi's expression was full of confidence.","Drones. He had personally operated one. With them, why fear not knowing what tricks Nanyue’s army was up to!","After hearing Wei Shouyi's words, Xu Shu set down the kettle heavily, his eyes gleaming as he looked at Wei Shouyi. \"Brother, I’ve heard that you are highly favored by the young master. Today, I see the rumors are not false!\"","Right as Wei Shouyi took out the two system-produced drones that Yue Fuguang had given him before his departure, astonishing Xu Shu—the head of the campaign logistics—at the border of Dayan.","Yue Fuguang, whom Wei Shouyi believed to be all-knowing and all-powerful, had just finished her daily rain-making task.","\"System, did my rainfall range increase a bit more this time?\"","[Host, this time I detected a rainfall range of over 170 miles. At this rate of growth, it will soon break 200 miles!]","\"But system, have you considered that even if I break 200 miles, our current vehicle speed can’t keep up?\"","[Ah? You’re right!] The system thought about it and gave her a bad idea: [Host, how about flying over?]","It didn’t know what obsession its host had with flying, but her storage ring contained several types of flying tools.","There were pretentious Lotus-Step Boots, flashy flying skateboards, cool flying cars, ethereal flying boats, and more.","She was stingy when buying other things but lavish with flying tools. If flying swords weren’t too dangerous for mortals—prone to falling and dying—her host would definitely have bought one.","Even in martial arts, she could skip everything else, but she reluctantly bought the expensive lightweight skill, and the system was smug—it had accurately read this trait in its host and dared to set the price high.","Yue Fuguang: If you’re not Chinese, it’s hard to understand a Chinese person’s obsession with flight etched into their genes.","Yue Fuguang seriously considered the system’s suggestion. The idea seemed unreliable, but she felt a stirring inside. \"Flying over... that’s not impossible, huh!\"","But there was no rush. For now, the team was advancing at full speed, and she was spreading rain along the way, just barely enough.","\"By the way, regarding the war between Dayan and Nanyue, how are the other countries reacting?\"","On the surface, this war had started because of her. She wondered if they still dared to make a move against her again.","[The Eastern Yi are currently dealing with a plague at home and can’t spare the energy to care about other countries.","The Northern Li and Western Qiang were thinking of jumping in—whether to take a bite out of Nanyue or continue targeting you, both countries have that intention.","However, due to the deaths of Zhuang Xiu and Feng Wuhuan, the army is in a panic over you. In the courts, conflicts of interest have led them to start quarreling. At the very least, they’ll be too busy to focus here for a while.","Finally, there’s Nanzhao. As Nanyue’s ally, they’ve been secretly supplying weapons and medicine.]","\"Nanzhao? Aren’t they afraid of being dragged down by Nanyue? What’s their Empress thinking?\"","[The power structure in Nanzhao’s court is even more complex. Apart from her daughter Lan Xuan'er, each of the Empress’s other children is backed by various factions in Nanyue.","As these children grow up, the Empress’s control over Nanzhao has been slowly weakening over the past two years.]","The system rolled over in Yue Fuguang’s hand. [Now, with the severe drought and rising popular discontent, the Empress has already issued two self-critical edicts.","Nanzhao also participated in that attack back then. If she doesn’t support Gan Sheng, he might not be able to do anything to Dayan, but dealing with Nanzhao—he has plenty of ways.]","The two countries were too tightly bound, familiar with each other’s strengths and weaknesses. When it came to making a move, it would be swift and precise.","\"Does that mean, if Dayan takes down Nanyue, Nanzhao won’t be far from destruction?\"","[Pretty much. Once Dayan captures Nanyue, they can easily deal with Nanzhao in passing. Host, don’t forget: it’s already mid-May, and the floods in Nanzhao and Nanyue are almost due!]","\"Right, System, check when heavy rain will start in Nanyue. Let’s hope it doesn’t slow down Dayan’s army’s advance.\"","If they got stuck halfway through because of heavy rain, Dayan’s efforts would have been in vain.","[Master, I just saw Gan Tang send a letter to Wei Shouyi at the border camp.] The system switched topics quickly—it had been talking about rain just a moment ago, and now it veered off to the letter.","Yue Fuguang’s heart stirred, and she asked casually, \"Little Zhu, you mean Gan Tang sent a letter to Wei Shouyi? What kind of letter? Are they even that close?\"","[Master, it’s not that they’re close. It’s because Gan Tang wants to bring down Gan Sheng and Nanyue. She passed on news of Gan Sheng’s severe illness and some of Nanyue’s troop deployments to Wei Shouyi.]","Outside guarding Yue Fuguang, Shen Jian paused in his steps, silently standing in her courtyard, listening intently.","\"Gan Sheng is seriously ill? What’s this all about? The emperor never mentioned it!\"","[He fell ill after we left the capital. Besides, Gan Sheng hid the news well. Even the emperor might not know it yet!]","\"I remember Gan Sheng was still on the throne until the fall of Dayan in the fourteenth year of Yuankang, right? How is he so ill now?","Is this illness fatal?\"","[Dying? Why wouldn’t it kill him! Master, you don’t know yet. Gan Sheng isn’t ill; he’s been poisoned. Poisoned with the same ‘Red Elixir’ that killed the former Crown Prince. In principle, this poison has no antidote.","Those poisoned with it first suffer from a depletion of vital energy and blood, leaving them weak and bedridden. Then comes Gan Sheng’s current state: fever and coughing.","Because it continuously saps vital energy and blood, it’s hard to detect as poisoning. Instead, it seems like a bout of cold or flu that won’t heal due to weakness.]","\"So, the one who made a move on Gan Sheng is Gan Tang—an eye for an eye!\"","[Yes. She learned the truth during the autumn hunt and began planning. The Red Elixir is a slow poison. In its early stages, the poisoned person barely notices anything; it’s considered a fairly gentle toxin.","But in the later stages, once it erupts, there’s no saving them.]","\"Since he was poisoned with the Red Elixir, Gan Sheng should know it’s poisoning, not illness!\" The Crown Prince’s death back then was the emperor’s doing, but the Jiang family and Gan Sheng weren’t entirely innocent.","Especially in following the example of the former Empress’s death—those who carried out the emperor’s orders were the Jiang family.","[He sensed it as soon as the poison took effect. That’s why he didn’t use the imperial physicians—partly to lull outsiders into a false sense of security.]"]},{"number":464,"title":"Chapter 464: Inquiry","paragraphs":["On the other hand, those imperial physicians lacked the ability to cure a poison that was nearly impossible to remedy.","Ever since discovering he had been poisoned, Gan Sheng trusted no one except his personal eunuch. The Red Powder was a slow-acting toxin. He knew someone close to him must have been responsible. As for the mastermind behind it, his primary suspect was Gan Tang.","He suspected Gan Tang because the poison was \"Red Medicine\" — the same method they used to kill the late Crown Prince and the Empress?","Yes. Gan Tang had been secretly investigating that incident for the past two years, and Gan Sheng knew it. Now that he himself had fallen victim to the same poison, his suspicion naturally fell on Gan Tang first.","Master, once Gan Sheng's poison takes full effect, he will die within a month or two at most. This period is Dayan's best opportunity.","The only concern now is whether Wei Shouyi and Xu Shu will believe the message Gan Tang has sent.","I don't know much about Xu Shu, but Wei Shouyi, though he might seem rough around the edges, is actually meticulous. He will find a way to verify the truth of the message.","So let's stop worrying about that and focus on solving the current drought first.","Master, if Dayan really takes over Nanyue, won't you have to go and manage the floodwaters there?","Yue Fuguang was taken aback. That was true. Once the territory was taken, Nanyue would belong to Dayan. The rulers and ministers of Dayan could not ignore it, and she certainly could not either.","The first country to fall would set a precedent for how its people were treated. The others would be watching closely. If handled poorly, even if Dayan forcibly conquered all the nations, the goodwill of the people would be lost, and it would be impossible to piece them together into one unified state. Otherwise, her mission would remain unfulfilled.","Yue Fuguang sighed. In ancient times, there was Yu the Great who controlled the floods; now, there was she, Yue Fuguang, who would have to manage the water. If she ever told anyone about this, it would be something to boast about for a lifetime.","Let's wait until Dayan successfully takes Nanyue. Gan Sheng is not the type to resign himself to death. He must have some tricks up his sleeve. Keep an eye on things and don't let Gan Tang really get killed by his men.","For now, Gan Tang was still useful. Even if Yue Fuguang truly intended to kill Gan Sheng and destroy the Gan dynasty, she might still consider sparing Gan Tang's life after all.","Come to think of it, Gan Sheng's plan to have Yue Fuguang marry into Dayan seemed like a way to harm Gan Tang. But no one expected that this very identity might eventually save her life.","While Yue Fuguang wanted to preserve Gan Tang's life, Gan Sheng had no intention of letting her go.","Gan Sheng lay on his dragon bed, gazing blankly at the golden dragon patterns and the ten-thousand-longevity patterns on the apricot-yellow canopy above.","Ten-thousand-longevity—how ironic. He could not even live to see the age of twenty-eight.","Feeling his body growing weaker by the day, his life force ebbing away with every moment, Gan Sheng looked at the densely woven longevity patterns on the canopy. They pressed down on him now like the entire parched land and cracked riverbeds beyond the court.","He lay flat on his back, his neck sunk deep into the soft pillow, leaving only his head resting on the bright yellow silk like a dried-up, weightless fruit—or a candle flame flickering in the wind, ready to go out at any moment.","His eyelids were heavy, half-closed. The shadow of his lashes fell on his cheekbones, where a patch of grayish pallor had settled, the sallow complexion of someone who had not slept well.","Gan Sheng's gaze lacked focus, floating vaguely, piercing through the threads of the canopy, as if entangled by the intricate patterns, suspended in midair.","\"Jixiang... what time is it now?\"","His voice was hoarse, and even this brief question brought a faint, rattling sound from deep in his throat—like a wheeze from an old bellows. He then breathed with difficulty.","\"Your Majesty, it is just past the hour of Wei (around 1–3 PM),\" replied the eunuch named Jixiang respectfully, careful not to show any trace of worry or pity for the emperor's condition in his expression.","He had served this master for over a decade and understood his stubborn character well. Those of us who served at his side had no right to worry about or pity the master.","Jixiang glanced out the window. Another cloudless day. Because of the drought, what used to irritate him about the scorching sun now made him yearn for it, unable to see enough.","Every look at the sunlight felt like it might be his last.","\"Already past Wei hour,\" Gan Sheng said, his voice so soft it was almost inaudible unless one leaned close.","His breathing was shallow, his chest barely moving. Only occasionally, when a breeze seemed to stir outside the hall, would the tassels on the canopy sway lazily, scattering the afternoon light into fragments. Fine motes of dust danced in the narrow beam of light that slipped in, rising and falling without a sound.","This was a sight Gan Sheng had stared at for five or six days in a row.","No one knew how long passed—it could have been a few breaths, or the time it took to drink a few cups of tea—when Jixiang, hunched over and counting the intricate patterns on the carpet, heard His Majesty's voice again.","\"Go see if Li Jie and Fei Yongxing have arrived. And Eunuch Zhao...\" Zhao Quan'an was his most trusted man, and he had been away all this time seeking a cure for the poison. Gan Sheng still clung to hope.","\"Your Majesty, wait here. This servant will step outside and check.\"","He did not really need to check. If Prime Minister Li and the others had truly arrived, the young eunuchs outside would have announced them.","Since the emperor had ordered him to go, Jixiang was also eager to get some air outside.","To be honest, although Gan Sheng's authority had weakened, staying near a dying, listless emperor was still too oppressive.","When on duty, they had to be even more cautious than usual, lest a minor slip-up be blown out of proportion by the overly sensitive ruler.","Just yesterday, a young eunuch was dragged out and beaten to death for walking a little too loudly. His Majesty had ordered it.","No one dared to step forward and point out that they had always walked this way, including His Majesty himself, who had not left his bed for days.","As Jixiang's figure disappeared beyond the doorway, the great hall fell silent once more. When he was gently awakened by Jixiang's voice again, Gan Sheng felt as though he had slept. His body had regained a little strength.","\"Your Majesty, Prime Minister Li and the other officials are all waiting outside the hall.\"","\"Jixiang, help me up.\"","Jixiang gently propped Gan Sheng against a soft cushion. After a moment, once he felt his mind was clear enough, Gan Sheng said, \"Call them in.\"","Within moments, the sound of hurried footsteps came from outside the hall. Gan Sheng turned his head to look through the thin gauze hanging from the bed canopy and saw five officials led by Prime Minister Li file in.","They did not have time to wipe the sweat from their foreheads before they bowed and offered salutations to Gan Sheng.","\"Your humble servant Li Jie pays respects to Your Majesty.\"","\"Your humble servant Fei Yongxing pays respects to Your Majesty.\"","\"Your humble servant...\"","\"Rise, all of you,\" Gan Sheng said, trying not to let the weakness seep into his voice.","But his efforts were in vain. To everyone in attendance, it was clear that His Majesty's spirit was waning with each passing day.","Although the thin gauze obscured the emperor's complexion, the faint life force they sensed was unmistakable—it was the aura of one near death. Some involuntarily began to let small, private thoughts creep into their minds.","At this point, even Prime Minister Li had no idea that their emperor had been poisoned with \"Red Medicine.\" They only believed it was an illness caused by a cold.","\"Dai Ping'an, how goes that matter you were handling?\"","The man called Dai Ping'an was of medium build, dressed in a dark close-fitting garment, strikingly different from the officials in their court robes.","He was the head of the Defense Bureau, elevated to his post by Gan Sheng himself. His duties included overseeing the officials, gathering intelligence, and planting spies."]},{"number":465,"title":"Chapter 465: The Fall of the Acropolis","paragraphs":["To put it plainly, he was the one who did the dirty work for Gan Sheng. This organization originated in the previous emperor's era, founded by the late emperor himself, and later passed down to Gan Sheng.","It could be said that the four ministers present both hated and feared Dai Ping'an.","Dai Ping'an stepped forward and bowed, saying, \"Your Majesty, my people have successfully entered the capital city. To get close to the princess, however, will take some effort.\"","That legitimate princess was no pushover. She was already wary of everyone in the envoy delegation, let alone those who had just arrived from Nanyue. They couldn't get anywhere near her.","Though the royal siblings had not yet openly fallen out, they were secretly scheming against each other, each trying to destroy the other.","It could be said that Dai Ping'an, as Gan Sheng's true confidant, was the only one present who knew he had been poisoned.","\"I want to hear of her death within a month!\" Gan Sheng knew that if Zhao Quan'an couldn't find the antidote, he probably wouldn't last more than two months. So before dying, he was determined to drag Gan Tang, the root cause of all this, down with him.","The bed curtains hung low, and curls of aloeswood smoke rose from the golden censer, dissipating before reaching the apricot-yellow brocade.","Hearing the emperor's murderous resolve, those who knew of the plan lowered their heads even further. Though the sun blazed brightly outside, a chill pervaded the room, settling on the shoulders of their crimson and purple court robes.","After these words, a long silence followed—so long that their hearts began to grow numb. Dai Yongxing lifted his eyes slightly, catching sight of a withered hand beneath the curtain, fingers waxy pale, resting on the bright yellow satin coverlet.","Suddenly, that hand moved. \"Dai Aiqing...\" a voice came from behind the curtain, dry as wind through withered reeds. \"Where is Gan Tang's dowry procession now?\"","Dai Yongxing bowed and replied, \"Your Majesty, the princess's dowry has entered Dayan and will reach the capital in about seven or eight days.\"","\"Prime Minister Li, how are the peace talks going? Has Dayan agreed to withdraw its troops?\" Even at this point, Gan Sheng still thought Dayan's attack on Nanyue was merely retaliation—a show put on for the world, or rather for Yue Fuguang.","No one in Nanyue had ever imagined that Dayan's campaign was aimed at swallowing the entire country. It had been so long since the six kingdoms split that they had forgotten they were once of the same root.","\"Your Majesty, the peace talks are not going well. However, the auspicious wedding date for the princess and Dayan's Sixth Prince has been set—one month from now.\"","Prime Minister Li and the other ministers hadn't understood why their sovereign had initially insisted on the Fifth Prince as a marriage partner, only to suddenly change his mind within a month, agreeing to the Sixth Prince and ordering the Bureau of Astronomy to pick the nearest auspicious date for a quick wedding.","Now, seeing the emperor's failing health, it became clear: he knew his time was short and wanted to marry off the princess, the one capable of returning to fight for the throne!","Among the emperor's many children, not one was of age. If a succession struggle broke out, it was uncertain whom the court would support.","Those loyal to the nation would of course back the adult legitimate princess, or even the imperial uncle, for the throne. But there were also ambitious types eager to seize power through a young ruler, naturally preferring a child emperor or empress.","Li Jie's peripheral vision swept over the eldest prince, who stood to one side in silence. A child—easy to control!","As for whom Li Jie himself hoped would ascend... only he knew best.","\"Prime Minister Li, I have drafted the edict appointing the eldest prince as the Crown Prince. Review it, and if there's no issue, announce it to the realm.\"","\"Appoint the Crown Prince?\" The ministers exchanged startled glances. \"Yes, Your Majesty!\"","Li Jie respectfully took the imperial decree handed over by Jixiang. The seal and signature were all in place.","\"Your son thanks you, Father!\" Gan Minghao, tears in his eyes, performed the kowtow to Gan Sheng, his small frame trembling uncontrollably.","\"Haor, learn well from Prime Minister Li and the other officials. They are all pillars of Nanyue.\"","\"Yes, Father. Your son will remember!\"","Gan Sheng then turned to another man. \"Wu Jiang, the army...\" Having spoken even this much, Gan Sheng clearly felt his strength failing. He couldn't finish his sentence before gasping for breath.","Though the emperor's words were incomplete, Wu Jiang, the Minister of War, understood what he most wanted to know.","He bowed and replied, \"Your Majesty, our 80,000 troops engaged the Dayan army outside Weicheng yesterday. We... suffered losses of over 20,000 men, and Weicheng... Weicheng has also been taken.\"","\"Weicheng... taken!\"","Pfft! Gan Sheng coughed up a mouthful of blood, staining the embroidered satin coverlet.","\"Your Majesty!\" Jixiang hurriedly caught the tottering emperor. \"Your Majesty, you must take care of your Dragon Body!\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty! Even if Weicheng is lost, we can take it back. You must not harm yourself over this!\"","\"Father, when I grow up, I will surely conquer vast lands for Nanyue!\"","Gan Sheng waved his hand weakly, furious at the loss of territory and even more so that no one had informed him voluntarily. He wasn't dead yet, yet these ministers had already stopped taking him seriously as a sovereign!","\"Crown Prince, what do you think of Prince Cheng's defeat and loss of territory?\"","Gan Minghao, suddenly addressed as Crown Prince, froze in surprise for a moment. Not just him—no one had expected the emperor to set the title so hastily.","Gan Minghao couldn't help but tremble. Less than twelve years old, he hadn't yet learned to hold his nerve like the old foxes in court.","He knew his father wasn't asking about his view of the military defeat and loss of land, but about the delayed reporting to the sovereign itself—what did he, the future heir, think?","On the surface, not informing the emperor seemed to spare a seriously ill ruler from worsening his condition, but in reality, even the underage Gan Minghao understood a thing or two.","Who commanded those 80,000 troops?","The late emperor's youngest brother, the emperor's own uncle, Prince Cheng Gan Chengyuan, now thirty-eight years old—and secretly supported by many in court to succeed the throne.","His defeat and loss of a city invited criticism, but no one dared reprimand him harshly, fearing he might use it as an excuse to start an armed rebellion.","Now a Crown Prince, Gan Minghao was even more wary of this royal uncle who might vie for the throne. Faced with his father's question, he wanted to say, \"Outright or sideways, Prince Cheng's defeat deserves death.\" But thinking it was one thing; forming words was another.","\"Father, your son believes that victory and defeat are common in warfare. As the officials say, losing a city is a small matter. As long as our court and our people stand united, I am confident that under your leadership, we can soon retake Weicheng.","What matters most is that you take care of your health. Do not let this harm you. Your son awaits the day you lead us to strike back—and maybe even take all of Dayan!\"","Whether Gan Sheng was satisfied with the new Crown Prince's answer remained unclear. He turned his head again to Wu Jiang. \"Didn't Uncle's last report claim his deployment was foolproof? How did we lose Weicheng in just a few days?\"","He had reviewed the matter himself. Gan Chengyuan's defensive arrangements for Weicheng and its surroundings seemed largely sound. How could a single battle cost them the city?"]},{"number":466,"title":"Chapter 466: Since you won't give it to me, I'll just take it myself","paragraphs":["Was the Dayan army too strong, or was his Nanyue simply too weak? It couldn't be that Gan Chengyuan was holding back, could it?","Didn't he want to be emperor? Surely he wouldn't just hand over his own territory.","Wu Jiang's face turned grim for a moment. He glanced at Fei Yongxing before saying, \"Prince Cheng's war report didn't go into detail, but according to what our spies have reported, Dayan has a very clear understanding of the deployment of our forces everywhere.","Therefore, Your Majesty, I suspect... there may be a problem with the defenses.\"","They were the defenders in Nanyue. When Dayan attacked, the allocation of troops along various routes was clearly targeted.","Although he hadn't directly said someone inside was compromised, Gan Sheng, who was the most adept at playing political games, could still read between the lines.","\"Minister Wu means... there's a traitor inside our court?\" Gan Sheng's words came out in fragments, his spirit clearly flagging after that mouthful of blood.","\"Your Majesty, I... I'm merely speculating that our military deployment was leaked. Whether or not it was an insiders' problem is still hard to say.\"","As he finished speaking, he cast a sidelong glance at Dai Ping'an, who stood cold and erect, silent as a clay or wooden statue.","Catching spies and investigating court colleagues—that wasn't the responsibility of the Minister of War.","This kind of thankless, offending task was best left to Dai the Infernal.","Gan Sheng waved his hand at them. \"I understand. All of you may withdraw.\"","\"Minister Dai, stay a moment.\"","\"We await Your Majesty's leave.\"","\"Father, please take care of your health. I take my leave.\"","After everyone had left, Gan Sheng said to Dai Ping'an, \"Ping'an, come closer.\"","Jixiang automatically withdrew to the palace gates. He had absolutely no desire to know what the emperor and his top enforcer were discussing. In this palace, the more you knew, the faster you died.","Gan Sheng stared at the canopy above his bed, the fading footsteps of Dai Ping'an and Jixiang echoing in his ears. Their footsteps were light and distant, as far away as the clouds in the sky, yet also near—so near he could hear exactly where each step fell.","The hall fell silent again. The mingled scent of aloeswood incense and medicinal herbs seemed to seep into Gan Sheng's frail body. It was a decaying, cloyingly sweet aroma that slowly, bit by bit, rotted away his very last shred of strength.","And the sister he was scheming and plotting to kill was, at that moment, also concerned about his 'illness' and his life.","\"Your Highness, Shen Liu reports... that one has now missed court for five consecutive days.\" Gan Tang's chief maid, Nan Feng, leaned in and whispered at her ear.","Gan Tang paused as she wrote. Outside the study, the sun shone brightly; but thanks to Junior Preceptor Yue's three consecutive rainfalls, the capital city was not suffering drought.","The trees outside her study were lush green, clusters of small flowers blooming cheerfully. The afternoon sunlight slanted through the tree shadows onto her windowsill, casting patches of deep and light shades of green—the color that life should be.","Gan Tang withdrew her gaze. \"Are you certain he can no longer get out of bed?\" Five days ago, the news she had received was that Gan Sheng had not held court for two days due to illness.","Now, after missing court for several consecutive days, while the Nanyue army was still fighting Dayan on the front lines—she could well imagine the chaos in the Nanyue court.","And then there was her good uncle, Gan Chengyuan. During her father's generation's struggle for the throne, he had been too young to participate. By the time their generation came around, he had been kept firmly in check by their father as well, ambitious but powerless.","Now that Gan Sheng was gravely ill, no one knew what kind of mess this uncle, sent to the front lines to fight, might make of the war.","\"What is the reaction of the ministers in the court?\" Gan Tang put down her brush completely, leaned back, and settled into a comfortable position.","Naturally, Nan Feng understood what the princess meant by 'reaction.' She chose her words carefully and said softly, \"Prime Minister Li and several other officials, including the Crown Prince and that Dai the Infernal, were summoned into the palace three days ago.","Moreover, the Crown Prince has been officially appointed as the Crown Prince!\"","\"Crown Prince?\" Gan Tang let out a derisive laugh. Her dear elder brother—neither earlier nor later—had chosen precisely this moment to appoint the heir!","\"He knows he doesn't have much time left!\"","Nan Feng nodded in agreement, glanced out the window, and continued, \"Our people couldn't get close to the emperor's bedchamber, but according to those stationed outside, they were inside for nearly half an hour.\"","\"Half an hour? Being able to keep the ministers talking for that long—it seems my dear brother's health isn't so bad after all!\" A sarcastic smile curled at the corner of Gan Tang's mouth. She hadn't been ruthless enough, always trying to take it slow, giving him too little of the medicine. That gave him the chance to send her off as a peace bride to Dayan.","\"The Ink Shadow Guard discovered that after seeing His Majesty, Prime Minister Li and the others secretly met with several officials separately after leaving the palace. The details of their conversations are unknown, but it's certain they were probing.","Testing their stance toward the new Crown Prince's succession, and testing how much they knew about the deployment of Weicheng's defenses.\"","Hearing that the Nanyue court was investigating the leak of defensive information from Weicheng, Gan Tang chuckled softly. \"So, the information we sent has taken effect!\"","It wasn't a question. From these fragmented details, she could already deduce that Nanyue had definitely been defeated—had even lost Weicheng.","\"Your Highness means Nanyue has lost? But... this is Prince Cheng!\" Prince Cheng was also considered a 'famous general' in Nanyue. He had only led troops three times before, but each time had been a resounding victory, which was why the emperor had appointed him as the commanding general this time.","\"I expect this news will soon spread to the Dayan court. By then, with Dayan's great victory, Emperor Mingxi certainly won't keep it hidden from his subjects.\"","Gan Tang was certain. This was news that would boost military morale and win people's hearts. Even she would publicize it heavily; failing to exaggerate the victory would be considered restraint.","Then she thought about Nan Feng's mention of the ministers' probing attitudes toward the new Crown Prince. \"What's the situation with Prince Cheng?\"","Gan Tang didn't believe that the information she could uncover, Prince Cheng, who had always coveted the throne, wouldn't know that Gan Sheng was dying, and had even chosen his successor before his death.","She even suspected that Prince Cheng's failure at Weicheng might also be part of some ulterior motive.","Those 80,000 troops at Weicheng were all his personal loyalists. Even if Dayan's forces attacked directly, with the defense map she had provided, this would have taken at least ten days to a fortnight to crack. But Weicheng fell in just four or five days... that was suspicious.","Her slender fingers tapped lightly one by one on the desk, producing a steady thumping sound. After a long silence, she said, \"Prince Cheng is conserving his strength!\"","If Gan Sheng were still the same powerful, vigorous ruler he once was, even if Prince Cheng didn't fight to the death, he would have held out longer.","But with Gan Sheng's life hanging by a thread and it being clear he wouldn't pass the throne to him, Prince Cheng had likely chosen to preserve his forces after learning the news, to help secure his own ascension.","Since you won't give it to me, then I'll take it myself!","\"Nan Feng, tell the Ink Shadow Guard to keep a close watch on the court's movements, especially Prince Cheng. I suspect he will use the defeat as a pretext to request permission to return to the capital and plead guilty!\"","While Nanyue was engaged in a hot war with Dayan, and the Nanyue court was in turmoil over the succession, Yue Fuguang's carriage had already traveled from Quanzhou to Yunzhou, through Yingzhou and Xuzhou, all the way to Xinzhou.","[Master, with your current power, you can now send rain over an area of over two hundred li with a single spell. Do you really still need to travel with these people? Isn't this just a waste of time!]"]},{"number":467,"title":"Chapter 467: Fly Over","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang teased the two black-and-white pandas, now much larger, with fresh bamboo shoots. Both of them, anxious, let out dog-like whines and clung to her legs, whimpering, until she reluctantly gave each a pile of tender shoots.","Of course, classic cornbread and red apples couldn't be missed, as they were staples in the cubs' diet. Yue Fuguang had been raising them just like the Flower and Leaf Sisters did.","Of course, the whole crowd outside the carriage had heard the system's words. Their hearts tightened at once, afraid that the Grand Preceptor would actually listen to the divine artifact and leave them behind to go ahead alone. They wouldn’t be able to catch up even if they ran their legs off.","Only Feng Tang and Shen Jian truly knew their limits!","\"Little Zhu, are you saying I should fly all the way there myself?\"","[Otherwise? Master, you can already fly—why waste time with these people?]","[Master, the drought won't wait!]","The system's words didn't move Yue Fuguang much, but they rendered the entire crowd outside the carriage speechless.","They desperately wanted to say they could afford to wait, but no matter how many times they opened their mouths, the words refused to come out. The Grand Preceptor hadn’t mentioned anything yet, and who would dare defy her authority?","Just as that thought crossed their minds, Yue Fuguang’s voice rang out loud and clear, \"Stop the carriage. Shen Jian, Feng Tang, He Jin, Dai Yuxing—come over here.\"","The four exchanged glances and hurried forward, already racking their brains for the best way to persuade her.","\"Your Excellency!\" They bowed in salute and took the chance to sneak a look at Yue Fuguang’s expression.","\"I have something to tell you.\" She swept her gaze across them, noticing how worn out everyone in the group looked, even herself, compared to when they left the capital.","\"Recently, my cultivation has progressed to the point where my rain-summoning range already exceeds our fastest daily travel speed. So, I’ve decided to go on ahead. You all will continue following the planned route and pace.\"","\"Your Excellency! If you leave us behind, your personal safety may not be a concern, but who will take care of all the trivial matters along the way?\"","It was impossible to guarantee they’d encounter no unexpected trouble on the road, and the person before them hated dealing with mundane chores the most.","Feng Tang’s remark hit Yue Fuguang right where it hurt—her lazy, easygoing nature.","How could wasting time on pointless socializing with local officials compare to eating, sleeping, and playing with her adorable pets?","Ah, speaking of which—she still had a whole carriage full of fluffy companions. She couldn’t just leave and let the little ones stay behind. Those clingy little babies would just raise a ruckus.","Treading Without Trace could carry the little foxes flying, but the now noticeably hefty panda cubs, Jiaotang and Nai Cha, were far too heavy to manage.","\"Little Zhu, get me a flying carriage!\"","By flying carriage, she naturally meant a classical cultivator-style one, not some sleek sci-fi interstellar vehicle—a thing of ethereal elegance, brimming with visual charm and full functionality, complete with two flying horses. The only drawback was the price: it was brutally expensive.","When the system heard Yue Fuguang wanted to make a purchase, it practically bounced with joy. The dazzling, shimmering bead vanished instantly from her hands.","The system moved fast, as if afraid she’d change her mind, quickly deducting 88,888 from her six-figure total points balance.","[Master, the carriage is ready. How many mortals are you taking with you?]","Shen Jian and Feng Tang had naturally heard the words \"flying carriage.\" At the divine artifact’s question, they all knowingly stole glances at Yue Fuguang.","A flying carriage, as the name implied, was a carriage that flew!","They wanted to go. The longing was practically written all over their faces. Even those not called over quietly edged closer to her carriage.","Yu Huaixian even hurried over with a kettle of hot water, offering to refill her flask—as if she really needed that!","\"Feng Tang has a point, so I have prepared a carriage.\" Her eyes swept over each of them, one by one. \"I will pick three of you to come with me.\"","\"Your Excellency, you know me. I may not be talented, but I’m excellent at handling all kinds of business and enjoy reasoning with subordinates. And if someone just won’t listen to reason, I’m also not half bad with my fists.\"","Feng Tang was quick off the mark. The moment Yue Fuguang finished speaking, he stepped forward to nominate himself on the spot.","Shen Jian, Dai Yuxing, and He Jin badly wanted to roll their eyes. Weren't they all supposed to be trying to persuade the Grand Preceptor to stay?","Admittedly, they hadn’t discussed it openly, but hadn’t that silent glance they exchanged said it all?","Had they been the only three with that thought?","Shen Jian, Dai Yuxing, and He Jin were either military men or from the martial arts world—practical, straightforward, lacking Feng Tang’s clever maneuvering.","Frustration were all over their faces. Feng Tang was a traitor among them! Not a single word of persuasion fell from his lips, yet he was abandoning everyone and running off with the Grand Preceptor at lightning speed!","Feng Tang: These three are still too young!","Did they really think they could change the Grand Preceptor’s mind once she’d set it?","Since persuasion was hopeless, finding a way to follow her was the smartest choice.","\"Your Excellency, as your personal guard captain, I must accompany you no matter what.\" Seeing it had come to this, He Jin quickly changed loyalties and vied for a spot.","Hadn’t she only said she’d take three? If they didn’t act fast, they wouldn’t even get a sip of soup!","Ah, Shen Jian was thoroughly exasperated. Traitors, every single one!","\"Your Excellency, I—\"","\"Your Excellency, this general—\"","\"General Shen, the troops still need your command. You have great skill and a heavy responsibility. The group can’t do without you here!\" Yue Fuguang slapped a big hat on him that directly shut down any further self-recommendation.","Shen Jian: I knew it would be just like this!","Ever since that time the divine artifact spilled about his background story, the Grand Preceptor had looked at him differently. He desperately wanted to stress—he was not a scumbag, not a philanderer!","Yue Fuguang turned to Dai Yuxing. \"Yuxing, He Jin is coming with me. As deputy commander of the guard, you also have an important role!\"","\"Sister! Me, pick me!\" Yu Huaixian came running back, still holding his kettle.","\"Alright, this time we’ll take He Jin, Feng Tang, and Cousin Xian.\" She cast a look at the disappointed faces around her. \"Next time, I’ll take someone else.\"","Not everyone got a chance this time, but every single one of them could hope to be the lucky one chosen later.","Yes, the lucky one!","In full view of them all, their all-powerful Grand Preceptor snapped her fingers at empty sky. The clouds above began to churn violently.","A tiny black dot appeared at the end of the cloud sea, at first no more than a moving glint of silver at the horizon.","As it drew closer, the crowd made it out to be a carriage. Two horses, all pure white, with manes and tails shimmering like pale blue moonlight, pulled it.","They galloped through the void. Their hooves didn’t stir up clouds but, instead, patches of starlit fluorescence—as if they had crushed the Milky Way underfoot, as if each step fell on the late night’s deepest dew.","Graceful white wings, smooth as snow, unfurled on each side, stirring no audible wind as they flapped, just casting faint, fleeting trails of iridescent light in their wake.","The crowd was utterly stunned by the sight of those horses, mouths wide open without making a sound.","Yu Huaixian’s heart thumped like drumbeats inside his chest. His sister truly was an immortal descended from heaven.","Could this magnificent vehicle be the one she had used as a means of transport all back in the celestial realms?","Heads tilted up, mouths gaping, the crowd turned their gaze to the carriage behind those white horses. Its intricacy and elegance surpassed anything of mortal craftsmanship.","Yu Huaixian thought to himself: mighty indeed was his little sister, worthy of being an immortal hero turned divine envoy."]},{"number":468,"title":"Chapter 468: Racing Cars","paragraphs":["Its body was crafted from translucent jade and pale emerald wood of an unknown material. The carriage curtains were made of moon-white gossamer silk as thin as cicada wings, embroidered with the pattern of the Big Dipper. As the carriage moved, the stars actually rotated slowly.","Only Yue Fuguang knew that those weren't flowing stars—they were burning spirit stones to supply the carriage's flight.","Tiny golden bells hung from the four corners of the carriage roof, emitting clear, melodious chimes when the wind passed, occasionally shaking down a scattering of fine starlight.","The carriage was surrounded by faint clouds, but they weren't ordinary white clouds. They shimmered with a rainbow luster like mother-of-pearl, as if the rosy dawn and sunset had been gathered together to weave a curtain.","Among the clouds, faint spiritual birds would occasionally appear and disappear, their tail feathers trailing long ribbons of light as they circled the carriage three times before vanishing into the depths of the cloud sea.","The most exquisite touch was the faint trail of light left in the clouds after the carriage passed, like someone using moonlight to draw a shallow mark across the blue sky that lingered long.","Yue Fuguang: Who needs exhaust fumes anyway!","Within that lingering light, the faint shadow of a lotus flower would occasionally flash, appearing for an instant before vanishing again—as if reminding the mortals gazing up from below that a celestial being had indeed just passed.","The crowd was stirred with excitement, thinking how fortunate anyone would be to ride in such an immortal's chariot!","They stared at He Jin, Feng Tang, and Yu Huaixian with envious, jealous eyes, wishing they could drag them down and take their place.","Yue Fuguang's own astonishment was no less than theirs.","This was the cheapest flying carriage she had selected from the system shop, boasting only basic defensive power along with its good looks and flight capability.","Even so, its original price was 288,000, so despite liking it, she had never bought it. She only kept it in her shopping cart, occasionally browsing it. If not for today's sale, she wouldn't have placed the order.","Needless to say, there was a vast gap between the system's introduction and animated images and the real thing.","If she had known the flying carriage would be so dazzling and elaborate, she would have long ago... put it in her cart and looked at it three times a day!","Cuizhu and Shen Chunying helped the caramel, milk tea, and three little foxes onto the carriage. Yue Fuguang cleared her throat softly, waking everyone from their daze.","“Alright, the carriage is here. Time for us to depart.” Before stepping onto the carriage, she turned to Shen Jian. “General Shen, I leave the troops to you.”","“Rest assured, Your Excellency. This general will not fail you!”","Shen Jian watched the carriage soar into the sky, tears of longing flowing from the corners of his eyes.","Inside the flying carriage sat Yue Fuguang and He Jin, while Feng Tang and Yu Huaixian acted as charioteers, though the carriage needed no guidance from them.","As the carriage skimmed over the clouds, Yue Fuguang lifted the gossamer curtain.","From above, she saw the vast Green Mulberry Plains stretching hundreds of miles, dotted with hills of varying heights.","It was a time of drought. Though the land was no longer cracked into countless dry fissures like the ugly scars she had seen before, thanks to the rain she had brought last time, a month had passed, and the seedlings had begun to wilt. Inch-long sprouts lay prostrate on the dry, sun-bleached soil, and even the wind was scorching hot.","Perhaps because the entire territory was arid, the water evaporated much faster than usual.","The rainfall she had delivered last time should have sustained the land for nearly two months, yet after only a month, widespread signs of severe water shortage appeared.","She could see the farmers below, bucket by bucket, drawing water from the few remaining ponds and ditches to irrigate their fields. “Just in time,” she murmured.","Had she delayed a few more days, the seedlings would have been beyond saving unless she sent spiritual rain. The manual watering below was clearly insufficient, a drop in the bucket.","Yue Fuguang, trying to conserve energy, had only added a tiny amount of enhancement to the rainfall last time, just enough to ensure crops grew robustly.","He Jin, standing at her side, grasped her sword and looked down. “The Dayan Kingdom has Your Excellency. That is Dayan's blessing and the people's blessing.” Her eyes sparkled as she gazed at Yue Fuguang, her tone as reverent as ever.","Yue Fuguang brushed off the compliment with a smile, instead pointing below with interest. “He Jin, isn't that the Sword Mountain where the Seven Swords Manor is located?”","The Sword Mountain was easy to recognize: its hundred-mile-long range resembled a giant sword, and the Seven Swords Manor was said to be built at the sword's hilt, like a gem set into it.","“Your Excellency, we are indeed approaching the Seven Swords Manor ahead,” He Jin replied, excitement creeping into her voice despite the distance remaining.","Seeing her expression, Yue Fuguang teased, “I know you're eager, but you don't need to rush. After we finish our work here, we’ll drop by your home for a visit.”","“You mentioned once that Seven Swords Manor is known for its pheasants and colorful mushrooms. Sounds like we're in for a treat today.”","In truth, she had never gone without these delicacies each season; He Qisha always personally delivered them to her mansion.","Today, she was arriving in such a grand carriage to pay a high-profile visit, hoping to boost He Qisha's standing. According to the system, the You Tan, Tian Xing Tower, and Pan Shan factions were causing trouble again.","A month ago, when she was still in Yizhou, she heard he had survived an assassination attempt by You Tan agents.","After all, Seven Swords Manor bore her name. She couldn't stand idly by.","“If my father knew Your Excellency was visiting today, he would be overjoyed,” He Jin said, thinking of her father He Qisha with a smile.","He could be counted among Your Excellency's most devout followers, burning incense for her three times a day. Her statue had been carved from an exquisite piece of jade he hoarded for years, by Master Cai.","She had seen it once. It wasn't just similar—it was strikingly lifelike, capturing the essence of Your Excellency as she stood on the carriage shaft, gazing down upon the world.","Yue Fuguang stood on the carriage shaft, her head slightly raised, her wide sleeves flapping loudly in the high-altitude wind.","Her expression was calm. She raised her hand slightly, her fingertips forming a complex hand seal, a spiritual light gathering into a pattern the others couldn't comprehend.","This was the first time the three of them had witnessed Your Excellency's full process of summoning clouds and rain.","“Go.”","A green light shot from her fingertips, straight into the sky.","Moments later, faint thunder rumbled from the horizon.","Yu Huaixian, sitting at the back of the carriage, leaned out to look down but was yanked back by Feng Tang. “Be careful, boy, or you'll fall off.”","[Master, why are you using hand seals this time?] Since Your Excellency's power had grown, over the past month, she had progressed from summoning clouds and rain with a wave to voice control; hand seals were a thing of the distant past.","“I just wanted to test how far I can extend the rain's range at full capacity with these hand seals.”"]},{"number":469,"title":"Chapter 469: Oh, Immortals","paragraphs":["The pale blue light at Yue Fuguang’s fingertips exploded within the clouds, causing them to churn from within as if detonated.","First, in the east, a thin thread of rain descended, like someone using a silver needle to stitch the first stitch into the earth.","Then, to the west, rain began to fall. To the south, the north—every direction at once—countless threads of rain plummeted simultaneously, weaving together into a vast curtain of water that shrouded the entire heavens and earth.","The rain hammered the parched, thirsty ground, lifting a white, misty veil of steam.","The cracked lines in the soil slowly closed, and the drooping seedlings gradually straightened their stalks in the rain, turning from yellow to green, from green to emerald.","Within the space of a single cup of tea, the whole landscape was lush with greenery.","Even more remarkable was the faint, shimmering azure light flickering within the rain curtain—it was a strand of wood spirit energy that Yue Fuguang had dissolved into the rainwater. With this enriched rain nourishing the land, even if no more rain fell for two months, the earth would never again be reduced to its former desolate state.","[Master, your rain-summoning skill has grown ever more refined. Did you mix wood spirit energy into the rain? The people of this land are truly blessed!]","Yue Fuguang herself had only realized, upon rising to this high altitude, that her abilities had suddenly changed.","She lifted her head to gaze into the high sky. The closer she was to that presence up there, the more dangerous it became, yet her power also seemed to grow stronger.","She withdrew her hand and stood on the carriage shaft, quietly watching for a moment.","The rain continued to fall. Below, the common folk who had been carrying water to irrigate their fields had long since stopped their work when the sky suddenly darkened.","Some pointed at the sky, seemingly shouting something. When they saw the raindrops falling, they dropped the buckets in their hands and the shoulder poles on their backs, kneeling in the muddy ground to kowtow in gratitude to the heavens.","This time, Yue Fuguang did not manifest a divine apparition while summoning the rain. But her carriage—radiant with spiritual light and ethereal grace, the horses galloping through the void with a river of stars forming beneath their hooves—stood out like a bright lantern in the endless dark night. It was impossible not to see her.","“Look! A celestial being riding a carriage across the sky!”","“See those horses treading on stars, with wings on their backs—they’re the winged steeds from the old folks’ stories!”","“Could the immortal in that carriage be our Divine Maiden?”","“Besides the Divine Maiden, what other god would spare a thought for us poor, suffering folk?”","“It must be the Divine Maiden on that celestial chariot!”","“I, Wang Dazhu, kowtow in thanks to the Divine Maiden!”","“I, Zhang Tieshan, an old man, kowtow in thanks to the Divine Maiden!”","“I, a common woman...”","“I, a maiden...”","Yue Fuguang faintly heard the words of gratitude and worship from below. Even though they had burned no incense or candles, she sensed the purest, most devout faith power, thread by thread, seeping into her body.","This faith power was like the finest tonic, slowly easing the exhaustion in her mind and body from the heavy expenditure of energy in spreading clouds and summoning rain.","She raised a hand to smooth her wind-tousled hair at her temples, then turned back into the carriage.","“Let’s go. To Seven Sword Manor.”","The winged horses began to gallop, flying toward the sword-hilt end of the Treasure Sword Mountains. The curtain of rain parted automatically along the path the carriage took, not a single drop touching it.","This left Feng Tang and Yu Huaixian—who had already donned straw rain capes in preparation for getting soaked—staring at each other in bewilderment.","High in the sky, the golden bells hanging from the eaves of the carriage chimed crisp and pleasant in the wind, the soft sound effortlessly overriding the noise of wind and rain.","The chime echoed in the ears of the common folk below.","Behind her, the entire Green Mulberry Plain and hillsides rippled with layers of green waves in the rain. The farmers, who had toiled ceaselessly, still knelt in the rain, while children ran chasing the heavenly carriage in the sky.","He Jin smiled faintly as she took one last look downward, then withdrew her gaze and let the curtain fall.","Although none of the three said a word, each of them had gained a new understanding of His Excellency’s abilities. Had it not been for their own identities, they—like the common folk below—would have bowed their heads in worship to the Divine Maiden who had rescued them from drought.","[Little Zhu, have you seen how far this rainfall extends?]","[Master, this rainfall covers two hundred and thirty-eight li—thirty li more than yesterday!]","In truth, it was more than that. This time, she had also added the spirit energy to the rain. Without it, the range might have been even longer.","So it seemed that summoning rain from the sky was the best method. At least she could borrow some power!","Yue Fuguang’s lips curled upward into a grin, like a cat that had stolen a fish.","She now treated that presence the same way she had once treated Emperor Mingxi: whoever ruled this world should shoulder more of the burden. Her approach was also the same: take whatever she could, little by little.","The winged horses were swift. Even what seemed like a great distance took them no longer than two or three cups of tea to reach the skies above Seven Sword Manor.","It was now the beginning of the Shen hour, and the rain was still falling.","“Oh? He Jin, look down. Lanterns and festoons everywhere—quite the lively scene. Is Seven Sword Manor celebrating a happy occasion?”","He Jin leaned out of the window to peer below. She saw the bright red silks and colorful lanterns still vivid in the rain, hanging from the eaves and corridors, and wore a puzzled expression.","Seven Sword Manor had only four masters: herself, her father, her elder brother, and his wife. She was away all year, and her elder brother had married only last year. His wife’s baby was due in three months. By all accounts, there was no other happy event at home!","He Jin began counting on her fingers. Today was the twenty-third of the fifth month. It was neither her elder brother’s nor his wife’s birthday, nor was it her father’s... Her father’s birthday seemed to be the twenty-eighth of the fifth month. That was still several days away—hardly the right date for a birthday banquet.","Still, as she looked down at the busy servants and the guests in splendid robes coming and going, the word “hardly” grew less and less confident in her mind.","Although her father had always celebrated his birthday on the actual day in previous years, who was to say he wouldn’t suddenly have a whim and do it early?","“Your Excellency, it looks like my father is holding a birthday celebration.” He Jin’s voice carried little certainty, but among all possibilities, it was the only one.","“Well then, we’ve come at just the right time!” Yue Fuguang smiled, but her mind was already racing to figure out what suitable birthday gift to give He Qisha.","The winged horses descended slowly. Just then, among a group of people drinking tea and playing chess in the garden corridor, someone happened to look up and saw the winged horses diving down from high above, accompanied by increasingly clear, ethereal chimes floating on the air.","He saw the exquisitely beautiful carriage with auspicious clouds drifting past. First, his mouth fell open in shock, but his treacherous lips could only produce hoarse, gasping sounds.","In his panic, he reached over and yanked at his friend. His friend had just lifted a cup of tea to his lips, and the liquid went straight into his nasal cavity.","Cough, cough!","“Sun Laoqi, are you trying to kill me?” he complained as he wiped his face, then looked up to see what the fuss was all about.","“You...” Sun Laoqi, still unable to speak properly, shook him violently with one hand while pointing at the sky with the other.","The man followed the direction of Sun Laoqi’s finger. “Ah... ah! A god... an immortal! An immortal, it’s an immortal!”","“Fei Wu, are you out of your mind? What immortal?” an onlooker watching the chess game said in displeasure, turning around."]},{"number":470,"title":"Chapter 470: Goddess Descends from Heaven","paragraphs":["Just as he spotted the winged horse flying toward the main courtyard, the folding fan in his hand clattered to the ground. \"My mother! It really is a divine being!\"","\"Brothers, look quickly—a divine being!\"","His hand swept across the battlefield of black and white pieces locked in fierce conflict, and in an instant, the game that was about to be decided became a chaotic mix, black streaked with white, white mingled with black.","\"Fei Wu, I'm going to...\" The words died in his throat, because the white player, who was about to win the game, also looked up and saw the luminous carriage in the sky, pulled by the winged horse.","By then, Yue Fuguang's carriage was less than a hundred meters above the ground, and more and more people below were spotting the flying chariot in the sky.","Soon, someone noticed He Jin standing on the carriage shaft, looking down.","Someone couldn't help shouting excitedly, \"Look quickly! Is that my niece He Jin standing up there?\"","\"You're right, that's my niece He Jin, no mistake!\"","\"What do you mean, 'your niece'? Are you even surnamed He to call her that?\"","The members of the He clan immediately objected.","\"Where's Qisha? Where's my brother Qisha!\" Someone started searching for the manor's master, He Qisha.","\"Yes, yes, go find Brother Qisha, tell him to come out quickly and welcome the Divine Maiden!\" The speaker's voice cracked with excitement.","\"Divine Maiden?\" someone wondered. How did she become the Divine Maiden?","Smack! A young man with a bewildered expression and a face full of question marks was slapped on the back of the head by his father. \"You fool! With abilities like that, and with your cousin attending her closely—who else could it be besides the Divine Maiden?\"","His father hissed through clenched teeth, frustrated at his son's lack of insight, \"Hurry up and go find your Uncle Qisha!\"","Then, still unsatisfied, he kicked his son in the backside, sending him stumbling five or six meters away.","He muttered curses inwardly, 'This clueless idiot. If I hadn't prompted him, he wouldn't even catch on to hot food!'","The already lively Seven Swords Manor instantly erupted into an uproar at the sight of Yue Fuguang and her companions in the sky.","He Qisha, the master of the manor, was at that moment in the wine cellar with his eldest son He Heng, selecting fine wine for the upcoming banquet.","He Heng watched his father hauling jar after jar of wine and couldn't help saying, \"Father, please drink less tonight.\"","\"You brat! Just because your sister isn't here, you think you can boss your old man around?\" He Qisha grumbled, sounding displeased.","\"Son isn't trying to boss you, but don't forget—you have to set out for Xinzhou tomorrow. If you're late, you might miss the Junior Preceptor and your sister!\"","His father had held his birthday feast a few days early precisely so he could go to Xinzhou to pay respects to the Junior Preceptor.","\"Don't let wine ruin your plans!\"","He Qisha realized his son had a point. Compared to drinking, meeting the Junior Preceptor was far more important.","\"Fine, this is enough!\" He patted the seven or eight wine jars on the floor. \"These will suffice for my old brothers to drink!\"","Father and son each picked up a five-jin wine jar. Before they even left the cellar, they heard a commotion outside—words like \"divine being\" and \"winged horse\" drifting faintly to their ears.","\"Something's happened outside?\" He Qisha's expression turned serious. He couldn't help thinking this, given that over the past year the Seven Swords Manor had been secretly targeted by several factions. Only the Junior Preceptor's influence had allowed him to resolve these issues one by one.","\"These scoundrels only dare to trip us up in secret,\" he muttered. Everyone knew he had Junior Preceptor Yue backing him—whether they were local officials or wealthy merchants, they all treated him with respect and deference.","Only the Nether Blossom Society, Rock-Solid Mountain, and Wind and Rain Pavilion dared to cause him trouble.","He Qisha drew the blade from his waist and strode outside, with He Heng gripping his sword and following closely behind.","Before he reached the wine cellar door, it was flung open from the outside. \"Uncle! Uncle, come out quickly!\"","The first to rush in, He Ming, ignored He Qisha's raised blade that nearly struck him and grabbed his arm, pulling him toward the door while shouting, \"Uncle, hurry! The Divine Maiden is here, and Cousin He Jin is with her!\"","\"What? The Divine Maiden is here? And Jin'er is back too?\"","He Qisha let himself be pulled along by He Ming, asking between breaths, \"Where are they? Jin'er too—if the Junior Preceptor was coming, why didn't she tell me beforehand?\"","\"Uncle, the Divine Maiden is in the sky. Cousin Jin probably didn't have time to tell you!\"","\"In the sky? What sky?\"","He Ming was taken aback. \"The sky is the sky!\"","In a few seconds, they reached the main courtyard. Without needing He Ming to point it out, He Qisha looked up and saw the carriage hovering directly above.","\"It really is in the sky!\"","Standing on the carriage shaft, He Jin spotted her father and older brother rushing from the main courtyard, and her sister-in-law Tian Yurou being helped from the side courtyard.","Under the crowd's blazing gaze, the carriage slowly descended into the main courtyard just as He Qisha arrived.","He solemnly straightened his slightly rumpled clothes, strode quickly to the front of the carriage, stopped, and bowed respectfully. \"He Qisha, together with my son He Heng and daughter-in-law Tian, welcomes the Junior Preceptor to our humble manor! I failed to greet you from afar; I hope you will not hold it against me, Your Excellency!\"","His eyes, slightly lowered, caught sight of the winged horse's lower body, its shimmering starlight gradually fading and its back wings slowly folding.","As He Qisha spoke, the crowd gathered behind him followed his example and bowed respectfully, each announcing their status—from minor officials to commoners, youths to scholars, wives to maidens. Clearly, He Qisha had a wide circle of friends and a diverse array of guests.","Yue Fuguang walked slowly out of the carriage and stood on the shaft, looking down. She raised her hand slightly. \"Manor Lord He, there's no need for such formality. I have come unbidden and intruded upon your gathering.\"","He Qisha's face flushed red with excitement. Hearing Yue Fuguang's words about intruding, he quickly shook his head. \"Your Excellency's visit to our humble manor is the greatest honor and privilege the Seven Swords Manor and I could ever hope for. There is no question of intrusion.\"","He made a gesture of invitation. \"The rain outside is heavy; please enter.\"","Mention of the heavy rain made everyone realize that this carriage and its occupants had remained completely dry from start to finish, unlike the rest of them drenched like drowned rats.","Indeed, the Divine Maiden was truly divine—even the rain avoided her.","No wonder it had been raining here today. So the Divine Maiden was passing through.","As she stepped slowly down from the carriage, Yue Fuguang saw all the guests, soaked through, still striving to maintain respectful and courteous poses.","She swept her wide sleeve, and everyone felt a cool breeze brush over them. Their summer clothes, which had been clinging wetly and uncomfortably to their skin, instantly became dry and fresh after that breeze passed.","\"This...\" someone stared at their dry clothes, eyes wide, momentarily speechless.","\"Thank you, Junior Preceptor!\" He Qisha was the first to react.","\"A small matter,\" Yue Fuguang said. She had put on another modest show, but in her heart, she was feeling immensely pleased.","The thought flashed through every mind there: The Junior Preceptor truly is a divine being! It turns out that Qisha's everyday boasting about how extraordinary the Divine Maiden was wasn't exaggerated flattery—it was an understatement!"]},{"number":471,"title":"Chapter 471: Giving Gifts","paragraphs":["He Qisha was feeling immensely proud at this moment. He respectfully led Yue Fuguang toward the main courtyard, with the others following in succession. A few people even sneakily circled the carriage several times.","The more they looked at it, the more they felt this carriage must only exist in the heavens—here on earth, it was a once-in-a-lifetime sight. There were also the white horses with wings on their backs, which everyone couldn't get enough of. Some suddenly felt that their own thousand-gold steeds were no longer so appealing!","\"If I were lucky enough to sit in such a carriage even for a moment, I could die without regrets!\"","\"Dear friend, why not go sleep in the guest room?\"","\"Brother, what do you mean by that?\"","\"Dear friend, in your dreams, anything is possible!\"","\"Oh? Brother speaks sense!\"","Yue Fuguang naturally had no idea people were drooling over her expensive carriage. On her side, He Jin was walking along, introducing Feng Tang and Yu Huaixian to her father and brother.","When everyone heard that Feng Tang was a Censor-in-Chief, their skin tensed involuntarily.","Especially the local officials, who hadn't had the chance to introduce themselves earlier. Now learning that this Lord Feng was the grand censor of the current court, they hurriedly tucked their tails between their legs and came forward to pay respects.","At this moment, they didn't know whether they were lucky or unlucky. If you called it unlucky, they had only come at the invitation to support a man under the Junior Preceptor, yet unexpectedly encountered the Junior Preceptor himself—the number one man of the court, whom even their prefecturn would struggle to meet.","If you called it lucky, they had finally met the Junior Preceptor but couldn't start a conversation; instead, they were forced to first bow to Poison Tongue Feng.","\"You gentlemen are the Tongpan, Jingli, Zhishi, and Xunjian of Jingmen Prefecture?\"","\"Reporting, my lord, it is indeed us!\"","Feng Tang glanced around. \"Why don't I see the Prefect and the Tongzhi?\"","\"Well...\" The Tongpan didn't know how to answer.","The Tongzhi had planned to come, but on the way out, the prefect called him away, claiming urgent matters to handle together. As for what those matters were, the Tongpan had no idea.","\"Enough, I was just asking casually.\" Not to mention that He Qisha was, on the surface, part of the Junior Preceptor's circle; the Seven Sword Villa’s importance to the region was something local officials had to pay attention to for the sake of their own political achievements and local stability. Whether they came or not, Feng Tang didn't dwell on it—so long as neither side caused trouble.","In the main hall of the Sword Intent Pavilion, Yue Fuguang was invited to the seat of honor, while Feng Tang, He Qisha, and officials like the Tongpan and Zhishi sat below in order.","Those who couldn't find seats stood automatically on either side of the hall, remaining silent. As for those who couldn't fit inside, they stood quietly under the eaves outside the hall.","At this point, even if He Qisha wanted to ask them to go to the front hall to sit, they probably wouldn't want to leave. Those who managed to sit or stand inside were all people of some status.","One could see they hopelessly stole glances at the Junior Preceptor, as if afraid no one would notice their behavior.","He Qisha really felt like shaking them awake and telling them to restrain themselves—after all, you lot have some standing!","As for being watched, Yue Fuguang didn't mind. She had faced much bigger crowds—what were a hundred or so people gawking at her?","She ignored the sea of starry eyes around her and said smilingly to He Qisha, \"We came in a rush, and I only just heard from He Jin that today is Lord He’s birthday celebration?\"","In fact, since He Qisha had pledged allegiance to Yue Fuguang, his birthday had always been honored by a generous gift sent in her name from her mansion every year. The same applied to Luo Xue.","But both the Yu family, He Qisha, and Luo Xue considered this routine and never brought it up in front of her.","He Qisha, his face beaming brighter than if he had drunk fake wine, nodded eagerly at Yue Fuguang's question. \"My lord, you've come at just the right time. Today, under the excuse of a birthday celebration, I invited friends over to gather at the villa and have some fun and excitement.\"","The others nodded repeatedly, saying in unison, \"Lord He warmly invited us; of course, we came to join the celebration.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"I didn't prepare anything in advance, only brought some small trinkets I had on hand.\"","With those words, she waved her right hand lightly before her, and amidst an invisible ripple, several boxes materialized unceremoniously in front of her.","As she expected, the next moment, gasps echoed from both inside and outside the hall.","Hiss!","Hiss!","Everyone’s minds were racing wildly: A divine power! This is exactly what divine power!","Pocket universe! This is just like the pocket universe described in storybooks!","People’s eyes were wide open, and but for the stubborn eye sockets holding them back, would have jumped right out. Their mouths hung agape, revealing tiny pink tongues. Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow—unexpected to find a few good sets of teeth in these ancient times when only tooth powder was available for cleaning!","Yue Fuguang was quite satisfied with the impression she had made today. Since rain had fallen and she had ridden in a carriage drawn by celestial horses, wasn’t it perfectly natural for her to make objects appear out of thin air?","Basic operations! All basic operations!","Amidst the crowd’s stunned gazes, she lightly waved her hand over the three boxes. \"These gifts are for Lord He today, as a birthday token.\"","The three boxes floated gently to He Qisha. Startled, he leaped from his chair. Staring at the boxes hovering before him, he shook his head and waved his hands frantically. \"No, no, too precious—my lord, you mustn't. You mustn't.\"","He swallowed hard, his face even redder than before. \"For you to grace this occasion is already the greatest blessing of your humble servant’s life and the Seven Sword Villa’s. How can I let you spend so lavishly today?\"","Did He Qisha not want those gifts?","Of course, he did—not because he was shallow, but because none of the gifts from Junior Preceptor Yue were ever subpar.","More importantly, to receive a gift personally delivered by my lord on his birthday—even if it were just a blade of grass, he would treasure it.","This experience alone would sustain him for a lifetime. In the future, when he recounted it to his descendants, it would always be the crowning topic.","He Qisha glanced at his daughter-in-law’s protruding belly standing beneath his son. Inside it was his soon-to-be-born grandchild, his future most attentive audience.","The unborn little girl shuddered even in her mother’s belly, unaware that for every remaining year of her life, she would hear every detail of this day repeated until she could recite it backward. After all, how many times would her grandfather bring it up yearly!","At that moment, Yue Fuguang, still ignorant of the role she would play in these tales, smiled at He Qisha. \"Lord He, do not decline. They're all just trinkets, worth very little.\"","Turning to He Jin, who had remained protectively by her side as her bodyguard even after returning home, she said, \"He Jin, why don't you urge your father? We’re all one of the family; there's no need for such formality.\"","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but wonder: was she usually not approachable enough that even a gift to a subordinate would make him too timid to receive it?","Hearing Yue Fuguang utter the words \"one of the family,\" He Qisha smiled even more brightly. Then his daughter said, \"Father, this is my lord’s genuine gesture—please accept it. In the future, just dedicate yourself more to your lordship’s affairs. When the work is done well, nothing else matters more!\""]},{"number":472,"title":"Chapter 472: Does He Truly Understand the Wine He Drinks","paragraphs":["He Jin had been following Your Excellency for nearly three years and understood her temperament well. At her level, there was no need for formalities. If she gave a gift, it was because she genuinely intended to. If she had looked down on his father, she would not have made this trip at all.","He Qisha bowed and said, \"This subordinate thanks Your Excellency in advance. I accept your generosity with gratitude.\"","As he spoke, he tentatively reached for one of the boxes, and the eyes of those around him followed his movement, fixed on the box.","When He Qisha had refused earlier, most of the onlookers looked as if they were in pain, as if he had rejected Yue Fuguang’s kindness on their behalf.","He Qisha had practiced martial arts for years, and even when severely injured, his hands had never trembled as much as they did now. Even when his eldest son was born and he held the child for the first time as a new father, he had not been as nervous as he was at this moment.","To his relief—or perhaps not—he felt no obstacle at the bottom of the box and smoothly touched the wooden container.","It was slightly heavy. As a martial arts master, He Qisha’s senses were sharp. The moment his hand steadily supported the box, he clearly felt the buoyancy of the box suddenly dissipate.","The crowd, seeing him take the box, unconsciously swallowed hard, their desire to see its contents written all over their faces.","He Qisha ignored how much they longed to look. He went on to take the other two boxes, one by one, placing them on the table beside him.","Once again, he expressed his thanks to Yue Fuguang.","Though politeness never hurts, Lord He’s excessive courtesy left Yue Fuguang somewhat helpless.","Seeing that He Qisha had no intention of opening the boxes, the crowd grew more restless than a cat scratching at their hearts. Their eyes clung to the boxes, unable to look away.","Yue Fuguang found it amusing but did not suggest he open the boxes to see if he liked the gifts—mainly because they were not familiar with each other.","Yes, even after nearly three years, she still did not know this subordinate of hers well. This shows just how laid-back Yue Fuguang usually was.","[Master, not only are you giving him weapons, but you also gave He Qisha wine. Can he even appreciate it?]","Hearing the Divine Tool Master’s words, He Qisha was startled. So the boxes contained weapons and wine?","He Qisha swallowed hard. A weapon from Lord Ying must be a divine blade, and the wine must be of the highest quality. But the Divine Tool Master saying he could not appreciate it—was that not a bit insulting?","He had been drinking for decades and considered himself knowledgeable. Even if he did not know what kind of wine Lord Ying had given him, he surely knew how to drink it.","He had several types of baijiu in his cellar, all premium vintages.","Just as He Qisha was puzzled, he caught a glimpse of something in the corner of his eye. Aside from his son and daughter-in-law, a few other people had expressions of momentary shock and confusion.","Seeing their faces, He Qisha understood and sensed trouble. He quickly stood up and said, \"Lord Ying, it is getting late. Shall we move to the front hall for the evening banquet?\"","Yue Fuguang was also feeling hungry, so she rose and said, \"In that case, I will accept your hospitality.\"","He Qisha made a gesture for her to proceed, leading the group toward the banquet hall.","As he turned, he gave his son a meaningful look. He Heng had accompanied him on visits to Yue Fuguang before and had heard her thoughts, so He Qisha trusted him to calm the uncles.","[It’s just two bottles of medicinal wine. What’s so hard to appreciate?]","[Master, that is medicinal wine. If you do not explain its effects, he will waste it.]","\"You've already drunk it all, so how can you say it's wasted? That stuff is just the effect of the Vitality Pill plus the Rejuvenation Pill. He Qisha's martial skills are good enough; he can handle the potency without getting sick from it.\"","The effect of the Vitality Pill plus the Rejuvenation Pill? He Qisha, walking beside Yue Fuguang, nearly soared with joy right on the spot.","Those who heard the inner thoughts had no idea what the Vitality Pill and Rejuvenation Pill were, but they could read expressions! Not to mention He Qisha, who looked like he was about to laugh his guts out, even He Heng, walking beside him, had a grin so wide it nearly split his ears. Clearly, that wine was something good—extraordinarily good!","[Master is right. He Qisha definitely won't get sick from this wine. But if we're talking about someone who drank too much and got into trouble, there actually is one here.]","\"Oh? Little Bead, one of He Qisha's guests drank himself sick?\"","Before she and the Crown Prince had jointly brewed the distilled liquor, the wines on the market in the Dayan Dynasty were mostly fermented rice wine and fruit wine, with low alcohol content.","For someone to ruin their health from everyday drinking, they'd have to be a proper drunk.","[Master, getting sick from drinking is a small matter. Letting alcohol ruin important business—that's the real disaster.]","By now, the group had entered the banquet hall. The birthday feast was set in the flower hall, where five rooms had been opened up to form a spacious, bright area.","The Seven Swords Manor truly lived up to its reputation as one of the Five Mountains and Six Manors of the Dayan Dynasty. The banquet hall was not only elegantly built but also large enough to hold four or five hundred people with ease.","Yue Fuguang stepped inside, and her eyes fell on a twelve-panel screen made of rosewood inlaid with mother-of-pearl. When fully folded, it formed a \"Hundred Deer\" picture: elderly men of longevity either standing or reclining, with pine trees and lingzhi fungus crafted from fine ivory threads, surrounded by a circle of peaches with faint pink blushes on their tips.","In front of the screen stood a long table covered with a red brocade cloth embroidered with gold threads. At the center sat a foot-tall jade statue of the God of Longevity, with a shiny forehead, a long beard flowing down to his chest, and a cheerful smile.","Before the statue were five tiers of gold and silver sacrificial vessels. On the top layer, a cloisonné incense burner shaped like a tripod emitted the sweet fragrance of lilies and sandalwood, wafting gently through the air.","What caught the most attention was a two-foot-tall jade statue of her, hanging above the God of Longevity. Not to mention the exquisite, lifelike craftsmanship, every inch of the whole jade piece screamed \"expensive.\"","With jade quality like that, Yue Fuguang only had a few pieces of similar size in her storage ring.","She, the subject of the statue, glanced at it briefly and pretended not to see—it wasn't her embarrassment if anyone felt awkward.","Walking further inside, the hall was neatly arranged with twenty-four large tables made of rosewood. Each table was covered with a brand-new red silk cloth, embroidered with gold-thread \"longevity\" characters in dense, circular patterns.","The cups and dishes were all pure white, unadorned \"Tuotai\" porcelain from Chenghua kilns. They were so thin that you could see your fingers through them in the light, and they felt weightless when held.","The wine flasks, however, were heavy, gold-inlaid filigree pots. They held osmanthus wine and the most trendy drink of the past two years: grape wine. The osmanthus wine was served in white porcelain cups painted with flowers and birds, while the bright red grape wine was best enjoyed in glass cups.","Thus, on the main table, besides the white porcelain cups, there was a baby's-fist-sized glass cup placed before each distinguished guest.","Yue Fuguang looked at the glass cup in front of her and twitched her lips. It seemed she had specially asked the Crown Prince to make a batch of these last year for New Year gifts. No wonder the Seven Swords Manor had them—it wasn't strange after all.","By then, the sky had grown completely dark. A few delicate colored-glass lamps hung from the beams above Yue Fuguang and her companions—some hexagonal, others octagonal, with long tasseled cords dangling beneath. A wisp of wind crept in through the door, and all the light in the hall seemed to come alive, trembling in fragmented patterns as it fell upon the table, the walls, and the faces of those present.","The embroidered, colorful canopies shimmered all the more brilliantly in the glow of the liuli lamps. He Jin quietly explained to her that this was a local custom: whenever a household celebrated a birthday, a wedding, or a daughter's marriage, friends and relatives would present such canopies as tokens of blessing."]},{"number":473,"title":"Chapter 473: There’s Melon","paragraphs":["The colorful curtains were red, purple, and blue, all embroidered with the character \"Longevity\" in gold thread. The characters, big and small, in various scripts, pressed densely together, as if they had gathered all the blessings in the world and hung them in this hall.","On the rosewood stand in the corner stood a red coral tree, as tall as a man, with twisted branches and a deep crimson hue. Yue Fuguang saw the congratulatory message and signature on it and recognized it as a gift from Luo Xue.","She felt something was missing, and now she realized it was because she hadn't seen He Qisha's close friend Luo Xue.","\"Lord He, why isn't Lady Luo here?\" Given their friendship, Luo Xue should not have missed He Qisha's birthday celebration.","\"To be honest with you, Lady Official, I moved up my birthday banquet by a few days. Lady Luo happened to be busy these two days and couldn't make it.\"","They were old friends and often thought about things in the same way. He Qisha wanted to celebrate his birthday early so he could go meet the Grand Preceptor, and Luo Xue had the same idea. She was already on her way, little knowing that the Grand Preceptor had never been with the procession but had instead come to him.","He Qisha inwardly felt sorry for his friend.","Just as everyone took their seats, maids and servants began bringing dishes to the tables.","Since the weather was hot, the first dishes served were various chilled fruits: purple plums, red strawberries, golden loquats, and pink cherries.","Yue Fuguang silently lamented that it wasn't yet watermelon season; otherwise, a mouthful of chilled watermelon would have been wonderfully refreshing.","While nibbling on the fruit, she remembered to continue the topic. \"Little Zhu, what was that about drinking causing trouble that you mentioned earlier?\"","If she couldn't have watermelon, at least she could enjoy the gossip about others—that would also whet her appetite.","[Master, look at the round man in the dark blue merchant's robe at the table next to you.]","\"Round man\"—was that really a way to describe someone?","Yue Fuguang followed the System's words and looked toward the secondary seating area below the main table. Besides their main table, the two tables closest to it were filled with guests who had close ties with He Qisha.","Those two tables had both men and women, and there were two men in dark blue merchant's robes, but only one of them was round.","This man appeared to be about the same age as He Qisha, around forty-something.","However, he clearly hadn't taken as good care of himself as He Qisha had, showing all the signs of middle-aged spread.","His belly, in particular, though not as large as He Qisha's eldest daughter-in-law Tian Yurou's seven-month pregnant belly, looked like she was three or four months along.","In this era, where overweight people were rare, this man, who weighed nearly two hundred pounds, took up two seats all by himself—his fatness was impossible to miss.","Not only was he fat, but he was also short; given his build, was he even five foot five?","Yue Fuguang remembered that he had sat at the very end of the Sword Intent Hall earlier, and even then, she couldn't help but notice him. At the time, he kept wiping sweat; as expected, fat people really didn't handle heat well.","\"What's up with him? Did his round figure all come from drinking?\"","[This man has always been the type to gain weight easily—just drinking water makes him bigger. Not only can he not control his appetite, but he also treats alcohol like water.","Because of this problem, look at him and He Qisha—both around the same age, but He Qisha is about to become a grandfather and is still a handsome middle-aged man.]","Calling him a handsome middle-aged man made He Qisha quickly shift his hand away from the meat dish and reach for a green vegetable platter.","He could only get better!","[Master, this man is named Feng Shuitu. After struggling for years, he only managed to have two daughters and one son—three children. The oldest is twelve, the youngest five.","Master, look at the children's table. The three siblings dressed in the fanciest clothes are Feng's children.]","Yue Fuguang glanced at those three children. They wore gold and silver, and their clothes were made of fine fabric, embroidered with patterns of wealth and blessings using gold and silver threads.","Yet, these three children were clearly much more thin and frail than their peers at the same table, or even at the other tables.","\"So these three siblings are so skinny? Given how they're dressed, Feng Shuitu doesn't seem like someone who would starve his children.\" The treatment of both boys and girls seemed about equal.","[This is all because of Feng Shuitu's drinking. His excessive alcohol consumption didn't just affect his ability to have children; even the children he ended up having were born with weaker constitutions.]","He Heng, whose wife was already pregnant and who planned to have at least two more children, held his wine cup and didn't know whether to drink it or not.","Several other men at the tables who had few children silently exchanged glances and replaced their wine with water. They nodded to each other, agreeing that when toasting later, they would use tea instead of wine and shame no one.","[But they were lucky today, Master, because you happened to send down rain from the sky. The life force you mixed into the rainwater benefits the bodies of these mortals.","If Feng Shuitu hadn't braved the rain with his three children to welcome you back then, they would have missed out on this good fortune.]","Yue Fuguang hadn't even reached the level of immortality, so the wood elemental energy in the rainwater was purchased from the System Shop. That brief shower was the only one to have that ingredient—it was enough to nourish everything. She certainly wasn't going to waste it on a continuous downpour.","There was no rainwater falling outside now; if the three children of the Feng family had stayed hidden in their room, they would indeed have missed it.","Those who had braved the rain to welcome Yue Fuguang at the main courtyard all had excited expressions. They said, how could they not have noticed that the dark ailments of the Lord Grand Mentor’s body had improved so much? At first, they thought it was an illusion brought on by sheer joy.","Now, hearing this, it turned out to be because they had been rained on!","The food and wine were already laid out. The crowd hurriedly took a few bites of the dishes and then began taking turns toasting Yue Fuguang. Of course, Yue Fuguang drank fruit juice, while the others drank a bright red wine.","However, Yue Fuguang was a bit disappointed with today’s system gossip. Just this? It wasn’t even as interesting as the appetizers in front of her.","Before Yue Fuguang could complain, the system continued. 【But the fact that Feng Shuitu’s children are few in number and poor in quality are all small matters.】","“This is still a small matter?” One had to understand the deep obsession of ancient people with having many children and grandchildren, continuing the family line, and ensuring incense offerings after death. Those who have never truly lived in ancient times or understand the customs of that era simply wouldn’t grasp it.","Let’s set aside other things for now. Did she not owe her own extraordinary powers, even now, to the incense offerings of the common people?","After learning that in this world there truly is an underworld with reincarnation, she no longer mocked others’ pursuits. She also realized that for ancient people, matters of children were grave issues—nothing like the system’s dismissal as small matters.","“So tell me, what counts as a big matter?”","【Master, look at Feng Shuitu’s two daughters and one son. His two daughters are twelve and ten years old; in a few years, they will marry into other families.】","【As for his five-year-old son, he is physically the weakest of the three children, not destined for a long life. A Taoist once gave Feng Baoyu a prophecy, asserting that he would not live past eighteen.】","“Not live past eighteen? But I sense his body is being repaired. He can live just fine to thirty-eight.”","However, living to seventy or eighty would be difficult—poor foundational health is a hard flaw.","【Master, the Feng clan will not let Feng Baoyu live past eighteen. In fact, not even eight will be easy.】"]},{"number":474,"title":"Chapter 474: Teammates Will Eventually Become Opponents","paragraphs":["\"What are you saying? Someone among the Feng clan wants to harm a child who's only five? Who's so heartless!\"","\"For wealth and profit, what's the life of a child worth! Feng Shuitu doesn't yet know that the so-called family he's been supporting and helping is already plotting against him to take over his estate.\"","Clatter—from Feng Shuitu's table came the shattering sound of a wine glass hitting the floor. He was sitting with his back to the main table, and now he could no longer hold back. Though his hand still kept the shape of holding a cup, it was already empty.","A small patch of liquor had spilled at his feet, and the clear, sharp fragrance of the wine slowly rose to his nostrils, calling back the last shred of his reason.","When he first heard that mysterious voice, he had already downed several cups of wine. Initially, he thought it was just the alcohol going to his head. But when his nephew from the He family noticed his strange behavior and whispered an explanation to him, he finally understood where the voice came from.","Before he could even finish toasting three full cups to celebrate his three children's improving health, he heard that divine artifact person stated that his precious son wouldn't live past eight years old, and that the clansmen he trusted and relied upon were actually plotting to seize his family business!","Feng Shuitu's plump, steamed-bun-like face flushed red with rage. His chest heaved unevenly as he gasped and wheezed, twitching tremors running through him. Anyone watching might have thought he was silently weeping.","\"When are those people planning to make their move, and what means will they use against him?\"","She had heard plenty about families fighting over inheritance, both in modern times and here in this ancient world. Even in her own family, her father's brothers and sisters had put on quite a show of family dramatics trying to get more from their old man.","That was also why she stopped living with her grandparents once she turned eighteen—it was just too aggravating.","There was no shortage of those who devoured entire family fortunes, but the last time she'd heard of someone forcing a scheme without any natural opening was the Wu Yong family.","\"They're moving tonight. Feng Shuitu is considered a wealthy man in this area. His alliance with He Qisha forced those people to advance their originally slow and careful plan.\"","\"What's He Qisha got to do with this?\"","Indeed, He Qisha's hand paused mid-reach for a dish. Silently, he thought to himself, what does this have to do with me?","\"Master, have you forgotten? In the original timeline, He Qisha's grave would already be overgrown. By the eighth year of the Yuan Kang era, the Seven Swords Manor would have fallen into his younger brother's hands.","That brother, colluding with Panshan and Youtan to overthrow the Dayan dynasty, bled dry the local gentry and wealthy households within the Seven Swords Manor's sphere of influence. He would never have paid any attention to someone like Feng Shuitu.","So, back then, Feng Shuitu didn't manage to latch onto such a powerful patron as the Seven Swords Manor. The Feng clan only made their move against him in the autumn of that year.\"","\"So they're afraid He Qisha will get involved, and now they're moving against Feng Shuitu tonight, taking advantage of He Qisha's original plan to leave the manor tomorrow?\"","\"Exactly. Feng Shuitu's uncle and cousin were already planning to give him one of their own children when he couldn't father any heirs.","Feng Shuitu refused. Later, both his wife and a concubine became pregnant. If he hadn't kept such a close watch, those people would have already struck against the pregnant women long before.\"","Feng Shuitu silently wiped his sweat. So that's it, he thought. No wonder so many strange things happened at home back when his wife and concubine were expecting. One day the food wasn't clean, the next day the ground was slippery, and on a trip to the garden to admire the flowers, they ran into a venomous snake.","Back then, he had thought it was just the women in the rear courtyard scheming out of jealousy, and he had even dealt with a few of the more troublesome ones.","Now it seemed that those who had moved against his wife and Concubine Fang were not only his concubines but also his uncles!","At this thought, Feng Shuitu’s hands paused in their work. Several of his concubines had been gifts from them, and the women he had punished in previous years all seemed to share that origin.","He remembered what the younger uncle and the cousin uncle had said to him back then... oh, it was something about broadening the family line!","It was his own stupidity. He had been too shallow in his thinking. He had assumed it was all about rivalry and favor among the women, but only today did he realize it was about the men vying for his wealth. Those women were just pawns!","「Feng Shuitu didn’t notice anything unusual? What an idiot!」Someone like this, even if He Qisha won him over, wouldn’t be of much use!","He Qisha also realized this and shot a subtle, apologetic glance at Yue Fuguang.","【He thought it was just a household feud among wives and concubines. Since he had already fathered two daughters, both of whom were frail in health, they hadn’t bothered to harm the girls.","After the birth of He’s second daughter, there were no more pregnancies in Feng Shuitu’s household for several consecutive years. This only made the He family more convinced that his estate would eventually belong to their sons.】","「Are the years of no pregnancy due to Feng Shuitu’s own health problems, or was someone pulling strings? Didn’t they ever bring up the matter of adopting an heir?」","【Master, it’s true that Feng Shuitu’s heavy drinking in his early years damaged his health, making it hard for him to father children. But later he followed the doctor’s advice to recover, drank less, and eventually had his eldest and second daughters.】","Feng Shuitu nodded vigorously. No wonder the Artifact Sage knew everything—he truly was a god. Wasn’t it precisely for the sake of having children that he had given up his beloved drink back then?","Otherwise, where would Yujie and Zhujie be?","【However, later Feng Shuitu’s cousins repeatedly tried to lead him astray. At first, they sought to lure him into a gambling addiction, plotting to take his family fortune directly through a rigged table.","But unfortunately for them, Feng Shuitu only had a love for wine. He had no interest in gambling. Instead, the cousins who tried to tempt him ended up falling into gambling themselves. Some, who once had comfortable families, eventually lost everything and became poor.】","「It’s the taste of their own medicine, isn’t it?」","Feng Shuitu kept nodding furiously. The Young Master was right—what else could you call it but reaping what you sow?","His younger uncle’s eldest son turned into a gambling addict, sneaking out all the family valuables to stake bets. Those were fine heirlooms left by their grandfather!","And the cousin uncle’s family fared even worse. They were already less well-off than the younger uncle’s household. His favorite youngest son became addicted to gambling just like the eldest cousin, but with no valuables to steal at home, he started swiping his wife’s dowry instead.","Feng Shuitu silently spat. Serves them right!","【After paying such a heavy price, these people still refused to give up. They tried again to tempt Feng Shuitu into drinking, ruining the health he had barely rebuilt.","Thus, for four or five consecutive years, no children were born. Partly due to his own failing health, but also because several concubines were secretly drinking contraceptive potions.】","Feng Shuitu clenched his teeth. He didn’t need to think twice about which ones they were.","【During those years, they worked to destroy his health while pressuring him with the clan’s need for an heir. Their goal was to force him to adopt a son from among the clan members.】","But while it was said to be adopting from among the clan members, it actually meant taking a son from the closest families—the younger uncle's or the paternal cousin's household.","\"Those two families really know how to play their cards!\"","Still, no matter how good their tactics, when matched against an equally capable ally, they were bound to become rivals.","These two families had originally been cooperating, but a dispute arose over whose child should be adopted, nearly causing their alliance to fall apart."]},{"number":475,"title":"Chapter 475: All Rumors Are Nothing but Lies","paragraphs":["In earlier years, when Feng Shuitu had no children, they had originally discussed adopting the grandson of his Great-Uncle’s family. After all, after much calculation, among the boys of both families, only that child was suitable.","But in recent years, the Little Uncle’s family had also been adding new members. The youngest son of his eldest son and the third son of his second son were both quite fitting. Naturally, they no longer wanted to hand such a good opportunity over to their Great-Uncle’s family, and in terms of blood relations, their own branch was closer.","Thus, the two families ended up quarreling fiercely over the matter.","The most ridiculous part was that behind the scenes, they maintained their cooperative relationship while also not holding back from badmouthing each other’s children in front of Feng Shuitu.","“Then Feng Shuitu definitely shouldn’t adopt children from those families!”","“Isn’t that the truth? Feng Shuitu gritted his teeth and insisted he could still father his own children, refusing to adopt anyone, dragging out the decision until the candidates grew too old.”","It wasn’t until Feng Baoyu was born—though he was even frailer than his older sisters—that Feng Shuitu finally had an heir. After that, no one could openly bring up adoption again.","After Feng Baoyu’s birth, the rear courtyard of the Feng household remained unsettled. Some even came up with the idea of surrogacy, but not until Feng Shuitu dealt with the most vocal concubines and tightened security in the rear courtyard did things finally calm down.","“The concubines he dealt with—were they gifts from Feng Shuitu’s Great-Uncle and Little Uncle? And by surrogacy, do you mean exactly what I think?”","In this ancient era, there was a peculiar custom where elders liked to send women to their juniors’ chambers, claiming it was for the sake of spreading the family line. Yue Fuguang believed it was just an excuse for men to enjoy themselves and take more concubines.","As for surrogacy, wasn’t that just laying one’s own egg in another’s nest?","When Feng Shuitu heard about the surrogacy plan, he broke out in a cold sweat. If they had succeeded a couple of years earlier, he would have been finished.","“Right, so after Feng Shuitu blocked every single one of those paths, they had no choice but to think of another way.”","“So now that they’re making a move, do they want Feng Shuitu dead?”","“Uh... not entirely. The Little Uncle’s goal tonight is to send Feng Shuitu a ‘romantic encounter.’ A month later, they’ll claim the woman is pregnant, and that’s when Feng Shuitu will meet his end.”","Feng Shuitu cursed inwardly. He could guarantee there was no way that woman would actually be carrying his child—he knew his own capabilities too well. But it didn’t matter whether it was true or not. Once he was dead and Baoyu also passed away, even a pillow could pass as that woman’s ‘child’ and become his rightful heir!","How ruthless!","“So next up is Feng Baoyu, right?”","“Right. After Feng Shuitu’s death, Feng Baoyu survived several assassination attempts. It wasn’t until he voluntarily gave up his claim to split the estate with his ‘brother’ Feng Baoshan that the people targeting him finally backed off.”","Thus, although Feng Baoyu died just a few years after the Da Yan dynasty fell—barely sixteen years of age—his life still outlasted the Da Yan dynasty.","When the system mentioned that Feng Baoyu had outlived the Da Yan, it struck a nerve for several people instantly. Some worried whether they’d be silenced by the emperor for overhearing such sensitive and dangerous information; others were simply unnerved by the event itself.","The Da Yan dynasty would fall?","That shouldn’t be possible! Setting aside how the new high-yield crops had boosted the nation’s strength, even this sweeping drought across five kingdoms had spared only Da Yan. How could it collapse even under such circumstances?!","If Da Yan could still fall after having the Divine Maiden, then it could only mean the incompetence of its rulers, ministers, and people.","“And that Feng Baoshan—was he really Feng Shuitu’s son?”","“Of course not. He was the illegitimate son of Feng Shuitian, the eldest son of the Little Uncle’s household. And even that identity was just what the Little Uncle’s family assumed.","In reality, that illegitimate son wasn’t even Feng Shuitian’s biological child. They schemed tirelessly, believing they had seized Feng Shuitu’s fortune, not knowing they were merely paving the way for someone else.”","“So wouldn’t the Little Uncle’s family be furious when they find out the truth?”","“Naturally. In fact, it was later Feng Baoyu who revealed this news to them. He had known all along that they were responsible for his father’s death.”","After finishing that piece of gossip, Yue Fuguang felt her belly full. Though the story held nothing particularly novel, she had no idea why the system triggered a mission like this—to keep Feng Shuitu and his children alive.","Looking at the reward—only three hundred points—Yue Fuguang wondered how long it had been since she last took on such a low-scoring task.","At that moment, while visiting the Seven Swords Manor, Yue Fuguang had no idea that news of her riding the flying-horse-drawn celestial chariot to dispense rain from the heavens was spreading at a terrifying speed.","“Hey, Old Sun, did you hear? The Divine Maiden has arrived in Xin Province, riding a chariot pulled by a celestial horse to dispense rain from the sky!”","A gray-clad old man, while tending to his seedlings in the field, was chatting with his neighbor across the ridge.","The man called Old Sun, who looked to be in his forties, straightened up, took a breath, and replied, “Brother Zhang, I have heard about it!”","Not just him—almost everyone in the village had heard about the Divine Maiden riding the flying-horse chariot and making it rain from the sky.","He looked up at the sky—bright sunshine, not a single cloud.","If only the Divine Maiden were flying overhead, he would surely see her.","Old Sun bent down again to continue weeding, saying, “I also heard that the rain the Divine Maiden brought this time is different from last time!”","He paused, furrowed his brow as if trying to recall, then went on, “Those learned lads call it ‘sweet dew’—true sweet dew.”","He gestured animatedly while telling Old Man Zhang what he had heard from the scholars at the teahouse: “Those scholars said this sweet dew makes the crops in the fields grow strong and fast, and that it’s sure to be a bountiful harvest this year.","Even people who drink it will grow stronger—they say it can cure those gravely ill! And something else... oh, they said it can ‘bring the dead back to life and regenerate flesh from bones!’”","If Yue Fuguang overheard Old Sun’s words, she’d certainly say the old man was exaggerating. At most, the rain had some mild health-boosting properties—nothing to boast about reviving the dead!","Rumors, all rumors!","She wasn’t that wealthy!","“Brother Sun, is what you’re saying true?” Old Man Zhang suddenly stood up, too quickly, making his vision go dark.","He didn’t care about that. He hurried over, stepping past the low ridge that separated their fields, and came to Old Sun’s plot.","Carefully treading through the slightly wilted crops, he rubbed his hands together and asked, “Brother Sun, is this information reliable?”","All he had heard in town was how magnificent the flying-horse chariot looked—how it gleamed and shone, how fast the horses galloped, and how faint golden bell sounds could be heard.","He hadn’t even finished showing off this tale to Old Sun yet before hearing such good news.","Old Sun hadn’t expected Old Man Zhang to get so worked up over his words, but upon thinking of his situation at home, it made sense.","So Old Sun stood up as well, thought seriously for a moment, and replied, “I only heard those scholars talking at the teahouse. They were going on about how good the sweet dew water was, so I remembered it—but I don’t know if it’s true or just talk.”","He too worried that he might have heard the information wrong or that the scholars had spread false rumors, raising Old Man Zhang’s hopes for nothing."]},{"number":476,"title":"Chapter 476: It would be nice if the Goddess could also take care of the Drought Demon.","paragraphs":["The Sun family was pitiable, too. Their future daughter-in-law had been falsely accused of being a reincarnated drought demon, and a perfectly good girl was burned alive. Her youngest son, Zhang Xiaosan, went to seek justice for his fiancée, only to be severely beaten by the villagers.","To treat Xiaosan's injuries, the Zhang family had drained their entire savings, yet he showed no sign of recovery.","\"The scholars have seen much of the world, so what they say must be right! Yes, it can't be wrong!\" Old Zhang nodded heavily, as if trying to convince Old Sun to agree with him.","\"How could the words of learned men be wrong! The Divine Maiden is all-powerful. The sweet dew she sends down... yes, the sweet dew will surely heal my son's wounds!\"","He suddenly covered his face with both hands, tears seeping through his fingers, and murmured softly, as if speaking both to Old Sun and to himself, \"If only the Divine Maiden could... handle the matter of the drought demon too!\"","His third daughter-in-law's experience was not an isolated case. According to what people in the town said, in the border counties around them, several people had been burned to death this past month—men and women, old and young alike.","Old Sun, seeing how Old Zhang’s back had hunched even lower, couldn't help but sigh. \"The higher-ups are supposedly looking into it, from what I hear. But these things are done behind closed doors in the villages. As long as one village keeps its mouth shut, outsiders can hardly find out.\"","So although the authorities had arrested a few people, they were all locked up. \"If the victims' families won't tell the truth, the officials are in the dark too. If the Divine Maiden ever passes through our area, old brother, you could try begging her!\" If she were willing to step in, the Zhang family might yet see justice.","He looked up at the sky again, thinking the same thing as Old Zhang: both hoped the Divine Maiden would somehow learn of the drought demon's doings.","They were still at war with Nanyue, and some of the village's men had enlisted. Old Zhang's second son, the most skilled fighter of the family, had joined the army. Otherwise, if all three brothers had gone to demand answers together, his eldest and youngest might not have been beaten so badly.","Just as Old Sun was thinking how fortunate it was that Old Zhang's eldest son wasn't badly hurt, he suddenly saw a black dot in the cloudless blue sky, slowly growing larger. That dot gradually turned into a dazzling emerald color—a carriage made of jade floating in the sky!","And beside it, white horses with wings flapping like giant birds. \"It matches! Everything matches!\" Old Sun muttered to himself.","The Divine Maiden—the Divine Maiden really was riding a celestial horse-drawn carriage to save them, the common people who suffered!","\"Z-Zhang! Look! Look up in the sky!\" Stuttering with excitement, Old Sun's voice came out all strained.","Old Zhang, who had just calmed himself, heard Old Sun's oddly pitched shout and instinctively looked up.","What he saw was a sight he would never forget for the rest of his life.","The sky was still the same sky, blue as if freshly washed, not a single cloud in sight. But in that blue, something was moving.","He squinted, shading his eyes with his hand, trying to focus. At first he thought his eyes, tired from working under the sun, were just playing tricks on him, conjuring floating black specks.","But the speck grew larger and clearer, until it became a flying carriage.","The carriage was a lustrous emerald, like the color of a river in spring, its surface gleaming with a moist sheen under the sunlight.","In front, two white horses pulled it. Wings sprouted from their flanks, white wings that flapped steadily, not like birds in a hurry, but as if swimming through water.","There seemed to be people on the driver's seat. By now, Old Zhang was even more excited than Old Sun, like a drowning man who had suddenly grabbed a piece of driftwood.","He flapped his arms, grabbing at Old Sun. \"Little brother, look... is that the Divine Maiden's carriage?\"","So high and so far away, Old Zhang couldn't see clearly. He was afraid his imagination was running wild, creating an illusion.","But the scene before him was too real. This old man could even see the carriage's curtain fluttering back in the wind, and behind that curtain, it seemed there was a figure—surely the Divine Maiden, seated behind the drape!","\"Old Zhang, that up there must be the Divine Maiden's carriage!\" Several years younger than Old Zhang, Old Sun had sharper eyes, honed by years of hunting.","Not only did Old Sun see the people, he even noticed that one of the two on the driver's seat held something in his hand and was tilting his head back to drink.","Yu Huaixian, who was just drinking from his water bag, had no idea he was being watched by the people below.","The carriage in the sky was soon spotted by all the farmers working in the fields, including Old Zhang and Old Sun.","\"Divine Maiden has come!\" The shouts, one after another, gathered into a chorus, drifting in fragments to the ears of Yue Fuguang, who was resting with her eyes closed.","\"He Jin, where are we now?\"","\"Your Excellency, we've reached the villages near Huacheng,\" replied He Jin. Seeing Yue Fuguang awake, she set out some pastries and tea.","After returning home, He Qisha had loaded Yue Fuguang with plenty of good food before their departure. The pastries and flower tea He Jin now served were parting gifts from three days ago.","Yue Fuguang looked out through the carriage window, seeing a sight very different from what others perceived.","Besides the slightly parched soil, the withered plants, and the commoners bowing down to her, she also saw faint strands of black-red energy and streaks of deep crimson.","The deep crimson was easy to explain—they were not far from Lancheng, where a great battle was raging, making blood-soaked energy natural.","But what was strange was the lingering aura of resentment and malice drifting from villages and towns along the way.","Yue Fuguang frowned. Unable to figure out why, she decided to ask the system after finishing today's rainfall.","Seeing the thousands of people below gazing up at their carriage, Yue Fuguang pulled back her wandering thoughts. Time to get to work!","Below, Old Zhang and Old Sun, still looking up at the sky, clearly saw whirlwinds gathering clouds from all directions.","Within a few breaths, those clouds turned from white to black. They didn't have to wait long. Soon, fine, dense drops, as if someone were spinning silk from the heavens, fell rapidly from above.","Old Zhang instinctively reached out his hand.","A coolness touched his palm.","In his hand lay a few droplets of water, so clear that each one reflected his old, weary face a thousand times.","The rain grew heavier. Old Zhang remained old, but the weariness on his face slowly dissolved in the falling rain.","By the field, someone dropped his hoe with a clatter and stretched out his hands to catch the celestial rain.","Old Sun's legs went weak. He wanted to kneel, but didn't quite manage. He just tilted his face upward, his mouth open, watching the jade carriage slowly drift westward, growing smaller and smaller until it shrank to a tiny glint and melted into the curtain of rain.","\"Oh no, in my daze, I forgot to let you beg the Divine Maiden!\" Old Sun exclaimed.","Old Zhang, startled from his trance by the sound of his neighbor's dropped hoe and Old Sun's words, was already beyond caring.","Staggering, he turned and ran toward home.","Old Sun shouted after him, \"Old Zhang, what are you doing?\"","The Divine Maiden had sent down sweet dew. The crops were already looking much livelier. If they didn't clear the weeds now, the rain-fed weeds would grow even bigger, competing with the crops for both soil nutrients and water."]},{"number":477,"title":"Chapter 477: Resentful Malice","paragraphs":["Old Sun, a seasoned farmer, didn't understand why Old Man Zhang was running.","\"Going home!\" Old Man Zhang had no time to spare for weeding now. He had to get back first, so his third son, lying in bed, could receive the baptism of the divine nectar.","Hadn't Old Sun said that the divine maiden's nectar could cure the gravely ill, even bring the dead back to life with flesh and bone?","Their third son had a chance to be saved!","\"Eldest, you keep working here!\" As his figure was about to disappear from the field's edge, Old Man Zhang left words for his eldest son, who had been toiling at the other end.","Old Man Zhang wasn't sure if it was his imagination, but drenched as he was, he felt an inexhaustible surge of strength. His legs, which had always troubled him, were now carrying him swiftly. Truly, the divine maiden's nectar possessed miraculous effects!","Word of the divine maiden's nectar's miraculous properties spread from Old Man Zhang and folks like him, passing from one person to ten, from ten to a hundred. Those who heard the rumors no longer only marveled at the beauty of the divine maiden's carriage but instead spoke of the nectar's healing powers.","In places yet to be reached by the nectar, families with sick members, upon hearing these tidings, began placing their patients in courtyards or at their doorsteps during the day, waiting for the rain to arrive.","The object of the people's devotion, Yue Fuguang, was at that moment resting in a guesthouse arranged by the city government of Huacheng.","After her evening meal, she finally had time to ask the system about what it had seen during the day. \"System, tell me, how is it that there are so many places around Huacheng—its villages and counties—tainted with such thick, baleful energies of resentment?\"","Though her studies at the Hongwen Academy had been middling over the past two years, Yue Fuguang had read no small number of strange books and unusual accounts.","Based on the knowledge she had acquired, baleful resentment rarely formed so easily in places brimming with human vitality. Even those who died from rage or violent deaths didn't always give rise to resentment radiating a reddish glow. For such energies to manifest as a blackish-red haze, the deceased must have died with a heaven-defying grudge and unimaginable agony.","[Host, need you ask? Some died unjustly, plain and simple!]","Yue Fuguang was speechless. Of course she knew that; it was precisely because she knew people had died wrongfully that she wanted to find out why.","She could have asked the assistant prefect of Huacheng, but asking him was no match for the clarity the system could provide.","\"So, tell me, how unjust were those deaths?\"","[Uh... They were tied to wooden frames and burned alive, on suspicion of being reincarnated drought demons—the Hanba. The belief was that they had caused the great drought across the land. What do you think? Unjust? Horrific?]","Bang!","Yue Fuguang slammed her hand on the table. The rosewood table before her shattered into pieces with a sharp crack.","\"Ma'am! Ma'am, what happened? Are you all right?\"","Hearing the commotion from Yue Fuguang's room, He Jin knocked on the door but dared not enter without permission.","\"He Jin, no need to worry. It's just that the table broke—I'm fine.\" Yue Fuguang glanced at the fragmented table, waved her hand, and collected the pieces into her storage ring.","\"Ma'am, shall I fetch a new table for you?\"","\"No need. You may go now. I'll call if I need anything.\"","After dismissing He Jin, Yue Fuguang continued questioning the system. \"The Hanba—that old rumor. Didn't the emperor ban its spread?\"","She had heard about it in a letter from her grandfather, but as the tale spread, it grew more distorted, seeming to target her subtly.","Yet, because she had been blessing the land with rain along her journey, though the common folk still spoke of the Hanba, none associated the demon with her. Even if some malicious individuals tried to pin the blame on her, the people wouldn't believe it. So the matter had soon been quelled.","As for the origin of the rumors, Wei Ping and Cai Xian had already tracked it down. After interrogation, it turned out the rumors had spread from refugees crossing the border from Nanzhao.","It was said that in Nanzhao, various rumors about droughts and demons were circulating, and as a result, many young women had been burned alive.","\"The flood in Nanzhao's southern regions is still more than half a month away. I wonder if, when they’re drowning in water, they’ll ever think of the innocent girls they burned as drought demons?\"","She didn’t care about Nanzhao’s affairs for now, but she wouldn’t ignore people being burned alive on the outskirts of Huacheng based on some baseless nonsense.","\"Because of your rainfall, people in other prefectures just took the story as gossip. But Huacheng was different—less than a hundred li from Nanzhao, with frequent exchanges between the people on both sides.","That’s why the commoners here were more inclined to believe the drought demon theory. However...\"","\"However what? There’s more to it?\" It wasn’t that Yue Fuguang was being overly suspicious—it was just that the death list the system had showed her included men and women, old and young. Unlike in Nanzhao, where only young women were targeted as drought demons, this situation was clearly problematic.","\"However, only about twenty percent of the victims were women burned as supposed reincarnations of the drought demon due to blind belief—others were victims of personal grudges and property disputes. Take that girl, Liu Fuling, for example.\"","Yue Fuguang’s gaze fell on the third name on the list. \"Was she deliberately killed under the pretext of being a drought demon?\"","\"She was an only daughter with a modest inheritance. Her father was a town doctor who, not long ago, encountered wild beasts while gathering herbs in the mountains and never returned.","Her uncles then set their sights on her family’s property—the town house and the small medical clinic in front of it.","After several failed attempts to extort the estate from her, they initially planned to sell the girl off in secret and then seize the property. But because Doctor Liu had built up good karma through years of practicing medicine, the neighborhood neighbors were willing to protect the orphan.","At a loss, the Liu family heard about a girl from a nearby village being branded a drought demon and burned alive. So her uncles conspired to have her bound and burned as a drought demon on the outskirts of town!\"","Outrageous! Yue Fuguang was so furious she wanted to smash something.","\"And the local authorities didn’t intervene?\"","\"Well... this was considered a clan’s internal matter. Although they initially acted in secret, the entire Liu clan was present when they carried out the burning, so it wasn’t a secret murder.","Moreover, there was a ‘reason’ for it...\"","\"An internal clan matter? A reason? How lovely! It seems it’s time to replace these local officials!\"","Yue Fuguang first laughed coldly, then her face turned icy. If they liked mediation so much, they could all go home and mediate there.","She might not be able to control the whole world or completely stop this kind of clan behavior, but she had one trump card—she would make them reap what they sowed!","She would show clans across the land what the consequences of evil deeds truly were. She refused to believe that if they ignored the law, they would remain indifferent when their own lives were at stake.","The system, not feeling that was enough, continued to fan the flames. \"Look at that one, Zhang Shitou. The reason he was burned alive was simple—his family were refugees who had fled to the area. With clanspeople few in number, they were often bullied by the dominant surname clans in the village.\"","It turned out that Zhang Shitou’s wife was quite a looker, and a local ruffian from the village had taken a fancy to her. After Zhang Shitou beat him up for trying to harass his wife, the ruffian held a grudge and falsely accused Zhang Shitou of being a reincarnated drought demon—a creature blamed for famine. That very day, Zhang Shitou was tied up and burned alive at the riverbank at the edge of the village.","This ruffian came from a prominent family in the village and was even the grandson of the clan chief. Although the villagers all knew Zhang Shitou was innocent, no one dared to speak up for him.","Hearing this, Yue Fuguang grew even angrier. She had gone to all the trouble of calling down rain to save both the people and their parched crops, only to discover that she had ended up saving such wretched scum!"]},{"number":478,"title":"Chapter 478: Punishment","paragraphs":["\"And then there's Old Man Zhou, a lonely old widower. In his youth, he obeyed his parents and supported his elder brother's family without complaint, working so hard that his wife wore herself out and died young.","He was left with only a daughter, who not long ago was sold for two taels of silver by her grandparents and uncle to raise money for her cousin's bride price.","Old Man Zhou may be called old, but he's actually only forty years old. However, from doing heavy labor in his youth, he's ruined his health, and these past two years he's gradually been unable to do hard work anymore.","His elder brother, sister-in-law, and nephew felt he was a waste of food alive, so they burned him as a drought-demon too!","And then there's Qian Xiaohu, Zhang Xiaocao...\"","Yue Fuguang listened as the system explained one story after another, and her mind went numb.","\"System, I don't think this task of preserving the population is absolutely necessary!\" It wasn't that she was desperately short on points, after all.","The thought that she had been working hard, rushing about, only to save people like this made her want to just throw in the towel!","Who cared anymore!","Upon hearing that Yue Fuguang wanted to quit, the system suddenly felt it had spoken a bit too much. It had simply blurted things out in a moment of impulsiveness—how could it have made its own host lose interest!","\"Host, don't go that far, really, don't go that far! We can't ruin the whole pot of soup just because of a few rats, right?\"","Yue Fuguang remained silent, so the system continued playing the role of the understanding confidant, \"What we're doing now isn't just about saving those commoners and completing the population preservation task.","It's also about keeping the national strength of Dayan on the rise. Ultimately, it's all for our main mission!\"","Hmph! Yue Fuguang turned her head away. Of course she understood these principles!","What weighed on her heart was the injustice of it all. The drought-demon case in Huacheng was just the tip of the iceberg. How many similar people and events were there throughout all of Dayan?","She'd never thought deeply about this before, but now that this window paper had been pierced, whenever she thought of those people living well off the blessings she had bestowed, her whole body felt uncomfortable.","\"Host, if you're truly too angry to bear it, just punish them. We can't let these irrelevant people affect your mission.","Think about your jade-white bones and hundred-flower beauty...\"","\"Alright, alright, I know. Don't keep bringing that up!\" When she first heard that, how old had her mentality been? And how old was she now? Didn't she have any pride left!","But the system had a point—if her heart was out of sorts, she might as well vent that anger through the fates of others!","\"Your suggestion isn't bad, but I'll need you to put in some effort here...\"","Yue Fuguang told the system her requirements.","The system: !!!","Yue Fuguang ignored the system's near-cracking expression. She flicked her fingertip lightly, and a single star of light gathered at her fingertips, slowly forming into a light clump the size of an egg. After she tapped it gently, the bright light clump whooshed out through the open window.","At this moment, it was just past the hour of You, and outside the window the moon was bright and the stars were sparse. Since it was still early, sleepless commoners gathered in small groups, swapping the latest gossip about this house and that.","The hot topic today was, of course, the divine lady who had descended from the heavens in a carriage pulled by a celestial steed.","Some were tirelessly describing to those who hadn't seen it how divine the celestial steed was, how beautiful the carriage was, but lamenting that the curtain blocked the view of the divine lady inside.","\"Granny Li, do you think the divine lady knows about this drought-demon ruining people's lives in our region?\"","The old woman called Granny Li paused mid-twist on the hemp rope she was braiding, and shook her head. \"How would an old woman like me know what a divine lady knows?\"","She sighed. \"If you ask me, the 'drought-demons' they burned to death might not be the real thing.","Granny Li's daughter-in-law, who was sitting beside her helping sort the hemp, chimed in, \"Mother's right. If those who were burned were truly drought-demon incarnations, why wait so many years to harm us now?\"","She shook her head. \"If it were true, after burning several people one after another, why hasn't a single drop of rain fallen?\"","She looked up at the sky. \"We still have to wait for the divine lady to come and bestow her life-saving sweet dew!\"","Granny Li nodded. \"The eldest son's wife is right. None of us in this family will listen to anyone else's claims. We only believe in the divine lady.\"","She glanced around and, seeing others still talking about the celestial steed, lowered her voice and said, \"Sister Wu, from now on you'd best not talk about the drought-demon matter anymore.\"","\"Why? Can't we even mention it?\" Sister Wu, who had spoken first, looked at Granny Li in confusion. \"Would the divine lady blame us for that?\"","After all, it wasn't as if they were the ones who killed those people.","They weren't all fools. At first, when one or two were called drought-demons, people still believed it. But after it happened repeatedly, they started to have their doubts—could it be a mistake?","\"If the divine lady wants to punish anyone, it's those who did the deed!\"","No sooner had she finished speaking than Granny Li's eldest daughter-in-law suddenly shrieked, \"Mother, look up in the sky!\"","Her eyes wide with terror, she stared at the sky above them.","The once clear and moon-bright night sky was suddenly shrouded in thick, dark clouds. \"Is it going to rain?\"","Granny Li and Sister Wu, whose eyesight was poor due to age, muttered that the weather was changing and rain was coming.","Someone else shouted, \"Is the divine lady about to bestow sweet dew?\"","They had heard that a neighboring county had already received rain that day, and they had thought it wouldn't be their turn until tomorrow. They hadn't expected it to rain so soon!","\"Mother, it's not going to rain. It's... there's a pair of eyes in the sky!\"","The moment Granny Li's daughter-in-law finished speaking, more people spotted the pair of eyes hidden among the dark clouds—eyes that were neither joyful nor sorrowful, penetrating the heart of heaven and earth and all human affairs.","\"Divine lady, it must be the divine lady!\" Someone began to kowtow toward the eyes in the sky.","Then, suddenly, a cold wind blew, and a huge, muffled rumbling resounded through heaven and earth.","Some thought it was an earthquake, but the sound was deep and heavy, followed by a creaking noise, like someone opening a long-sealed door.","With this muffled rumble and creak, commoners who had been indoors came running out of their houses, some heading to the streets to find out what was happening.","Had Yue Fuguang been flying in the sky at that moment, she would have seen that, centered on Huacheng, people within a radius of two hundred li had all been stirred into commotion.","In the towns and villages where drought-demons had appeared, if there were nearby forests or mountains, boulders peeled away from the mountain faces in sheets, tumbling and crashing into the valleys below, causing muffled thunderclaps.","The earth beneath their feet was like a roused giant beast, its back heaving violently. The ridges of the fields shifted out of place in an instant. Rivers were forced to change their courses, water crashing backward onto the banks.","Fissures opened beneath the feet of the perpetrators, spreading wildly like cobwebs in every direction, each crack exhaling the dangerous breath of the deep abyss from beneath the earth.","Trembling, they knelt in the centers of those fissures.","The land beneath their knees was collapsing, yet they lacked even the courage to stand up—or rather, their spines had gone soft.","That softness wasn't lax muscles; it was their very marrow replaced by fear, turning each bone into reeds ready to snap at any moment.","Some tried to scream for help, others kowtowed to the unseen pair of eyes in the sky, begging for mercy.","But no matter what they tried to say, the sounds squeezed from their throats were crushed by the roar of the earth, leaving only broken, tuneless sobs."]},{"number":479,"title":"Chapter 479: Visitors from the Abyss","paragraphs":["\"No... no... I don’t want to die!\"","\"Divine Maiden, I was wrong, we know we were wrong!\"","\"Divine Maiden, spare us, Divine Maiden...\"","The voices were pitifully faint, like a baby's babble, like the last sighs of the dying.","Yue Fuguang stood by the window, the pleas for mercy coming to her ears one after another.","Her expression appeared calm, her fingers idly playing with the multicolored pearl in her hand.","He Jin and Yu Huaixian guarded her courtyard, while outside the gate, Feng Tang was receiving a flurry of Flower City officials who had rushed over to assess the situation.","\"Censor Feng, what do you make of this...?\" The Prefect of Flower City had cold sweat beading on his forehead. Outside, the sky looked like a torn bolt of silk; clouds peeled back on either side, revealing behind them a churning, thick darkness.","It was not the darkness of night—night has stars. This was pure, light-devouring blackness, an abyss of nothingness.","Seeing this, the Prefect had a fair idea of what was happening. He and his subordinates were not actually worried that the Young Master would harm innocent commoners.","As for those who had done evil—if they died, they died. What concerned them most now was: after the Young Master had finished dealing with those people, how would she turn to handle them?","Wind blew in from outside, and the assembled officials shivered. This was no ordinary wind. It was bone-bitingly cold, carried a metallic, rusty scent, and felt clammy and sticky, cutting into their bodies as if it could burrow into their very bones.","Of all the people in the room, only Feng Tang seemed unaffected. The wind appeared to recognize him, swirling around him but never touching him.","The wind swept over the mountains, forcing ten thousand trees to bow. It swept through villages, sending roof tiles scattering. It swept over the gathered crowd, and everyone shuddered at once—a cold that rose from the depths of the soul, unrelated to body temperature.","The onlookers wanted to run.","But their legs refused to obey.","Some were muttering under their breath—perhaps prayers, perhaps pleas for mercy, perhaps just meaningless syllables. Some clamped their hands over their children's eyes, while their own eyes bulged so wide they threatened to split.","Some fell to their knees, the impact against the stone floor unfelt, because pain had been drowned by fear.","What were they afraid of?","They were afraid of that gaze falling from the heavens.","That gaze had no form, yet it was more oppressive than any form could be.","It seemed to rest upon each person, yet also upon no one in particular.","It felt as though it had settled onto every heart, transforming into an invisible blade that sliced through flesh, through bone, straight down into the deepest corner where all sins were hidden.","Someone suddenly remembered stealing a neighbor’s egg when they were ten. Someone recalled the knife they had once stabbed into a rival’s back. Someone dredged up those shameful secrets they thought would never see the light.","So the Divine Maiden really does know everything—this thought echoed in countless minds.","Those who had once personally taken part in burning the so-called drought demon lay prostrate on the ground, their fingers clawing into the dirt, nails bent backward without their notice.","Their bodies seemed squeezed by an invisible force, every inch of skin pressing toward the earth as if they wanted to bury themselves alive, as if anything was worth it just to disappear.","Their lips quivered, repeating only a few words over and over:","\"I was wrong... I was wrong...\"","But it was too late.","The mountains let out another sigh.","This time, cracks split open beneath their feet, gaping wide like the maw of some colossal beast.","But those people did not fall into the abyss as expected. Instead, to the horror of the onlookers, something began to climb out from the depths!","Clatter, rustle, hiss!","Dirt and gravel from the abyss seemed to peel away and fall.","Something in the hearts of those kneeling also seemed to fall along with it.","Under the crowd’s gaze—some terrified, some \"anticipating\"—the things from the abyss finally crawled onto solid ground.","\"Liu Fuling!\"","\"Zhou Old Man!\"","\"Zhang Stone!\"","\"Qian Xiaohu!\"","\"Zhang Xiaocao!\"...","Name after name was called out from the lips of the villagers. And these \"people\" who had crawled up from the abyss of hell grinned at them.","With that grin, endless flames erupted from their bodies, and the scent of charred meat rushed into everyone’s nostrils.","Ugh!","That smell dragged the villagers’ memories back to that day. They might not be as scared as the perpetrators, terrified unto death, but to merely watch everything, to do nothing at all—that itself was a sin.","Crack!","Purple lightning slithered through the churning dark clouds, followed by booming thunder.","\"Today, I grant you all special privilege: Those with grievances may settle them; those with wrongs may avenge them. You will not be punished by the Lord of the Underworld!\"","Yue Fuguang’s voice sounded across the sky, spreading outward like ripples. At the same time, her colossal divine manifestation slowly materialized against the pitch-black firmament.","The deity bent her head to gaze upon mortals, her solemn and majestic visage commanding awe without anger—striking such terror into the guilty that they wished they could burrow into a crevice.","Perhaps due to the circumstances, the Divine Maiden’s manifestation now looked very different from when the people had first seen her bring wind and rain. It seemed more imposing... and heartless?","Her eyes looked down upon them as one would regard ants to be crushed beneath the foot at any moment.","Not only did the commoners collapse, unable to stand, upon hearing Yue Fuguang’s words and seeing her manifestation—even the gathered officials of Flower City, at the moment her apparition appeared, hurriedly straightened their robes and prostrated themselves in reverence, no longer daring to defend themselves in the slightest.","The deity sees all clearly. The Young Master, as the Divine Maiden, would surely know every deed they had done. There was no point in speaking further now.","\"Thank you, Divine Maiden!\"","\"Thank you, Divine Maiden!\"...","The visitors who had emerged from the depths of the earth voiced their thanks in unison, their voices hoarse and icy—making everyone who heard them shudder with dread."]},{"number":480,"title":"Chapter 480: What Are You All Doing","paragraphs":["Among those who had carried out the violence, some with weaker constitutions were so terrified that they had soiled themselves, barely clinging to life. Yue Flowing Light would secretly act to spare them, for death without suffering was far too merciful.","As for those trembling like leaves in the wind, they could already feel something cold and slippery coiling around their bodies...","\"Caramel, you’re stealing Milky Way’s bamboo again!\" While cries of agony echoed outside, inside the secluded courtyard, Yue Flowing Light was teasing two black-and-white fluffy creatures.","At her feet lay three more fuzzy little ones, having just charmed their way into coaxing some delicious Spirit Beast Pills from her with their cuteness. After swallowing a tiny pill, the three wobbled as if drunk and collapsed motionless on the ground.","But Caramel and Milky Way were exceptional; even after taking the pills, they still had energy to fight over bamboo. For the tenderest stalk, the sibling duo didn’t hesitate to brawl.","\"Woof! Woof!\" Furious at being bested by his sister, Caramel let out a fierce, puppy-like bark at Milky Way.","Yue Flowing Light burst into laughter.","Amid her chuckles, the vendetta outside was nearing its end. Through her Dharma Eye, she glanced down.","Everyone had shown restraint—though the victims were left in a pitiful state, none had died.","Indeed, after this ordeal, these people would find living far more painful than dying. Not to mention others—even the villagers and relatives they had dragged into trouble could drown them with spit and scorn!","\"You love to preach clan loyalty and mutual protection, hiding wrongdoing under the guise of solidarity, don’t you? Then share the hardship!\"","Her Dharma Form once again gazed down upon the masses. \"To see what is right and do nothing—though no swords may strike, the heart commits murder. For the wicked, the law demands execution. For you who stand idly by, your sin is unforgivable!\"","Hearing \"stand idly by,\" those who had been cheering on the sidelines—thinking themselves uninvolved—felt their hearts sink. Cold sweat beaded on their foreheads.","Some inwardly protested, trembling as they knelt. They mumbled defenses only they could hear: \"I... I just didn’t speak out. I didn’t hurt him!\"","But they forgot how loudly they had cheered, how much praise they had lavished on the attackers, how they had wished they could be the ones to light the fire themselves.","Yue Flowing Light’s gaze swept over them like she was looking at filthy trash. \"You claim you didn’t harm anyone with your own hands? Then what were you doing when evil was committed?\"","With a sweep of her sleeve, countless images flickered through the air: people helping the assailants break into homes and drag out the bound victims, clapping and cheering as the condemned faced death by fire, spitting on them, shouting \"Burn her! Burn her!\"","Some cursed and recited the victims’ supposed wrongdoings turning them into reasons to deserve death. Their hearts were filled with malice!","\"And you think you are innocent?\" Yue Flowing Light’s voice thundered. \"When evil unfolds before your eyes, your silence itself is an offering to malice. Though you didn’t act, inside you silently permitted—even approved—the wrong. That silent permission and approval is itself a sin!\"","She raised her hand. \"I hereby withdraw all my blessings from you all. From this day forth, you are no longer my followers.\" As her words faded, something seemed to slowly vanish.","This was far more terrifying than any physical punishment.","The Divine Maiden was revoking all favor. They could no longer worship her.","What was that, if not death itself?","\"It’s all your fault! You’ve ruined us!\" Someone, almost mad with desperation, lunged at the barely breathing ringleaders.","\"You wanted their house and their land, so you falsely accused them of being a drought demon reincarnated! You must have lost your minds!\"","You see, they had known the truth all along. Yet instead of revealing it or stopping the injustice, they had simply gone to watch and cheer.","Those who had hidden at home, doing nothing, shrank back quietly, relieved they hadn’t joined the spectacle or hurled abuse at the dying.","Their only hope now was that the Divine Maiden wouldn’t abandon them.","Why was Yue Flowing Light so furious? Not only because the victims had died horribly, but because the bystanders’ apathy and cover-ups had shattered any remaining belief in justice among the truly kind-hearted.","If the good remain silent and the wicked are shielded, what would the world become? She wanted to complete her mission, yes, but within her power, she also sought to draw a clear line in people’s hearts.","Not everything accepted by convention is right!","The System remarked: Our host must be thinking of certain people back home in the modern world.","Though he had only spent a few days in modern times, he had witnessed much—including a young man about to jump from a building.","While the police were working desperately to save him, onlookers below not only photographed, filmed, and livestreamed, but shouted, \"Are you jumping or not? Hurry up! Stop dragging this out—people want to get home for dinner!\"","Someone chimed in, \"Yeah, jump already! Too scared to die and still pretend you want to? Loser!\"","Their vicious words were exactly like those who had cheered as the \"drought demon\" was burned alive!","The System shook its head. Throughout history, the evil in people’s hearts never disappears, no matter how society advances.","\"Now that you’ve seen vengeance served, it’s time for you to return!\"","With another flick of her sleeve, a cloud of dust swept by, and the crowd that had gathered from far and wide vanished instantly.","Then, Yue Flowing Light’s Dharma Form slowly faded. The pitch-black storm clouds receded like tidal waters, or like fine sand scattered by the wind.","The bright moon hung high, stars twinkled.","Beneath the heavens, the people stood still, unmoving for a long time.","Some found their foreheads slick with sweat, others had damp patches on their backs—whether from heat or fear, no one knew.","Faces were stained with tears, yet they couldn’t recall when they had started crying.","Some realized they had wet themselves, though they had no idea when it happened.","A bewildered child asked their parents, \"Father, Mother, where has the Divine Maiden gone?\"","\"Father, Mother, when will the Divine Maiden send us sweet dew? I’m so thirsty!\"","No one answered, because no one knew.","The people of Flowers City didn’t have to wait long for an answer. The next morning, after seeing the Divine Maiden’s carriage soar into the sky, the clouds shifted, and soon rain began to fall.","Quick-witted observers soon realized that this rainwater was no different from ordinary water. The crops that drank it didn’t bounce back with lush vitality, unlike those in neighboring towns blessed by thick dew.","As for the ill and ailing, the rain brought no relief at all.","Those who had hoped for healing medicine from the Divine Maiden’s gifts were sorely disappointed. Had no one seen with their own eyes how the land once nurtured by her sweet dew flourished, they might have doubted the legend entirely.","And long before the capital’s royal court learned of it, word that Yue Flowing Light’s chariot drawn by heavenly horses to scatter sweet dew across the skies had already reached the desk of Emperor Mingxi."]},{"number":481,"title":"Chapter 481: This Sign Is Wrong","paragraphs":["At this moment in the Hall of Mental Cultivation, after the grand morning court session, Emperor Mingxi, as usual, kept several trusted ministers behind to discuss state affairs.","Emperor Mingxi had Eunuch Qian pass a confidential letter to the ministers for their perusal. When it reached Yu Chongshan, his eyes crinkled with delight upon seeing his granddaughter riding a flying horse and scattering sweet dew.","His eldest son, Yu Zhongchun, noticed the old man's beaming face and couldn't help but lean over to read along.","The elder shot a glance at his increasingly unsteady eldest son and couldn't suppress a snort. The first son was lucky to have picked up such a wonderful daughter.","Yu Shuchun, too, felt his elder brother was fortunate. If only he had been in the capital back then and had the chance to adopt Fuguang as a daughter, he would definitely have fought for it.","After everyone had finished reading, Emperor Mingxi asked, \"What do my esteemed ministers think?\" His eyes were filled with barely concealed joy.","\"Your Majesty, this is a blessing for Dayan and a blessing for you!\" Ling Yinghua was the first to speak.","Wang Shouchen nodded repeatedly upon hearing this. \"Ling Jijiu is right. The Grand Preceptor's actions have also brought blessings to the people.\"","He stroked his beard with a delighted expression. \"I thought that even with the Grand Preceptor's ceaseless efforts to bring rain day and night, after this great drought, the best-case scenario for the people's harvest would be seventy to eighty percent of a normal year. But now, with the sweet dew the Grand Preceptor has bestowed, why worry about this year's harvest not being abundant?\"","Wang Shouchen grew more and more excited as he spoke, but Wei Ping, closest to him, couldn't help but shift slightly to the side. Old Sir Wang's spittle was almost flying into his face.","Cai Xian thought: You dodged, so it's all about to land on my face!","\"Hahaha! Minister Wang speaks truly. With Fuguang, why should Dayan worry about poor harvests or weak national strength?\"","He turned his gaze to Xie Zhiyan. \"Crown Prince, you must ensure that all the people in the capital and surrounding prefectures know the great blessings the Grand Preceptor has bestowed on Dayan and its citizens.\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty. I will see that this matter is handled properly, ensuring the Grand Preceptor's good name spreads across the lands of the six kingdoms!\"","Aren't the people of other nations fleeing famine? Let them all come to Dayan, where there's high-yield grain and a divine maiden who can scatter sweet dew.","Emperor Mingxi looked up again, his gaze burning as it swept over the ministers, and spoke solemnly, \"My esteemed ministers, it's not just the people who should remember this grace—even I and all the officials in this court should not forget what the Grand Preceptor has done for us.\"","Emperor Mingxi recalled the secret letters from spies in other nations, received late last night, describing the pitiful plight of their people due to drought—words could not do it justice!","Driven by hunger and thirst, citizens had begun to flee, while their governments, emperors, and officials were racked with headaches. The courts were plagued by internal strife as everyone tried to shift blame. It was clear that chaos had emerged among Dayan's neighbors.","If they were not fortunate enough to have Fuguang, Dayan might now be no better off, and the calamity that nearly destroyed the nation in the 14th year of the Yuan Kang era would have had a precedent.","Everyone nodded in agreement. With the Grand Preceptor, their burdens were also lighter. Otherwise, they would be just as troubled as the others.","\"Your Majesty speaks truly. With our Grand Preceptor, why worry about unifying the world under one rule?\" The ministers' secret ambitions were no less than those of Emperor Mingxi, who aspired to be a sage ruler throughout the ages.","If he could unify the five kingdoms in his lifetime, even if his prior record had been lackluster, the history books would still record a glorious chapter for him.","\"Huo Ying, have Generals Xu and Wei sent their latest battle reports?\"","Huo Ying immediately stepped forward and respectfully presented a sealed letter. \"Your Majesty, this is the frontline report I just received. I haven't had a chance to read it yet.\"","The wax seal bearing General Xu's soaring roc was still intact. Huo Ying had barely had time to warm it in his hands before Emperor Mingxi summoned him.","Emperor Mingxi took the letter from Eunuch Qian, scanned it quickly in three lines, and his face was soon wreathed in joy. Finally, he slapped the table and exclaimed, \"Excellent!\"","Seeing the emperor's delight, Ji Hongming couldn't help but ask, \"Your Majesty, have Generals Xu and Wei won another victory?\"","\"Hahaha, it's a great victory! A great victory for Dayan!\" He handed the letter to Eunuch Qian. \"Eunuch Qian, pass it around for my ministers to see. Dayan has not only won the battle but also the hearts of the people!\"","With that, he raised his tea and drank it in one gulp, as if toasting. This showed just how overjoyed the emperor was.","\"These people are all drawn here by Fuguang. We must not tarnish the Divine Maiden Fuguang's reputation.\"","He turned to the Minister of Revenue, Dong Qianli, and the Left Vice Minister, Yu Shuchun. \"Ensure the Ministry of Revenue has sufficient funds and grain to settle the refugees seeking refuge.\"","\"Your humble servants obey!\" Both had read the letter and would carry out the emperor's orders without compromise. The Ministry of Revenue was now flush with resources. Once Dongyi was taken, they might even need to expand their warehouses.","\"Minister Zheng, the Secret Intelligence Directorate must conduct thorough vetting to ensure no spies are mixed in with the refugees.\"","Zheng Zicheng and Xie Zhiyan both nodded solemnly. The rats within the country had yet to be fully exterminated, and they dared not let new ones slip in.","Wang Shouchen couldn't help but ask, \"Your Majesty, what policy should we adopt for the refugees from Nanyue?\"","The most pressing issue was land. Without land to farm, everything else was meaningless.","After his initial joy, Emperor Mingxi had also pondered this question. People live by food, and food comes from the land. Without land, more arrivals would only invite greater trouble—what could easily turn into a blessing might become a curse.","\"My esteemed ministers, do any of you have a good strategy?\" Emperor Mingxi scanned the room. Unfortunately, Feng Tang, who always had brilliant ideas, was absent. Otherwise, he would surely devise an excellent plan!","Everyone fell silent, deep in thought. After a moment, the Crown Prince spoke up. \"Your Majesty, with Dayan having already captured Nanyue's Walled City and Fengcheng, why not distribute the land within these two prefectures to the people?\"","The Crown Prince recalled what Yue Fuguang had said about land distribution policies. She had suggested that if Dayan seized Nanyue, the land policies should be different.","As to how different, he had glimpsed her ideas through their daily interactions and words. What he needed now was the Emperor and the ministers' approval. With a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity presented by Heaven and the Grand Preceptor, Xie Zhiyan believed that while the interests within Dayan proper remained unchanged, the newly conquered lands could be open to a new land policy. He had to seize this rare chance!","Emperor Mingxi raised his eyes and glanced at his eldest son, pausing to consider the matter. \"Crown Prince, do you have a specific implementation plan?\"","Xie Zhiyan bowed. \"Your Majesty!\" After a quick exchange of glances with his father, he elaborated on his views. \"I believe...\"","While Dayan's monarch and ministers were strategizing over how to allocate the newly acquired lands in Nanyue, at the Hongwen Hall's guest quarters, Gan Tang from Beiye and his party, who had been lingering in Dayan for nearly a year, had gathered again.","In the same tea room, the same seats and same group of people, but this time their topic had shifted from Dongyi's flood disaster to the life-and-death struggle between Nanyue and Dayan.","Yes, a life-and-death struggle!","Watching as detached observers, they could see that this war, waged by Dayan's monarch and ministers united in purpose, had, from the very beginning, not been aimed at simply capturing a city or a piece of land.","The signs were wrong—very wrong."]},{"number":482,"title":"Chapter 482: If South Vietnam Falls","paragraphs":["In past conflicts between nations, there were instances of cities and territories being seized, but usually, after capturing one or two cities, the invaders would not push further due to various reasons, instead waiting for the defeated side to sue for peace by offering concessions.","But this war between Dayan and Nanyue was clearly different. By rights, capturing two cities in succession should have achieved Dayan’s intended objectives, yet even though they accepted Nanyue’s peace talks—and the two countries were about to form a marriage alliance—the fighting at the front showed no sign of stopping.","Dayan clearly did not fear being attacked from behind by other nations while they were engaged on this front.","“What do you all think Dayan is really up to? Could they actually be planning to wipe out Nanyue?”","Bei Ye held his teacup without drinking, merely swirling the liquid to watch the emerald-green tea leaves rise and fall.","When Nanyue was mentioned, he raised his eyebrows and glanced at Gan Tang, who had remained silent the whole time. To be honest, he was finding it increasingly difficult to understand what she was thinking.","Did she truly want to marry the Sixth Prince of Dayan? How could she hesitate between becoming a princess consort and claiming the throne of a queen?","Among those present, Bei Ye was the one most desperate for the supreme seat. Even knowing that his father treated his brothers like pawns and already had a chosen heir, he had never fully given up.","How could he know he wasn’t capable without fighting for it?","Thinking of the agents he had planted in the harem, it was time to set them in motion!","“Isn’t it obvious now? Dayan really intends to swallow Nanyue this time.” Xi Ling slammed his teacup heavily onto the table, producing a loud bang.","The others were puzzled by his sudden outburst. What did Nanyue and Dayan’s affairs have to do with him, a prince of Xiqiang? Why was he so agitated?","Xi Ling realized his lapse and flushed with embarrassment. “Forgive me, everyone. I was just reading the military dispatches. I have to admit, Dayan’s campaign was... was...”","He glanced cautiously at the composed Gan Tang, but did not finish his sentence.","“I understand your meaning, Cousin,” Gan Tang said, seeing his discomfort. She knew he was sparing her pride as a princess of Nanyue by refraining from praising Dayan outright.","“Dayan’s new weapons are indeed formidable. Conquering cities and seizing territory... Nanyue’s defeat is already a foregone conclusion.”","She shook her head, letting out a bitter laugh. “They say these things are also related to the Divine One.”","She pointed vaguely in the direction of the Yu residence. Even a scrap of power leaked from the fingers of a celestial being was beyond what mortals like them could withstand.","Her spirit had been worn down by one incident after another.","Her single statement—“Nanyue cannot resist”—silenced everyone in the room. If Nanyue could not hold out, could Nanzhao, Xiqiang, Beili, and Dongyi?","They had never seen the mysterious weapons, rumored to be louder than thunder.","From intelligence secretly sent by spies, those devices killed swaths of people with each explosion. Storming a city no longer required feeding human lives to the meat grinder.","All it took was tossing that thing at the city gates, and after a rumbling chaos lasting the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, any gate would be blasted wide open!","“What do you think the Divine One is thinking? It’s said that immortals value life and show mercy to the world, and what she does now seems to align with that—but handing out such a devastating weapon...”","This was what Xi Yuanshan could not understand. He even suspected that the intel he had obtained from the black market was somehow connected to the Divine One.","Lan Xuan’er’s beautiful eyes trembled slightly. Though reluctant to admit it, they all had to face reality. “Mercy to the world? If it exists at all, it’s only for Dayan, isn’t it?”","In the end, they were all outsiders. Even if the Divine One had descended as a goddess, her first blessing would always be for the people of Dayan.","Lan Xuan’er was now deeply worried about Nanzhao. The war between Nanyue and Dayan might seem like a conflict between two states, but anyone with eyes knew that Nanyue had Nanzhao’s support behind the scenes.","If Dayan truly intended to swallow Nanyue, would they simply overlook Nanzhao—a piece of fat that had offended them many times and was now covertly backing Nanyue?","She raised her eyes to Gan Tang, her gaze filled with concern. “Sister Tang, what are you thinking? If... if Nanyue truly falls, how will you... will you be treated in Dayan?” Her position would become awkward.","Strangely, when Lan Xuan’er said Nanyue might fall, no one found her words questionable. Instead, they all looked at Gan Tang—the future consort of the Sixth Prince of Dayan, a princess of a fallen nation. Even as a prince’s consort, life would not be easy!","Seeing the worry in Lan Xuan’er’s eyes, Gan Tang patted her hand gently and forced a light smile. “What’s there to worry about? As long as the Divine One is there, even if I become a princess of a fallen state, no one will dare do anything to me.”","What she did not say was that she might well be a precedent for the others. For the sake of their future plans, Dayan would not treat her poorly.","As for what Dayan was planning, she had been observing clearly these days, and a vague guess had formed in her mind. That was why, after weighing the pros and cons, she had ultimately agreed to remain in Dayan for marriage.","If Dayan was truly determined to swallow Nanyue, how long could she sit on the throne even if she fought for it?","It was better to preserve her strength, secure a path of survival for those loyal to her, and add another layer of protection for her own future.","Otherwise, with the men her brother had left her for self-defense—too few for major undertakings—she could still manage a successful return to Nanyue.","Killing off the useless spies Gan Sheng had sent to prevent her return would not be difficult for her.","But now she had found her place. The same could not be said for her good sister, Xuan’er... Gan Tang sighed inwardly, and eventually could not resist reminding her, “Xuan’er, when will you return to your country? If you have the chance, it might be better to make plans early.”","Some things were merely her speculation, and she could not speak them openly. But if Nanyue fell, could the weaker, entangled Nanzhao survive?","If she were Dayan, wielding such sharp weapons, her appetite would only grow. With that thought, she swept her eyes over Bei Ye, Beiyue, Xi Yuanshan, and Xi Ling, before finally landing on Yanji and Oshima, the two brothers from Dongyi, who had remained silent throughout.","Dongyi was still plagued by plague, with many dead—even members of the royal family had not been spared. If Nanyue fell, Nanzhao would be next, and after Nanzhao, Dongyi!","Gan Tang had, after all, been the only one among them in her past life to ascend the throne. Her vision was sharp—just from these guesses, she had hit on seven or eight tenths of the harvesting plans being drawn up by Dayan’s ministers and Yue Fuguang.","“I... I follow my mother’s orders. Until she issues her decree, I can only remain in Dayan,” Lan Xuan’er said, her face full of bitterness.","Her current situation in Nanzhao was no better than Gan Tang’s—perhaps even worse.","Gan Tang might have lost her parents, but she still had her own people and a strong fist.","Lan Xuan’er’s mother, the empress, was still alive, but over the past two years, Nanzhao’s court had been controlled by her elder siblings and their supporters. Much of the support for Nanyue came from behind their backs.","She could not return home. This might partly be her mother’s intent, but at the root, it was that her siblings were guarding against her."]},{"number":483,"title":"Chapter 483: How Did They Lose, and How Can We Win","paragraphs":["Upon hearing Lan Xuan'er's words, Beiyue's gaze flickered. \"Sister Xuan'er staying in Dayan now might not necessarily be a bad thing.\"","Just like himself, staying in Dayan was the only way to survive. If he returned to Beili, the poison in his body might flare up at any moment, and that would truly be the end of him.","Gan Tang nodded in strong agreement. \"I heard that quite a few of my Nanyue citizens have fled to Dayan during the war between our two countries, just in time for the Divine Maiden's bestowal of sweet dew.\"","Her eyes swept over the group, and she lowered her voice slightly. \"You must have received the news too: the Divine Maiden rides in a jasper carriage pulled by winged heavenly horses that can fly through the sky. The sweet dew she bestows works wonders on both crops and people.\"","Thinking of what her informants had written in their secret letters, Gan Tang let out a deep sigh again. \"With Her around, tell me—how can Dayan lose when they face us? How can we possibly win?\"","The more she spoke, the more she felt she should thank Gan Sheng for sending her to marry into Dayan.","Hearing Gan Tang say this, Bei Ye, who was bent on becoming emperor, grew even more worried. He couldn't help lowering his voice. \"Have you noticed that Her power is constantly rising? Think about the range of rainfall the first time, and the range now.\"","\"Besides, she rides a flying chariot... Even if it can't cover a thousand li a day, it must cover several hundred, right?\" Dayan had Yue Fuguang, who not only brought tangible benefits but more importantly served as a symbol that won people's hearts. The Nanyue refugees fleeing here were the best proof of that.","\"They say soldiers in the Nanyue battlefield have defected mid-battle. Is that rumor true or false?\"","His gaze fell on Gan Tang. Bei Ye knew that Gan Tang's intelligence resources were no less than theirs, and she would certainly know more about what happened on the battlefields.","Since Bei Ye asked, Gan Tang no longer tried to cover for the Nanyue army and nodded frankly. \"Brother is right. In the battle of Fengcheng, our army not only suffered heavy losses, but a ten-thousand-strong unit was scared out of their wits by Dayan's formidable weapons and defected on the spot.\"","As for how her dear imperial uncle, who was stationed in Jialing City right next to Fengcheng, had been too afraid to fight, leading to Fengcheng falling in just three days—she didn't go into detail.","After all, Gan Tang still had some face to save. Seeing the Nanyue army fight like this made her own eyes ache.","So it was because of those weapons. Bei Ye's hand, which was pouring tea, paused. He gently set down the pot and casually glanced at Xi Yuanshan before finally venturing a probe. \"Brothers from the Xi family, what do you think of this?\"","\"If Nanyue is conquered, Nan Zhao will surely be next. It might be hard for our two countries to stay out of this. If we don't join hands...\"","They might end up like Nanyue—done for sooner or later.","Yanji, who had been idly tracing patterns on the table with water, suddenly stopped. In his little head swirled big questions: what did he mean by \"after Nanyue comes Nan Zhao\"?","Was Dayan's appetite really that big?","The Dongyi brothers were completely baffled, and everyone else simply ignored them. Those two...","Xi Yuanshan frowned in thought for a moment, then let out a helpless, self-deprecating chuckle. \"These major matters of national diplomacy involving multiple countries are beyond the reach of a powerless, idle prince like me.\"","His mother, ignoring the objections of his adoptive father and maternal uncle, had insisted on sending him back to Xiqiang to reclaim his lineage. It wasn't without the calculation that one day he might ascend the throne.","But by the time he entered Xiqiang and changed back to his original surname, his status was only that of an adopted son.","Xiqiang's royal family had no shortage of sons. Being an adopted son essentially cut off his path to advancement.","To this day, he only held the empty title of prince, constantly targeted and suppressed by his brothers, with little real power.","The fire in his heart had gradually cooled over the past two years.","When Xi Yuanshan said this, Xi Ling was even more straightforward. Smiling, he shook his head at Bei Ye. \"There's no need to mention my situation. I don't want that position anymore. As for Xiqiang's future, let those who care worry about it.\"","He too saw through Bei Ye's intentions. Not only was there no hope for him in the succession struggle, but even if there were, would he dare to openly show any intention of joining forces with another country against Dayan?","Was that asking for a short life?","If they dared to do such a thing, even if Dayan's rulers and ministers didn't know, the True God out there spreading rain and dew would surely find out.","Xi Ling subtly shifted away from Bei Ye. This guy, with his bushy brows and big eyes, had seemed clever before—but now, chasing after a throne that might never be his, he had clearly lost his mind.","He discreetly distanced himself a little more. People who courted death like this weren't worth getting close to.","Seeing that the Xi brothers weren't taking his bait, Bei Ye turned to urge Beiyue, completely missing Xi Ling's slight movement and the flicker of disdain on his face.","\"Brother, what do you think?\" he said, his voice extremely low. \"We should make plans soon and return to our country as quickly as possible.\"","Once war broke out between the nations, they might immediately transform from envoys of goodwill into hostages.","At the mention of returning, Beiyue shook his head frantically. Return? Not even a dog would go back if it were him.","\"Fifth brother, you know my situation. It's not that I don't want to return—I can't go home!\"","He put on a sad expression. \"I don't want to die, and I don't want to get in anyone's way. Let me just muddle along like this.\"","Beiyue looked deeply melancholic. In Bei Ye's eyes, this second imperial brother was as good as finished.","But he had no idea that this seemingly despondent Beiyue was silently cursing in his heart, looking at Bei Ye as if he were already a dead man.","Among those present, Gan Tang understood Beiyue's feelings best. Over the past two days, she had noticed several unusual people among the dowry convoy.","Why unusual? Because all signs suggested they were less like guards and more like assassins—assassins sent by Gan Sheng to kill her.","And Gan Sheng would surely have guessed that she was the one who had poisoned him.","\"Brother Beiyue is right to stay in Dayan for now. When those close to you want to strike in the dark, it's impossible to guard against them.\"","\"As long as we remain in Dayan, the entire nation must ensure our safety.\"","She couldn't help but laugh as she spoke. \"It really does seem safer here than in our own countries.\"","Even if misfortune befell them, and someone tried their best to save them—that someone would probably be from Dayan.","What a huge joke that was, and yet it was the truth.","What Emperor Mingxi had asked the Crown Prince to do spread through the cities and counties around Shangjing within two days, traveling at the speed of Dayan's fastest horses.","The happiest to hear this news, aside from farmers who lived off the land, were those with sick family members.","Ever since they heard the news of the Divine Maiden bestowing sweet dew, these people had been hoping and waiting every day for that compassionate and almighty Junior Preceptor to remember them.","Before the Divine Maiden even arrived, they first heard about the drought demon and the Flower City. As for the Divine Maiden's punishment of the Flower City people, Dayan's citizens naturally sang her praises.","As for those clan heads and elders who thought they held the power of life and death over their people—what they thought didn't matter."]},{"number":484,"title":"Chapter 484: Rainfall in Fengcheng","paragraphs":["At this moment, where was Yue Fuguang, the one being thought of by the rulers of Dayan and the countless common people?","Setting out from Flower City, in no more than five or six days, she had already traveled through the entire regions of Xingzhou and Yizhou. One could say that working from a flying carriage was not only efficient but also far less tiring than riding in a horse-drawn carriage.","Aside from Feng Tang, the people in her flying carriage had changed from He Jin and Yu Huaixian to the two sisters, Shen Chunying and Luo Shendong.","\"Your Excellency, look down there!\"","Yue Fuguang, who had been busy playing with three little white fluffballs, heard Luo Shendong’s exclamation and couldn't help but stop what she was doing. She followed the direction of Luo Shendong's finger and looked down.","What came into view were bombs exploding one after another, sending mud, grass, and debris flying into the air. Mixed in with the debris were splatters of red blood and shreds of flesh!","From the uniforms of the two armies below, it was easy to distinguish which side was the Dayan army and which was the Nanyue army.","The situation on the battlefield was a one-sided crushing defeat.","\"Your Excellency, are we about to win?\" Luo Shendong also pressed against the window to look down.","\"Your Excellency, is that Nanyue's third city, Yucheng, down there? If Generals Xu and Wei take Yucheng, they'll be only four or five hundred li from Nanyue's capital, Gancheng!\"","As long as the Dayan army breached Gancheng, most of Nanyue would be in Dayan’s hands!","\"I hope Generals Xu and Wei can hurry up. In another ten days, both Nanyue and Nanzhao will see heavy rain, and the situation will be almost the same as it is now in Dongyi.\"","Yue Fuguang had heard that Weicheng and Fengcheng, already captured by the Dayan army, were beginning to restore order. So, she thought she would come over to bring some rain, letting the Nanyue people below know that Dayan regarded them as citizens of the same nation and would not treat them differently.","This was also her way of helping Emperor Mingxi win the people's hearts!","Flying past the battlefield littered with blood and bodies, Yue Fuguang turned the carriage back. The area around Fengcheng and Weicheng spanned nearly four hundred li. With her current abilities, she couldn’t finish it in one day, and two days would be too much.","But judging by today’s battle at Yucheng, it was possible that by tomorrow, Yucheng would be Dayan’s territory. She might as well relieve the drought for the people down there while she was at it.","Wherever the Dayan army advanced, her rain would follow—truly a remarkable sight!","[Host, weren’t you curious to see what an ancient battlefield looked like? Why did you only take one glance and leave?]","The system couldn’t understand. Its host had changed bodies, but it seemed her ancestral warrior genes were still tagging along.","It really didn’t get what was so interesting about a bloody battlefield, yet its host would eagerly travel a long way to see it.","\"I did want to see the clash of ancient cold weapons, but I forgot that the Dayan army not only has the weapons and armor forged with the iron-smelting techniques I provided but also gunpowder!","This kind of steamrolling offensive is just a one-sided slaughter, nothing interesting to watch.\"","At least it was nothing like what she had seen in movies and TV shows. There was no epic showdown of cold weapons, as the two sides were too mismatched in strength.","[After Generals Xu and Wei take Yucheng, they probably won’t rush toward Gancheng, but will first capture the neighboring city of Jialing, connecting the captured cities into a continuous line. That way, they’ll have no worries about their rear.]","\"System, isn’t the current defender of Jialing City Nanyue’s Prince Cheng?\"","[Yes, it’s him. This man also covets the throne, especially after learning that Gan Sheng is gravely ill. To preserve his own forces, he’s even more reluctant to venture out and fight.","He lost Weicheng, didn’t reinforce Fengcheng when it was besieged, and now he won’t save Yucheng either. If this man really becomes emperor, he’d be much easier to deal with than Gan Sheng.]","\"Little Zhu, when Wei Shouyi and the others attack Jialing City, keep an eye out. Make sure Prince Cheng doesn’t die, and leave him an escape route if possible.\"","[Does master mean to let Prince Cheng flee back to Gancheng to compete for the throne?]","\"Exactly. Let them fight among themselves. After they’ve worn each other out or a victor emerges, the Dayan army can then swoop in to harvest the spoils. Wouldn’t that be simpler?\"","[When the sandpiper and the clam grapple, it’s the fisherman who gains. Master, what a brilliant idea!]","When Feng Tang heard the phrase \"when the sandpiper and the clam grapple, it’s the fisherman who gains,\" his heart stirred. Although he had never heard that allusion before, he couldn’t help but feel that the Divine Artifact’s analogy was very apt.","They of Dayan were to be that fisherman. If they followed the Junior Preceptor’s strategy, many Dayan soldiers might be spared from dying pointless deaths in sieges.","In this regard, Feng Tang and Yue Fuguang were of one mind. She also hoped that even in war, as few lives as possible would be lost.","\"It’s raining! It’s raining!\"","Everyone in the flying carriage heard the joyful cheers of the people below.","Yue Fuguang wasn’t the type to do good deeds and stay anonymous. Their flying carriage was flying very low at this point, just a few hundred meters above the ground, allowing the Dayan army and the Nanyue people below to clearly see its full outline.","\"Look up! It’s the Divine Maiden!\"","\"The Divine Maiden! The Divine Maiden has bestowed sweet rain upon us!\"","\"Thank the Divine Maiden for her blessing!\"","\"Thank the Divine Maiden for her blessing!\"","When it came to thanking the Divine Maiden for the rain, the Nanyue people did not hold back.","Especially those who had secretly enshrined statues of Yue Fuguang in their homes were busy rushing back to fetch incense and candles.","They would burn incense in her presence right then and there!","Yue Fuguang: \"There’s really no need for that.\" (Mental note)","As for those Nanyue residents who had once mocked their neighbors and fellow villagers for worshipping a foreign girl, they were now filled with nothing but shock and regret!","They had never imagined that the Dayan Junior Preceptor, who had introduced high-yield crop seeds, was genuinely a Divine Maiden—not, as they had initially thought, a mortal elevated to divinity!","Neither was it Dayan fabricating a deity; she was divine by nature, and now that it could no longer be hidden, they were fortunate enough to witness it!","This meant the rumors of the Divine Maiden bringing rain within Dayan’s borders must also be true!","\"So my friend, who lives just across the river that borders Dayan—his letters were all real!\"","A scholarly-looking man stared up at the beautiful celestial carriage pulled by two white flying horses in the sky, his eyes full of sudden realization.","\"Brother Liu, what did you say?\" Another scholar, equally stunned into speechlessness, heard his friend’s murmuring and couldn’t help asking.","\"Ziyi, do you still remember the letter Brother Huang Wei sent me a month ago?\"","\"Brother Liu means... the prophecy that ‘the Divine Maiden descends, and destiny lies with Dayan’ is also real?\" The young man called Ziyi widened his eyes.","They had never seen that inscription plaque in person, but from Brother Huang Wei’s description alone, they knew it was no ordinary object. And those words... they truly made one think.","Although the court had quickly suppressed the matter and strictly forbade discussion, the seed had already been planted in many hearts.","Now, watered by Yue Fuguang’s rain, it was time for it to sprout.","\"Brother Ziyi, do you think such a saying could be false when the Divine Maiden herself has appeared?\"","Brother Liu, the scholar, replied to his classmate while spending some silver coins to buy a few sticks of incense from a woman.","Following the example of the people on the street, he bowed respectfully toward the flying carriage in the sky."]},{"number":485,"title":"Chapter 485: Why doesn’t the goddess look like the statue we worship at home","paragraphs":["He lowered his voice and delivered a soul-searching question to his devout friend who was burning incense: \"Brother Liu, when did you change? This isn’t what you used to say!\"","Among their circle of friends, Brother Liu had once been the staunchest disbeliever in the tale of the Divine Maiden.","Whenever the Goddess of Dayan was mentioned, the disdain on his face practically spilled over. But it hadn’t been long—just a sighting of the Divine Maiden’s manifestation—and now this guy was the first to kneel!","Zhang Ziyi stood there, surrounded by common folk and fellow students who were all earnestly offering incense to the heavens. He was the only one still standing, and it made him stick out like a sore thumb.","Before long, he earned glares from several elderly men and women.","Zhang Ziyi glanced around. Besides Brother Liu, the other classmates who had slipped out of the academy were kneeling down smoothly too. With great solemnity, he knelt beside Brother Liu and gently nudged him with his shoulder. \"Brother Liu, give me three sticks of incense!\"","Below, the entire city’s populace—men and women, young and old—was united in one task: kneeling in the heavy rain to burn incense for Yue Fuguang.","Inside the carriage, Yue Fuguang felt the abundant power of faith filling her body and stretched with satisfaction.","\"Little Zhu, the people of Nanyue really are giving too much!\" In a city of fewer than two hundred thousand, the energy she received was almost on par with the faith power from medium-sized cities.","【Perhaps they’ve been plagued by drought for too long. This rain of yours has saved countless lives. Master, look—the rows of fresh graves on the outskirts of the city are all for those who fell in battle.】","Yue Fuguang thought of the heavy rain due in ten days. These people had already endured a drought; if a flood were to follow, how many ordinary folks would perish?","\"System, is there any way to stop the rainfall?\"","She knew the art of summoning clouds and rain, but she didn’t know how to halt a torrential downpour like a hole in the sky itself!","【Host, the Seal of Sky-Binding Cloud-Locking, the Ten-Thousand-Li Cloud Screen, the Rain Prohibition Command, and the Cloud Dispelling Art all meet your needs. It’s up to you which one to choose.】","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow, surprised at the system’s abundant inventory. Where did it get things not even available in the shop?","Had it stolen them from the background again?","\"System, be careful! Don’t let the main system catch on and drag me down!\"","She was still a rookie who hadn’t even completed a single mission world. If she got implicated, all her future plans would go up in smoke!","The system found her words baffling. It was just selling some of its own stock—what did that have to do with the old bigwig of the main system?","Yue Fuguang had no idea what the system was thinking. She focused on examining the differences among these methods.","Seal of Sky-Binding Cloud-Locking: Uses spiritual power to set up a massive formation across the heavens, \"locking\" the rain clouds inside. The clouds could churn within but couldn’t release a single drop of rain.","Rain Prohibition Command (Word as Law): With just a single word or phrase, the rules of heaven and earth shift. Within a hundred li, rain ceases and clouds disperse.","Ten-Thousand-Li Cloud Screen: Instead of destroying the rain clouds, it erects a transparent barrier between heaven and earth, diverting all rain elsewhere. The barrier might be formless and intangible or transform into a shimmering, multicolored dome. While protecting one area’s tranquility, the sweet rain could still nourish other lands.","Cloud Dispelling Art: Uses gentle spiritual power to move clouds, redirecting rain belts to drought-stricken lands. This method goes against no natural order, solves the immediate crisis, and aligns with the way of the world.","Yue Fuguang read through them all, finding each appealing, but with her current abilities, she couldn’t perform the Seal of Sky-Binding Cloud-Locking—she didn’t know formations.","As for buying formation books from the system, she might have done it if she had no other options, but with several paths still open, she wasn’t about to waste money unnecessarily.","The Rain Prohibition Command involved word-as-law magic. She could control rain with her voice, but only over small areas and for short durations. Faced with Nanyue’s coming month-long, unending rain, even exhausting herself wouldn’t make it work.","The Ten-Thousand-Li Cloud Screen seemed possible, but when Yue Fuguang considered that rain would fall across Nanyue as a whole, and the Dayan army would keep pushing their offensive, she couldn’t just divert the rain elsewhere.","\"System, I’ll take the Cloud Dispelling Art. When the time comes, I’ll transfer all the rain clouds into Dayan’s territory. That’ll save me the trouble of making it rain there myself.\"","【Host, excellent choice! The Cloud Dispelling Art is a good pick.】 After a half-hearted compliment, the system got to the point. 【Host, the discounted price is 8,888 points. Trust in your system—you won’t get ripped off or cheated.】","Hah!","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes, didn’t haggle, and paid the points generously.","Now that she had a way to control the impending heavy rain in Nanyue, she decided to grant them another favor and give them an early warning.","As a woman of action, she instantly changed into a more impressive flowing celestial gown.","Shen Chunying and Luo Shendong watched, wide-eyed, as their mistress’s clothing flickered with light and transformed into something new.","The sisters gasped briefly. Shen Chunying’s eyes sparkled. \"Mistress, this gown is beautiful!\" she praised sincerely, making Yue Fuguang slightly embarrassed.","Luo Shendong, starry-eyed, nodded vigorously in agreement with her sister. \"It’s as pretty as the one you wore at the Helian Mountains!\"","Of course it looked good—it was bought from the system shop, and the price was equally stunning.","\"Is Mistress planning to go out?\" Normally, their mistress didn’t dress up so lavishly unless she was about to meet someone.","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"I’m going out to meet Dayan’s new citizens.\"","Before her figure vanished through the carriage door, she couldn’t help but instruct, \"You two stay put in the carriage.\"","She was afraid that the excitable Luo Shendong might, in a moment of enthusiasm, fall out the window.","\"Don’t worry, Mistress. I’ll keep an eye on Shendong!\" As the older sister, Shen Chunying naturally understood her younger sister’s temperament.","Yue Fuguang nodded, stepped out of the carriage, and as she set foot onto the air, Feng Tang, sitting on the carriage shaft, knew his mistress could fly. Still, watching her step into the void made his heart leap into his throat.","The moment Yue Fuguang’s foot touched the empty air, a golden lotus bloomed beneath it. She walked down, descending a hundred or so meters, each step spawning a new lotus beneath her feet.","Lotus after lotus unfurled, paving the path she had come.","Within moments, the lotuses behind her slowly dissipated, dissolving into countless specks of light that merged into the pouring rain.","Soon, someone spotted the small yet unmissable figure in moon-white robes high above. Her gown, woven as if from moonlight, trailed through the void, swaying gently with her steps.","There was no embroidery on the skirt, no jewels sewn in—just the liquid sheen of moonlight itself.","At her waist, a jade-green ribbon fluttered, its two ends trailing behind her like slender fish swimming through the air.","\"Lotuses! The Divine Maiden is stepping down on lotuses!\"","\"It’s the Divine Maiden!\"","\"The Divine Maiden has come down to see us!\"","\"Wah, I’ve finally seen the Divine Maiden!\"","\"Why doesn’t the Divine Maiden look like the statue I have at home?\" Someone realized the carver had cheated them. The expensive shrine they had bought hadn’t even captured the true appearance of the revered one."]},{"number":486,"title":"Chapter 486: Heavy Rain Warning","paragraphs":["The divine maiden statue in his home didn't possess even one ten-thousandth of the presence of the goddess now descending from the heavens above!","Wind and rain both parted around her. Yue Fuguang stopped her descent when she was still three to four hundred meters above the ground.","Her skirts drew together, and beneath her feet bloomed a great white lotus, glowing like a lantern made of lotus petals against the dim, overcast sky.","Behind her stood her divine manifestation—solemn, majestic, yet radiating compassion for all living beings.","The Divine Maiden lowered her gaze. The downpour softened from a roaring torrent into a fine, drizzling curtain of rain. Among the common folk who looked up at the deity, some, for reasons they could not explain, suddenly found tears streaming down their faces. A nameless emotion surged in their chests—something that made them choke up one moment and want to shout aloud the next.","Every eye below was fixed on Yue Fuguang. In that instant, her image became impossibly clear—not that her features had sharpened, but her very presence had become undeniable.","Every single person realized the same thing at the same moment: the being standing in the sky was not an illusion, not a symbol, but a living, breathing deity.","She stood there the way a mountain stands there. No words needed. No gestures needed. Simply existing in that space was enough to make every soul below comprehend their own insignificance.","Yue Fuguang waited until the emotions of the crowd had settled, then she spoke.","Her voice was not loud, but it rode the wind, reaching every ear with perfect clarity.","It was like moonlight falling on water—neither cold nor warm. Each word landed on the heart like a bead of dew: cool to the touch, yet leaving an inexplicably lingering aftertaste.","She said, \"I am Yue Fuguang.\"","Five simple words, yet they inexplicably put countless hearts at ease.","\"Your humble subject pays respects to the Divine Maiden!\"","\"Your student pays respects to the Divine Maiden!\"","\"Your subordinate pays respects to the Divine Maiden!\"","\"Your warrior pays respects to the Divine Maiden!\"","\"Your humble daughter pays respects to the Divine Maiden!\"","A cascade of self-introductions rose up—chaotic, jumbled, yet strangely harmonious.","Yue Fuguang stood at the center of the sky, her eyelids lowered as she gazed down at the hundreds of thousands of upturned faces spread across the hundred li around her. Every eye reflected awe and reverence.","She spoke again.","This time, her voice carried even more weight and conviction: \"The moon invades the Nine Ditches—floodwaters will engulf the land.\"","Eight plain words, delivered as calmly as if she were stating a fact utterly unrelated to herself.","No pressure. No intimidation. Not even a hint of emotion.","But everyone sensed something. It was not a warning, not a threat. On closer reflection, it seemed laced with a trace of goodwill and pity.","Still, the common folk had no idea what \"the moon invades the Nine Ditches\" meant. But \"floodwaters will engulf the land\"—that, they seemed to grasp. Did it mean rain? Wasn't it already raining?","Seeing the sea of bewildered faces below, Yue Fuguang had no choice but to continue speaking in the cryptic, oracle-like manner she had adopted: \"The ditches overflow, a hundred rivers boil.\"","\"A hundred rivers boil\"—surely even they could understand that!","Zhang Ziyi edged closer to Liu Hui and whispered, \"Brother Liu, do you understand what the Divine Maiden is saying?\"","Liu Hui furrowed his brow. His grades at the academy had always been excellent, and he had read widely in miscellaneous texts, including some on celestial phenomena. Though he could not recall the exact meaning of \"the moon invades the Nine Ditches,\" combined with the following twelve characters, it was not hard to deduce—it had to do with rain. And heavy rain, at that.","Otherwise, why would the Divine Maiden, after blessing them with rainfall, make a special appearance to deliver such a speech? He had a feeling she was issuing a warning to the people of Dayan.","It also meant that even before they had fully accepted their new identity, the Divine Maiden had already acknowledged them.","\"The Divine Maiden seems to have already accepted us as people of Dayan.\"","Liu Hui's words were abrupt and vague, catching Zhang Ziyi completely off guard. The latter blinked his round, innocent eyes at him. \"Huh?\"","\"Brother Liu means—the Divine Maiden is warning us? Fengcheng is going to see heavy rain, or even... flooding?\"","A scholar standing in front of the two turned around and looked at Liu Hui. Like Liu Hui, he was a top student—if Liu Hui could figure it out, so could he.","Liu Hui glanced up at Yue Fuguang in the sky and spoke quietly. \"Brother Xinzhi is right. That is exactly how I understand it too.\"","\"Flooding?\" Zhang Ziyi, the less academically inclined of the group, could not stop himself from raising his voice. \"But we've been in a drought for eight months! How could there suddenly be flooding? Where would the water even come from?\"","Yes—where would the water come from? Even the wind was dry. How could there possibly be that much rain?","Having his guess confirmed by his classmate Liu Hui, Fang Xinzhi's expression darkened. He could not help but repeat those words: \"Floodwaters will engulf the land.\"","Yue Fuguang naturally heard their whispered discussion. Seeing that intelligent people had finally understood her meaning, she pressed on with further hints. \"The moon veils the Celestial Abyss—water will pour without cease.\"","Understand now? The rain will be very, very heavy!","Her voice continued, still in that same flat, calm tone, but the urgency of the warning was unmistakable. \"Star halos darken to blue-black—one month without pause.\" In ten days, the rain will fall, and it won't stop for a month or more!","[Host, can't you just tell them directly: in ten days, heavy rain, continuous for a month, the city will be flooded and houses destroyed? Look at all this cryptic gobbledygook—how many illiterate common folk below can actually understand you?]","«If I said it plainly, wouldn't that be a letdown for my divine image? Look at my homeland—all those prophetic sayings are vague, enigmatic, without head or tail. This manner of speaking is practically my family heirloom!»","The system nearly laughed in exasperation at her claiming her \"family heirloom.\"","While Yue Fuguang was bickering with her system, the clever ones below were slowly piecing together her successive pronouncements about celestial omens. They were catching on—this was the Divine Maiden issuing them a warning!","\"Divine Maiden, does this mean... Fengcheng... Fengcheng will face a flood in the future?\" Liu Hui finally could not hold back. Boldly raising his voice, he asked the question outright and then solemnly bowed to her. \"Please, Divine Maiden, clarify for us—your student Liu Hui, on behalf of the people of Fengcheng, will be forever grateful!\"","Hearing the word \"flood,\" every single resident of Fengcheng in the crowd turned pale. They stared in horror at Liu Hui, then looked back up at the all-powerful Divine Maiden in the sky.","Some quick thinkers immediately joined in bowing and pleading. \"Please, Divine Maiden, clarify! This old man is forever grateful!\"","\"Please, Divine Maiden, clarify! This humble wife is forever grateful!\"","Though their mouths begged for clarity, in their hearts they all secretly hoped to hear a denial from her lips.","A trace of pity flickered across Yue Fuguang's face. As she looked down at the crowd, she genuinely wore an expression of merciful compassion.","But inwardly, she quietly breathed a sigh of relief. Since someone asked, I can finally drop this cryptic act!","Her voice remained cold, utterly devoid of emotion. \"In ten days, the entire lands of Nanyue and Nanzhao will receive heavy rain. The downpour will be continuous, lasting for over a month without stop.\"","\"Good heavens!\"","\"Waaah—what sin have we committed? Heaven is simply not giving us a way to survive!\"","\"Old Heavenly Father, open your eyes and look upon us, we beg you!\"","Yue Fuguang's single short sentence was met with a wave of weeping.","She didn't actually know whether these natural disasters were truly Heaven's doing, but the common folk clearly all believed Heaven was punishing them.","Amid the cries and sobs, her words continued. \"The waters will crest the dikes. The flood will surge into the city!\""]},{"number":487,"title":"Chapter 487: Great Yan Person","paragraphs":["If the nonstop January downpour was like a massive boulder thrown into a tranquil lake, instantly sending up a thousand waves, then the words \"flood waters entering the city\" were nothing less than drops of water into a searing cauldron of oil—the entire city erupted at once!","\"Oh, my heavens above, are they trying to drive us to our deaths?\" Some were already sobbing uncontrollably, while others bit their lips hard, tears streaming down their faces.","\"Run, we have to run!\" Someone leapt up like a madman, desperate to rush home and pack before fleeing.","\"Run where? The Divine Maiden said there's heavy rain in both Nanzhao and Nanyue! We... we can only wait to die...\"","The words \"wait to die\" struck like a hammer, and the middle-aged man's face instantly drained of color, all will to live vanishing in that moment.","Eight straight months of drought had already piled misery upon families that were none too well-off to begin with. Now with days of relentless rain and floodwaters swallowing the streets, most people had been shoved to the very edge of despair!","\"Right, the Divine Maiden—let's beg the Divine Maiden to save us!\" Someone managed to pull themselves together from the shock and looked up at the sky.","But when they did, all they saw was the fine, dense curtain of falling rain. There was no trace of Yue Fuguang or her flying carriage anywhere.","When someone realized the flying light had vanished from the sky, despair overtook them and they broke down sobbing, clutching their heads. \"Divine Maiden... could it be that even the Divine Maiden has abandoned us?\"","\"Careful what you say!\" The words were barely out when they were cut off by a loud voice—it was Liu Hui.","Liu Hui exchanged a glance with Fang Zhixin, and Fang Zhixin stepped forward on his own initiative, addressing the crowd in a loud voice. \"I am Fang Zhixin, a student of Fengcheng Academy. Please, everyone, hear me out. Today the Divine Maiden showed her mercy by sending down blessed rain to relieve our suffering, and she warned us before the danger arrived. These two deeds alone are already a great kindness to us!\"","His sharp gaze swept across the crowd. \"We may go and beseech the Divine Maiden, but you must all understand, neighbors—the Divine Maiden has no obligation to take care of us!\"","\"We... aren't we also... Da Yan people now?\" A man stammered this out, his face turning from pale to red.","He snuck a sheepish glance at those around him, but found no contempt as he had expected. In fact, a few of the younger ones nodded in agreement. Only some of the older folks furrowed their brows at his words, though not a single word of reprimand was spoken.","Liu Hui, standing beside Fang Zhixin, let out a light laugh. He looked the man straight in the eye and asked, word by word, \"Do you really believe that yourself? Do you truly accept that you are a Da Yan citizen and not a Nanyue one? Do you all genuinely embrace your new identity from the bottom of your hearts?\"","His gaze swept over faces that were either embarrassed or ashamed. \"The Divine Maiden sent rain down on our Fengcheng only because this land now belongs to Da Yan. If I'm not mistaken, Weicheng received rain as well. As for other parts of Nanyue, unless ten days have passed, I don't believe a single drop will fall.\"","He gave a bitter shake of his head. \"Do you think the Divine Maiden doesn't know what you're all thinking?\"","His gaze suddenly turned even sharper than Fang Zhixin's. \"The divine cannot be deceived! All of you, remember this well! And do not speak recklessly—it harms others and yourselves!\"","The people around him were soaked in cold sweat, their clothes clinging to them, wet and clammy—whether from rain or perspiration, no one could tell.","The young man who had first called himself a Da Yan citizen now had a face the color of pig's liver. He nervously twisted the hem of his clothes with his fingers and asked Liu Hui in a low, timid voice, \"Scholar Liu, is our court really losing battle after battle?\"","His voice grew smaller and smaller as he spoke, but it was still loud enough for everyone standing nearby to hear. If this had been said a dozen or so days ago, he wouldn't have dared even in his wildest dreams.","But now, with Da Yan troops both inside and outside the city, saying such things didn't put him in fear of the Nanyue officials.","Liu Hui lowered his brows, pondered for a moment, then said with certainty, \"Based on the intelligence I've received, Nanyue has faced Da Yan in five battles and lost all five—two cities lost in less than two months!\"","Fang Zhixin, however, pursed his lips and said, \"Brother Liu, your information is already outdated.\"","\"How so?\" Liu Hui raised an eyebrow, turning to face Fang Zhixin as if asking for his wisdom.","Fang Zhixin made a slight bow with his hands toward him. \"From what I understand, the Da Yan army has already advanced to Yu City as of late.\"","Liu Hui's expression changed. \"Brother Fang, are you saying the defenders of Yu City are doomed to fall?\"","Fang Zhixin spread his hands helplessly. \"Brother Liu, with a weapon like that thing called the Heaven-Shaking Thunder in their arsenal, do you really think those Nanyue army roughnecks stand a chance against the Da Yan forces?\"","Liu Hui was visibly taken aback by this statement, and couldn't help but size up Fang Zhixin more carefully.","Facing Liu Hui's scrutiny, Fang Zhixin remained perfectly composed, even flashing him a wry smile. \"To be able to bask in the Divine Maiden's grace even for just one day—that is my fortune, Fang Zhixin's honor!\"","\"So... Nanyue is about to fall?\" The young man didn't understand the subtext between the two scholars. All he knew was that after listening to them, he had reached a conclusion: Nanyue was done for.","The young man's words were bold, no doubt about it. In the old days, that single sentence would have been enough to have him dragged off to the execution grounds at the west end of town.","But now, few people paid his audacious talk any mind. Instead, all their thoughts were consumed by the question: if Nanyue was really falling, what were they supposed to do?","Earlier, there had been a lingering hope in some hearts—that the court would come back and reclaim Fengcheng eventually. But after hearing the two scholars speak, they began to have their doubts.","For a moment, a heavy silence fell over the crowd, broken only by the sound of rain pelting down all around them.","\"Uh... the real question now isn't whether Nanyue will fall—it's whether we're going to die!\"","Someone nodded in agreement. \"Right, right, right. Whether Nanyue falls or not is a problem for the emperor and the officials to worry about. But the Divine Maiden said this heavy rain could kill a lot of people!\"","\"Maybe our lives will end before Nanyue's does!\" That sentence struck straight through many hearts, but it was the painful truth.","\"Exactly—who's the emperor, what country we're a part of—for us common folks, isn't life the same either way? If the Divine Maiden can save us, then... then I'm more than willing to be a Da Yan person!\"","\"My kids are still young—I can't die. They haven't even had a single good day in their lives, and I refuse to let them die like this!\"","A young, sturdy man with tears brimming in his eyes shouted into the empty, raining sky, \"Divine Maiden! I, Zhang Laosan, am willing to be a Da Yan citizen! I beg the Divine Maiden to save us!\"","As soon as his words fell, more and more people followed his example, shouting up into the endless rain, willingly declaring themselves Da Yan citizens, begging only for her to appear and save them.","Did Yue Fuguang hear all of this?","Of course she did—every word, without missing a single syllable. Because she had never actually gone far. Taking advantage of the crowd's daze, she had swiftly returned to her carriage and hidden it within the churning storm clouds.","[Host, that was a brilliant move on your part. These people, without you having to persuade them at all, are already starting to turn their loyalties on their own!]","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"This kind of acceptance is only temporary.\" This kind of acceptance they were showing was merely a shift in thinking driven by self-preservation in a time of crisis.","Truly erasing the mark of one's former nation was never such an easy thing.","It would take at least a decade, maybe even several decades, and two or three generations of effort before they could forget their homeland.","But people always gravitate toward the strong. As long as Da Yan continued to grow more powerful, these commoners longing for a stable life would eventually come around for real.","[So what do we do next? The cloud-dispelling technique isn't hard to learn, but actually using it will take a fair bit of effort on your part, won't it?]"]},{"number":488,"title":"Chapter 488: News from Fengcheng","paragraphs":["Although its host had grown quickly enough, she wasn't like those cultivators in the immortal cultivation world; her foundation was built on incense-fire \"sainthood,\" which was vastly different from someone who relied entirely on their own cultivation.","No wonder its host looked down on the path of incense and faith. Indeed, power cultivated through one's own efforts was far more reliable to wield.","\"Wait.\"","[Wait for what?]","\"For the heavy rain you mentioned to arrive, and the flood to come.\" If these people weren't made to truly suffer, how could they ever cherish the hard-won peace and stability?","She was human too, and she understood humanity's flaws well. Most people didn't cherish things that came too easily, and after enough times, they might even come to take them for granted.","\"If they don't beg, and I go out of my way to help uninvited, wouldn't that make me look cheap!\"","The system processed the data and understood Yue Fuguang's meaning at once. [Feng City, Wei City, and that Yu City too—when the time comes, whoever shows the most sincerity, we'll help them first!","Host, speaking of your warning today, do you think the people and the courts of Nan Shao and Nan Yue will believe it?]","Believe it or not?","This question didn't keep Yue Fuguang and the system waiting long. Just as she began to pour rain freely across Lianzhou, the system relayed the latest news it had received.","[Host, your warning has caused an uproar in both Nan Yue and Nan Shao. The citizens of both countries are scrambling to pack their belongings and flee to Da Yan.","Fortunately, the Da Yan army received your message in advance and has already sealed the border.]","\"Aren't spies and soldiers from the Nan Yue and Nan Shao armies mixed in among these people?\"","[Host, you're right. Of the civilians rushing to the border trying to force their way into Da Yan, a full seventy percent are disguised soldiers from the two armies.","The real civilians are locked inside their cities, and even the roads out of the villages are sealed off. Without real strength, moving an inch is nearly impossible.]","\"Isn't this all standard procedure!\" Yue Fuguang wasn't particularly surprised by this outcome. The importance of population to a country didn't need explaining—especially in an agrarian civilization, where people weren't just labor but also potential soldiers. A massive loss of population was no different from bleeding the nation dry.","The emperors and high officials sitting loftily above didn't care about the life or death of one or two commoners, but when two hundred thousand people started to flee, they'd feel the pain too. Preventing the people from escaping was definitely something they'd do.","[Host, guess what happened with that rain you sent down over Feng City and Wei City five days ago?]","\"What do you mean 'what happened'? Didn't it already relieve the famine for the people within those two cities? Is there more to this?\"","That made sense—news must have spread to other citizens of Nan Yue, and perhaps, for the sake of that rain, their hearts would lean a little toward Da Yan.","After all, for most common folk, who sat on the throne mattered less to them than reaping a few extra bushels of grain from the fields.","You could put a dog on the throne, and as long as it filled their bellies and gave them a stable life, they probably wouldn't care.","They might even praise the emperor for being so wise.","[The people across all of Nan Yue heard about this—who wouldn't envy the citizens of Feng City and Wei City? Even the people on the Nan Shao border secretly hoped Da Yan would take them in too.]","Not long ago, quite a few Nan Shao citizens had fled to Da Yan just like the Nan Yue people. The rumors about the drought demon had come in around that time.","After the tragedy of ordinary people being burned alive as suspected drought demons, and following its host's spectacular display of divine power in Huacheng, Da Yan had shut down the border crossing with Nan Shao. That was why those slow-moving Nan Shao citizens were now slapping their thighs in regret.","[But as for who's most gutted about all this—host, want to take a guess?]","Yue Fuguang heard the system's \"time to guess\" game again, and the hand that was tugging at Caramel's ear paused. She said in a deadpan tone, \"Well, it's definitely not my Caramel.\"","[Host, it's Yu City! The citizens of Yu City, which Da Yan just conquered, are the most shattered! Five days ago, the Da Yan army just marched into the city.","At the time, there were still small groups of Nan Yue soldiers hiding among the civilians, sneaking attacks on lone Da Yan troops. Because of that, Da Yan lost over a hundred men.","Two days later, news that the Divine Maiden had brought sweet rain to the people of Feng City and Wei City reached the ears of Yu City's residents—the closest city to them. You should have seen the looks on their faces.]","With that, the system thoughtfully showed Yue Fuguang a video.","Yu City's land was cracked open like a turtle's shell. Whether in the town or the countryside, the wells were bone-dry, leaving only mud at the bottom. Every day, the people knelt at the City God Temple praying for rain, their knees bleeding, yet the sky still blazed an aching blue, not a cloud in sight.","News of the Divine Maiden sending blessed dew to Feng City and Wei City arrived precisely under these circumstances, at noon two days later.","At that time, the bloodstains left from the battle between the Nan Yue army and the Da Yan army had still not been fully cleaned up. The Nan Yue soldiers trapped inside the city had mixed in with the civilians, launching sneak attacks on Da Yan soldiers everywhere.","The two countries were at war, yet with Da Yan having successfully taken Yu City, daily trade was unaffected, so merchants continued to move freely between the various towns and cities.","That day, a traveling merchant who had just returned from the neighboring city of Fengcheng entered Yucheng through the northern gate. His water skins were all filled to the brim, and this time, the goods in the cart behind him were not needles and threads, nor herbs and grain, but the thing the people of Yucheng needed most—water.","\"Old Fei, you've got a grin a mile wide. Did you rake in a good profit on this trip?\"","Traveling merchant Fei had barely set foot in the city when he ran into two familiar faces.","\"Shopkeeper Liu, Shopkeeper Qian.\" He smiled and clasped his hands in greeting to both men. \"Your humble servant here runs but a small trade, earning only a bit of honest sweat. I can't compare to you two, with your grand businesses and vast estates.\"","Shopkeeper Liu, a man of about forty with a goatee, wore a gray silk robe that, due to the water shortage, had grown rather crumpled. He waved a hand dismissively. \"Yucheng's dry spell, on top of the war between the two kingdoms—my little shop hasn't opened its doors in three days straight.\"","He glanced cautiously at the Dayan soldiers patrolling nearby, men who were disciplined and showed not the slightest inclination to plunder the common folk. \"If these fellows truly won't rob the people, I plan to reopen tomorrow.\"","Just from these past few days alone, these Dayan troops were far better than the Southern Yue soldiers of their own.","Standing beside him, Shopkeeper Qian was of a similar age, though he was stouter, his dark blue silk clothing stretched taut over his plump frame. He nodded as well. \"Old Liu and I have the same plan. If today passes peacefully, we'll open our doors tomorrow.\"","With that, he cast a glance at Old Fei across from him. His round, fleshy face showed a look of surprise, and a sharp glint flashed through his small eyes.","He stepped forward, drew close to Old Fei, and looked him over carefully from head to toe several times. \"Old Fei, you... you—what's this?\" He pointed at Old Fei's clothes, then at his own and Shopkeeper Liu's crumpled, days-unwashed robes. \"Water—where did you get water?\"","Without enough water, a man couldn't possibly be this clean all over. Even if he'd just come back from a trade run outside the city, he was still far cleaner than the two of them.","Shopkeeper Qian even leaned in and sniffed at him. If it weren't for the fact that they were all men, all acquaintances, and that Old Fei looked a bit older than his years—which is to say, appeared haggard—one might have mistaken Shopkeeper Qian for flirting with a respectable middle-aged man!"]},{"number":489,"title":"Chapter 489: Burn It for Me, Do You Think I'll Get It","paragraphs":["Old Fei saw how he was acting and didn't get angry. Instead, he burst out laughing. To the citizens of Yucheng, who had just survived a war and were still enduring a drought, his laughter sounded somewhat jarring and out of place.","\"You two noticed? Little brother here really isn't short on water right now.\" He patted the cart behind him. \"This time I made a trip to Fengcheng, and I only brought back one thing.\"","\"Old Fei, you went to Fengcheng? How are things over there?\" This was asked by Shopkeeper Liu, whose eldest daughter had married into Fengcheng two years ago. Ever since he and his old wife learned that Fengcheng had been taken by the Dayan army, they had been worried sick.","Shopkeeper Qian, on the other hand, was more concerned about the water problem. \"Old Fei, give your big brother the straight truth here—does Fengcheng have water? What goods did you bring back from Fengcheng? Considering how our two families have gotten along in the past, your big brother wants to reserve some in advance.\"","By saying this, Shopkeeper Qian was essentially planning to pay for the goods as a fee for the information.","Old Fei saw the two of them staring at him expectantly, so he didn't drag it out. \"To be honest with you two, the only goods I brought back this time is water—water brought all the way from Fengcheng.\"","Old Fei glanced at the squads of Dayan soldiers passing by. He wasn't afraid these two would swindle him, nor was he afraid the desperately thirsty citizens of Yucheng would try to seize his water. He had seen how the Dayan soldiers in Fengcheng conducted themselves, and he figured those in Yucheng couldn't be much different.","He wanted to quickly trade the water for silver and supplies, then flee with his family.","The Divine Maiden had said heavy rain would come in ten days, and two days had already passed. Time was running out for him.","\"Brother Fei, are you telling the truth? The cart really is full of water?\" A greedy glint flickered in Shopkeeper Qian's small eyes, and his address shifted from \"Old Fei\" to \"Brother Fei.\"","He wasn't thinking about robbing Old Fei of his water, but his eyes were full of calculations as he wondered how he could get his hands on more water. Even if the price were higher, he'd accept it.","Shopkeeper Liu's focus was slightly different from Shopkeeper Qian's. Upon hearing about the water, his eyes also lit up. \"Brother Fei, did you haul this water all the way from Fengcheng? If Fengcheng isn't short on water anymore, then where did the water come from?\"","Just a few days ago, he had received a message sent by his daughter. Fengcheng was in the same drought as Yucheng. His two grandchildren, a boy and a girl, didn't even dare cry anymore—every tear was water!","How could Fengcheng suddenly have water just a few days later? Where did it come from? Did it fall from the sky?","Just as the thought crossed Shopkeeper Liu's mind, Old Fei's voice reached his ears. \"Of course it fell from the sky. The Divine Maiden herself came to Fengcheng and brought down sweet rain from the heavens!\"","\"The Divine Maiden?\" Shopkeeper Qian froze with his hand halfway to lifting the cart's curtain, then turned around to stare at Old Fei, trying to read his face for any signs of lying.","\"Isn't the Divine Maiden the deity of Dayan? For the past few months, everything we've heard is that She only brings rain and blessing to the people within Dayan's borders. Why would She come to our Nanyue?\"","Shopkeeper Liu also nodded vigorously. He thought Shopkeeper Qian had a point. Had Old Fei mistaken cheap wine for water and drunk too much, making him spout nonsense to fool the two of them?","\"Old Fei, be straight with your big brother. My friend and I will buy all the water on your cart. We'll pay twenty percent above market price—guaranteed you won't lose out.\"","Old Fei looked at the two of them, their faces utterly refusing to believe a word he said, and his expression was full of helplessness. How was it that the rare times he actually told the truth, no one believed him!","\"I tell you both, never mind Fengcheng—even Weicheng on the border doesn't lack water now, and that's all thanks to the Divine Maiden.\"","His voice rose slightly, and the words happened to reach the ears of a squad of Dayan patrol soldiers who had just passed by them.","\"Fengcheng and Weicheng are now under Dayan's rule. The Divine Maiden, in Her benevolence, appeared in the sky two days ago to relieve that drought and brought a great downpour.\"","His eyes suddenly sparkled. \"This little brother saw it with his own eyes!\"","\"The Divine Maiden rode a flying chariot pulled by heavenly horses across the sky. She wore a beautiful celestial gown, stepped on lotus blossoms, and with a single wave of Her sleeve came the rain. It rained in Fengcheng for a whole day, and presumably in neighboring Weicheng as well. Before I left, the crops on the outskirts of Fengcheng had all revived!\"","It was lucky that Nanyue had never been short of water before. Eight months without rain had dried up the rivers, but by luck, one could still find springs in the mountains that hadn't fully run dry, which preserved a little bit of the crops in the fields. But thinking about the great flood that would come with the rain in a few days, those crops wouldn't last much longer anyway.","Old Fei gestured wildly as he spoke, not noticing that as he described the Divine Maiden bringing rain to Fengcheng, more and more people had slowly gathered around him.","Besides the Dayan soldiers, there were far more ordinary citizens of Yucheng.","Apart from Old Fei's voice, the crowd was eerily silent. Everyone seemed to hold their breath, afraid of missing a single word of his story.","From the video, Yue Fuguang also noticed that when Old Fei mentioned how Fengcheng had rain for a whole day, many people involuntarily swallowed their saliva.","\"And there I was with the citizens of Fengcheng, standing right on the main street, looking up and seeing the Divine Maiden descend from the sky, one lotus bloom at a time! She—\"","What followed was a string of praise so effusive that Yue Fuguang herself began to doubt whether the Divine Maiden he was describing was really her.","You'd need at least ten layers of filter to say all those things!","\"System, how does a traveling merchant come up with so many words of praise?\"","[Probably learned it from those scholars at the Fengcheng Academy! After you left, those scholars wrote countless essays praising you, and they even burned them as offerings in front of your shrine!]","The smile that had been blooming on Yue Fuguang's face suddenly cracked. \"Burned them to me? As if I could receive those!\"","Yue Fuguang snorted twice and went back to watching her video.","The crowd remained silent. The Dayan soldiers listened to Old Fei's unbridled flattery of their Divine Maiden with looks of shared pride on their faces. Some of the younger soldiers couldn't help puffing out their chests when the people of Yucheng glanced their way.","The squad leader even unconsciously reached toward the pouch at his waist. This fellow talked even better than the storytellers at the teahouse. He deserved a reward!","Shopkeeper Qian saw that Old Fei had finally paused after talking himself tired, and couldn't help confirming, \"Brother Fei... are you... are you saying it's true? The Divine Maiden really brought rain down on Fengcheng and Weicheng?\"","\"Would I lie about this?!\" Old Fei confidently patted the carriage behind him. \"And I might joke about other things, but when it comes to the Divine Maiden, even if you lent me three hundred guts, I wouldn't dare!\"","His mother had been the most devoted follower of the Divine Maiden these past two years. If she ever found out her son was taking the Divine Maiden's name in vain, she wouldn't even need to lift a hand herself—his two older brothers would beat him so badly he could barely take care of himself.","Not because his brothers were going easy on him, but because neither of them wanted to be the one stuck taking care of him afterwards!","On that point, Fei San had plenty of experience!","\"The Divine Maiden... why doesn't She come to Yucheng? Isn't Yucheng also under Dayan's rule now?\"","As a young man said this, he unconsciously glanced at the Dayan soldiers standing in the crowd.","Following his gaze, the others also cast look after look at those Dayan soldiers, as if hoping that if they nodded, the Divine Maiden would come and bring rain.","\"Is it because we haven't been under Dayan's control for very long, so the Divine Maiden doesn't know yet that Yucheng is also under Dayan's rule?\""]},{"number":490,"title":"Chapter 490: The Blessing of the Goddess","paragraphs":["Old Fei shook his head, utterly disagreeing with the man's words. Who was the Divine Maiden? How could she not know something so trivial? \"The Divine Maiden is all-powerful and all-knowing. I'd stake my head on it—She definitely knows!\"","\"The fact that She didn't come must mean She has Her reasons!\" Old Fei's two sentences made everyone's faces fall, especially those clever types who liked to overthink things. Staring at the still-damp bloodstains on the street, a storm of thoughts raged in their heads.","\"It must be those soldiers—they refused to surrender and dressed up as common folk like us to ambush the Dayan troops!\" someone gnashed their teeth. \"They're the ones who dragged us down, making the Divine Maiden think we aren't truly loyal to Dayan!\"","\"Those people are blocking us from receiving the Divine Maiden's blessings!\" another voice shouted along.","A woman sobbed quietly, \"Those damned bastards forced my husband to guard the city gates, then they ran away themselves before the city even fell!\"","\"They stole our grain too!\" an old woman chimed in through gritted teeth. \"A full hundred catties of grain, they just took it by force.\"","\"My wife's dowry jewelry—those soldier-bandits barged into our house and snatched it all!\" a man stretched out his arm. \"And they beat me too.\"","\"Those who robbed us weren't the Dayan army—they were our own Southern Yue soldiers!\" an old man wailed, covering his face.","The citizens of Yu City traded stories one after another, and as they counted up the grievances, they realized just how much havoc the Southern Yue soldiers had wreaked.","They had treated them worse than the Dayan outsiders.","Young people were the most hot-blooded and impulsive. A young lad shouted, \"We need to find them and make them pay blood for blood! Then the Divine Maiden will surely look favorably upon us citizens of Yu City!\"","\"That's right, Da Wa's right! Find those troublemakers and hand them over to the Dayan army. No one's going to stand between us and the Divine Maiden's blessings!\"","Seeing the crowd's righteous fury, the system popped up again, [Host, when it rained a few days ago, you never expected this little bonus, did you?]","Yue Fuguang nodded. Indeed, she hadn't expected it!","As the old saying went, things forced on people never work out, but this time, without her saying a word, these people had taken the initiative themselves.","Old Fei, who was standing right there, was also taken aback by the angry crowd. But thinking about how hard it had been for his whole family during the water shortage, he—who had just drunk his fill—could understand where they were coming from.","But now wasn't the time to dwell on those rats who were destined for nothing. He still had a big piece of news to share!","He'd delivered the good news; now it was time to deliver the bad. Well, the unfortunate news, that is.","\"No need to panic, everyone!\" Fei San's voice wasn't loud, but the people standing in a circle around him all heard it. \"In another ten days, Southern Yue is bound to get heavy rain!\"","Someone couldn't help but dig a finger in their ear, looking absolutely incredulous. \"Fei the Third, are you serious? In another ten days, the Divine Maiden will bring rain to our Yu City too?\"","\"The Divine Maiden said so herself? How do you know?\"","\"Fei the Third, you're not pulling our leg, are you? We're all neighbors here—you'd better not be conning your own people!\"","The crowd buzzed with discussion, and by then, Fei the Third's family had rushed over to the 'battlefield' after hearing the news.","His mother came straight at him and grabbed his ear. \"You little brat! You tell me right now—how do you know it's going to rain in ten days?\"","Her spittle nearly sprayed all over Fei the Third's face. \"If you tell a single lie, I'll skin you alive!\"","\"Ow, ow, ow! Mom, ease up, that hurts!\" Fei the Third stood on his tiptoes, following the direction his mother twisted, not daring to struggle.","The way he did it was so practiced it was almost pitiful to watch.","\"Sister Fei, calm down first, let the Third explain himself,\" a familiar woman stepped in to mediate.","Fei the Third looked utterly wronged. \"Mom, everything I'm saying is true. I heard the Divine Maiden say it with my own ears.\"","He swore an oath. \"If you don't believe me, go ask around—I'm not the only one who came from Feng City. If I'm lying, may the Divine Maiden forsake me and never accept my offerings!\"","In those days, that was a heavy oath indeed—almost as serious as swearing you'd never become rich!","\"The Divine Maiden really said that? You actually saw her with your own eyes?\" His mother's first sentence was skeptical, but the second one sounded... awfully envious.","\"More real than real pearls! The Divine Maiden was standing up in the sky,\" Fei the Third pointed to the sky above. \"She was standing on a glowing lotus flower. The moment I saw that flower, I wanted to kneel!\"","He really had wanted to kneel forever the moment he laid eyes on the Divine Maiden.","At the very front stood old man Zhao Quan, over sixty years old, his face wrinkled like a dried-up riverbed. Listening to Fei the Third's words, his expression barely changed at first. Over these past few months, he'd heard plenty of hope and plenty of disappointment.","But this time was different. This time it wasn't 'might rain'—it was really going to rain!","His lips moved, but no sound came out.","Then his eyes changed. Something cracked behind the cloudy film.","His eyes slowly turned red, and then his face broke into a smile he hadn't worn in a long time. Just eight more days—eight more days and they'd have water!","Their whole family wouldn't die of thirst, and as long as they worked hard, they could still plant another crop in the fields.","Many people around him had the same thought. No one spoke, but the atmosphere suddenly came alive.","\"Water! The Divine Maiden be praised—we're getting water too!\" Fei the Third's mother had tears in her eyes as well, and she hastily wiped them with the sleeve of a shirt she hadn't washed in a month.","\"That's right, the hard times are finally coming to an end!\"","Some couldn't help but let their imagination run wild. \"We're under Dayan's rule now... think they'll let us plant that miracle grain that yields a thousand catties per mu?\"","They lived in Yu City, but some weren't originally city folk. Some had a few thin plots of land in the countryside, and if you had land, of course you wanted high-yield crops.","The people nearby perked up at the idea. \"We don't dare dream of the multi-thousand-catty yields, but even if they give us the lowest-yield corn to plant, I'd burn three sticks of incense a day for the Divine Maiden!\"","One impatient woman turned and sprinted for home. \"I'm going right now to light incense for the Divine Maiden and beg Her properly!\"","She had a son and two daughters; even the youngest was five, and none of her three children had ever really eaten their fill in their entire lives.","\"Right, right, I'm going home to burn incense too!\"","\"I'm going to Sage Hand Liu to get a statue of the Divine Maiden. From now on, our family worships only the Divine Maiden!\"","\"Brother Zhao, let's go together!\"","Fei the Third had actually been feeling a little guilty, watching his parents and the neighbors get so excited about the rain. He was agonizing over whether to ruin their mood by dropping the bad news at the happiest moment.","But when he saw the crowd starting to disperse, he gritted his teeth. Time waited for no one, and better to rip the bandage off fast. A quick sting beats a slow ache... He ran through every shred of self-encouragement he could muster.","After mentally steeling himself, Fei the Third shouted, \"Wait! Everyone, wait! I still have something to say!\"","\"Third, speak quickly! Don't keep an old man like me from going to burn incense for the Divine Maiden!\""]},{"number":491,"title":"Chapter 491: News of the Heavy Rain","paragraphs":["Fei the Third looked at the faces before him—some familiar, some not—and began to stammer again. His expression was troubled. “That... that, Father, Mother, dear neighbors all, the Divine Maiden said that heavy rain would fall across the entirety of Nanzhao and Nanyue within ten days, and two days have already passed since then.”","The time left for them to flee—or to find some other way—was running out.","Fei the Third’s mother could tell from her son’s expression that there was more to it than that. In a rare moment of gentleness, she asked quietly, “Third, is there something else going on here?”","“Mother, the Divine Maiden said that Nanzhao and Nanyue will see ten days of heavy rain, and that rain will continue unabated for over a month—there will be floods!”","Fei the Third shut his eyes and let it all out in one breath.","For a moment, there was a strange, suffocating silence. Then someone broke into sobs. “This... this is no way for us to survive!”","“First drought, then flood! Have we committed some crime against heaven? Is the old sky trying to kill us all?” Cries mixed with shouts and curses, and the scene dissolved into chaos.","It could be said that they were all people of the same nation, for the citizens of Yucheng cursed in much the same way as those of Fengcheng—the blame all falling on the heavens.","“Divine Maiden! The Divine Maiden cannot treat us like this! She cannot drown us with water! We belong to Dayan now, we are Dayan people!”","Someone knelt and kowtowed to the sky, shouting for the Divine Maiden’s forgiveness.","Fei the Third’s face turned grim first. He had witnessed the Divine Maiden’s power with his own eyes, and thus held the deepest faith in her. The moment he heard someone trying to pin the flood on the Divine Maiden—","He stepped forward first and said sharply to that person, “Sir, please watch your words! The Divine Maiden is kind and benevolent—first she brought rain to Wei City and Fengcheng to relieve the drought. Then she warned us in advance so we could prepare! The Divine Maiden means well, so how can you claim that She is the one bringing this great rain?”","Seeing the man fall silent, he continued in a louder voice, “I just said it—Nanzhao and Nanyue are both under this heavy rain. This rain is from the heavens; it is the old sky’s doing, making trouble for us. What does it have to do with the Divine Maiden?”","“The Emperor is without virtue! It must be the Emperor’s lack of virtue that brought us this punishment!” Someone in the crowd shouted.","“Yes, surely the Emperor has done evil deeds, and we are all suffering for his sins!”","Watching the noisy, chaotic scene, the system could not help but complain, “Host, see—someone really is trying to blame the rain on you! Fortunately, this Fei the Third is a smart one. If this spread, it would be trouble!”","Now that the blame had landed on the Emperor instead, it was an unexpected gift. The system silently noted the names of the person who first said that and of Fei the Third’s family. If the chance came, it wouldn’t mind lending a hand—and earn itself some merit in the process.","Yue Fuguang nodded. Human hearts had always been like this; she had long guessed that someone would try to pin the rain on her, seeing as she was the only one in the world who could control the rain!","“System, keep an eye on public opinion. This is a perfect chance to slander me—the courts of Nanzhao and Nanyue will not let it pass.”","“Well—host, you called it. Based on the intelligence I’ve gathered so far, there are two dominant voices in Nanyue and Nanzhao right now.” The system paused. “One is that the Emperor is without virtue and heaven has inflicted punishment. The other is that the two nations waged war, and the Divine Maiden sent down great rain to help the Dayan army take both countries. As for the early warning—they claim it was not warning at all, but a threat—threatening both the people and both courts!”","Although she had expected this, hearing the system’s concrete intelligence still made Yue Fuguang speechless.","“Why hasn’t Gan Sheng died yet? Is he really that stubborn?” Yue Fuguang’s hand twitched. If he didn’t go cold soon, she might have to send him down herself.","“Master, soon, soon! Prince Cheng, who was supposed to be holding Jia Ling City and putting up a fight against our army, secretly returned to the capital yesterday. Not only did he leave, he took most of his elite troops with him.”","Yue Fuguang’s eyes flickered. “Little Zhu, is he in a hurry to grab the throne?”","“That’s right! He heard that his nephew Gan Sheng’s health is getting worse day by day, and he’s afraid that if he returns too late, the throne will fall into the young crown prince’s hands instead!”","“So he’s planning to storm the palace, or just kill Gan Sheng and take the throne himself?”","“Given Prince Cheng’s temperament and Gan Sheng’s current condition, he’ll certainly charge straight into the imperial palace, force Gan Sheng to abdicate, and make him write out an edict of succession.”","“Prince Cheng took most of his elite troops—so isn’t Jia Ling City practically empty now? If the Dayan army were to attack Jia Ling at this moment...”","“Then it would surely fall with minimal losses!”","Inside the carriage, Shen Chunying’s hand, pouring tea for Yue Fuguang, paused for a moment. Outside, sitting on the carriage shaft, Feng Tang’s spirits lifted—this intelligence had come at exactly the right time.","He calculated the timing—Prince Cheng, with his army, would return to the capital slower than they would. From Jia Ling City to Gan City, the fastest trip would take five days. That was enough time for the Dayan army to make their preparations.","As for the rumors about the Young Master spreading through Nanzhao and Nanyue—that must be reported to His Majesty as soon as possible. Their Young Master’s name allowed for no slander or defilement from anyone.","\"Little Zhu, keep an eye on Prince Cheng's side. Whatever you do, don't let him die at this critical moment.\"","【Master means Gan Sheng is about to make a move against Prince Cheng?】","\"Given how Gan Sheng operates, if Prince Cheng had obediently stayed in Jialing City and fought to the death against Dai Yan, Gan Sheng naturally wouldn't have touched him. But now he's returned to the capital without an imperial summons and abandoned Jialing City altogether.","Gan Sheng will definitely go after him. It won't be easy for Prince Cheng to reach the capital safely.\"","With such a commotion, hiding one's tracks is nearly impossible, and a schemer like Gan Sheng would surely have planted a spy close to Prince Cheng.","【If Prince Cheng were smart, he should have taken precautions.】","The System was only saying that for the sake of saying it. Judging by Prince Cheng's past actions, he had some wit, but not much. If it came to a battle of wits with Gan Sheng, two Princes Cheng together still wouldn't match one Gan Sheng.","Given Prince Cheng's intelligence and temperament, the fact that he'd survived this many years after Gan Sheng took the throne, and even kept his grip on a major army—there had to be a reason behind it. As a System, it couldn't believe otherwise.","\"If Prince Cheng were wise, we wouldn't have put him on the throne in the first place. A fool sitting on the emperor's seat means Nan Yue falls to Dai Yan all the faster—and whether it's Nan Yue or Dai Yan, fewer people die either way.\"","Yue Fuguang's voice was filled with compassion, which indirectly explained why she paid such close attention to the wars and aided Dai Yan—it was all for the sake of 'fewer deaths'!","【Master is truly benevolent. If you ask me, a mortal's life is only a few short decades—what difference does dying sooner or later make? Master needn't trouble herself over it!】","Hearing the Sacred Artifact's words, Shen Chunying and Luo Shendong inside the carriage, and Feng Tang outside it, all twitched at the corners of their mouths and bowed their heads, not daring to make a sound.","\"I've accepted their incense offerings. Though it wasn't my intention, this karmic debt cannot go unpaid.\"","【Master, after we finish with Hezhou and Jizhou, how about we take a detour and swing by Gan City for a visit?】","\"Little Zhu, your 'detour' is a thousand leagues north and south?\" Hezhou was the farthest prefecture in Dai Yan from Nan Yue and Nanzhao.","It was also the borderland adjoining Beili, long regarded as a vital frontier defense post."]},{"number":492,"title":"Chapter 492: This Dowager Empress Shall Have His Entire Clan Executed","paragraphs":["In the future, Dayan will send troops to Beili, and Hezhou will be at the front line. Therefore, Yue Fuguang decided that this time when it rained in Hezhou, she must add some extra \"spices\", which was considered as stockpiling food in advance.","\"Could it be that you just want to go for fun!\"","Having been guessed correctly by Yue Fuguang, the system was not annoyed. Instead, it continued to encourage her. [My master, don't you want to see the real - life version of the fight for the imperial throne?]","Of course, Yue Fuguang wanted to see it. In Dayan, with her around, she couldn't watch such a wonderful drama.","But if she could go to Nanyue to watch a drama, it was indeed a good idea.","Yue Fuguang gave a hard hug to the little fox with snow - white and smooth fur. \"Alright, after I'm done with the things in Hezhou and Jizhou, we'll fly there to watch the show.\"","[My master, trust Little Zhu. This trip will definitely be worth your while.]","Yue Fuguang was intrigued by its words. Years of understanding between them made her follow the system's words and continue the topic without much thought.","\"Little Zhu, is there something else going on here? Come on, what is there that I, your master, can't know?\"","[My master, don't you think it's a bit strange that Prince Cheng, being just a prince, can live well under a man like Gan Sheng? It would be good enough for him to have a little job, but how could he be in command of a large army?]","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"It's really suspicious. With Gan Sheng's character and ambition, instead of being on high alert and restricting his power like he did with Gan Tang, he even let him command an army of eight or ninety thousand. There must be something fishy going on.\"","[I had my suspicions, so I just checked it out, and I really found some clues.]","If it weren't for the fact that this was related to their next mission, even if the system was extremely curious, it would have to hold back to avoid wasting its abilities.","However, just when it invited Yue Fuguang to \"visit\" Nanyue, a new mission was triggered, and that's how it got the current data.","[My master, I previously said that Gan Chengjiang was able to successfully push his favorite son onto the imperial throne and secretly get rid of the former crown prince and the queen. There was the shadow of Panshan behind all this.]","\"So? Their carefully - supported candidate is about to die. Isn't the Panshan organization going to do anything? Instead of trying to save Gan Sheng, they should have already found a new candidate, right? Is it the crown prince?\"","[My master, the poison that Gan Sheng was poisoned with was originally incurable except by you. Naturally, the people of Panshan have already given up on him.","What I want to say is that Panshan did choose a successor as you said, the son of Consort Shu. But this is only the idea of a part of the people behind Panshan.","Another part of them supports Prince Cheng.]","\"Prince Cheng? So there are two factions within Panshan?\" It seemed that Panshan was not as united as it seemed. This was really good news!","[There are at least two factions, maybe even more. The people who support Prince Cheng started after the death of the former crown prince. Although the majority support Gan Sheng, there are always those who like to take the less - traveled path in every era.","Although there aren't many of them, they can still ensure Prince Cheng's safe survival and give him a certain amount of power.]","\"So, in a few days, what seems to be a fight between Gan Sheng and Prince Cheng, his uncle and nephew, is actually a fight between two factions within Panshan?\"","[Yes, so we can't miss it!]","\"You're right. We really can't miss it. It's a pity that the influence of Panshan spreads across six countries. We can't wipe them out all at once!\"","It would be good if they could destroy their lair and the main leaders. Otherwise, after Dayan unified the world, Panshan would still be a threat. Eliminating Panshan was also an important side mission for her.","Of course, as long as Dayan unified the world and it didn't affect the completion of her main mission, this side mission wasn't mandatory. But Panshan was so well - hidden and so destructive. Yue Fuguang was really afraid that one day the Heavenly Dao of this world would \"ask for after - sales service\" from her!","[My master, this trip to Nanyue might bring some unexpected rewards!]","Yue Fuguang raised her eyebrows. \"Oh? Then tell me. What kind of unexpected rewards could there be?\"","[Gan Sheng's early demise has disrupted Panshan's plan for Nanyue. The successor they supported is too young and might not be able to hold the throne firmly.","Moreover, there's the unexpected situation of Prince Cheng suddenly returning to the capital and trying to seize power by force. So the people sent by Panshan this time should be quite important figures.","If we just catch one of them and search their soul, won't we know where their lair is?]","Yue Fuguang gave the system a thumbs - up and thought the system's idea was very feasible.","While Yue Fuguang was having an animated conversation with the system, she didn't know that the rumor about the upcoming floods in Nanzhao and Nanyue, despite the two countries' courts' efforts to suppress it and even shift the blame to her, was now causing an uncontrollable wave of public resistance as the date of the heavy rain she predicted was approaching.","\"Empress Dowager, please come up with a plan as soon as possible.\" In the Nanyue Palace, several officials led by Prime Minister Li were now in the side hall next to the emperor's bedroom.","Sitting in front of them was Gan Sheng's mother, the current Empress Dowager Jiang. Below her sat the Queen, Chen Yuli. Since Gan Sheng was critically ill, the administration of the court had been handed over to several important officials, but the final decision - making power was still in the hands of Empress Dowager Jiang.","\"Didn't I tell you to guide public opinion and shift all the blame to that young girl from Dayan?\" Since her son fell seriously ill, Empress Dowager Jiang, whose face was originally well - maintained, had been hit by a series of bad news in recent days and suddenly looked ten years older.","Wrinkles quietly crept up on the corners of her eyes and lips. The empress dowager, who cared very much about her appearance, didn't want to look in the mirror in recent days.","Several expensive mirrors bought from Dayan in the empress dowager's palace had been smashed by her one after another.","Prime Minister Li also looked unhappy. When he thought of the news his servants had gathered from Fengcheng, an inexplicable chill ran down his spine. \"Your Majesty, Empress Dowager, your humble servants have tried our best to guide public opinion, but... but there are countless people in our country who believe in the Goddess.","More people only believe in the Goddess's warning. As for the flood in Nanyue, the rumor in the streets is that...\"","The empress dowager was twirling a string of emerald green Buddhist beads in her hand. When she didn't hear the rest of Prime Minister Li's words, she stopped her hand, raised her eyelids unhappily, pursed her lips, and said, \"What is it? Prime Minister Li, just say it. I forgive you for any offense!\"","\"People in the streets say that it's because His Majesty is immoral that God has sent down punishment! They also say... they say that His Majesty's current serious illness is the retribution for killing the former crown prince!\"","Prime Minister Li really didn't want to say these things, especially in front of the empress dowager. But if he didn't say it today and the empress dowager kept delaying the approval of their memorials, Nanyue would be in chaos before Dayan's troops even invaded.","Now it seemed that the common people's storming of the palace yesterday was just a minor matter. The immediate crises were not only the common people fleeing but also Prince Cheng, who was still on his way.","\"Ridiculous! Simply ridiculous!\"","With a bang and a crash,","\"Who is spreading these heart - wrenching words? Dai Ping'an, tell Dai Ping'an to arrest people for me. I want to execute his entire family!\"","As soon as Prime Minister Li finished speaking, a teacup shattered at his feet, and the empress dowager's angry scolding seemed to lift the roof off.","\"Forgive me, Your Majesty, Empress Dowager!\" Prime Minister Li looked extremely frightened on the surface and quickly knelt down to plead for forgiveness, but actually, he wasn't that scared in his heart."]},{"number":493,"title":"Chapter 493: Releasing Water","paragraphs":["With the Emperor fallen, the Empress Dowager was nothing more than a toothless tiger. She could only rely on her status to press these outer ministers, but when it came to real power play, she truly did not dare make a rash move.","Behind Empress Dowager Jiang stood her natal family, the Jiang clan—true enough. And for a long time, thanks to their status as the Emperor's maternal relatives, the Jiang family had indeed enjoyed considerable glory.","But that was only how outsiders saw it. To powerful ministers like Li Jie, the Jiang family was merely a case of flowers embroidered on brocade, flames fed by boiling oil—all show, no substance. Though they outwardly bore imperial favor, in reality their true power had been whittled away by the Emperor time and again. They could no longer stir up any waves.","\"Prime Minister Li, you tell me—where did these venomous words come from?\" Empress Dowager Jiang's originally kindly face twisted into something terrifying in that moment.","Like a cat whose tail has been stepped on, she was furious enough to smash everything in front of her! But she knew she could not. Not now. Her son was gravely ill, the Crown Prince was still young, and even the help her natal family offered was limited. She, her son, and her grandson all still depended on these outsiders to prop them up.","The cup in front of Li Jie was her vent after reaching the limit of her endurance.","What did Empress Dowager Jiang care about most? Aside from her son, it was her face and her reputation. It was precisely on these three pillars that she had climbed from being the daughter of a disgraced official to the supreme seat of Empress Dowager.","Now she was old, and her only son was about to die. All she had left was her good name. With that good name intact, she could support the young Emperor's ascension and, as his grandmother, hold the curtain and oversee court affairs from behind.","Now someone was driving a knife into the only thing she had left—how could she not hate it, not rage?","Li Jie glanced at Dai Ping'an. \"Her Majesty the Empress Dowager, please see clearly. These are merely rumors Your minister heard from the common folk in the streets. As for where they originated... I imagine Commissioner Dai would know better than I.\"","Li Jie deftly kicked the ball away—better his fellow minister dies than he himself. Indeed, after meeting with the steward who had returned from Feng City, he had eased off on the matter of slandering Yue Fuguang. He no longer dared to offend her to the death. Even when the womenfolk in his own household secretly worshipped her divine statue, he chose to turn a blind eye.","The Empress Dowager turned her gaze to the Emperor's favored minister, Dai Ping'an. \"Ping'an, you heard what Prime Minister Li said, did you not?\"","Li Jie and Fei Yongxing behind him felt a stir in their hearts—the rumor that the imperial mother and son treated Dai the Infernal differently from everyone else seemed to carry some weight after all.","Hearing the Empress Dowager's question, Dai Ping'an immediately stepped forward and bowed respectfully. \"In reply to Your Majesty the Empress Dowager, according to intelligence gathered by my men, the rumor of His Majesty's lack of virtue first spread from Yu City a few days ago.\"","\"Yu City? How could it be Yu City! Wasn't the matter of the heavy rains in Nanyue first reported from Wei and Feng Cities?\"","\"It must be reckless talk from commoners stirred up by petty troublemakers.\" On Dai Ping'an's perpetually unsmiling face, there was now obvious awkwardness. Could he say that it was because the Goddess had only brought rain to Feng City and Wei City, making the people of Yu City—also occupied by the Dayan army—burn with jealousy?","All were cities seized by Dayan, yet the Goddess had been partial. That imbalance shattered their composure. The common folk dared not direct their resentment at the Goddess, so they picked the softest persimmon to squeeze—and in their eyes, His Majesty was that soft persimmon.","Though Dai Ping'an was deeply favored by the Emperor and bore the title of Dai the Infernal, he did not dare speak as recklessly as that old scoundrel Li Jie. He was different from outside ministers like Li Jie. His power came solely from the Emperor's favor—something utterly insubstantial.","\"Go on.\" Dai Ping'an had no idea how much of his words the Empress Dowager believed, but he steadied himself and moved to the next question.","\"As for the second rumor that Prime Minister Li mentioned, it first spread from teahouses and taverns in the capital.\" Dai Ping'an felt the words burning his tongue, but he had no choice but to steel himself and continue.","\"I had my men investigate carefully for two days. But the first people to spread those words mysteriously vanished just as we were closing in on their trail.\"","\"Vanished? Not a single one caught?\" The Empress Dowager's gaze was sharp, cutting across Dai Ping'an's face.","The Emperor had once told her that this man was the most loyal and capable. The Emperor cherished talent and trusted him deeply—but seeing him today, he was nothing special. He couldn't even catch a single person. Utterly useless!","Under that piercing stare, even Dai Ping'an, who carried the name of the Infernal, could not hold his ground. He hastily begged forgiveness. \"Your Majesty, please forgive me. My men ultimately traced these people back to... to the Former Crown Prince and the Late Empress—there is an inescapable connection.\"","At the mention of the Late Empress, the Empress Dowager unconsciously tightened her grip on her prayer beads. Some memories she would rather forget came surging back to assault her.","The Empress, who had remained as still and silent as a bodhisattva of clay, stirred slightly at the mention of the Former Crown Prince. In truth, she was merely a spectator in all this.","The Empress of the central palace had borne no children. The Crown Prince had only been registered under her name in name alone. As his nominal mother, she shared no real bond of affection with the boy.","After all, his birth mother was still alive, and she was the darling of the Emperor's heart. There was simply no need for Empress Chen to raise the Crown Prince or cultivate any mother-son feelings with him.","At this moment, Empress Chen was far more interested in enjoying the drama. She was deeply curious about the feud between the Empress Dowager and the Late Empress. As for the death of the Former Crown Prince—as the one who slept beside Gan Sheng—Empress Chen felt it was ten to one that he had done it. Even if he hadn't done it with his own hands, he was inextricably involved.","That saying about retribution might very well be true!","If so, the Later Empress's death afterwards is also highly suspicious.","Empress Chen munched on her melon while her mind raced, unaware that her guesses were already close to the truth. In the future, she would uncover even more.","The Empress Dowager didn't want to dwell on this topic. She waved her hand weakly. \"Alright, I'm tired. All of you may withdraw.\"","Since it was connected to the Former Crown Prince's people, the Empress Dowager inevitably thought of the force the prince had hidden away.","There were too many matters at hand right now; it wasn't yet time to track down those people.","Chancellor Li saw that after all this talk, not a single problem had been solved, and grew anxious. Fei Yongxing was even more anxious than he was. \"Your Majesty, Empress Dowager, Prince Cheng will arrive in the capital in no more than three to five days. How should we respond?\"","Three to five days already included the time bought by their obstruction. None of the outside officials could see the emperor now. If not for the various signs indicating the emperor was still alive, they would all think he had already passed and the Empress Dowager was secretly withholding the announcement of his death.","Now that the emperor couldn't be seen, and the only person who could make decisions—the Empress Dowager—refused to set a course of action, what were they, as subjects, supposed to do?","At the end of the day, this was both a matter of state and a family matter. It was up to the imperial family themselves to decide.","The final say did not belong to them, outsiders.","Everyone deliberately ignored the second most powerful woman in the dynasty—Empress Chen.","Empress Chen: Peace and quiet!","\"Didn't we send Hu An's fifty thousand troops to block him?\" The Empress Dowager's gaze turned cold. \"Fei Yongxing, are you saying Hu An can't stop Prince Cheng?\"","Even when the emperor was alive, she had never realized that every single minister at court was useless!","Fei Yongxing's face darkened. He considered himself one of the emperor's closest officials, yet the Empress Dowager seemed even more indifferent to him than to Dai Ping'an. \"Your Majesty, Empress Dowager, with an external enemy at the gates, if Prince Cheng forces his way through, General Hu—in order to preserve our dynasty's fighting strength to deal with the coming Dayan army—will certainly not move against Prince Cheng.\"","At most, he would delay Prince Cheng's entry into the capital, buying time for the ministers to handle the situation."]},{"number":494,"title":"Chapter 494: Isn't your ability improving a bit too fast","paragraphs":["\"Prince Cheng's unauthorized entry into the capital is a grave offense!\" The Empress Dowager's eyes darkened, and her voice was cold and harsh. \"Li Jie, Dai Ping'an, Fei Yongxing, and all the important ministers of Nanyue, you should all remember that our dynasty still has a Crown Prince. He is the future emperor of Nanyue!","You should be loyal to the emperor and the Crown Prince!\"","She stepped down the steps one by one. \"As for Prince Cheng, daring to force his way into the capital makes him a traitor! The imperial prison will be his destination!\"","She looked at them coldly. \"Have you all heard clearly?\"","Those whose names were called and those whose names were not, under the Empress Dowager's piercing gaze, all bowed and replied in unison, \"We obey the imperial edict of the Empress Dowager!\"","\"As for the proposals put forward by Prime Minister Li regarding appeasing the people and preventing floods, you should discuss them carefully again. If there are no problems, implement them as soon as possible!\"","After all, the Empress Dowager had never witnessed Yue Fuguang's miraculous powers with her own eyes, so she only half - believed her words.","However, regardless of whether this matter was true or not, the court had to prepare as if it were true. Firstly, it was for show to the people, and secondly, it was to be on the safe side.","The Empress Dowager had been proud all her life and did not believe in the legend of the Divine Maiden. However, many court officials had gathered a lot of information from Fengcheng. In some families, like Li Jie's, the servants had witnessed the Divine Maiden's supernatural feats with their own eyes.","These people believed Yue Fuguang's words. So, while they were trying to stop the common people from fleeing, they secretly sent their own younger generations out of the city.","Some went to the mountains, and some headed all the way to Fengcheng and Weicheng.","Since Yue Fuguang planned to go to Gancheng to \"watch the show\", she acted quickly. In just four days, she made it rain across the entire Hezhou and Jizhou.","The reason for such a fast pace was thanks to the flying vehicle and the improvement of her own abilities.","Now, each time she made it rain, she could cover an area of nearly four hundred square kilometers. Even she herself couldn't figure out why she had improved so fast.","[Host, isn't your ability improving a bit too fast?] At this rate of improvement, it wouldn't be long before she could control the weather of an entire state at once.","\"It's a bit fast, but I don't feel anything wrong with my body.\" Even because her rain - making had saved many people, the Heavenly Way had bestowed golden light of merit, which had strengthened her soul a lot.","Yue Fuguang even felt that now, if she wanted to, she could transform the appearance of her soul according to her imagination.","Since Yue Fuguang said she hadn't found anything wrong, the system stopped dwelling on this issue and brought up another matter. [Host, should we go around through Nanzhao?]","\"Enter Nanyue through Nanzhao? What you're suggesting is not a detour but a big turn, okay?\" However, based on Yue Fuguang's understanding of the system, there was probably something behind this suggestion!","\"Come on, what are you hiding from me?\"","[Hehe, it's not that I'm hiding something from you. I just want you to take a look at the current situation in Nanzhao along the way.] And then urge the emperor and those civil and military officials to capture Nanyue earlier and annex Nanzhao by the way.","In the past few days, seeing the lives of the Nanzhao people, the system couldn't bear it anymore.","If you asked why the 07 system had suddenly developed a kind heart, it was because the data repair of the Gossip System had stalled, while the Merit System had caught up and was now taking the lead.","The Gossip System and the Merit System were often like a person fighting with themselves. Sometimes one system got the upper hand, and sometimes the other did.","\"Is it that bad?\" As the host, Yue Fuguang had noticed the system's change, but since they were originally a Merit System, it was understandable.","[You'll know when you go and see!]","Yue Fuguang, the system, and Feng Tang and the others flew at full speed. In less than a day, they flew from the north to the south of Dayan.","Feng Tang and the others were so shocked by this speed that they had become numb and kept drinking water to calm their nerves.","Yue Fuguang pretended not to see their shocked faces and just chatted with the system. \"Little Zhu, is that Baihua City of Nanzhao up ahead?\"","[Yes. The closest cities to Dayan are Baihua City and Fangcheng. We won't go to Fangcheng. We'll go straight through Baihua City and then detour to Suixicheng and enter Nanyue from there.]","\"Baihua City. Is it true that there are flowers planted both inside and outside the city?\"","[Yes. This place is rich in flowers. Poppies were first discovered here!] The system really knew how to ruin a conversation!","Seeing Yue Fuguang roll her eyes, the system knew it had said the wrong thing and quickly tried to make amends. [Master, your former defeated opponent Kong You's ancestral home is also in Baihua City. And the Poison King Li Sanming also used to live in Baihua City at first.","This place not only produces a lot of flowers but also grows a great deal of herbs and poisonous plants. Many of the flowers planted by the flower farmers can also be used as medicine.]","Yue Fuguang had heard about this. The medicinal herbs that Murong Liang had secretly traded with Nanzhao mainly came from Baihua City.","If it weren't for the fact that her system mall had everything, she would have been tempted to stock up on some herbs here, even if she didn't need them now, for the next mission world.","Just as Yue Fuguang was concentrating on checking her belongings in the storage ring, she suddenly heard the system shout in her ear. [Master, look over there!]","Yue Fuguang followed the system's prompt and looked out of the window. What she saw were layers upon layers of mountains. It was no exaggeration to say that Nanzhao and Nanyue were full of mountains and forests.","The reason why she had warned Fengcheng about the flood was not only to gain favor but also because she considered that these countries had many mountains and forests within their territories. If they were lucky, they might be able to hide in the mountains before the heavy rain came and save their lives.","As for whether there would be a mudslide, she didn't consider it. Before Dayan captured the other cities, she couldn't go to help.","System: Is it possible that it's because your own strength is not enough?","Yue Fuguang: System, didn't your predecessors ever tell you that telling the truth can hurt others and yourself? Raising a big club JPG","However, since it hadn't rained for eight or nine months, the mountains and forests were not the lush green they should be but a dry and lifeless yellow - brown color with occasional patches of dull green.","The yellow - brown fallen leaves covered the soil, as if autumn and winter had come early. The originally moss - covered and moist stone walls were now just a pale white. If someone touched them, the moss would surely fall off in flakes.","The streams had turned into deep pools, and the rivers had dried up, leaving only the riverbeds exposed. The stones were shining white under the scorching sun, and there were occasionally a few thin fish bones in the cracks, so white that they were blinding.","If it weren't for this sight, Yue Fuguang and the others would have almost forgotten that it was not only the dry season but also the middle of summer.","The trees were still standing, but there were very few leaves on them. The remaining few leaves were curled up into dry strips and would surely fall to the ground without hesitation if touched.","There were deep cracks on the tree trunks, with no sap, only the dry color of the wood.","The most peculiar thing was the sound. There were no bird calls, no insect chirps, and even the wind made a dry and brittle sound.","The whole mountain was as quiet as a well - burned kiln.","Occasionally, a hot wind would blow through, making the dry branches crackle, which only made the surroundings seem more empty. Only the cracked bark, the pale riverbed, and the fallen leaves all over the ground were all telling the same word: thirst.","Flying forward for a while, three continuous mountains appeared in front of them. The situation of these three mountains seemed a little better than that of the small mountains, but only a little."]},{"number":495,"title":"Chapter 495: Just Giving the Believers Some Water","paragraphs":["“Master, are those moving little dots down there people?”","“Judging by their clothes, they’re Nan Zhao commoners. They’re fleeing famine—no wait, the entire Nan Yue territory is suffering the same drought, so fleeing would be pointless.”","But as Yue Fuguang followed the direction they came from, she spotted something off. “This isn’t far from Hundred Flowers City. They seem to be coming from the city’s direction.”","The situation wasn’t hard to assess. Standing as high as she was, she could see far, and following those mountain ridges with her gaze, she saw families stretching for miles—men, women, and children loaded down with bundles, all trudging painfully up the slopes.","“What are they doing?”","Yue Fuguang had already figured it out. “Don’t you remember? Rain is set to start in less than three days. These people are heading up the mountains to take shelter from it.”","“So that means the warning you issued in Feng City not only reached Nan Zhao—they actually believed it?”","The weather right now was clear and scorching every single day, and to have families dragging themselves up into the mountains at this very moment meant that not only did they have their own sense of resolve, they also trusted their host quite deeply.","“Some won’t believe, but naturally some will. Look at the travelers on the road—there aren’t even ten thousand of them yet. Now think about the population of Hundred Flowers City.”","Even though Yue Fuguang was hovering directly above Hundred Flowers City, she had no intention of appearing to warn them. She had already given these people one chance—that was enough.","She had always held to the principle of respecting others’ fates.","Feng City was the trade hub between Nan Yue and Nan Zhao, which was also why she had chosen to reveal herself there that day—because the city hosted not only Nan Yue citizens traveling between its various towns, but also many Nan Zhao people.","She didn’t doubt that after witnessing her miracle that day, those people couldn’t resist spreading word back to Nan Zhao—sharing such an extraordinary divine event was simply human nature.","The two nations were close in distance, and within two or three days, the Nan Zhao towns bordering Nan Yue should all have heard of it by now.","But looking at how the citizens of Hundred Flowers City were reacting, Yue Fuguang shook her head.","Still, before the heavy rains truly began, they had one more chance to escape. If they missed that one, then life and death would truly be left to fate.","“Mother, I can’t walk anymore!” A young girl of seven or eight carried a tiny bundle on her back, keeping close to her mother’s side.","In front of them walked a man carrying a large basket and a boy of eleven or twelve, who had not a bundle but a toddler of two or three strapped to his back.","The whole family was thin, with sallow faces, cracked lips, and crumpled clothes that hung loose on their bodies. Because of their gauntness, the garments seemed oversized, making their eyes look bigger too—but those eyes were no longer bright. They held only numbness and the exhaustion of trudging a hard road.","“Aying, bear with it a little longer. Once we reach up ahead, we’ll rest a while.” The woman’s voice was hoarse, the result of long travel without enough water.","The girl’s steps faltered, and her voice was just as hoarse as her mother’s. Even though she knew she shouldn’t be talking, her craving for water made her ask the mother who always knew more.","“Mother, did the Divine Maiden really say it’s about to rain soon? Once it rains, will we finally have water to drink?”","“Your third cousin on my side came to the house the day before yesterday and said the Divine Maiden had spoken of it—so it must be true!” In their home, the woman kept a small idol of the Divine Maiden, and while others dismissed what her third cousin had brought back, their family believed.","“Then when I burn incense for the Divine Maiden tonight, I’ll beg her to make the rain come soon, so we can have water at home!” The girl shook the bamboo canteen on her waist, and a faint sound rattled inside—proof it was almost completely empty.","Hearing their daughter’s words, the mother walking beside her and the father and brother ahead all wore grim expressions.","Of course, they longed for rain—were it not something both officials and common folk prayed for once or twice a month? But if it rained continuously for a whole month without stopping, that would be too much for ordinary people to bear either!","Thinking back to a month ago, they recalled a letter from her eldest sister who had married into Fragrant City on the border. The letter said they had secretly slipped into Da Yan, where the Divine Maiden had truly brought rain, and the people there lacked no water, and the crops in the fields were flourishing!","The whole family couldn’t help but envy them. Every time the wife and daughter burned incense to the Divine Maiden, they muttered prayers that Da Yan’s army would come to Nan Zhao soon—they too wanted to become Da Yan citizens blessed by the Divine Maiden’s care.","“Wife, the children are worn out. Let’s stop here for a bit!” The man carefully lowered the most critical thing for the family—their food—from his shoulder.","The woman handed her husband a bamboo canteen. “Father, drink some water.”","The man took the canteen, drank a small sip, then handed it back to his wife. “Don’t worry only about us. You should drink too.”","The woman smiled, took a small sip, then passed the canteen to her son, and then to her daughter.","The little girl didn’t take her mother’s canteen. Instead, she firmly shook her own smaller bamboo tube. “Mother, I still have water in my canteen.”","A little girl so small, yet so considerate it tugged at the heart.","“Aying, drink your mother’s first. Save yours for later.” The woman coaxed her overly mature daughter in a gentle voice, her eyes turning slightly red.","At that moment, Yue Fuguang was several hundred meters up in the sky, but she could see everything below clearly.","“System, this is what you wanted me to see?”","Facing Yue Fuguang’s accusation, the system chose to play dead.","“If you stay silent, are you trying to get me to help the enemy?” If she took pity on these people now, a single rain might not save them—because they were unarmed and couldn’t possibly hold on to water that was more precious than food.","But her rain would absolutely save the Nan Zhao armies stationed at Hundred Flowers City and Fragrant City.","Since the start of the war between Da Yan and Nan Yue, half of Nan Zhao’s troops had been pulled to these two towns and their surroundings, ready at any moment to strike at Da Yan.","“I didn’t—No such thing—Don’t you dare accuse me!” The system’s triple denial was quick and firm.","Yue Fuguang let out a cold snort. “You’d better not be!” Don’t do something well-intentioned yet end up harming everyone.","With that, she shifted from lying on her side to sitting cross-legged. Her hands formed hand seals, and she sank her mind deeper. Following the faint threads of incorporeal incense smoke, she began shaping the water-gathering seal.","“Master, you just—?”","“Sending some water to my believers, that’s all.” Yue Fuguang said it lightly, but it was a delicate task, and she was a bit clumsy at it. No sooner had the words left her mouth than she heard a stir below.","“Father! Mother! My canteen... my canteen is leaking water on its own!” The girl’s voice was a mix of shock and joy.","She stared wide-eyed as clear water flowed down the sides of the canteen and hurriedly tilted her head back to catch the stream in her mouth.","The girl’s parents saw it too. Just as they stood bewildered, someone else nearby cried out in surprise, “Mine! Mine suddenly filled with water too!”","It was a young man around seventeen or eighteen, holding his canteen high above his head to show his family. “I drank the last drop not a moment ago!”","His own parents stood with wide, stunned eyes, staring at the canteen in their son’s hands. Water was now more precious than grain, and as parents, they knew exactly how much water their family still had left."]},{"number":496,"title":"Chapter 496: Why Don't We Have It","paragraphs":["It was precisely because they understood so clearly that they felt both surprise and delight—though luckily, theirs wasn't the only household blessed this way, so they didn't have to worry about being singled out or robbed.","“Father, my bamboo tube suddenly filled up with water too!” The girl's mother only then noticed the weight of the large bamboo vessel in her hands.","Just moments ago, after her husband and children had drunk from it, there had clearly been only a little less than half left—and now it was full.","“Really?” The man took the tube, saw the clear water inside, and instinctively swallowed.","He said in a low voice to his wife, “Check the other bamboo containers in the house!”","Before his wife could rummage through the remaining tubes, their eldest son had already grinned and said to them, “Father, Mother, no need to check—every empty bamboo tube has been filled with water!”","The eleven- or twelve-year-old boy looked at his father. “Father, which deity do you think bestowed this life-saving water upon us?”","The little girl's voice, after drinking, was no longer so hoarse. “Brother, do you think it could be the Divine Maiden?”","In the girl's memory, only that deity excelled at controlling rain, and their family now worshipped Her the most faithfully.","Whether it was Her or not, the girl's parents couldn't say.","And the others soon discovered that every empty water container in their homes had been filled to the brim with clear water. Astonished and puzzled, they nevertheless felt a surge of hope for surviving the remaining three days.","“Wh-why doesn't my family have any water?” A middle-aged man's face turned ugly as he looked at the barely concealed joy on the faces of several neighboring families, feeling both stung and confused.","Everyone was on the mountain—how could they alone have been skipped? Did he open his bamboo tube the wrong way?","“I—mine doesn't have any either!” A young man hugged his empty bamboo tube, on the verge of tears.","Before his tears could fall, more voices rose one after another nearby: “Our family doesn't have water either!”","“Why do they have water and we don't?” Someone shouted angrily at the families who clearly did.","Those who had water formed the vast majority. They exchanged glances, silently drew together, and without a word, a unified front was established.","They were numerous enough not to fear the others, but they too were curious—just like the waterless families—why they had received it and the others hadn't.","“It's the Mountain God! The Mountain God must have shown His power!” A man clutching an empty bamboo tube fell to his knees with a thud and kowtowed repeatedly toward the mountain.","He kept muttering, “Mountain God, have mercy! I beg You, grant this humble one a tube of water! My father and mother are dying of thirst! I beg You to be compassionate and save their lives—I swear I'll build You a golden statue and offer incense in Your honor!”","After speaking, he thumped his head three more times in the direction of the mountain peak.","When he finished kowtowing, he held up his bamboo tube and stayed perfectly still. Seeing his display, the people around him fell silent. No one left; they all watched, waited, hoping to see the tube fill with water, to witness a miracle.","The surroundings grew so quiet that everyone seemed to hear each other's heartbeats.","All eyes were fixed on the young man's earth-yellow bamboo tube, especially those from the waterless families—their eyes were beginning to redden with desperation.","No one knew how long passed—maybe a few breaths, maybe a dozen, or even longer. The tube showed no sign of water. At last, the man could no longer contain himself and moved.","In frustration, he shook the tube. No splashing sound came. “Why not? Why isn't there any!”","In a rage, he smashed the tube onto the ground with a bang. “What exactly am I lacking? Why won't they give my family water!”","“Could it be... that our water wasn't granted by the Mountain God at all?” A clever onlooker couldn't help voicing his suspicion.","The young man's elder brother, reminded by that remark, seemed to have a realization. “Right! Brother, is it possible that... you just prayed to the wrong deity?”","“Ah, the wrong deity?” Murmurs spread through the crowd as everyone began discussing which gods their families usually worshipped.","“Our family now only believes in the Divine Maiden!”","“Ours too, we only believe in the Divine Maiden!”","“Same for us—three sticks of incense every day!”","“Hey, ours too!”","“Our family—”","As they compared notes, whether by coincidence or not, they discovered that every family with water was a follower of the Divine Maiden.","Those with quick minds couldn't help but call out loudly to the furious, waterless families: “Hey there, brother—which deity does your family worship on a daily basis?”","A slightly stout man froze, as if a thought had struck him, and said uncertainly, “I—my family runs a small restaurant. We worship the Kitchen God at home.”","The stout man's brother, who bore a three-part resemblance to him, also spoke up: “My brother and I both run small businesses—I run a general store, and our family worships the God of Wealth.”","Another young man stepped forward. “My father is a doctor. Our family worships the Medicine God.”","“Ours is—”","These people soon noticed something off: some households had ancestral shrines with statues, while others, apart from visiting temples and monasteries, didn't keep any idols at home.","But the biggest difference between them and the families who had water was this: whether they worshipped deities at home or not, not a single one of them believed in the Divine Maiden of the Great Yan Dynasty.","The difference between having water and not... the answer seemed almost obvious.","Those who guessed the truth trembled, their lips quivering. “This... I—we—”","“Waah! I refuse to accept this!”","Yue Fuguang, now far away, could still faintly hear the weeping below, and she felt little remorse—without a statue to serve as a connection, she had no way to send them water, and besides, she owed them no karmic debt.","A few minutes later, her flying carriage hovered over the city of Hundred Blossoms. Inside and outside the city walls, there wasn't a single flower—only withered branches, fallen leaves, and ash-gray battlements.","Because of the intense heat, the streets were nearly deserted; only a few shops still open had a sparse handful of idle laborers sitting beneath their eaves.","Most shops along the street had shuttered, but a handful stubbornly remained open.","Inside one general store, a couple in their thirties sat listlessly, staring outside. Their shop had almost no goods left to sell—when people couldn't even drink water, who would come to buy sundries?","But the man had been so used to running his shop that staying at home all day made him restless. “Husband, shouldn't we really go up to the mountain to shelter?” the woman asked her husband, who had started wiping down the counter yet again.","The man set down his rag and replied casually, “You actually believe what those people said?”","“They spoke so vividly—it sounded real to me.”","“Foolish woman's talk!” The man sneered. “If that little girl from Great Yan could control rain, why haven't we seen a single drop?”","The woman, seeing her husband's obstinance, wanted to say: She's the Divine Maiden of Great Yan—why would she bring rain to Nan Zhao?","But cowed by her husband's authority, she only said, “In any case, since the Divine Maiden can control rain, what she said might be true. Why don't we—”","“Enough. You don't need to worry about anything—just take care of the children. Leave everything else to me!”","The man cut her off roughly, half out of sulk, half as if to prove his own judgment. “We're not going anywhere. I'll see for myself whether it pours in three days!”"]},{"number":497,"title":"Chapter 497: Belief and Unbelief","paragraphs":["[Host, this man is stubbornly set in his ways—in the end, won't he bring disaster upon his entire family?]","\"We'll see if they believe it once they see the rain.\" If they believe it in time and head up the mountain, they'll survive. If not, fate will decide for them.","Wah! Wah!","Just then, Yue Fuguang and the others suddenly heard the sound of crying.","Yue Fuguang followed the sound of the sobs and saw, first, a man in his thirties. He was squatting in the vegetable plot he had carved out of his own courtyard, both hands braced on the ground, fingers digging into the cracked, dry earth. The greens in the plot had withered to yellow, clearly beyond saving.","In the past, these plots had grown flowers and herbs that could be sold for money. Only later, forced by circumstance, had they been converted into vegetable patches—but unfortunately, not a single plant had survived.","The crying came from a woman who had collapsed on the ground beside him. Her surname was Liu, and she had three children, the youngest only three years old.","She had heard from traveling merchants that the Divine Maiden of Fengcheng had brought rain, and her heart had been filled with envy. Then they said that Nanzhao would also see heavy rain soon. Before she could even feel glad, they added, as they spoke to the neighbors, that the heavy rain would bring floods!","Some believed it; some didn't. Her family was one of those that didn't.","But she believed it! She believed the Divine Maiden would not use such words to deceive common folk like them.","Yet her in-laws were stubborn, and her husband and brother-in-law both listened to their parents. She and her sister-in-law were just two women with little say in the matter.","But ever since she had returned from her natal home that morning, her heart had been in a panic. Thinking of her family members who had already headed toward Baiyao Mountain, along with her eldest son they had taken with them, and then thinking of her little girl of three and her second son still at home, she couldn't hold back her sobs.","Her tears kept falling—one drop, two drops—hitting the dry earth, carving out tiny pits that were instantly absorbed, leaving not even a mark behind.","She tried to wipe her face with her sleeve, but her hand stopped halfway. She went completely rigid, mouth open, chin trembling—because when she looked up, she saw her mother-in-law's gaunt face and those triangular, downward-slanting eyes.","Instinctive fear made the woman shiver involuntarily. But before she could say anything, the old woman suddenly burst into loud wailing.","It wasn't soft whimpering—it was a howl torn up from the depths of her heart, exploding like a clap of thunder in the household. The sound was loud, yet not a single tear fell. Her commotion immediately attracted the neighbors.","She plopped down on the ground, both hands slapping the dirt, sending puffs of dry dust into the air.","\"Who have I done all this for! My daughter-in-law won't listen, and she's even trying to turn my son against his own mother!\"","\"My son and daughter-in-law are unfilial—this old woman might as well be dead!\"","Seeing his mother like this, the man had no choice but to stand up and explain helplessly, \"Mother, Huijie didn't say anything, please stop crying. The ground is hot.\"","\"I won't get up, let me burn to death, then!\" She turned to her husband, who had just returned from outside, and said, \"Old man, your children are heartless. I'll go on ahead—don't you miss me!\"","The old man watched as his wife produced thunder without rain, knowing she was just scaring the children again. He shook his head helplessly. \"Alright, I understand. I won't miss you.\"","The old woman's mournful face froze mid-cry. She hadn't expected that her husband of a lifetime, who had yielded to her every time, would say such a thing today.","\"Wah! I really can't go on living!\" she cried, covering her face with her hands while peeking through her fingers at her husband.","\"Father!\" the couple both looked at the old man, thinking that their father must have had a change of heart today—he wasn't even coaxing their mother anymore.","The old man nodded. \"Eldest, Second—fix up the cart and load the grain.\"","Glancing at his wife, whose cries were growing softer, he then instructed his two daughters-in-law, \"Eldest's wife, Second's wife, you two go cook right away. Make as much food as possible, especially things that will store well—the more, the better!\"","The eldest son was stunned by his father's words. \"Father, what are we—\"","The old man's face turned stern, and he said flatly, \"Up the mountain. We leave at dawn tomorrow!\"","Once the rain came, it would be heavy. If they delayed and tried to flee with their whole family and belongings, it would be far too difficult.","The second son, though a little puzzled as to why his stubborn father had suddenly changed his mind, was overjoyed that the old man had finally seen reason. He eagerly agreed and went off to work.","But the eldest son couldn't help asking, \"Father, weren't you the one who never believed in the Divine Maiden's words?\"","Had his parents not been so stubborn, he and his wife wouldn't have had to send their eldest son to his maternal grandparents, asking them to take the boy up the mountain.","A flicker of embarrassment passed over the old man's face, though his skin was dark enough that no one could see him blush. \"Hmph!\" He put on the air of a family patriarch and waved impatiently at his eldest son. \"None of your business—just do as I say!\"","As the eldest son ran off to work, he figured his father must have heard something from someone outside just now.","[Master, this family got lucky—they came to their senses before the great rain. Far better off than the shopkeeper at the general store!]","Yue Fuguang nodded. This seemingly small choice would ultimately decide the life or death of an entire family.","\"I hope we see more people like them these next two days.\" People follow the crowd. Even if they didn't quite believe her words, seeing others flee would stir unease in their hearts, and they'd find themselves following along.","[Master, look—is that the government office of Baihua City?]","\"It should be. From the outside, it doesn't look much different from the government offices of Dayan.\"","[The six nations were all split from one Great Yong Dynasty. They all inherited their 'father's' cultural foundation. Even after a few hundred years, similarities are hardly surprising.]","Yue Fuguang commanded the flying chariot to draw closer. She wanted to see exactly what the government office of Nanzhao looked like.","The government office of Baihua City stood on the city's busiest street, facing south, occupying a vast area. With its gray bricks and dark tiles, tall walls and deep courtyards, it carried a stern, awe-inspiring air—yet to her eyes, it was a typical southern-style building.","Facing the street stood a tall spirit wall, its white surface and black eaves featuring a painted mural of a beast resembling a qilin, called \"Tan.\"","Behind the spirit wall was the main gate, three bays wide with an open central section. The vermilion doors were studded with copper nails, and above the lintel hung a black-lacquered plaque bearing five gilded characters: \"Government Office of Baihua City\"—written with vigorous brushwork, though whose calligraphy it was remained unknown.","Flanking the gate stood two stone lions, the male on the left and the female on the right. Beneath the gate's canopy were two tiger-head plaques reading \"Silence\" and \"Step Aside,\" their lacquered surfaces gleaming with reflected gold under the blazing sun.","[Master, that up ahead is the ceremonial gate. Shall we go in and take a look?]","\"Past the ceremonial gate lies the core of the government office. Little Zhu, are you trying to eavesdrop?\" She had seen through this trick all along—the little thing was deliberately flying this way, wanting to save its own energy for gathering information by listening in on conversations already happening here.","\"I'm not, I didn't—Master, don't falsely accuse little me!\"","Crossing the ceremonial gate was the main hall, five bays wide with a single-eaved hard-ridged roof. Chiwen beasts crouched along the ridge, layered bracket sets clustered under the eaves, and the black-lacquered beams and columns were thick as a pair of outstretched arms.","Beyond the main hall, the first thing that came into view was the warm chamber at the center, a private space partitioned off by a wooden screen.","The floor of the warm chamber was half a foot higher than the rest of the hall, and at its center stood an ebony judge's desk."]},{"number":498,"title":"Chapter 498: Do You Think Those Grand Ministers at Court Don't Believe It","paragraphs":["On the desk were arranged in order: a lot box (containing red and green command sticks), a brush stand, an inkstone, a wooden gavel, and a seal box holding a bronze official seal.","Behind the desk was a grand armchair, its backrest carved with lion patterns, the armrests polished shiny by successive officials over the years.","At this moment, it was high noon, and apart from two duty constables, the hall was empty.","\"Judging by the look of this yamen, they didn't take my words to heart!\" It was too quiet. Normally, shouldn't they be busy at this hour?","Drought relief, flood control—which of these shouldn't have them run off their feet? Yet here they were, the duty constables dozing off.","【Maybe they're busy in the back? They're lucky the whole country's in drought, otherwise the people would all be fleeing famine, turning into refugees and then rioters—then they'd have real trouble on their hands.】","Behind the warm chamber stood a folding screen painted with a scene of waves and a rising sun. Behind the screen was a small door leading to the rear residence, the area where officials both worked and lived.","Yue Fuguang looked down at the scene from above, quickly scanning. The side chambers on both sides of the main hall were where the six bureaus of clerks worked—personnel, revenue, rites, military, justice, and public works—arranged left and right.","In the eastern side chamber, long tables held abacuses, brushes, and ink. Several secretaries were buried in their work, the occasional clack of abacus beads breaking the silence. Apart from that, only the rustle of paper and the sound of coughing could be heard.","Behind the main hall, passing through a corridor, was the second hall—smaller in scale, yet it was where the prefect handled daily affairs and confidential matters. That was exactly where the system wanted to obtain information for free.","The flying carriage quietly drew closer, its form concealed, and the sound of voices came from within.","Feng Tang took a look and recognized the people inside. He said in a low voice to Yue Fuguang, \"My lord, the man inside wearing the deep blue brocade robe—this subordinate recognizes him. He is Zhou Zhifei, the prefect of Baihua City.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. She deliberately drew close rather than eavesdrop from the sky, all so that all three people in the carriage could hear clearly, saving herself and the system the trouble of relaying.","\"Feng, what sort of man is this Zhou Zhifei?\" Yue Fuguang observed his ordinary features. She couldn't tell good from evil at a glance, but under her probing gaze, Zhou Zhifei's fortune was middling, and his merit value was also middling.","\"This subordinate only met him once eight years ago, when the Nanzhao envoy mission came to Dayan. I had little dealings with him, but from what I could tell, he's one who advocates the doctrine of the golden mean.","Still, he's governed Baihua City for three years now, steady and methodical. His achievements aren't as prominent as his predecessor's, but the people often speak well of him.\"","The second hall had simpler furnishings. There was no warm chamber, just a single writing desk and a few round-backed chairs. At this moment, Prefect Zhou Zhifei and three other subordinate officials were seated.","On the desk sat a celadon incense burner with wisps of green smoke curling upward. The walls were hung with portraits of past officials and calligraphy or paintings, mostly landscapes—clearly the master's attempt to seek a trace of literati tranquility in this seat of power.","At this moment, one of the officials—a man with a long beard, a pale complexion, and in his thirties, wearing blue robes—looked at Zhou Zhifei and said, \"My lord, are we truly not following the imperial decree to close the city gates?\"","Hearing his question, the other two also turned to look at the prefect. Zhou Zhifei's brow was deeply furrowed, and his voice came unhurried, \"Zheng, we aren't defying the imperial decree. We're merely delaying its execution.\"","\"Delaying its execution? But... but we've already seen His Majesty's edict. If we don't close the city gates in time, let alone the three of us, that General Lan stationed thirty li outside the city—once he gets wind of this, he'll inevitably send a secret report to Her Majesty the Empress!\"","\"Prefect, what Zhao says is right. The fear now is that Lan Shoucheng will file a report against us behind our backs.\"","Zhou Zhifei saw that Zheng, Zhao, and Qu all wanted to persuade him to follow the emperor's decree, and he felt helpless inside. \"Gentlemen, once we close the city gates, if the torrential rains truly come and continue for a full month, what do you think this city of Baihua will become?\"","The three exchanged glances. That went without saying. If it kept raining nonstop, even ten days would be more than the city's drainage system could handle.","At that point, the closed city gates would turn this place into one big fish pond, and they'd all be the fish inside it!","The youngest official, Qu Huai, had a pale, beardless face. He glanced at his two superiors, Zheng and Zhao, before asking cautiously, \"Prefect, are you actually believing the words of that Goddess Yue?\"","Zhou Zhifei, who had been lowering his head to sip tea, paused mid-motion, the cup in his hand. He lifted his eyelids and said in a voice that betrayed no emotion, \"What? You don't believe it?\"","\"I... I...\" Qu Huai opened his mouth, stammering for a long while before trailing off. If he said he didn't believe it, that would be a lie—he had already secretly sent his entire family to Baibao Mountain at dawn today.","If he said he did believe it, then he was clearly going against the emperor's decree. The decree had stated these were baseless rumors, strictly prohibiting the people from discussing them, and also strictly forbidding the people and officials' families from leaving the city.","This was tying everyone together and letting them wait to be soaked!","They had all sensed something amiss. The intent of the edict, it seemed, was that the court was not only desperately stopping the people from fleeing to Dayan, but not even allowing them to take refuge in the mountains. This decree was most unlike their Empress's usual way of doing things.","\"Or rather, do you think the ministers at court don't believe it? That the princes and princesses in power don't believe it?\"","Zheng's hand tightened under his sleeve. He leaned forward, lowering his voice, \"Prefect, have you heard something?\"","He looked around the room, then glanced at Zhao and Qu, \"Please speak frankly, my lord, so that the rest of us can have confidence. We will follow your lead without question!\"","Zhao and Qu, equally perceptive, nodded in unison and clasped their hands in salute, \"Please speak frankly, my lord. We will follow your lead!\"","In truth, the three of them were quite uneasy themselves. Nanzhao had already lost three cities to Dayan, and Jialing City was on the verge of falling. They had watched coolly from the sidelines and could see that Nanyue was in grave danger this time.","If Nanyue fell, what good fate awaited Nanzhao, which had been secretly supporting it? Everyone knew Nanzhao's national strength was far inferior to Nanyue's, and they had mostly relied on it for development in the past—why else would they have involved themselves in the conflict between the two nations?","Both Yu City and Jialing City had Nanzhao troops sent to reinforce them. All three nations knew this perfectly well. They would eventually be dealt with by Dayan.","When that day came, where would they, as imperial officials, go from here?","Die for their country, or defect?","The eavesdropping Yue Fuguang and the others felt a surge of excitement. They sensed the real meat of the conversation was coming.","Still, the fact that the Nanzhao court had ordered the city gates closed, forbidding the people from fleeing the coming flood, was something she hadn't expected.","Keeping people from fleeing to another country was understandable. But preventing the people from escaping to save their own lives—what kind of operation was that? Did they think they had too many people and needed to eliminate some?","Zhou Zhifei set down his teacup, straightened his posture, and tapped his fingers lightly on the tea table. After a pause, he said, \"In my view, the decision the three of you made today is correct!\"","When he said this, not only Qu Huai, but even Zheng Yu and Zhao Gong were startled. Startlement gave way to embarrassment.","They had thought themselves discreet, yet the prefect knew all about it. They exchanged awkward glances with one another. It seemed their fellow officials weren't fools either—between trusting their own court on the one hand, and that Goddess Yue on the other, they had all chosen the latter."]},{"number":499,"title":"Chapter 499: Leave a way for the people to survive, and also leave a way out for yourself.","paragraphs":["“It's not just you, to be honest, this official has also sent his family away.” Zhou Zhifei first came clean with the few of them, considering it a way to align their interests. Since they were all on the same side, it made what came next much easier to discuss.","The men sincerely cupped their fists in deference, “Your Excellency is most wise!”","Zhou Zhifei shook his head. “From what this official knows, it's not just the few of us. Even those above us—every single household—has sent away some of their younger kin?”","Even those who didn't believe the words of the Goddess Yue had, at the very least, secretly sent away one or two promising descendants.","He tapped the imperial edict on the table. “The messenger is still unconscious. According to the laws of the court, we shouldn't have laid eyes on this edict yet!”","The men froze for a moment, then their eyes all lit up, and they nodded in rapid succession.","Seeing this, Zhou Zhifei continued. “It's not that we won't close the city gates. At the latest, the messenger will awaken by noon the day after tomorrow, and only then will we carry out the edict as instructed.”","He slapped the armrest of his chair vigorously. “By that time, those who want to leave should have already gone. Those who don't, will stay in the city and let fate take its course!”","He had done his best, and had given these people a chance. If they chose not to leave, whether they lived or died was up to fate!","Zheng Yu asked quietly, “Your Excellency, is the word of the Goddess Yue really that reliable?”","Because of court decrees, they, as officials, were forbidden from enshrining statues of the Great Yan Goddess at home. So even though they'd heard she had the power to control the rain, they never truly linked her to divinity.","They had studied the teachings of the sages. They had never seen a ghost or monster, and gods existed only in paintings and myth—how could they believe in a living goddess?","A faint smile crept onto Zhou Zhifei's otherwise grave face. “This official has some connections with the prefect of Fengcheng. What you've heard doesn't even amount to a tenth of the truth.”","The merchants traveling between the two kingdoms were mostly common folk, unlettered. Their descriptions of the Goddess's manifestations naturally fell short of the mark.","Hearing Zhou Zhifei's matter-of-fact words, the men were so startled they nearly jumped out of their chairs.","“Your Excellency, are you telling the truth?” Zheng Yu felt his face burning with embarrassment. He had just been about to scoff at the notion that no goddess could exist, and now Prefect Zhou was telling him she did—and not only that, many people had witnessed her with their own eyes!","Zhou Zhifei gave him a meaningful glance. “Whether or not it's true, you will all see for yourselves in due time.”","With that, he picked up a cup of tea and took a sip, his face gradually turning serious again. “There is one more matter. This official had not intended to say much about it, but given the years we've worked together, I would hate to see you all kept in the dark and lose your lives over it.”","He set the cup down and lowered his voice. “So I might as well tell you!”","The men exchanged glances, cupped their fists, and adopted looks of rapt attention. “We thank Your Excellency for your consideration. We will hold this kindness in our hearts forever.”","Zhou Zhifei's voice was low, every word clear and deliberate: “I have heard that Her Majesty the Empress fell gravely ill five days ago, and all court affairs have been handed over to several of the imperial heirs.”","“The Empress's illness is no simple bedridden state! Those heirs, seeing her condition deteriorating, are fighting among themselves fiercely!”","He pointed again at the edict on the table. “Whether this edict even came from the Empress is another matter entirely!”","The three men, suddenly hearing such life-threatening news, widened their eyes in shock. “Your Excellency, is what you say true? Then... then that edict sent to the Sixth Princess in Dayan a few days ago...”","Zhou Zhifei gave a cold laugh. “Either the Empress has recalled the Princess for some other arrangement, or someone is trying to use the Empress's name to ambush and kill her! A great upheaval is coming, and some people are already too eager to make their move!”","“Then... what should we do?” A change of the imperial bloodline was always the most perilous of affairs, especially now with troubles from within and threats from without. Though they were far from the capital, they were equally cut off from information, and it would be all too easy for them to be used as cannon fodder.","“Alas!” Zhao Gong sighed. “If Her Majesty had left behind an edict of succession, whether it be for a crown prince or a crown princess, we would at least have someone to rally behind!”","Once the dynasty had a clear heir, at least they would know whom to obey!","Zhou Zhifei shook his head. “The Empress fell ill suddenly...” She probably hadn't expected someone to move against her so quickly.","[Master, is the Empress of Nan Zhao about to die? Isn't Lan Xuan'er in danger then?]","Yue Fuguang shook her head. “As long as she stays in Dayan, her life is safe. The fear is that she might make a rash decision and come back.”","“As for whether the Empress is on her deathbed, judging by this Zhou Zhifei's demeanor, the Empress's condition is no mere illness.”","[So some prince or princess has laid hands on their own mother?]","“Perhaps someone is seeking to seize power amidst the chaos. The question is whether they can hold onto the throne!”","“Let's go.” Yue Fuguang glanced at Feng Tang. No doubt he would quickly report the news of the Empress's 'grave illness' to Emperor Mingxi.","The spies Dayan had left in Nan Zhao, due to various reasons such as strict checks on those leaving the region, might have discovered the news but been unable to send it out. Otherwise, they wouldn't have needed to make this journey themselves.","The flying carriage had just left the City of a Hundred Blossoms when, high in the sky not far below their feet, several arrows whistled through the air, striking precisely the pigeons flying above.","[Master, what are they doing?] Twenty li ahead lay the Southern Zhao army camp—surely they weren't out hunting here!","“Probably preventing messages from being sent by carrier pigeon.”","[Ah, so that's why Dayan's spies haven't sent word back lately! By the way, Master, what did you write in the letter you left for Zhou Zhifei earlier?]","“Naturally, urging him to leave a path of survival for the common people, and also to leave a way out for himself!”","Back with Zhou Zhifei, after frightening his subordinates, he waved the shell-shocked trio away and walked alone toward the rear courtyard.","Beyond the second hall, a tall wall separated off Zhou Zhifei's private residence.","The garden behind the official compound was small and delicate, planted with a few stalks of bamboo and an old locust tree. At present, both the bamboo and the locust, along with the flowers in the corner flowerbeds, had withered and lost all vitality.","The main room served as his living quarters, elegantly furnished with bookshelves, a tea table, and a qin desk—a world apart from the stern authority of the front hall. Unfortunately, this usually lively residence now felt profoundly desolate.","“Sir, you've returned?” The steward Chen Fu poured Zhou Zhifei a full cup of tea and stood waiting at his side to report.","“Uncle Chen, has everything been taken care of?”","“Rest assured, sir. The old madam, the mistress, the young master, and the young miss have all been settled safely.”","Zhou Zhifei nodded. “Did I not tell you to have Ada come back instead? Why did you return as well?”","Chen Fu smiled. “Those youngsters are rash and careless. I couldn't rest easy leaving you here alone, sir.”","Chen Fu looked around before continuing, “Time is short, so we could only find two boats. Sir...”","Zhou Zhifei set down his teacup. “Uncle Chen, speak your mind. It's fine.”","“Since you are so certain of the Goddess's words, why do you insist on staying in the city? It's hardly as safe here as on Mount Baibao.”","Even with a boat, hiding out on the mountain would be safer than this.","“I am the prefect, the parent official of this region. If I leave, what about the common people who remain? And the court's laws are still weighing on us.”","He had barely finished speaking when the master and servant saw a letter slowly materialize on the table where there had previously only been an empty teacup."]},{"number":500,"title":"Chapter 500: If the Goddess Does Not Make It Rain, I Will Kneel Here Until I Die","paragraphs":["Chen Fu was so startled that the teapot in his hand slipped straight out of his grip. With a crash, the white porcelain kettle shattered into pieces, and the tea inside splashed everywhere, soaking both master and servant's shoes and the hems of their robes.","\"Old... Old Master! This... this...\" Wasn't this a ghost wandering around in broad daylight?","Chen Fu looked toward the door — the sun was blazing high, the day even hotter and drier than yesterday. Yet at this moment, he felt cold from the inside out, as if submerged in ice water.","His back was covered in sweat, not from the heat but from sheer terror at what he had just witnessed!","Zhou Zhifei's state of mind was no better than Chen Fu's. The large, pitch-black characters \"To Zhou Zhifei, personal\" on the pale blue envelope scared him out of his wits, nearly making his liver and gallbladder split.","This mysterious letter, appearing out of thin air, was addressed to him by name. He couldn't even deceive himself into thinking it had been misdelivered.","\"This!\" His terrified gaze finally landed on the bright moon in the upper right corner of the envelope. Calling it a bright moon was one thing — it was actually a perfectly round white ring, and around its edge seemed to linger a hazy, wispy aura.","Why did Zhou Zhifei immediately recognize it as a bright moon rather than a sun?","Zhou Zhifei: Intuition!","Zhou Zhifei swallowed hard, his hand trembling like that of a man with ten years of Parkinson's disease, and slowly reached for the letter on the table.","\"Old Master!\"","\"Uncle Chen, rest assured!\" Zhou Zhifei, upon seeing that bright moon, seemed to be reminded of something — that was the only reason he dared to reach out right away.","Even though he guessed in his heart that there was likely no danger, his body still tensed up instinctively, his hand shaking like a decade-long Parkinson's patient.","Zhou Zhifei swallowed hard again before carefully opening the envelope. Once he saw what was inside, his eyes widened as if he'd just had eyelid surgery — they grew massively bigger!","Yue Fuguang naturally had no idea that her unique method of delivering letters had scared the prefect and his servant half to death.","By now, they had already left Nanzhao and entered the territory of Nanyue.","[Master, great victory at Jialing City!]","\"What, it's already over so soon? What are the casualties for Dayan?\"","[Because there was no commander in Jialing City, the defending soldiers' morale was scattered. Dayan took the entire city without much effort. Dayan's side had over two hundred wounded and less than a hundred dead. Jialing City had over two thousand casualties, with more than ten thousand prisoners captured.]","\"The next city is Sui City, right?\"","[Yes, that's the one — Nanyue's granary!] Taking it would sever half of Nanyue's food supply. Sui City and the surrounding territories under its rule were, aside from Gan City, the second-largest city in Nanyue.","\"Who are the defenders of Sui City?\"","[This person, Master, you've definitely heard of — they are the You family, the military clan of Nanyue, who in the original historical timeline of Gan Tang were her husband's family. The defenders are You Hui and his son You Hong. One would have been Gan Tang's father-in-law, the other would have been Gan Tang's consort.]","\"So it's their family! Now that Gan Tang has married the Sixth Prince, that You Hong must still be a bachelor, right?\"","[Master, isn't your focus a bit off? Shouldn't you be asking how capable the troops led by this father-son pair are?]","Yue Fuguang waved her hand dismissively. \"What's there to worry about? If Generals Xu and Wei, armed with gunpowder, still can't take down the You family, it just means the two of them lack ability — better to replace them early!\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's words, Feng Tang and the other two silently lit a memorial candle for Wei Shouyi in their hearts.","After all, they had spent over a month together, so there was some friendship. Should they remind Wei Shouyi to fight this battle well? As for Yue Fuguang's words — as long as they didn't involve national secrets, such casual remarks would only be recorded in the files. They wouldn't breathe a single word to anyone unrelated.","[Once Dayan takes Sui City and Ye City, most of Nanyue's territory will be in our hands. This speed is a bit beyond what I predicted, which means those two do have some ability, and they have merit for Dayan.]","The group rarely heard the Divine Artifact praise anyone. To earn the evaluation of \"some ability\" and \"merit for Dayan,\" Generals Xu and Wei had secured their status. No need to worry about the suspicion of overshadowing the sovereign after conquering Nanyue.","This was practically a death-exemption medal! Feng Tang's eyes rolled — this had to be spread around.","\"Of course, generals who expand territory are all worthy of...\"","\"What right—\" Yue Fuguang's words were cut off by a sharp, piercing cry that shot through the sky and drilled straight into her ears.","Before they could figure out what was happening, the voice continued: \"What right! What right do they have to get rain... We... what did we do wrong...\"","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. Even without knowing the full story, she could guess the gist from those two brief sentences.","Fuming about something like this was truly bizarre!","\"Go down and take a look!\"","\"Yes, ma'am!\" The other three were all sharp-minded people and could guess roughly as well. Their brows furrowed involuntarily.","The flying vehicle descended invisibly. Soon, they saw a crowd gathered on a street. This was a town called Heshui, under Nanping Prefecture in Nanyue, less than a hundred li ahead lay Gan City.","This street was one of Heshui Town's main thoroughfares. The one who had just spoken was a woman covered in dirt and grime. Her head was lowered as she wept, making it hard to tell her exact age.","Beside her, several other women cried along with her, one after another, like a row of knocked-over dominoes.","Some crouched, some sat slumped on the ground, some leaned against the wall, their bodies slowly sliding down.","A young man, just over twenty years old, stood to one side, staring fixedly at the crying figures in the middle. The flesh on his face twitched, his jaw muscles clenched tight, bulging in and out.","Both hands were balled into fists, his knuckles white from the pressure. His whole body was like a drawn bow pulled taut.","A woman's voice was hoarse as she shouted with all her might toward the sky: \"My child is dying of thirst! Why hasn't it rained? Why hasn't it rained?!\"","Whether by coincidence or not, the direction she faced as she looked up was exactly where Yue Fuguang's flying vehicle was invisibly hovering.","That young man suddenly lowered his head, bent down, and with his clenched fist, slammed it into the dirt road with a dull thud.","The skin on his knuckles was scraped off, and blood seeped out. He didn't look at it. His forehead pressed against the ground as he gasped for breath, his chest heaving violently.","His shoulders slowly sagged, his whole body as though his spine had been pulled out. Bent over, hands braced on the ground, droplets fell to the earth — indistinguishable between sweat and tears.","His voice rasped as he repeated the same words as the woman earlier: \"Why hasn't it rained? Why won't the Divine Maiden make it rain?!\"","\"The Divine Maiden is Dayan's Divine Maiden, not Nanyue's!\" A young woman stepped out from the crowd. She looked to be sixteen or seventeen years old, with slightly sallow skin and cracked lips, but her eyes were exceptionally bright.","She wore a plain cloth garment that, while no longer clean, was still neat. Behind her followed a young man of similar age, with darker skin, also dressed in coarse, somewhat soiled clothing.","The kneeling young man suddenly raised his head, a hint of hostility in his eyes. \"Third brother, third sister-in-law!\"","\"Big brother.\" The young man behind the girl reached out, trying to pull the one on the ground to his feet.","He shook his head in refusal. \"Third brother, don't worry about me. If the Divine Maiden doesn't make it rain today, I... I'll kneel here until I die!\""]}]);
